# BOOK	001	GEN	Genesis	Genesis
001	GEN	001	001	In the bigynnyng God made of nouyt heuene and erthe.
001	GEN	001	002	Forsothe the erthe was idel and voide, and derknessis weren on the face of depthe; and the Spiryt of the Lord was borun on the watris.
001	GEN	001	003	And God seide, Liyt be maad, and liyt was maad.
001	GEN	001	004	And God seiy the liyt, that it was good, and he departide the liyt fro derknessis,
001	GEN	001	005	and he clepide the liyt, dai, and the derknessis, nyyt. And the euentid and morwetid was maad, o daie.
001	GEN	001	006	And God seide, The firmament be maad in the myddis of watris, and departe watris fro watris.
001	GEN	001	007	And God made the firmament, and departide the watris that weren vndur the firmament fro these watris that weren on the firmament; and it was don so.
001	GEN	001	008	And God clepide the firmament, heuene. And the euentid and morwetid was maad, the secounde dai.
001	GEN	001	009	Forsothe God seide, The watris, that ben vndur heuene, be gaderid in to o place, and a drie place appere; and it was doon so.
001	GEN	001	010	And God clepide the drie place, erthe; and he clepide the gadryngis togidere of watris, the sees. And God seiy that it was good;
001	GEN	001	011	and seide, The erthe brynge forth greene eerbe and makynge seed, and appil tre makynge fruyt bi his kynde, whos seed be in it silf on erthe; and it was doon so.
001	GEN	001	012	And the erthe brouyte forth greene erbe and makynge seed bi his kynde, and a tre makynge fruyt, and ech hauynge seed by his kynde. And God seiy that it was good.
001	GEN	001	013	And the euentid and morwetid was maad, the thridde dai.
001	GEN	001	014	Forsothe God seide, Liytis be maad in the firmament of heuene, and departe tho the dai and niyt; and be tho in to signes, and tymes, and daies, and yeeris;
001	GEN	001	015	and shyne tho in the firmament of heuene, and liytne tho the erthe; and it was doon so.
001	GEN	001	016	And God made twei grete liytis, the gretter liyt that it schulde be bifore to the dai, and the lesse liyt that it schulde be bifore to the niyt;
