002	EXO	021	032	If the oxe asailith a seruaunt, and handmaide, the lord of the oxe schal yyue thretti siclis of siluer to `his lord; forsothe the oxe schal be oppressid with stoonus.
002	EXO	021	033	If ony man openeth a cisterne, and diggith, and hilith it not, and an oxe ether asse fallith in to it,
002	EXO	021	034	the lord of the cisterne schal yelde the prijs of the werk beestis; forsothe that that is deed schal be his.
