002	EXO	034	035	whiche sien that the face of Moyses goynge out was horned, but eft he hilide his face, if ony tyme he spak to hem.
002	EXO	035	001	Therfor whanne al the cumpanye of the sones of Israel was gaderid, Moises seide to hem, These thingis it ben, whiche the Lord comaundide to be doon.
002	EXO	035	002	Sixe daies ye schulen do werk, the seuenthe dai schal be hooli to you, the sabat and reste of the Lord; he that doith werk in the sabat schal be slayn.
002	EXO	035	003	Ye schulen not kyndle fier in alle youre dwellyng places bi the `dai of sabat.
002	EXO	035	004	And Moises seide to al the cumpeny of the sones of Israel, This is the word which the Lord comaundide, and seide,
002	EXO	035	005	Departe ye at you the firste fruytis to the Lord; ech wilful man and of redi wille offre tho to the Lord, gold, and siluer, and bras,
002	EXO	035	006	and iacynct, and purpur, and reed selk twies died, and bijs, heeris of geet,
002	EXO	035	007	and skynnys of rammes maad reed, and of iacynt,
002	EXO	035	008	trees of Sechym, and oile to liytis to be ordeyned, and that the oynement be maad, and encense moost swete,
002	EXO	035	009	stoonus of onochyn and gemmes, to the ournyng of the `cloth on the schuldris, and of the racional.
002	EXO	035	010	Who euer of you is wijs, come he, and make that, that the Lord comaundide,
002	EXO	035	011	that is, the tabernacle, and the roof therof, and the hilyng; ryngis, and bildyngis of tablis, with barris, stakis, and foundementis;
002	EXO	035	012	the arke, and barris; the propiciatorie, and the veil, which is hangid byfore it;
002	EXO	035	013	the bord with barris, and vesselis, and with looues of settyng forth;
002	EXO	035	014	the candilstike to susteyne liytis, the vesselis, and lanternes therof, and oile to the nurschyngis of fyris; the auter of encense, and the barris;
002	EXO	035	015	the oile of anoyntyng, and encense of swete smellynge spiceries; the tente at the dore of the tabernacle;
002	EXO	035	016	the auter of brent sacrifice, and his brasun gridele, with hise barris, and vessels; the `greet waischyng vessel, and `his foundement;
002	EXO	035	017	the curteyns of the large street, with pileris and foundementis; the tente in the doris of the porche;
002	EXO	035	018	the stakis of the tabernacle and of the large street, with her coordis;
002	EXO	035	019	the clothis, whose vss is in `the seruyce of seyntuarie; the clothis of Aaron bischop, and of hise sones, that thei be set in preesthod to me.
002	EXO	035	020	And al the multitude of the sones of Israel yede out of `the siyt of Moises,
002	EXO	035	021	and offride with moost redi soule and deuout the firste thingis to the Lord, to make the werk of the tabernacle of witnessyng, what euer was nedeful to the ournyng, and to hooli clothis.
002	EXO	035	022	Men and wymmen yauen bies of the armes, and eeryngis, ryngis, and ournementis of `the arm niy the hond; ech goldun vessel was departid in to the yiftis of the Lord.
002	EXO	035	023	If ony man hadde iacynt, and purpur, and `reed selk twies died, bijs, and the heeris of geet, skynnes of rammes maad reed, and of iacynt,
002	EXO	035	024	metals of siluer, and of bras, thei offeryden to the Lord, and trees of Sechym in to dyuerse vsis.
