002	EXO	035	026	and bijs, and the heeris of geet; and yauen alle thingis by her owne fre wille.
002	EXO	035	027	Forsothe princes offeriden stoonys of onychyn and iemmes, to the `cloth on the schuldris, and to the racional, and swete smellynge spiceries,
002	EXO	035	028	and oyle to the liytis to be ordeyned, and to make redi oynement, and to make the encense of swettist odour.
002	EXO	035	029	Alle men and wymmen offeriden yiftis with deuout soule, that the werkis schulden be maad, whiche the Lord comaundide bi the hond of Moyses; alle the sones of Israel halewiden wilful thingis to the Lord.
002	EXO	035	030	And Moises seide to the sones of Israel, Lo! the Lord hath clepid Beseleel bi name, the sone of Hury, sone of Hur, of the lynage of Juda;
002	EXO	035	031	and the Lord hath fillid hym with the spirit of God, of wisdom, and of vndurstondyng, and of kunnyng, and with al doctryn,
002	EXO	035	032	to fynde out and to make werk in gold, and siluer, and bras, and in stoonys to be grauun,
002	EXO	035	033	and in werk of carpentrie; what euer thing may be foundun craftili,
002	EXO	035	034	the Lord yaf in his herte; and the Lord clepide Ooliab, the sone of Achymasech, of the lynage of Dan;
002	EXO	035	035	the Lord tauyte bothe `with wisdom, that thei make the werkis of carpenter, of steynour, and of broiderere, of iacynt, and purpur, and of `reed selk, and of bijs, and that thei make alle thingis, and fynde alle newe thingis.
002	EXO	036	001	Therfor Beseleel, and Ooliab, and ech wijs man, to whiche the Lord yaf wisdom and vndurstondyng, that thei kouden worche crafteli, maden thingis that weren nedeful in to vsis of seyntuarie, and whiche the Lord comaundide to be maad.
002	EXO	036	002	And whanne Moises hadde clepid hem, and ech lerned man, to whom the Lord hadde youe wisdom and kunnyng, and whiche profriden hem bi her wille to make werk,
002	EXO	036	003	he bitook to hem alle the yiftis of the sones of Israel. And whanne thei weren bisi in the werk ech dai, the puple offride auowis eerli.
002	EXO	036	004	Wherfor the werkmen weren compellid to come,
002	EXO	036	005	and thei seiden to Moises, The puple offrith more than is nedeful.
002	EXO	036	006	Therfor Moises comaundide to be cried bi the vois of a criere, Nether man nether womman offre more ony thing in the werk of seyntuarie; and so it was ceessid fro yiftis to be offrid, for the thingis offrid sufficiden,
002	EXO	036	007	and weren ouer abundant.
002	EXO	036	008	And alle wise men in herte to fille the werk of the tabernacle maden ten curteyns of bijs foldid ayen, and of iacynct, and purpur, and of reed selk twies died, bi dyuerse werk, and bi the craft of many colouris.
002	EXO	036	009	Of whiche curteyns oon hadde in lengthe eiyte and twenti cubitis, and foure cubitis in breede; o mesure was of alle curteyns.
002	EXO	036	010	And he ioynede fyue curteyns oon to anothir, and he couplide othere fyue to hem silf to gidere;
002	EXO	036	011	and he made handlis of iacynt in the hemme of o curteyn on euer either side,
002	EXO	036	012	and in lijk maner in the hemme of the tother curteyn, that the handlis schulen comen to gidere ayens hem silf, and schulen be ioyned togider;
002	EXO	036	013	wherfor he yettide also fifti goldun serclis, that schulen `bite the handlis of curteyns; and o tabernacle was maad.
002	EXO	036	014	`He made also enleuene saies of the heeris of geet, to hile the roof of the tabernacle;
002	EXO	036	015	o saie hadde thretti cubitis in lengthe, foure cubitis in breede; alle the saies weren of o mesure;
002	EXO	036	016	of whiche saies he ioynede fyue bi hem silf, and sixe othere bi hem silf.
002	EXO	036	017	And he made fifti handlis in the hemme of o say, and fifti in the hemme of the tother say, that tho schulden be ioyned to hem silf to gidere; and he made fifti bokelis of bras bi whiche
002	EXO	036	018	the roof was fastned to gidere, that oon hilyng were maad of alle the saies.
002	EXO	036	019	He made also an hilyng of the tabernacle of the skynnes of rammes maad reed, and another veil aboue of skynnes of iacynt.
002	EXO	036	020	He made also stondynge tablis of the tabernacle of the trees of Sechym;
002	EXO	036	021	the lengthe of o table was of ten cubitis, and the breede helde o cubit and an half.
002	EXO	036	022	Twey dentyngis weren bi ech table, that the oon schulde be ioyned to the tother; so he made in al the tablis of the tabernacle.
002	EXO	036	023	Of whiche tablis twenti weren at the mydday coost ayens the south,
002	EXO	036	024	with fourti foundementis of siluer; twey foundementis weren set vndur o table on euer either side of the corneris, where the dentyngis of the sidis weren endid in the corneris.
002	EXO	036	025	And at the coost of the tabernacle that biholdith to the north he made twenti tablis,
002	EXO	036	026	with fourti foundementis of siluer, twei foundementis bi ech table.
002	EXO	036	027	Forsothe ayens the west he made sixe tablis,
002	EXO	036	028	and tweyne othere tablis bi ech corner of the tabernacle bihinde,
002	EXO	036	029	whiche weren ioyned fro bynethe til to aboue, and weren borun in to o ioynyng to gidere; so he made on euer either part bi the corneris,
002	EXO	036	030	that tho weren eiyte tablis to gidere, and hadden sixtene foundementis of siluer, that is, twei foundementis vndur ech table.
002	EXO	036	031	He made also barris of the trees of Sechym, fyue barris to holde to gidere the tablis of o side of the tabernacle,
002	EXO	036	032	and fyue othere barris to schappe to gidere the tablis of the tother side; and without these, he made fyue othere barris at the west coost of the tabernacle ayens the see.
002	EXO	036	033	He made also another barre, that schulde come bi the myddil tables fro corner til to corner.
002	EXO	036	034	Forsothe he ouergildide tho wallis of tablis, and yetide the siluerne foundementis `of tho, and he made the goldun serclis `of tho, bi whiche the barris myyten be brouyt in, and be hilide the same barris with goldun platis.
002	EXO	036	035	He made also a veil dyuerse and departid, of iacynt, and purpur, and reed selk, and bijs foldid ayen bi werk of broiderie.
002	EXO	036	036	He made also foure pileris of `the trees of Sechym, whyche pileris with the heedis he ouergildide, and yetide the siluerne foundementis `of tho.
002	EXO	036	037	He made also in the entryng of the tabernacle a tent of iacynt, and purpur, and reed selk `and bijs foldid ayen bi the werk of a broydreie.
002	EXO	036	038	And he made fyue pileris with her heedis, whiche he hilide with gold, and he yetide the brasun foundementis `of tho, whiche he hilide with gold.
002	EXO	037	001	Forsothe Beseleel made also an arke of the trees of Sechym, hauynge twey cubitis and an half in lengthe, and a cubit and an half in breede; forsothe the hiynesse was of o cubit and an half; and he clothide the arke with purest gold, with ynne and without forth.
002	EXO	037	002	And he made to it a goldun coroun `bi cumpas,
002	EXO	037	003	and yetide foure goldun ryngis, bi foure corneris therof, twey ryngis in o side, and twei ryngis in the tother side.
002	EXO	037	004	And he made barris of the trees of Sechym, whiche barris he clothide with gold,
002	EXO	037	005	and whiche barris he putte into the ryngis that weren in the sidis of the arke, to bere it.
002	EXO	037	006	He made also a propiciatorie, that is, Goddis answeryng place, of pureste gold, of twei cubitis and an half in lengthe, and of o cubit and an half in breede.
002	EXO	037	007	Also he made twei cherubyns of gold, betun out with hamer, whiche he settide on euer eithir side of the propiciatorie,
002	EXO	037	008	o cherub in the hiynesse of o part, and the tother cherub in the hiynesse of the tothir part; twei cherubyns, oon in ech hiynesse of the propiciatorie, stretchynge out the wengis,
002	EXO	037	009	and hilynge the propiciatorie, and biholdynge hem silf togidere and that.
002	EXO	037	010	He made also a boord of `the trees of Sechym, in the lengthe of twey cubitis, and in the breede of o cubit, whiche boord hadde `a cubit and an half in heiythe.
002	EXO	037	011	And he cumpaside the boord with clenneste gold, and made to it a goldun brynke bi cumpas;
002	EXO	037	012	and he made to that brynke a goldun coroun, rasid bitwixe of foure fyngris; and on the same coroun he made anothir goldun coroun.
