# BOOK	003	LEV	Leviticus	Leviticus
003	LEV	001	001	Forsothe the Lord clepide Moyses, and spak to him fro the tabernacle of witnessyng, `and seide,
003	LEV	001	002	Speke thou to the sones of Israel, and thou schalt seie to hem, A man of you, that offrith to the Lord a sacrifice of beestis, that is, of oxun and of scheep, and offrith slayn sacrifices, if his offryng is brent sacrifice,
003	LEV	001	003	and of the droue of oxun, he schal offre a male beeste without wem at the dore of the tabernacle of witnessyng, to make the Lord plesid to hym.
003	LEV	001	004	And he schal sette hondis on the heed of the sacrifice, and it schal be acceptable, and profityng in to clensyng of hym.
003	LEV	001	005	And he schal offre a calf bifor the Lord, and the sones of Aaron, preestis, schulen offre the blood ther of, and thei schulen schede bi the cumpas of the auter, which is bifor the dore of the tabernacle.
003	LEV	001	006	And whanne the skyn of the sacrifice is drawun awei, thei schulen kitte the membris in to gobetis;
003	LEV	001	007	and thei schulen put vndur in the auter fier, and thei schulen make an heep of wode bifore; and thei schulen ordeyne aboue
003	LEV	001	008	`the trees tho thingis that ben kit, that is, the heed, and alle thingis that cleuen to the mawe,
003	LEV	001	009	whanne the entrailis and feet ben waischid with watir; and the preest schal brenne tho on the auter, in to brent sacrifice, and swete odour to the Lord.
003	LEV	001	010	That if the offryng is of litle beestis, a brent sacrifice of scheep, ethir of geet, he schal offre a male beeste with out wem,
003	LEV	001	011	and he schal offre at the side of the auter that biholdith to the north, bifore the Lord. Sotheli the sones of Aaron schulen schede the blood therof on the auter `bi cumpas,
003	LEV	001	012	and thei schulen departe the membris, the heed, and alle thingis that cleuen to the mawe, and thei schulen putte on the trees, vndur whiche the fier schal be set;
003	LEV	001	013	sotheli thei schulen waische in watir the entrailis and feet; and the preest schal brenne alle thingis offrid on the auter, in to brent sacrifice, and swettest odour to the Lord.
