# BOOK	005	DEU	Deuteronomy	Deuteronomy
005	DEU	001	001	These ben the wordis whiche Moyses spak to al Israel ouer Jordan, in the wildirnesse of the feeld, ayens the reed see, bitwix Pharan and Tophel and Laban and Asseroth, where is ful myche gold,
005	DEU	001	002	by enleuene daies fro Oreb bi the weie of the hil of Seir, til to Cades Barne.
005	DEU	001	003	In the fortithe yeer, in the enleuenth monethe, in the firste dai of the monethe, Moises spak to the sones of Israel alle thingis whiche the Lord commandide to hym that he schulde seie to hem,
005	DEU	001	004	after that he smoot Seon, kyng of Ammorreis, that dwellide in Esebon, and Og, the kyng of Basan, that dwelide in Asseroth and in Edray, ouer Jordan, in the lond of Moab.
005	DEU	001	005	And Moyses bigan to declare the lawe, and to seie,
005	DEU	001	006	Oure Lord God spak to vs in Oreb, and seide, It suffisith to you that ye han dwellid in this hil;
005	DEU	001	007	turne ye ayen, and come ye to the hil of Amorreis, and to othere placis that ben next it; to places of feeldis, and of hillis, and to lowere places ayens the south, and bisidis the brenke of the see, to the lond of Cananeys, and of Liban, `til to the greet flood Eufrates.
005	DEU	001	008	Lo, `he seith, Y haue youe to you; entre ye, and `welde ye `that lond on which the Lord swoor to youre fadrys, Abraham, Ysaac, and Jacob, that he schulde yyue it to hem, and to her seed after hem.
005	DEU	001	009	And Y seide to you in that time, Y may not aloone susteyne you, for youre Lord God hath multiplied you,
005	DEU	001	010	and ye ben ful many to dai, as the sterris of heuene;
005	DEU	001	011	the Lord God of youre fadris adde to this noumbre many thousyndis, and blesse you, as he spak.
005	DEU	001	012	Y may not aloone susteyne youre causis, and birthun, and stryues; yyue ye of you men wise `in dyuyn thingis,
005	DEU	001	013	and witti `in mennus thingis worthi to be don, whose conuersacioun is preued in youre lynagis, that Y sette hem princes to you.
005	DEU	001	014	Thanne ye answeriden to me, The thing is good which thou wolt do.
005	DEU	001	015	And Y took of youre lynagis men wise and noble, `in vertues and kyn; and Y ordeynede hem princis, tribunes, and centuryouns, and quynquagenaries, and denys, whiche schulden teche you all thingis.
005	DEU	001	016	And Y comaundide to hem, and seide, Here ye hem, and deme ye that that is iust, whether he be a citeseyn, whether a pilgrym.
005	DEU	001	017	No difference schal be of persones; ye schulen here so a litil man, `that is, pore, as a greet man, nether ye schulen take the persoone of ony man, for it is the doom of God. That if ony thing semeth hard to you, telle ye to me, and Y schal here.
005	DEU	001	018	And Y comaundide alle thingis whiche ye ouyten to do.
005	DEU	001	019	Forsothe we yeden forth fro Oreb, and passiden bi a feerdful deseert, and grettiste wildirnesse, which ye sien, bi the weye of the hil of Ammorrey, as oure Lord God comaundide to vs. And whanne we hadden come in to Cades Barne,
005	DEU	001	020	Y seide to you, Ye ben comen to the hil of Ammorrey, which youre Lord God schal yyue to you;
005	DEU	001	021	se thou the lond which thi Lord God schal yyue to thee; `stie thou, and welde it, as oure Lord God spak to thi fadris; `nyle thou drede, nether `drede thou in herte ony thing.
005	DEU	001	022	And alle ye neiyiden to me, and ye seiden, Sende we men, that schulen biholde the lond, and telle to vs bi what weye we owen stie, and to whiche citees we owen to go.
