# BOOK	012	2KI	2 Kings	2 Kings
012	2KI	001	001	Forsothe Moab trespasside ayens Israel, after that Achab was deed.
012	2KI	001	002	And Ocozie felde thorou the aleris of his soler, which he hadde in Samarie, and was sijk; and he sente messangeris, and seide to hem, Go ye, and councele Belzebub, god of Acharon, whether Y may lyue after this sijknesse of me.
012	2KI	001	003	Forsothe the aungel of the Lord spak to Elye of Thesbi, and seide, Rise thou, and go doun into the metynge of the messangeris of the kyng of Samarie; and thou schalt seie to hem, Whether God is not in Israel, that ye go to counsel Belzebub, god of Acharon?
012	2KI	001	004	For which thing the Lord seith these thingis, Thou schalt not go doun of the bed, on which thou stiedist.
