018	JOB	003	001	Aftir these thingis Joob openyde his mouth,
018	JOB	003	002	and curside his dai, and seide, Perische the dai in which Y was borun,
018	JOB	003	003	and the nyyt in which it was seid, The man is conceyued.
018	JOB	003	004	Thilke dai be turnede in to derknessis; God seke not it aboue, and be it not in mynde, nethir be it liytned with liyt.
018	JOB	003	005	Derknessis make it derk, and the schadewe of deeth and myist occupie it; and be it wlappid with bittirnesse.
018	JOB	003	006	Derk whirlwynde holde that niyt; be it not rikynyd among the daies of the yeer, nethir be it noumbrid among the monethes.
018	JOB	003	007	Thilke nyyt be soleyn, and not worthi of preisyng.
018	JOB	003	008	Curse thei it, that cursen the dai, that ben redi to reise Leuyathan.
018	JOB	003	009	Sterris be maad derk with the derknesse therof; abide it liyt, and se it not, nethir the bigynnyng of the morwetid risyng vp.
018	JOB	003	010	For it closide not the doris of the wombe, that bar me, nethir took awei yuels fro min iyen.
018	JOB	003	011	Whi was not Y deed in the wombe? whi yede Y out of the wombe, and perischide not anoon?
018	JOB	003	012	Whi was Y takun on knees? whi was Y suclid with teetis?
018	JOB	003	013	For now Y slepynge schulde be stille, and schulde reste in my sleep,
018	JOB	003	014	with kyngis, and consuls of erthe, that bilden to hem soleyn places;
018	JOB	003	015	ethir with prynces that han gold in possessioun, and fillen her housis with siluer;
018	JOB	003	016	ethir as a `thing hid not borun Y schulde not stonde, ethir whiche conseyued sien not liyt.
018	JOB	003	017	There wickid men ceessiden of noise, and there men maad wery of strengthe restiden.
018	JOB	003	018	And sum tyme boundun togidere with out disese thei herden not the voys of the wrongful axere.
018	JOB	003	019	A litil man and greet man be there, and a seruaunt free fro his lord.
018	JOB	003	020	Whi is liyt youun to the wretche, and lijf to hem that ben in bitternesse of soule?
018	JOB	003	021	Whiche abiden deeth, and it cometh not;
018	JOB	003	022	as men diggynge out tresour and ioien greetly, whanne thei han founde a sepulcre?
018	JOB	003	023	Whi is liyt youun to a man, whos weie is hid, and God hath cumpassid hym with derknessis?
018	JOB	003	024	Bifore that Y ete, Y siyhe; and as of watir flowynge, so is my roryng.
018	JOB	003	025	For the drede, which Y dredde, cam to me; and that, that Y schamede, bifelde.
018	JOB	003	026	Whether Y dissymilide not? whether Y was not stille? whether Y restide not? and indignacioun cometh on me.
018	JOB	004	001	Forsothe Eliphat Themanytes answeride, and seide,
018	JOB	004	002	If we bigynnen to speke to thee, in hap thou schalt take it heuyli; but who may holde a word conseyued?
018	JOB	004	003	Lo! thou hast tauyt ful many men, and thou hast strengthid hondis maad feynt.
018	JOB	004	004	Thi wordis confermyden men doutynge, and thou coumfortidist knees tremblynge.
018	JOB	004	005	But now a wounde is comun on thee, and thou hast failid; it touchide thee, and thou art disturblid.
018	JOB	004	006	Where is thi drede, thi strengthe, and thi pacience, and the perfeccioun of thi weies?
018	JOB	004	007	Y biseche thee, haue thou mynde, what innocent man perischide euere, ethir whanne riytful men weren doon awei?
018	JOB	004	008	Certis rathir Y siy hem, that worchen wickidnesse, and sowen sorewis,
018	JOB	004	009	and repen tho, to haue perischid bi God blowynge, and to be wastid bi the spirit of his ire.
018	JOB	004	010	The roryng of a lioun, and the vois of a lionesse, and the teeth of `whelpis of liouns ben al to-brokun.
018	JOB	004	011	Tigris perischide, for sche hadde not prey; and the whelpis of a lioun ben distried.
018	JOB	004	012	Certis an hid word was seid to me, and myn eere took as theueli the veynes of priuy noise therof.
018	JOB	004	013	In the hidousnesse of `nyytis siyt, whanne heuy sleep is wont to occupie men,
018	JOB	004	014	drede and tremblyng helde me; and alle my boonys weren aferd.
018	JOB	004	015	And whanne the spirit `yede in my presence, the heiris of `my fleisch hadden hidousnesse.
018	JOB	004	016	Oon stood, whos chere Y knewe not, an ymage bifor myn iyen; and Y herde a vois as of softe wynd.
018	JOB	004	017	Whether a man schal be maad iust in comparisoun of God? ethir whethir a man schal be clennere than his Makere?
018	JOB	004	018	Lo! thei that seruen hym ben not stidefast; and he findith schrewidnesse in hise aungels.
018	JOB	004	019	Hou myche more thei that dwellen in housis of cley, that han an ertheli foundement, schulen be wastyd as of a mouyte.
018	JOB	004	020	Fro morewtid til to euentid thei schulen be kit doun; and for no man vndurstondith, thei schulen perische with outen ende.
018	JOB	004	021	Sotheli thei, that ben residue, schulen be takun awei; thei schulen die, and not in wisdom.
018	JOB	005	001	Therfor clepe thou, if `ony is that schal answere thee, and turne thou to summe of seyntis.
018	JOB	005	002	Wrathfulnesse sleeth `a fonned man, and enuye sleeth a litil child.
018	JOB	005	003	Y siy a fool with stidefast rote, and Y curside his feirnesse anoon.
018	JOB	005	004	Hise sones schulen be maad fer fro helthe, and thei schulen be defoulid in the yate, and `noon schal be that schal delyuere hem.
018	JOB	005	005	Whos ripe corn an hungri man schal ete, and an armed man schal rauysche hym, and thei, that thirsten, schulen drynke hise richessis.
018	JOB	005	006	No thing is doon in erthe with out cause, and sorewe schal not go out of the erthe.
018	JOB	005	007	A man is borun to labour, and a brid to fliyt.
018	JOB	005	008	Wherfor Y schal biseche the Lord, and Y schal sette my speche to my God.
018	JOB	005	009	That makith grete thingis, and that moun not be souyt out, and wondurful thingis with out noumbre.
018	JOB	005	010	Which yyueth reyn on the face of erthe, and moistith alle thingis with watris.
018	JOB	005	011	Which settith meke men an hiy, and reisith with helthe hem that morenen.
018	JOB	005	012	Which distrieth the thouytis of yuel willid men, that her hondis moun not fille tho thingis that thei bigunnen.
018	JOB	005	013	Which takith cautelouse men in the felnesse `of hem, and distrieth the counsel of schrewis.
018	JOB	005	014	Bi dai thei schulen renne in to derknessis, and as in nyyt so thei schulen grope in myddai.
018	JOB	005	015	Certis God schal make saaf a nedi man fro the swerd of her mouth, and a pore man fro the hond of the violent, `ethir rauynour.
018	JOB	005	016	And hope schal be to a nedi man, but wickidnesse schal drawe togidere his mouth.
018	JOB	005	017	Blessid is the man, which is chastisid of the Lord; therfor repreue thou not the blamyng of the Lord.
018	JOB	005	018	For he woundith, and doith medicyn; he smytith, and hise hondis schulen make hool.
018	JOB	005	019	In sixe tribulaciouns he schal delyuere thee, and in the seuenthe tribulacioun yuel schal not touche thee.
018	JOB	005	020	In hungur he schal delyuere thee fro deeth, and in batel fro the power of swerd.
018	JOB	005	021	Thou schalt be hid fro the scourge of tunge, and thou schalt not drede myseiste, `ethir wretchidnesse, whanne it cometh.
018	JOB	005	022	In distriyng maad of enemyes and in hungur thou schalt leiye, and thou schalt not drede the beestis of erthe.
018	JOB	005	023	But thi couenaunt schal be with the stonys of erthe, and beestis of erthe schulen be pesible to thee.
018	JOB	005	024	And thou schalt wite, that thi tabernacle hath pees, and thou visitynge thi fairnesse schalt not do synne.
018	JOB	005	025	And thou schalt wite also, that thi seed schal be many fold, and thi generacioun schal be as an erbe of erthe.
018	JOB	005	026	In abundaunce thou schalt go in to the sepulcre, as an heep of wheete is borun in his tyme.
018	JOB	005	027	Lo! this is so, as we han souyt; which thing herd, trete thou in minde.
018	JOB	006	001	Forsothe Joob answeride, and seide,
018	JOB	006	002	Y wolde, that my synnes, bi whiche Y `desseruede ire, and the wretchidnesse which Y suffre, weren peisid in a balaunce.
018	JOB	006	003	As the grauel of the see, this wretchidnesse schulde appere greuousere; wherfor and my wordis ben ful of sorewe.
018	JOB	006	004	For the arowis of the Lord ben in me, the indignacioun of whiche drynkith vp my spirit; and the dredis of the Lord fiyten ayens me.
018	JOB	006	005	Whether a feeld asse schal rore, whanne he hath gras? Ethir whether an oxe schal lowe, whanne he stondith byfor a `ful cratche?
018	JOB	006	006	Ether whethir a thing vnsauery may be etun, which is not maad sauery bi salt? Ether whether ony man may taaste a thing, which tastid bryngith deeth?
018	JOB	006	007	For whi to an hungri soule, yhe, bittir thingis semen to be swete; tho thingis whiche my soule nolde touche bifore, ben now my meetis for angwisch.
018	JOB	006	008	Who yyueth, that myn axyng come; and that God yyue to me that, that Y abide?
018	JOB	006	009	And he that bigan, al to-breke me; releesse he his hond, and kitte me doun?
018	JOB	006	010	And `this be coumfort to me, that he turmente me with sorewe, and spare not, and that Y ayenseie not the wordis of the hooli.
018	JOB	006	011	For whi, what is my strengthe, that Y suffre? ethir which is myn ende, that Y do pacientli?
018	JOB	006	012	Nethir my strengthe is the strengthe of stoonus, nether my fleisch is of bras.
018	JOB	006	013	Lo! noon help is to me in me; also my meyneal frendis `yeden awey fro me.
018	JOB	006	014	He that takith awei merci fro his frend, forsakith the drede of the Lord.
018	JOB	006	015	My britheren passiden me, as a stronde doith, that passith ruschyngli in grete valeis.
018	JOB	006	016	Snow schal come on hem, that dreden frost.
018	JOB	006	017	In the tyme wherynne thei ben scaterid, thei schulen perische; and as thei ben hoote, thei schulen be vnknyt fro her place.
018	JOB	006	018	The pathis of her steppis ben wlappid; thei schulen go in veyn, and schulen perische.
018	JOB	006	019	Biholde ye the pathis of Theman, and the weies of Saba; and abide ye a litil.
018	JOB	006	020	Thei ben schent, for Y hopide; and thei camen `til to me, and thei ben hilid with schame.
018	JOB	006	021	Now ye ben comun, and now ye seen my wounde, and dreden.
018	JOB	006	022	Whether Y seide, Brynge ye to me, and yiue ye of youre catel to me? ethir,
018	JOB	006	023	Delyuere ye me fro the hond of enemy, and rauysche ye me fro the hond of stronge men?
018	JOB	006	024	Teche ye me, and Y schal be stille; and if in hap Y vnknew ony thing, teche ye me.
018	JOB	006	025	Whi han ye depraued the wordis of trewthe? sithen noon is of you, that may repreue me.
018	JOB	006	026	Ye maken redi spechis oneli for to blame, and ye bryngen forth wordis in to wynde.
018	JOB	006	027	Ye fallen in on a fadirles child, and enforsen to peruerte youre frend.
018	JOB	006	028	Netheles fille ye that, that ye han bigunne; yyue ye the eere, and se ye, whether Y lie.
018	JOB	006	029	Y biseche, answere ye with out strijf, and speke ye, and deme ye that, that is iust.
018	JOB	006	030	And ye schulen not fynde wickidnesse in my tunge, nethir foli schal sowne in my chekis.
018	JOB	007	001	Knyythod is lijf of man on erthe, and his daies ben as the daies of an hired man.
018	JOB	007	002	As an hert desireth schadowe, and as an hirede man abideth the ende of his werk;
018	JOB	007	003	so and Y hadde voide monethis, and Y noumbrede trauailous niytes to me.
018	JOB	007	004	If Y schal slepe, Y schal seie, Whanne schal Y rise? and eft Y schal abide the euentid, and Y schal be fillid with sorewis `til to derknessis.
018	JOB	007	005	Mi fleisch is clothid with rot, and filthis of dust; my skyn driede vp, and is drawun togidere.
018	JOB	007	006	My daies passiden swiftliere thanne a web is kit doun `of a webstere; and tho daies ben wastid with outen ony hope.
018	JOB	007	007	God, haue thou mynde, for my lijf is wynde, and myn iye schal not turne ayen, that it se goodis.
018	JOB	007	008	Nethir the siyt of man schal biholde me; but thin iyen ben in me, and Y schal not `be in deedli lijf.
018	JOB	007	009	As a cloude is wastid, and passith, so he that goith doun to helle, schal not stie;
018	JOB	007	010	nether schal turne ayen more in to his hows, and his place schal no more knowe hym.
018	JOB	007	011	Wherfor and Y schal not spare my mouth; Y schal speke in the tribulacioun of my spirit, Y schal talke togidere with the bitternesse of my soule.
018	JOB	007	012	Whether Y am the see, ethir a whal, for thou hast cumpassid me with prisoun?
018	JOB	007	013	If Y seie, My bed schal coumfort me, and Y schal be releeuyd, spekynge with me in my bed;
018	JOB	007	014	thou schalt make me aferd bi dremys, and thou schalt schake me with `orrour, ethir hidousnesse, `bi siytis.
018	JOB	007	015	Wherfor my soule `chees hangyng, and my boonys cheesiden deth.
018	JOB	007	016	`Y dispeiride, now Y schal no more lyue; Lord, spare thou me, for my daies ben nouyt.
018	JOB	007	017	What is a man, for thou `magnifiest hym? ether what settist thou thin herte toward hym?
018	JOB	007	018	Thou visitist hym eerly, and sudeynli thou preuest hym.
018	JOB	007	019	Hou long sparist thou not me, nether suffrist me, that Y swolowe my spotele?
018	JOB	007	020	Y haue synned; A! thou kepere of men, what schal Y do to thee? Whi hast thou set me contrarie to thee, and Y am maad greuouse to my silf?
018	JOB	007	021	Whi doist thou not awei my sinne, and whi takist thou not awei my wickidnesse? Lo! now Y schal slepe in dust, and if thou sekist me eerli, Y schal not abide.
018	JOB	008	001	Sotheli Baldath Suytes answeride, and seide,
018	JOB	008	002	Hou longe schalt thou speke siche thingis? The spirit of the word of thi mouth is manyfold.
018	JOB	008	003	Whether God supplauntith, `ethir disseyueth, doom, and whether Almyyti God distrieth that, that is iust?
018	JOB	008	004	Yhe, thouy thi sones synneden ayens hym, and he lefte hem in the hond of her wickidnesse;
018	JOB	008	005	netheles, if thou risist eerli to God, and bisechist `Almyyti God, if thou goist clene and riytful,
018	JOB	008	006	anoon he schal wake fulli to thee, and schal make pesible the dwellyng place of thi ryytfulnesse;
018	JOB	008	007	in so miche that thi formere thingis weren litil, and that thi laste thingis be multiplied greetli.
018	JOB	008	008	For whi, axe thou the formere generacioun, and seke thou diligentli the mynde of fadris.
018	JOB	008	009	For we ben men of yistirdai, and `kunnen not; for oure daies ben as schadewe on the erthe.
018	JOB	008	010	And thei schulen teche thee, thei schulen speke to thee, and of her herte thei schulen bring forth spechis.
018	JOB	008	011	Whether a rusche may lyue with out moysture? ethir a spier `may wexe with out watir?
018	JOB	008	012	Whanne it is yit in the flour, nethir is takun with hond, it wexeth drie bifor alle erbis.
018	JOB	008	013	So the weies of alle men, that foryeten God; and the hope of an ypocrite schal perische.
018	JOB	008	014	His cowardise schal not plese hym, and his trist schal be as a web of yreyns.
018	JOB	008	015	He schal leene, `ether reste, on his hows, and it schal not stonde; he schal vndursette it, and it schal not rise togidere.
018	JOB	008	016	The rusche semeth moist, bifor that the sunne come; and in the risyng of the sunne the seed therof schal go out.
018	JOB	008	017	Rootis therof schulen be maad thicke on an heep of stoonys, and it schal dwelle among stoonys.
018	JOB	008	018	If a man drawith it out of `his place, his place schal denye it, and schal seie, Y knowe thee not.
018	JOB	008	019	For this is the gladnesse of his weie, that eft othere ruschis springe out of the erthe.
018	JOB	008	020	Forsothe God schal not caste a wei a symple man, nethir schal dresse hond to wickid men;
018	JOB	008	021	til thi mouth be fillid with leiytir, and thi lippis with hertli song.
018	JOB	008	022	Thei that haten thee schulen be clothid with schenschip; and the tabernacle of wickid men schal not stonde.
018	JOB	009	001	Joob answeride, and seide, Verili Y woot, that it is so,
018	JOB	009	002	and that a man comparisound to God schal not be maad iust.
018	JOB	009	003	If he wole stryue with God, he may not answere to God oon for a thousynde.
018	JOB	009	004	He is wiys in herte, and strong in myyt; who ayenstood hym, and hadde pees?
018	JOB	009	005	Which bar hillis fro o place to anothir, and thei wisten not; whiche he distriede in his strong veniaunce.
018	JOB	009	006	Which stirith the erthe fro his place, and the pilers therof schulen `be schakun togidere.
018	JOB	009	007	Which comaundith to the sunne, and it risith not; and he closith the sterris, as vndur a signet.
018	JOB	009	008	Which aloone stretchith forth heuenes, and goith on the wawis of the see.
018	JOB	009	009	Which makith Ariture, and Orionas, and Hiadas, `that is, seuene sterris, and the innere thingis of the south.
018	JOB	009	010	Which makith grete thingis, and that moun not be souyt out, and wondurful thingis, of whiche is noon noumbre.
018	JOB	009	011	If he cometh to me, `that is, bi his grace, Y schal not se hym; if he goith awey, `that is, in withdrawynge his grace, Y schal not vndurstonde.
018	JOB	009	012	If he axith sodeynli, who schal answere to hym? ethir who may seie to hym, Whi doist thou so?
018	JOB	009	013	`God is he, whos wraththe no man may withstonde; and vndur whom thei ben bowid, that beren the world.
018	JOB	009	014	Hou greet am Y, that Y answere to hym, and speke bi my wordis with hym?
018	JOB	009	015	Which also schal not answere, thouy Y haue ony thing iust; but Y schal biseche my iuge.
018	JOB	009	016	And whanne he hath herd me inwardli clepynge, Y bileue not, that he hath herd my vois.
018	JOB	009	017	For in a whirlewynd he schal al to-breke me, and he schal multiplie my woundis, yhe, without cause.
018	JOB	009	018	He grauntith not, that my spirit haue reste, and he fillith me with bittirnesses.
018	JOB	009	019	If strengthe is souyt, `he is moost strong; if equyte of doom is souyt, no man dar yelde witnessynge for me.
018	JOB	009	020	If Y wole make me iust, my mouth schal dampne me; if Y schal schewe me innocent, he schal preue me a schrewe.
018	JOB	009	021	Yhe, thouy Y am symple, my soule schal not knowe this same thing; and it schal anoye me of my lijf.
018	JOB	009	022	O thing is, which Y spak, he schal waste `bi deth also the innocent and wickid man.
018	JOB	009	023	If he betith, sle he onys, and leiye he not of the peynes of innocent men.
018	JOB	009	024	The erthe is youun in to the hondis of the wickid; he hilith the face of iugis; that if he is not, who therfor is?
018	JOB	009	025	Mi daies weren swiftere than a corour; thei fledden, and sien not good.
018	JOB	009	026	Thei passiden as schippis berynge applis, as an egle fleynge to mete.
018	JOB	009	027	Whanne Y seie, Y schal not speke so; Y chaunge my face, and Y am turmentid with sorewe.
018	JOB	009	028	Y drede alle my werkis, witynge that thou `woldist not spare the trespassour.
018	JOB	009	029	Sotheli if Y am also thus wickid, whi haue Y trauelid in veyn?
018	JOB	009	030	Thouy Y am waischun as with watris of snow, and thouy myn hondis schynen as moost cleene,
018	JOB	009	031	netheles thou schalt dippe me in filthis, and my clothis, `that is, werkis, schulen holde me abhomynable.
018	JOB	009	032	Trewli Y schal not answere a man, which is lijk me; nether that may be herd euenli with me in doom.
018	JOB	009	033	`Noon is, that may repreue euer eithir, and sette his hond in bothe.
018	JOB	009	034	Do he awei his yerde fro me, and his drede make not me aferd.
018	JOB	009	035	Y schal speke, and Y schal not drede hym; for Y may not answere dredynge.
018	JOB	010	001	Yt anoieth my soule of my lijf; Y schal lete my speche ayens me, Y schal speke in the bitternesse of my soule.
018	JOB	010	002	Y schal seie to God, Nyle thou condempne me; schewe thou to me, whi thou demest me so.
018	JOB	010	003	Whether it semeth good to thee, if thou `falsli chalengist and oppressist me, the werk of thin hondis; and if thou helpist the counsel of wickid men?
018	JOB	010	004	Whethir fleischli iyen ben to thee, ethir, as a man seeth, also thou schalt se?
018	JOB	010	005	Whether thi daies ben as the daies of man, and `thi yeeris ben as mannus tymes;
018	JOB	010	006	that thou enquere my wickidnesse, and enserche my synne?
018	JOB	010	007	And wite, that Y haue do no `wickid thing; sithen no man is, that may delyuere fro thin hond?
018	JOB	010	008	Thin hondis han maad me, and han formed me al in cumpas; and thou castist me doun so sodeynli.
018	JOB	010	009	Y preye, haue thou mynde, that thou madist me as cley, and schalt brynge me ayen in to dust.
018	JOB	010	010	Whether thou hast not mylkid me as mylk, and hast cruddid me togidere as cheese?
018	JOB	010	011	Thou clothidist me with skyn and fleisch; thou hast ioyned me togidere with boonys and senewis.
