018	JOB	040	021	He slepith vndur schadewe, in the pryuete of rehed, in moiste places.
018	JOB	040	022	Schadewis hilen his schadewe; the salewis of the ryuer cumpassen hym.
018	JOB	040	023	He schal soupe vp the flood, and he schal not wondre; he hath trist, that Jordan schal flowe in to his mouth.
018	JOB	040	024	He schal take hem bi `the iyen of hym, as bi an hook; and bi scharpe schaftis he schal perse hise nosethirlis.
018	JOB	041	001	Whether thou schalt mowe drawe out leuyathan with an hook, and schalt bynde with a roop his tunge?
018	JOB	041	002	Whethir thou schalt putte a ryng in hise nosethirlis, ethir schalt perse hyse cheke with `an hook?
018	JOB	041	003	Whether he schal multiplie preieris to thee, ether schal speke softe thingis to thee?
018	JOB	041	004	Whether he schal make couenaunt with thee, and `thou schalt take him a seruaunt euerlastinge?
018	JOB	041	005	Whether thou schalt scorne hym as a brid, ethir schalt bynde hym to thin handmaidis?
018	JOB	041	006	Schulen frendis `kerue hym, schulen marchauntis departe hym?
018	JOB	041	007	Whether thou schalt fille nettis with his skyn, and a `leep of fischis with his heed?
018	JOB	041	008	Schalt thou putte thin hond on hym? haue thou mynde of the batel, and adde no more to speke.
018	JOB	041	009	Lo! his hope schal disseyue hym; and in the siyt of alle men he schal be cast doun.
018	JOB	041	010	I not as cruel schal reise hym; for who may ayenstonde my face?
018	JOB	041	011	And who `yaf to me bifore, that Y yelde to hym? Alle thingis, that ben vndur heuene, ben myne.
018	JOB	041	012	Y schal not spare hym for myyti wordis, and maad faire to biseche.
018	JOB	041	013	Who schal schewe the face of his clothing, and who schal entre in to the myddis of his mouth?
018	JOB	041	014	Who schal opene the yatis of his cheer? ferdfulnesse is bi the cumpas of hise teeth.
018	JOB	041	015	His bodi is as yotun scheldys of bras, and ioyned togidere with scalis ouerleiynge hem silf.
018	JOB	041	016	Oon is ioyned to another; and sotheli brething goith not thorouy tho.
018	JOB	041	017	Oon schal cleue to anothir, and tho holdynge hem silf schulen not be departid.
018	JOB	041	018	His fnesynge is as schynynge of fier, and hise iyen ben as iyelidis of the morewtid.
018	JOB	041	019	Laumpis comen forth of his mouth, as trees of fier, that ben kyndlid.
018	JOB	041	020	Smoke cometh forth of hise nosethirlis, as of a pot set on the fier `and boilynge.
018	JOB	041	021	His breeth makith colis to brenne, and flawme goith out of his mouth.
018	JOB	041	022	Strengthe schal dwelle in his necke, and nedynesse schal go bifor his face.
018	JOB	041	023	The membris of hise fleischis ben cleuynge togidere to hem silf; God schal sende floodis ayens hym, and tho schulen not be borun to an other place.
018	JOB	041	024	His herte schal be maad hard as a stoon; and it schal be streyned togidere as the anefeld of a smith.
018	JOB	041	025	Whanne he schal be takun awei, aungels schulen drede; and thei aferd schulen be purgid.
018	JOB	041	026	Whanne swerd takith hym, it may not stonde, nethir spere, nether haburioun.
018	JOB	041	027	For he schal arette irun as chaffis, and bras as rotun tre.
018	JOB	041	028	A man archere schal not dryue hym awei; stoonys of a slynge ben turned in to stobil to hym.
018	JOB	041	029	He schal arette an hamer as stobil; and he schal scorne a florischynge spere.
018	JOB	041	030	The beemys of the sunne schulen be vndur hym; and he schal strewe to hym silf gold as cley.
018	JOB	041	031	He schal make the depe se to buyle as a pot; and he schal putte, as whanne oynementis buylen.
018	JOB	041	032	A path schal schyne aftir hym; he schal gesse the greet occian as wexynge eld.
018	JOB	041	033	No power is on erthe, that schal be comparisound to hym; which is maad, that he schulde drede noon.
018	JOB	041	034	He seeth al hiy thing; he is kyng ouer alle the sones of pride.
018	JOB	042	001	Forsothe Joob answeride to the Lord, and seide,
018	JOB	042	002	Y woot, that thou maist alle thingis, and no thouyt is hid fro thee.
018	JOB	042	003	Who is this, that helith counsel with out kunnyng? Therfor Y spak vnwiseli, and tho thingis that passiden ouer mesure my kunnyng.
018	JOB	042	004	Here thou, and Y schal speke; Y schal axe thee, and answere thou to me.
018	JOB	042	005	Bi heryng of eere Y herde thee, but now myn iye seeth thee.
018	JOB	042	006	Therfor Y repreue me, and do penaunce in deed sparcle and aische.
018	JOB	042	007	Forsothe aftir that the Lord spak these wordis to Joob, he seide to Eliphat Themanytes, My stronge veniaunce is wrooth ayens thee, and ayens thi twey frendis; for ye `spaken not bifor me riytful thing, as my seruaunt Joob dide.
018	JOB	042	008	Therfor take ye to you seuene bolis, and seuene rammes; and go ye to my seruaunt Joob, and offre ye brent sacrifice for you. Forsothe Joob, my seruaunt, schal preie for you; Y schal resseyue his face, that foli be not arettid to you; for ye `spaken not bifor me riytful thing, as my seruaunt Joob dide.
018	JOB	042	009	Therfor Eliphat Themanytes, and Baldach Suythes, and Sophar Naamathites, yeden, and diden, as the Lord hedde spoke to hem; and the Lord resseyuede the face of Joob.
018	JOB	042	010	Also the Lord was conuertid to the penaunce of Joob, whanne he preiede for hise frendis. And the Lord addide alle thingis double, whiche euere weren of Joob.
018	JOB	042	011	Sotheli alle hise britheren, and alle hise sistris, and alle that knewen hym bifore, camen to hym; and thei eeten breed with hym in his hows, and moueden the heed on hym; and thei coumfortiden hym of al the yuel, which the Lord hadde brouyt in on hym; and thei yauen to hym ech man o scheep, and o goldun eere ring.
018	JOB	042	012	Forsothe the Lord blesside the laste thingis of Joob, more than the bigynnyng of hym; and fouretene thousynde of scheep weren maad to hym, and sixe thousinde of camels, and a thousynde yockis of oxis, and a thousynde femal assis.
018	JOB	042	013	And he hadde seuene sones, and thre douytris;
018	JOB	042	014	and he clepide the name of o douytir Dai, and the name of the secounde douytir Cassia, and the name of the thridde douytir `An horn of wymmens oynement.
018	JOB	042	015	`Sotheli no wymmen weren foundun so faire in al erthe, as the douytris of Joob; and her fadir yaf eritage to hem among her britheren.
018	JOB	042	016	Forsothe Joob lyuede aftir these betyngis an hundrid and fourti yeer, and `siy hise sones, and the sones of hise sones, `til to the fourthe generacioun;
018	JOB	042	017	and he was deed eld, and ful of daies.
