# BOOK	019	PSA	Psalms	Psalms
019	PSA	001	001	Blessid is the man, that yede not in the councel of wickid men; and stood not in the weie of synneris, and sat not in the chaier of pestilence.
019	PSA	001	002	But his wille is in the lawe of the Lord; and he schal bithenke in the lawe of hym dai and nyyt.
019	PSA	001	003	And he schal be as a tree, which is plauntid bisidis the rennyngis of watris; which tre schal yyue his fruyt in his tyme. And his leef schal not falle doun; and alle thingis which euere he schal do schulen haue prosperite.
019	PSA	001	004	Not so wickid men, not so; but thei ben as dust, which the wynd castith awei fro the face of erthe.
019	PSA	001	005	Therfor wickid men risen not ayen in doom; nethir synneres in the councel of iust men.
019	PSA	001	006	For the Lord knowith the weie of iust men; and the weie of wickid men schal perische.
019	PSA	002	001	Whi gnastiden with teeth hethene men; and puplis thouyten veyn thingis?
019	PSA	002	002	The kyngis of erthe stoden togidere; and princes camen togidere ayens the Lord, and ayens his Crist?
019	PSA	002	003	Breke we the bondis of hem; and cast we awei the yok of hem fro vs.
019	PSA	002	004	He that dwellith in heuenes schal scorne hem; and the Lord schal bimowe hem.
019	PSA	002	005	Thanne he schal speke to hem in his ire; and he schal disturble hem in his stronge veniaunce.
019	PSA	002	006	Forsothe Y am maad of hym a kyng on Syon, his hooli hil; prechynge his comaundement.
019	PSA	002	007	The Lord seide to me, Thou art my sone; Y haue gendrid thee to dai.
019	PSA	002	008	Axe thou of me, and Y schal yyue to thee hethene men thin eritage; and thi possessioun the termes of erthe.
019	PSA	002	009	Thou schalt gouerne hem in an yrun yerde; and thou schalt breke hem as the vessel of a pottere.
019	PSA	002	010	And now, ye kyngis, vndurstonde; ye that demen the erthe, be lerud.
019	PSA	002	011	Serue ye the Lord with drede; and make ye ful ioye to hym with tremblyng.
019	PSA	002	012	Take ye lore; lest the Lord be wrooth sumtyme, and lest ye perischen fro iust waie. Whanne his `ire brenneth out in schort tyme; blessed ben alle thei, that tristen in hym.
019	PSA	003	001	`The salm of Dauid, whanne he fledde fro the face of Absolon, his sone. Lord, whi ben thei multiplied that disturblen me?
019	PSA	003	002	many men rysen ayens me. Many men seien of my soule, Noon helthe is to hym in his God.
019	PSA	003	003	But thou, Lord, art myn vptakere; my glorye, and enhaunsyng myn heed.
019	PSA	003	004	With my vois Y criede to the Lord; and he herde me fro his hooli hil.
019	PSA	003	005	I slepte, and `was quenchid, and Y roos vp; for the Lord resseyuede me.
019	PSA	003	006	I schal not drede thousyndis of puple cumpassynge me; Lord, rise thou vp; my God, make thou me saaf.
019	PSA	003	007	For thou hast smyte alle men beynge aduersaries to me with out cause; thou hast al to-broke the teeth of synneris.
019	PSA	003	008	Helthe is of the Lord; and thi blessyng, Lord, is on thi puple.
019	PSA	004	001	`To the victorie in orguns; the salm of Dauid. Whanne Y inwardli clepid, God of my riytwisnesse herde me; in tribulacioun thou hast alargid to me.
019	PSA	004	002	Haue thou mercy on me; and here thou my preier. Sones of men, hou long ben ye of heuy herte? whi louen ye vanite, and seken a leesyng?
019	PSA	004	003	And wite ye, that the Lord hath maad merueilous his hooli man; the Lord schal here me, whanne Y schal crye to hym.
019	PSA	004	004	Be ye wrothe, and nyle ye do synne; `and for tho thingis whiche ye seien in youre hertis and in youre beddis, be ye compunct.
019	PSA	004	005	Sacrifie ye `the sacrifice of riytfulnesse, and hope ye in the Lord; many seien, Who schewide goodis to vs?
019	PSA	004	006	Lord, the liyt of thi cheer is markid on vs; thou hast youe gladnesse in myn herte.
019	PSA	004	007	Thei ben multiplied of the fruit of whete, and of wyn; and of her oile.
019	PSA	004	008	In pees in the same thing; Y schal slepe, and take reste. For thou, Lord; hast set me syngulerli in hope.
019	PSA	005	001	To the ouercomere on the eritagis, the song of Dauid. Lord, perseyue thou my wordis with eeris; vndurstonde thou my cry.
019	PSA	005	002	Mi kyng, and my God; yyue thou tent to the vois of my preier.
019	PSA	005	003	For, Lord, Y schal preie to thee; here thou eerly my vois.
019	PSA	005	004	Eerli Y schal stonde nyy thee, and Y schal se; for thou art God not willynge wickidnesse.
019	PSA	005	005	Nethir an yuel willid man schal dwelle bisidis thee; nethir vniust men schulen dwelle bifor thin iyen.
019	PSA	005	006	Thou hatist alle that worchen wickidnesse; thou schalt leese alle that speken leesyng. The Lord schal holde abhomynable a manquellere, and gileful man.
019	PSA	005	007	But, Lord, in the multitude of thi merci Y schal entre in to thin hows; Y schal worschipe to thin hooli temple in thi drede.
019	PSA	005	008	Lord, lede thou forth me in thi riytfulnesse for myn enemyes; dresse thou my weie in thi siyt.
019	PSA	005	009	For whi treuthe is not in her mouth; her herte is veyn.
019	PSA	005	010	Her throte is an opyn sepulcre, thei diden gilefuli with her tungis; God, deme thou hem. Falle thei doun fro her thouytis, vp the multitude of her wickidnessis caste thou hem doun; for, Lord, thei han terrid thee to ire.
019	PSA	005	011	And alle that hopen in thee, be glad; thei schulen make fulli ioye with outen ende, and thou schalt dwelle in hem. And alle that louen thi name schulen haue glorie in thee;
019	PSA	005	012	for thou schalt blesse a iust man. Lord, thou hast corouned vs, as with the scheeld of thi good wille.
019	PSA	006	001	To the ouercomere in salmes, the salm of Dauid, `on the eiythe. Lord, repreue thou not me in thi stronge veniaunce; nether chastice thou me in thin ire.
019	PSA	006	002	Lord, haue thou merci on me, for Y am sijk; Lord, make thou me hool, for alle my boonys ben troblid.
019	PSA	006	003	And my soule is troblid greetli; but thou, Lord, hou long?
019	PSA	006	004	Lord, be thou conuertid, and delyuere my soule; make thou me saaf, for thi merci.
019	PSA	006	005	For noon is in deeth, which is myndful of thee; but in helle who schal knouleche to thee?
019	PSA	006	006	I traueilide in my weilyng, Y schal waische my bed bi ech nyyt; Y schal moiste, `ether make weet, my bedstre with my teeris.
019	PSA	006	007	Myn iye is disturblid of woodnesse; Y waxe eld among alle myn enemyes.
019	PSA	006	008	Alle ye that worchen wickidnesse, departe fro me; for the Lord hath herd the vois of my wepyng.
019	PSA	006	009	The Lord hath herd my bisechyng; the Lord hath resseyued my preier.
019	PSA	006	010	Alle my enemyes be aschamed, and be disturblid greetli; be thei turned togidere, and be thei aschamed ful swiftli.
019	PSA	007	001	For the ignoraunce of Dauid, which he songe to the Lord on the wordis of Ethiopien, the sone of Gemyny. Mi Lord God, Y haue hopid in thee; make thou me saaf fro alle that pursuen me, and delyuere thou me.
019	PSA	007	002	Lest ony tyme he as a lioun rauysche my soule; the while noon is that ayenbieth, nether that makith saaf.
019	PSA	007	003	Mi Lord God, if Y dide this thing, if wickidnesse is in myn hondis;
019	PSA	007	004	if Y `yeldide to men yeldynge to me yuels, falle Y `bi disseruyng voide fro myn enemyes;
019	PSA	007	005	myn enemy pursue my soule, and take, and defoule my lijf in erthe; and brynge my glorie in to dust.
019	PSA	007	006	Lord, rise thou vp in thin ire; and be thou reysid in the coostis of myn enemyes.
019	PSA	007	007	And, my Lord God, rise thou in the comaundement, which thou `hast comaundid; and the synagoge of puplis schal cumpasse thee.
019	PSA	007	008	And for this go thou ayen an hiy; the Lord demeth puplis. Lord, deme thou me bi my riytfulnesse; and bi myn innocence on me.
019	PSA	007	009	The wickidnesse of synneris be endid; and thou, God, sekyng the hertis and reynes, schalt dresse a iust man.
019	PSA	007	010	Mi iust help is of the Lord; that makith saaf riytful men in herte.
019	PSA	007	011	The Lord is a iust iuge, stronge and pacient; whether he is wrooth bi alle daies?
019	PSA	007	012	If ye ben `not conuertid, he schal florische his swerd; he hath bent his bouwe, and made it redi.
019	PSA	007	013	And therynne he hath maad redi the vessels of deth; he hath fulli maad his arewis with brennynge thingis.
019	PSA	007	014	Lo! he conseyuede sorewe; he peynfuli brouyte forth vnriytfulnesse, and childide wickidnesse.
019	PSA	007	015	He openide a lake, and diggide it out; and he felde in to the dich which he made.
019	PSA	007	016	His sorewe schal be turned in to his heed; and his wickidnesse schal come doun in to his necke.
019	PSA	007	017	I schal knouleche to the Lord bi his riytfulnesse; and Y schal synge to the name of the hiyeste Lord.
019	PSA	008	001	To the ouercomere, for pressours, the salm of Dauid. Lord, thou art oure Lord; thi name is ful wonderful in al erthe. For thi greet doyng is reisid, aboue heuenes.
019	PSA	008	002	Of the mouth of yonge children, not spekynge and soukynge mylk, thou madist perfitli heriyng, for thin enemyes; that thou destrie the enemy and avengere.
019	PSA	008	003	For Y schal se thin heuenes, the werkis of thi fyngris; the moone and sterris, whiche thou hast foundid.
019	PSA	008	004	What is a man, that thou art myndeful of hym; ethir the sone of a virgyn, for thou visitist hym?
019	PSA	008	005	Thou hast maad hym a litil lesse than aungels; thou hast corouned hym with glorie and onour,
019	PSA	008	006	and hast ordeyned hym aboue the werkis of thin hondis.
019	PSA	008	007	Thou hast maad suget alle thingis vndur hise feet; alle scheep and oxis, ferthermore and the beestis of the feeld;
019	PSA	008	008	the briddis of the eir, and the fischis of the see; that passen bi the pathis of the see.
019	PSA	008	009	Lord, `thou art oure Lord; thi name `is wondurful in al erthe.
019	PSA	009	001	In to the ende, for the pryuytees of the sone, the salm of Dauid. Lord, Y schal knouleche to thee in al myn herte; Y schal telle alle thi merueils.
019	PSA	009	002	Thou hiyeste, Y schal be glad, and Y schal be fulli ioieful in thee; Y schal synge to thi name.
019	PSA	009	003	For thou turnest myn enemy abac; thei schulen be maad feble, and schulen perische fro thi face.
019	PSA	009	004	For thou hast maad my doom and my cause; thou, that demest riytfulnesse, `hast set on the trone.
019	PSA	009	005	Thou blamedist hethene men, and the wickid perischide; thou hast do awei the name of hem in to the world, and in to the world of world.
019	PSA	009	006	The swerdis of the enemy failiden in to the ende; and thou hast distried the citees of hem. The mynde of hem perischide with sown;
019	PSA	009	007	and the Lord dwellith with outen ende. He made redi his trone in doom; and he schal deme the world in equite,
019	PSA	009	008	he schal deme puplis in riytfulnesse.
019	PSA	009	009	And the Lord is maad refuyt, `ether help, `to a pore man; an helpere in couenable tymes in tribulacioun.
019	PSA	009	010	And thei, that knowen thi name, haue hope in thee; for thou, Lord, hast not forsake hem that seken thee.
019	PSA	009	011	Synge ye to the Lord, that dwellith in Syon; telle ye hise studyes among hethene men.
019	PSA	009	012	God foryetith not the cry of pore men; for he hath mynde, and sekith the blood of hem.
019	PSA	009	013	Lord, haue thou merci on me; se thou my mekenesse of myn enemyes.
019	PSA	009	014	Which enhaunsist me fro the yatis of deeth; that Y telle alle thi preisyngis in the yatis of the douyter of Syon.
019	PSA	009	015	Y schal `be fulli ioyeful in thin helthe; hethene men ben fast set in the perisching, which thei maden. In this snare, which thei hidden, the foot of hem is kauyt.
019	PSA	009	016	The Lord makynge domes schal be knowun; the synnere is takun in the werkis of hise hondis.
019	PSA	009	017	Synneris be turned togidere in to helle; alle folkis, that foryeten God.
019	PSA	009	018	For the foryetyng of a pore man schal not be in to the ende; the pacience of pore men schal not perische in to the ende.
019	PSA	009	019	Lord, rise thou vp, a man be not coumfortid; folkis be demyd in thi siyt.
019	PSA	009	020	Lord, ordeine thou a lawe makere on hem; wite folkis, that thei ben men.
019	PSA	010	001	Lord, whi hast thou go fer awei? thou dispisist `in couenable tymes in tribulacioun.
019	PSA	010	002	While the wickid is proud, the pore man is brent; thei ben taken in the counsels, bi whiche thei thenken.
019	PSA	010	003	Forwhi the synnere is preisid in the desiris of his soule; and the wickid is blessid.
019	PSA	010	004	The synnere `wraththide the Lord; vp the multitude of his ire he schal not seke.
019	PSA	010	005	God is not in his siyt; hise weies ben defoulid in al tyme. God, thi domes ben takun awei fro his face; he schal be lord of alle hise enemyes.
019	PSA	010	006	For he seide in his herte, Y schal not be moued, fro generacioun in to generacioun without yuel.
019	PSA	010	007	`Whos mouth is ful of cursyng, and of bitternesse, and of gyle; trauel and sorewe is vndur his tunge.
019	PSA	010	008	He sittith in aspies with ryche men in priuytees; to sle the innocent man.
019	PSA	010	009	Hise iyen biholden on a pore man; he settith aspies in hid place, as a lioun in his denne. He settith aspies, for to rauysche a pore man; for to rauysche a pore man, while he drawith the pore man.
019	PSA	010	010	In his snare he schal make meke the pore man; he schal bowe hym silf, and schal falle doun, whanne he hath be lord of pore men.
019	PSA	010	011	For he seide in his herte, God hath foryete; he hath turned awei his face, that he se not in to the ende.
019	PSA	010	012	Lord God, rise thou vp, and thin hond be enhaunsid; foryete thou not pore men.
019	PSA	010	013	For what thing terride the wickid man God to wraththe? for he seide in his herte, God schal not seke.
019	PSA	010	014	Thou seest, for thou biholdist trauel and sorewe; that thou take hem in to thin hondis. The pore man is left to thee; thou schalt be an helpere to the fadirles and modirles.
019	PSA	010	015	Al to-breke thou the arme of the synnere, and yuel willid; his synne schal be souyt, and it schal not be foundun.
019	PSA	010	016	The Lord schal regne with outen ende, and in to the world of world; folkis, ye schulen perische fro the lond of hym.
019	PSA	010	017	The Lord hath herd the desir of pore men; thin eere hath herd the makyng redi of her herte.
019	PSA	010	018	To deme for the modirles `and meke; that a man `leie to no more to `magnyfie hym silf on erthe.
019	PSA	011	001	To the victorie of Dauid. I triste in the Lord; hou seien ye to my soule, Passe thou ouere in to an hil, as a sparowe doith?
019	PSA	011	002	For lo! synneris han bent a bouwe; thei han maad redi her arowis in an arowe caas; `for to schete in derknesse riytful men in herte.
019	PSA	011	003	For thei han distryed, whom thou hast maad perfit; but what dide the riytful man?
019	PSA	011	004	The Lord is in his hooli temple; he is Lord, his seete is in heuene. Hise iyen biholden on a pore man; hise iyelidis axen the sones of men.
019	PSA	011	005	The Lord axith a iust man, and vnfeithful man; but he, that loueth wickidnesse, hatith his soule.
