019	PSA	035	015	And thei weren glad, and camen togidere ayens me; turmentis weren gaderid on me, and Y knew not.
019	PSA	035	016	Thei weren scaterid, and not compunct, thei temptiden me, thei scornyden me with mowyng; thei gnastiden on me with her teeth.
019	PSA	035	017	Lord, whanne thou schalt biholde, restore thou my soule fro the wickidnesse of hem; `restore thou myn oon aloone fro liouns.
019	PSA	035	018	I schal knowleche to thee in a greet chirche; Y schal herie thee in a sad puple.
019	PSA	035	019	Thei that ben aduersaries wickidli to me, haue not ioye on me; that haten me with out cause, and bikenen with iyen.
019	PSA	035	020	For sotheli thei spaken pesibli to me; and thei spekynge in wrathfulnesse of erthe thouyten giles.
019	PSA	035	021	And thei maden large her mouth on me; thei seiden, Wel, wel! oure iyen han sien.
019	PSA	035	022	Lord, thou hast seen, be thou not stille; Lord, departe thou not fro me.
019	PSA	035	023	Rise vp, and yyue tent to my doom; my God and my Lord, biholde in to my cause.
019	PSA	035	024	Mi Lord God, deme thou me bi thi riytfulnesse; and haue thei not ioye on me.
019	PSA	035	025	Seie thei not in her hertis, Wel, wel, to oure soule; nether seie thei, We schulen deuoure hym.
019	PSA	035	026	Shame thei, and drede thei togidere; that thanken for myn yuels. Be thei clothid with schame and drede; that speken yuele thingis on me.
019	PSA	035	027	Haue thei ful ioie, and be thei glad that wolen my riytfulnesse; and seie thei euere, The Lord be magnyfied, whiche wolen the pees of his seruaunt.
019	PSA	035	028	And my tunge schal bithenke thi riytfulnesse; al day thin heriyng.
019	PSA	036	001	`To victorie, to Dauid, `the seruaunt of the Lord. The vniust man seide, that he trespasse in hym silf; the drede of God is not bifor hise iyen.
019	PSA	036	002	For he dide gilefuli in the siyt of God; that his wickidnesse be foundun to hatrede.
019	PSA	036	003	The wordis of his mouth ben wickidnesse and gile, he nolde vndirstonde to do wel.
019	PSA	036	004	He thouyte wickidnesse in his bed, he stood nyy al weie not good; forsothe he hatide not malice.
019	PSA	036	005	Lord, thi merci is in heuene; and thi treuthe is `til to cloudis.
019	PSA	036	006	Thi riytfulnesse is as the hillis of God; thi domes ben myche depthe of watris. Lord, thou schalt saue men and beestis;
019	PSA	036	007	as thou, God, hast multiplied thi merci. But the sones of men; schulen hope in the hilyng of thi wyngis.
019	PSA	036	008	Thei schulen be fillid gretli of the plentee of thin hows; and thou schalt yyue drynke to hem with the steef streem of thi likyng.
019	PSA	036	009	For the wel of life is at thee; and in thi liyt we schulen se liyt.
019	PSA	036	010	Lord, sette forth thi mercy to hem, that knowen thee; and thi ryytfulnesse to hem that ben of riytful herte.
019	PSA	036	011	The foot of pryde come not to me; and the hond of the synnere moue me not.
019	PSA	036	012	There thei felden doun, that worchen wickidnesse; thei ben cast out, and myyten not stonde.
019	PSA	037	001	To Dauith. Nile thou sue wickid men; nether loue thou men doynge wickidnesse.
019	PSA	037	002	For thei schulen wexe drie swiftli as hey; and thei schulen falle doun soone as the wortis of eerbis.
019	PSA	037	003	Hope thou in the Lord, and do thou goodnesse; and enhabite thou the lond, and thou schalt be fed with hise richessis.
019	PSA	037	004	Delite thou in the Lord; and he schal yyue to thee the axyngis of thin herte.
019	PSA	037	005	Schewe thi weie to the Lord; and hope thou in hym, and he schal do.
019	PSA	037	006	And he schal lede out thi riytfulnesse as liyt, and thi doom as myddai;
019	PSA	037	007	be thou suget to the Lord, and preye thou hym. Nile thou sue hym, that hath prosperite in his weie; a man doynge vnriytfulnessis.
019	PSA	037	008	Ceese thou of ire, and forsake woodnesse; nyle thou sue, that thou do wickidli.
019	PSA	037	009	For thei, that doen wickidli, schulen be distried; but thei that suffren the Lord, schulen enerite the lond.
019	PSA	037	010	And yit a litil, and a synnere schal not be; and thou schalt seke his place, and schalt not fynde.
019	PSA	037	011	But mylde men schulen enerite the lond; and schulen delite in the multitude of pees.
019	PSA	037	012	A synnere schal aspie a riytful man; and he schal gnaste with hise teeth on hym.
019	PSA	037	013	But the Lord schal scorne the synnere; for he biholdith that his day cometh.
019	PSA	037	014	Synners drowen out swerd; thei benten her bouwe. To disseyue a pore man and nedi; to strangle riytful men of herte.
019	PSA	037	015	Her swerd entre in to the herte of hem silf; and her bouwe be brokun.
019	PSA	037	016	Betere is a litil thing to a iust man; than many richessis of synneris.
019	PSA	037	017	For the armes of synneris schal be al to-brokun; but the Lord confermeth iust men.
019	PSA	037	018	The Lord knowith the daies of vnwemmed; and her heritage schal be withouten ende.
019	PSA	037	019	Thei schulen not be schent in the yuel tyme, and thei schulen be fillid in the dayes of hungur;
019	PSA	037	020	for synneris schulen perische. Forsothe anoon as the enemyes of the Lord ben onourid, and enhaunsid; thei failynge schulen faile as smoke.
019	PSA	037	021	A synnere schal borewe, and schal not paie; but a iust man hath merci, and schal yyue.
019	PSA	037	022	For thei that blessen the Lord schulen enerite the lond; but thei that cursen hym schulen perische.
019	PSA	037	023	The goyng of a man schal be dressid anentis the Lord; and he schal wilne his weie.
019	PSA	037	024	Whanne he fallith, he schal not be hurtlid doun; for the Lord vndursettith his hond.
019	PSA	037	025	I was yongere, and sotheli Y wexide eld, and Y siy not a iust man forsakun; nethir his seed sekynge breed.
019	PSA	037	026	Al dai he hath merci, and leeneth; and his seed schal be in blessyng.
019	PSA	037	027	Bouwe thou awei fro yuel, and do good; and dwelle thou in to the world of world.
019	PSA	037	028	For the Lord loueth doom, and schal not forsake hise seyntis; thei schulen be kept with outen ende. Vniust men schulen be punyschid; and the seed of wickid men schal perische.
019	PSA	037	029	But iust men schulen enerite the lond; and schulen enabite theronne in to the world of world.
019	PSA	037	030	The mouth of a iust man schal bithenke wisdom; and his tunge schal speke doom.
019	PSA	037	031	The lawe of his God is in his herte; and hise steppis schulen not be disseyued.
019	PSA	037	032	A synnere biholdith a iust man; and sekith to sle hym.
019	PSA	037	033	But the Lord schal not forsake hym in hise hondis; nethir schal dampne hym, whanne it schal be demed ayens hym.
019	PSA	037	034	Abide thou the Lord, and kepe thou his weie, and he schal enhaunse thee, that bi eritage thou take the lond; whanne synneris schulen perische, thou schalt se.
019	PSA	037	035	I siy a wickid man enhaunsid aboue; and reisid vp as the cedris of Liban.
019	PSA	037	036	And Y passide, and lo! he was not; Y souyte hym, and his place is not foundun.
019	PSA	037	037	Kepe thou innocence, and se equite; for tho ben relikis to a pesible man.
019	PSA	037	038	Forsothe vniust men schulen perische; the relifs of wickid men schulen perische togidere.
019	PSA	037	039	But the helthe of iust men is of the Lord; and he is her defendere in the tyme of tribulacioun.
019	PSA	037	040	And the Lord schal helpe hem, and schal make hem fre, and he schal delyuere hem fro synneris; and he schal saue hem, for thei hopiden in hym.
019	PSA	038	001	`The salm of Dauid, to bythenke on the sabat. Lord, repreue thou not me in thi strong veniaunce; nether chastice thou me in thin ire.
019	PSA	038	002	For thin arowis ben fitchid in me; and thou hast confermed thin hond on me.
019	PSA	038	003	Noon helthe is in my fleisch fro the face of thin ire; no pees is to my boonys fro the face of my synnes.
019	PSA	038	004	For my wickidnessis ben goon ouer myn heed; as an heuy birthun, tho ben maad heuy on me.
019	PSA	038	005	Myn heelid woundis weren rotun, and ben brokun; fro the face of myn vnwisdom.
019	PSA	038	006	I am maad a wretche, and Y am bowid doun til in to the ende; al dai Y entride sorewful.
019	PSA	038	007	For my leendis ben fillid with scornyngis; and helthe is not in my fleisch.
019	PSA	038	008	I am turmentid, and maad low ful greetli; Y roride for the weilyng of myn herte.
019	PSA	038	009	Lord, al my desire is bifor thee; and my weilyng is not hid fro thee.
019	PSA	038	010	Myn herte is disturblid in me, my vertu forsook me; and the liyt of myn iyen `forsook me, and it is not with me.
019	PSA	038	011	My frendis and my neiyboris neiyiden; and stoden ayens me. And thei that weren bisidis me stoden afer;
019	PSA	038	012	and thei diden violence, that souyten my lijf. And thei that souyten yuels to me, spaken vanytees; and thouyten gilis al dai.
019	PSA	038	013	But Y as a deef man herde not; and as a doumb man not openynge his mouth.
019	PSA	038	014	And Y am maad as a man not herynge; and not hauynge repreuyngis in his mouth.
019	PSA	038	015	For, Lord, Y hopide in thee; my Lord God, thou schalt here me.
019	PSA	038	016	For Y seide, Lest ony tyme myn enemyes haue ioye on me; and the while my feet ben mouyd, thei spaken grete thingis on me.
019	PSA	038	017	For Y am redi to betyngis; and my sorewe is euere in my siyt.
019	PSA	038	018	For Y schal telle my wickidnesse; and Y schal thenke for my synne.
019	PSA	038	019	But myn enemyes lyuen, and ben confermed on me; and thei ben multiplyed, that haten me wickidli.
019	PSA	038	020	Thei that yelden yuels for goodis, backbitiden me; for Y suede goodnesse.
019	PSA	038	021	My Lord God, forsake thou not me; go thou not awei fro me.
019	PSA	038	022	Lord God of myn helthe; biholde thou in to myn help.
019	PSA	039	001	For victorie, to Iditum, the song of Dauid. I seide, Y schal kepe my weies; that Y trespasse not in my tunge. I settide kepyng to my mouth; whanne a synnere stood ayens me.
019	PSA	039	002	I was doumb, and was mekid ful gretli, and was stille fro goodis; and my sorewe was renulid.
019	PSA	039	003	Myn herte was hoot with ynne me; and fier schal brenne out in my thenkyng.
019	PSA	039	004	I spak in my tunge; Lord, make thou myn eende knowun to me. And the noumbre of my daies what it is; that Y wite, what failith to me.
019	PSA	039	005	Lo! thou hast set my daies mesurable; and my substaunce is as nouyt bifor thee. Netheles al vanytee; ech man lyuynge.
019	PSA	039	006	Netheles a man passith in ymage; but also he is disturblid veynli. He tresorith; and he noot, to whom he `schal gadere tho thingis.
019	PSA	039	007	And now which is myn abiding? whether not the Lord? and my substaunce is at thee.
019	PSA	039	008	Delyuere thou me fro alle my wickidnessis; thou hast youe me schenschip to the vnkunnynge.
019	PSA	039	009	I was doumbe, and openyde not my mouth; for thou hast maad,
019	PSA	039	010	remoue thou thi woundis fro me.
019	PSA	039	011	Fro the strengthe of thin hond Y failide in blamyngis; for wickidnesse thou hast chastisid man. And thou madist his lijf to faile as an yreyne; netheles ech man is disturblid in veyn.
019	PSA	039	012	Lord, here thou my preier and my bisechyng; perseyue thou with eeris my teeris.
019	PSA	039	013	Be thou not stille, for Y am a comelyng at thee; and a pilgrime, as alle my fadris. Foryyue thou to me, that Y be refreischid, bifor that Y go; and Y schal no more be.
019	PSA	040	001	For victorie, the song of Dauid. Y abidynge abood the Lord; and he yaf tent to me.
019	PSA	040	002	And he herde my preieris; and he ledde out me fro the lake of wretchidnesse, and fro the filthe of draft. And he ordeynede my feet on a stoon; and he dresside my goyngis.
019	PSA	040	003	And he sente in to my mouth a newe song; a song to oure God. Many men schulen se, and schulen drede; and schulen haue hope in the Lord.
019	PSA	040	004	Blessid is the man, of whom the name of the Lord is his hope; and he bihelde not in to vanitees, and in to false woodnesses.
019	PSA	040	005	Mi Lord God, thou hast maad thi merueils manye; and in thi thouytis noon is, that is lijk thee. I teld, and Y spak; and thei ben multiplied aboue noumbre.
019	PSA	040	006	Thou noldist sacrifice and offryng; but thou madist perfitli eeris to me. Thou axidist not brent sacrifice, and sacrifice for synne;
019	PSA	040	007	thanne Y seide, Lo! Y come. In the heed of the book it is writun of me,
019	PSA	040	008	that Y schulde do thi wille; my God, Y wolde; and thi lawe in the myddis of myn herte.
019	PSA	040	009	I telde thi riytfulnesse in a greet chirche; lo! Y schal not refreine my lippis, Lord, thou wistist.
019	PSA	040	010	I hidde not thi riytfulnesse in myn herte; Y seide thi treuthe and thin helthe. I hidde not thi mercy and thi treuthe; fro a myche counsel.
019	PSA	040	011	But thou, Lord, make not fer thi merciful doyngis fro me; thi mercy and treuthe euere token me vp.
019	PSA	040	012	For whi yuels, of whiche is no noumbre, cumpassiden me; my wickidnessis token me, and y myyte not, that Y schulde se. Tho ben multiplied aboue the heeris of myn heed; and myn herte forsook me.
019	PSA	040	013	Lord, plese it to thee, that thou delyuere me; Lord, biholde thou to helpe me.
019	PSA	040	014	Be thei schent, and aschamed togidere; that seken my lijf, to take awei it. Be thei turned abac, and be thei schamed; that wolen yuels to me.
