019	PSA	041	006	And if he entride for to se, he spak veyn thingis; his herte gaderide wickidnesse to hym silf.
019	PSA	041	007	He yede with out forth; and spak to the same thing. Alle myn enemyes bacbitiden pryuyli ayens me; ayens me thei thouyten yuels to me.
019	PSA	041	008	Thei ordeineden an yuel word ayens me; Whether he that slepith, schal not leie to, that he rise ayen?
019	PSA	041	009	For whi the man of my pees, in whom Y hopide, he that eet my looues; made greet disseit on me.
019	PSA	041	010	But thou, Lord, haue merci on me, and reise me ayen; and Y schal yelde to hem.
019	PSA	041	011	In this thing Y knew, that thou woldist me; for myn enemye schal not haue ioye on me.
019	PSA	041	012	Forsothe thou hast take me vp for ynnocence; and hast confermed me in thi siyt with outen ende.
019	PSA	041	013	Blessid be the Lord God of Israel, fro the world and in to the world; be it doon, be it doon.
019	PSA	042	001	To victorie, to the sones of Chore. As an hert desirith to the wellis of watris; so thou, God, my soule desirith to thee.
019	PSA	042	002	Mi soule thirstide to God, `that is a `quik welle; whanne schal Y come, and appere bifor the face of God?
019	PSA	042	003	Mi teeris weren looues to me bi dai and nyyt; while it is seid to me ech dai, Where is thi God?
019	PSA	042	004	I bithouyte of these thingis, and Y schedde out in me my soule; for Y schal passe in to the place of the wondurful tabernacle, til to the hows of God. In the vois of ful out ioiyng and knoulechyng; is the sown of the etere.
019	PSA	042	005	Mi soule, whi art thou sory; and whi disturblist thou me? Hope thou in God, for yit Y schal knouleche to hym; he is the helthe of my cheer,
019	PSA	042	006	and my God. My soule is disturblid at my silf; therfor, God, Y schal be myndeful of thee fro the lond of Jordan, and fro the litil hil Hermonyim.
019	PSA	042	007	Depthe clepith depthe; in the vois of thi wyndows. Alle thin hiye thingis and thi wawis; passiden ouer me.
019	PSA	042	008	The Lord sente his merci in the dai; and his song in the nyyt.
019	PSA	042	009	At me is a preier to the God of my lijf; Y schal seie to God, Thou art my `takere vp. Whi foryetist thou me; and whi go Y sorewful, while the enemy turmentith me?
019	PSA	042	010	While my boonys ben brokun togidere; myn enemyes, that troblen me, dispiseden me. While thei seien to me, bi alle daies; Where is thi God?
019	PSA	042	011	Mi soule, whi art thou sori; and whi disturblist thou me? Hope thou in God, for yit Y schal knouleche to hym; `he is the helthe of my cheer, and my God.
019	PSA	043	001	God, deme thou me, and departe thou my cause fro a folc not hooli; delyuere thou me fro a wickid man, and gileful.
019	PSA	043	002	For thou art God, my strengthe; whi hast thou put me abac, and whi go Y soreuful, while the enemy turmentith me?
019	PSA	043	003	Sende out thi liyt, and thi treuthe; tho ledden me forth, and brouyten in to thin hooli hil, and in to thi tabernaclis.
019	PSA	043	004	And Y schal entre to the auter of God; to God, that gladith my yongthe. God, my God, Y schal knowleche to thee in an harpe; my soule,
019	PSA	043	005	whi art thou sory, and whi troblist thou me? Hope thou in God, for yit Y schal knouleche to hym; he is the helthe of my cheer, and my God.
019	PSA	044	001	`To victorie, lernyng to the sones of Chore. God, we herden with oure eeris; oure fadris telden to vs. The werk, which thou wrouytist in the daies of hem; and in elde daies.
019	PSA	044	002	Thin hond lost hethene men, and thou plauntidist hem; thou turmentidist puplis, and castidist hem out.
019	PSA	044	003	For the children of Israel weldiden the lond not bi her swerd; and the arm of hem sauyde not hem. But thi riyt hond, and thin arm, and the liytnyng of thi cheer; for thou were plesid in hem.
019	PSA	044	004	Thou art thi silf, my kyng and my God; that sendist helthis to Jacob.
019	PSA	044	005	Bi thee we schulen wyndewe oure enemyes with horn; and in thi name we schulen dispise hem, that risen ayen vs.
019	PSA	044	006	For Y schal not hope in my bouwe; and my swerd schal not saue me.
019	PSA	044	007	For thou hast saued vs fro men turmentinge vs; and thou hast schent men hatinge vs.
019	PSA	044	008	We schulen be preisid in God al dai; and in thi name we schulen knouleche to thee in to the world.
019	PSA	044	009	But now thou hast put vs abac, and hast schent vs; and thou, God, schalt not go out in oure vertues.
019	PSA	044	010	Thou hast turned vs awei bihynde aftir oure enemyes; and thei, that hatiden vs, rauyschiden dyuerseli to hem silf.
019	PSA	044	011	Thou hast youe vs as scheep of meetis; and among hethene men thou hast scaterid vs.
019	PSA	044	012	Thou hast seeld thi puple with out prijs; and multitude was not in the chaungyngis of hem.
019	PSA	044	013	Thou hast set vs schenschip to oure neiyboris; mouwyng and scorn to hem that ben in oure cumpas.
019	PSA	044	014	Thou hast set vs into licnesse to hethene me; stiryng of heed among puplis.
019	PSA	044	015	Al dai my schame is ayens me; and the schenschipe of my face hilide me.
019	PSA	044	016	Fro the vois of dispisere, and yuele spekere; fro the face of enemy, and pursuere.
019	PSA	044	017	Alle these thingis camen on vs, and we han not foryete thee; and we diden not wickidli in thi testament.
019	PSA	044	018	And oure herte yede not awei bihynde; and thou hast bowid awei oure pathis fro thi weie.
019	PSA	044	019	For thou hast maad vs lowe in the place of turment; and the schadewe of deth hilide vs.
019	PSA	044	020	If we foryaten the name of oure God; and if we helden forth oure hondis to an alien God.
019	PSA	044	021	Whether God schal not seke these thingis? for he knowith the hid thingis of herte.
019	PSA	044	022	For whi we ben slayn al dai for thee; we ben demed as scheep of sleyng.
019	PSA	044	023	Lord, rise vp, whi slepist thou? rise vp, and putte not awei in to the ende.
019	PSA	044	024	Whi turnest thou awei thi face? thou foryetist oure pouert, and oure tribulacioun.
019	PSA	044	025	For oure lijf is maad low in dust; oure wombe is glued togidere in the erthe.
019	PSA	044	026	Lord, rise vp thou, and helpe vs; and ayenbie vs for thi name.
019	PSA	045	001	To the ouercomere for the lilies, the most loued song of lernyng of the sones of Chore. Myn herte hath teld out a good word; Y seie my workis `to the kyng. Mi tunge is `a penne of a writere; writynge swiftli.
019	PSA	045	002	Crist, thou art fairer in schap than the sones of men; grace is spred abrood in thi lippis; therfor God blessid thee withouten ende.
019	PSA	045	003	Be thou gird with thi swerd; on thi hipe most myytili.
019	PSA	045	004	Biholde thou in thi schaplynesse and thi fairnesse; come thou forth with prosperite, and regne thou. For treuthe, and myldenesse, and riytfulnesse; and thi riyt hond schal lede forth thee wondurfuli.
019	PSA	045	005	Thi scharpe arowis schulen falle in to the hertis of the enemyes of the kyng; puplis schulen be vndur thee.
