019	PSA	086	005	For thou, Lord, art swete and mylde; and of myche merci to alle men inwardli clepynge thee.
019	PSA	086	006	Lord, perseyue thou my preier with eeris; and yyue thou tente to the vois of my bisechyng.
019	PSA	086	007	In the dai of my tribulacioun Y criede to thee; for thou herdist me.
019	PSA	086	008	Lord, noon among goddis is lijk thee; and noon is euene to thi werkis.
019	PSA	086	009	Lord, alle folkis, whiche euere thou madist, schulen come, and worschipe bifore thee; and thei schulen glorifie thi name.
