019	PSA	090	013	Lord, be thou conuertid sumdeel; and be thou able to be preied on thi seruauntis.
019	PSA	090	014	We weren fillid eerli with thi merci; we maden ful out ioye, and we delitiden in alle oure daies.
019	PSA	090	015	We weren glad for the daies in whiche thou madist vs meke; for the yeeris in whiche we siyen yuels.
019	PSA	090	016	Lord, biholde thou into thi seruauntis, and in to thi werkis; and dresse thou the sones of hem.
019	PSA	090	017	And the schynyng of oure Lord God be on vs; and dresse thou the werkis of oure hondis on vs, and dresse thou the werk of oure hondis.
019	PSA	091	001	He that dwellith in the help of the hiyeste God; schal dwelle in the proteccioun of God of heuene.
019	PSA	091	002	He schal seie to the Lord, Thou art myn vptaker, and my refuit; my God, Y schal hope in him.
019	PSA	091	003	For he delyuered me fro the snare of hunteris; and fro a scharp word.
019	PSA	091	004	With hise schuldris he schal make schadowe to thee; and thou schalt haue hope vnder hise fetheris.
019	PSA	091	005	His treuthe schal cumpasse thee with a scheld; thou schalt not drede of nyytis drede.
019	PSA	091	006	Of an arowe fliynge in the dai, of a gobelyn goynge in derknessis; of asailing, and a myddai feend.
