019	PSA	100	001	`A salm to knouleche; `in Ebrew `thus, A salm for knouleching.
019	PSA	100	002	Al erthe, singe ye hertli to God; serue ye the Lord in gladnesse. Entre ye in his siyt; in ful out ioiyng.
019	PSA	100	003	Wite ye, that the Lord hym silf is God; he made vs, and not we maden vs. His puple, and the scheep of his lesewe,
019	PSA	100	004	entre ye in to hise yatis in knoulechyng; entre ye in to hise porchis, `knouleche ye to him in ympnes.
019	PSA	100	005	Herye ye his name, for the Lord is swete, his merci is with outen ende; and his treuthe is in generacioun and in to generacioun.
019	PSA	101	001	`The salm of Dauid. Lord, Y schal synge to thee; merci and doom.
019	PSA	101	002	I schal synge, and Y schal vndurstonde in a weie with out wem; whanne thou schalt come to me. I yede perfitli in the innocence of myn herte; in the myddil of myn hous.
019	PSA	101	003	I settide not forth bifore myn iyen an vniust thing; Y hatide hem that maden trespassyngis.
019	PSA	101	004	A schrewide herte cleuede not to me; Y knewe not a wickid man bowynge awei fro me.
019	PSA	101	005	I pursuede hym; that bacbitide priueli his neiybore. With the proude iye and an herte vnable to be fillid; Y eet not with this.
019	PSA	101	006	Myn iyen weren to the feithful men of erthe, that thei sitte with me; he that yede in a weie with out wem, mynystride to me.
019	PSA	101	007	He that doith pride, schal not dwelle in the myddil of myn hous; he that spekith wickid thingis, seruede not in the siyt of myn iyen.
019	PSA	101	008	In the morutid Y killide alle the synners of erthe; that Y schulde leese fro the citee of the Lord alle men worchynge wickidnesse.
019	PSA	102	001	The preier of a pore man, whanne he was angwishid, and schedde out his speche bifore the Lord. Lord, here thou my preier; and my crie come to thee.
019	PSA	102	002	Turne not awei thi face fro me; in what euere dai Y am troblid, bowe doun thin eere to me. In what euere day Y schal inwardli clepe thee; here thou me swiftli.
019	PSA	102	003	For my daies han failid as smoke; and my boonus han dried vp as critouns.
019	PSA	102	004	I am smytun as hei, and myn herte dried vp; for Y haue foryete to eete my breed.
019	PSA	102	005	Of the vois of my weilyng; my boon cleuede to my fleische.
019	PSA	102	006	I am maad lijk a pellican of wildirnesse; Y am maad as a niyt crowe in an hous.
019	PSA	102	007	I wakide; and Y am maad as a solitarie sparowe in the roof.
019	PSA	102	008	Al dai myn enemyes dispisiden me; and thei that preisiden me sworen ayens me.
019	PSA	102	009	For Y eet aschis as breed; and Y meddlide my drinke with weping.
019	PSA	102	010	Fro the face of the ire of thin indignacioun; for thou reisinge me hast hurtlid me doun.
019	PSA	102	011	Mi daies boweden awei as a schadewe; and Y wexede drie as hei.
019	PSA	102	012	But, Lord, thou dwellist with outen ende; and thi memorial in generacioun and in to generacioun.
019	PSA	102	013	Lord, thou risinge vp schalt haue merci on Sion; for the tyme `to haue merci therof cometh, for the tyme cometh.
019	PSA	102	014	For the stones therof plesiden thi seruauntis; and thei schulen haue merci on the lond therof.
019	PSA	102	015	And, Lord, hethen men schulen drede thi name; and alle kingis of erthe schulen drede thi glori.
019	PSA	102	016	For the Lord hath bildid Sion; and he schal be seen in his glorie.
019	PSA	102	017	He bihelde on the preier of meke men; and he dispiside not the preier of hem.
019	PSA	102	018	Be these thingis writun in an othere generacioun; and the puple that schal be maad schal preise the Lord.
019	PSA	102	019	For he bihelde fro his hiye hooli place; the Lord lokide fro heuene in to erthe.
019	PSA	102	020	For to here the weilingis of feterid men; and for to vnbynde the sones of slayn men.
019	PSA	102	021	That thei telle in Sion the name of the Lord; and his preising in Jerusalem.
019	PSA	102	022	In gaderinge togidere puplis in to oon; and kingis, that thei serue the Lord.
019	PSA	102	023	It answeride to hym in the weie of his vertu; Telle thou to me the fewnesse of my daies.
019	PSA	102	024	Ayenclepe thou not me in the myddil of my daies; thi yeris ben in generacioun and in to generacioun.
019	PSA	102	025	Lord, thou foundidist the erthe in the bigynnyng; and heuenes ben the werkis of thin hondis.
019	PSA	102	026	Tho schulen perische, but thou dwellist perfitli; and alle schulen wexe eelde as a clooth. And thou schalt chaunge hem as an hiling, and tho schulen be chaungid;
019	PSA	102	027	but thou art the same thi silf, and thi yeeris schulen not faile.
019	PSA	102	028	The sones of thi seruauntis schulen dwelle; and the seed of hem schal be dressid in to the world.
019	PSA	103	001	`Of Dauid. Mi soule, blesse thou the Lord; and alle thingis that ben with ynne me, blesse his hooli name.
019	PSA	103	002	Mi soule, blesse thou the Lord; and nyle thou foryete alle the yeldyngis of him.
019	PSA	103	003	Which doith merci to alle thi wickidnessis; which heelith alle thi sijknessis.
019	PSA	103	004	Which ayenbieth thi lijf fro deth; which corowneth thee in merci and merciful doyngis.
019	PSA	103	005	Which fillith thi desijr in goodis; thi yongthe schal be renulid as the yongthe of an egle.
019	PSA	103	006	The Lord doynge mercies; and doom to alle men suffringe wrong.
019	PSA	103	007	He made hise weies knowun to Moises; hise willis to the sones of Israel.
019	PSA	103	008	The Lord is merciful doer, and merciful in wille; longe abidinge, and myche merciful.
019	PSA	103	009	He schal not be wrooth with outen ende; and he schal not thretne with outen ende.
019	PSA	103	010	He dide not to vs aftir oure synnes; nether he yeldide to vs aftir oure wickidnessis.
019	PSA	103	011	For bi the hiynesse of heuene fro erthe; he made strong his merci on men dredynge hym.
019	PSA	103	012	As myche as the eest is fer fro the west; he made fer oure wickidnessis fro vs.
019	PSA	103	013	As a fadir hath merci on sones, the Lord hadde merci on men dredynge him;
019	PSA	103	014	for he knewe oure makyng.
019	PSA	103	015	He bithouyte that we ben dust, a man is as hey; his dai schal flowre out so as a flour of the feeld.
019	PSA	103	016	For the spirit schal passe in hym, and schal not abide; and schal no more knowe his place.
019	PSA	103	017	But the merci of the Lord is fro with out bigynnyng, and til in to with outen ende; on men dredinge hym. And his riytfulnesse is in to the sones of sones;
019	PSA	103	018	to hem that kepen his testament. And ben myndeful of hise comaundementis; to do tho.
019	PSA	103	019	The Lord hath maad redi his seete in heuene; and his rewme schal be lord of alle.
019	PSA	103	020	Aungels of the Lord, blesse ye the Lord; ye myyti in vertu, doynge his word, to here the vois of hise wordis.
019	PSA	103	021	Alle vertues of the Lord, blesse ye the Lord; ye mynystris of hym that doen his wille.
019	PSA	103	022	Alle werkis of the Lord, blesse ye the Lord, in ech place of his lordschipe; my soule, blesse thou the Lord.
019	PSA	104	001	Mi soule, blesse thou the Lord; my Lord God, thou art magnyfied greetli. Thou hast clothid knouleching and fairnesse; and thou art clothid with liyt,
019	PSA	104	002	as with a cloth. And thou stretchist forth heuene as a skyn;
019	PSA	104	003	and thou hilist with watris the hiyer partis therof. Which settist a cloude thi stiyng; which goest on the fetheris of wyndis.
019	PSA	104	004	Which makist spiritis thin aungels; and thi mynystris brennynge fier.
019	PSA	104	005	Which hast foundid the erthe on his stablenesse; it schal not be bowid in to the world of world.
019	PSA	104	006	The depthe of watris as a cloth is the clothing therof; watris schulen stonde on hillis.
019	PSA	104	007	Tho schulen fle fro thi blamyng; men schulen be aferd of the vois of thi thundur.
019	PSA	104	008	Hillis stien vp, and feeldis goen doun; in to the place which thou hast foundid to tho.
019	PSA	104	009	Thou hast set a terme, which tho schulen not passe; nether tho schulen be turned, for to hile the erthe.
019	PSA	104	010	And thou sendist out wellis in grete valeis; watris schulen passe bitwix the myddil of hillis.
019	PSA	104	011	Alle the beestis of the feeld schulen drynke; wielde assis schulen abide in her thirst.
019	PSA	104	012	Briddis of the eir schulen dwelle on tho; fro the myddis of stoonys thei schulen yyue voices.
019	PSA	104	013	And thou moistist hillis of her hiyer thingis; the erthe schal be fillid of the fruyt of thi werkis.
019	PSA	104	014	And thou bringist forth hei to beestis; and eerbe to the seruyce of men. That thou bringe forth breed of the erthe;
019	PSA	104	015	and that wiyn make glad the herte of men. That he make glad the face with oile; and that breed make stidefast the herte of man.
019	PSA	104	016	The trees of the feeld schulen be fillid, and the cedris of the Liban, whiche he plauntide;
019	PSA	104	017	sparewis schulen make nest there. The hous of the gerfaukun is the leeder of tho;
019	PSA	104	018	hiye hillis ben refute to hertis; a stoon is refutt to irchouns.
019	PSA	104	019	He made the moone in to tymes; the sunne knewe his goyng doun.
019	PSA	104	020	Thou hast set derknessis, and nyyt is maad; alle beestis of the wode schulen go ther ynne.
019	PSA	104	021	Liouns whelpis rorynge for to rauysche; and to seke of God meete to hem silf.
019	PSA	104	022	The sunne is risun, and tho ben gaderid togidere; and tho schulen be set in her couchis.
019	PSA	104	023	A man schal go out to his werk; and to his worching, til to the euentid.
019	PSA	104	024	Lord, thi werkis ben magnefiede ful myche, thou hast maad alle thingis in wisdom; the erthe is fillid with thi possessioun.
019	PSA	104	025	This see is greet and large to hondis; there ben crepinge beestis, of which is noon noumbre. Litil beestis with grete;
019	PSA	104	026	schippis schulen passe there. This dragoun which thou hast formyd; for to scorne hym.
019	PSA	104	027	Alle thingis abiden of thee; that thou yyue to hem meete in tyme.
019	PSA	104	028	Whanne thou schalt yyue to hem, thei schulen gadere; whanne thou schalt opene thin hond, alle thingis schulen be fillid with goodnesse.
019	PSA	104	029	But whanne thou schalt turne awey the face, thei schulen be disturblid; thou schalt take awei the spirit of them, and thei schulen faile; and thei schulen turne ayen in to her dust.
019	PSA	104	030	Sende out thi spirit, and thei schulen be formed of the newe; and thou schalt renule the face of the erthe.
019	PSA	104	031	The glorie of the Lord be in to the world; the Lord schal be glad in hise werkis.
019	PSA	104	032	Which biholdith the erthe, and makith it to tremble; which touchith hillis, and tho smoken.
019	PSA	104	033	I schal singe to the Lord in my lijf; Y schal seie salm to my God, as longe as Y am.
019	PSA	104	034	Mi speche be myrie to him; forsothe Y schal delite in the Lord.
019	PSA	104	035	Synneris faile fro the erthe, and wickid men faile, so that thei be not; my soule, blesse thou the Lord.
019	PSA	105	001	Alleluya. Knouleche ye to the Lord, and inwardli clepe ye his name; telle ye hise werkis among hethen men.
019	PSA	105	002	Synge ye to hym, and seie ye salm to him, and telle ye alle hise merueylis;
019	PSA	105	003	be ye preisid in his hooli name. The herte of men sekynge the Lord be glad;
019	PSA	105	004	seke ye the Lord, and be ye confermed; seke ye euere his face.
019	PSA	105	005	Haue ye mynde on hise merueilis, whiche he dide; on his grete wondris, and domes of his mouth.
019	PSA	105	006	The seed of Abraham, his seruaunt; the sones of Jacob, his chosun man.
019	PSA	105	007	He is oure Lord God; hise domes ben in al the erthe.
019	PSA	105	008	He was myndeful of his testament in to the world; of the word which he comaundide in to a thousynde generaciouns.
019	PSA	105	009	Which he disposide to Abraham; and of his ooth to Isaac.
019	PSA	105	010	And he ordeynede it to Jacob in to a comaundement; and to Israel in to euerlastinge testament.
019	PSA	105	011	And he seide, I shal yiue to thee the lond of Canaan; the cord of youre eritage.
019	PSA	105	012	Whanne thei weren in a litil noumbre; and the comelingis of hem weren ful fewe.
019	PSA	105	013	And thei passiden fro folk in to folk; and fro a rewme in to another puple.
