019	PSA	105	019	The speche of the Lord enflawmede him;
019	PSA	105	020	the king sente and vnbond hym; the prince of puplis sente and delyuerede him.
019	PSA	105	021	He ordeynede him the lord of his hous; and the prince of al his possessioun.
019	PSA	105	022	That he schulde lerne hise princis as him silf; and that he schulde teche hise elde men prudence.
019	PSA	105	023	And Israel entride in to Egipt; and Jacob was a comeling in the lond of Cham.
019	PSA	105	024	And God encreesside his puple greetli; and made hym stidefast on hise enemyes.
019	PSA	105	025	He turnede the herte of hem, that thei hatiden his puple; and diden gile ayens hise seruauntis.
019	PSA	105	026	He sent Moises, his seruaunt; thilke Aaron, whom he chees.
019	PSA	105	027	He puttide in hem the wordis of hise myraclis; and of hise grete wondris in the lond of Cham.
019	PSA	105	028	He sente derknessis, and made derk; and he made not bitter hise wordis.
019	PSA	105	029	He turnede the watris of hem in to blood; and he killide the fischis of hem.
019	PSA	105	030	And the lond of hem yaf paddoks; in the priue places of the kyngis of hem.
019	PSA	105	031	God seide, and a fleische flie cam; and gnattis in alle the coostis of hem.
019	PSA	105	032	He settide her reynes hail; fier brennynge in the lond of hem.
019	PSA	105	033	And he smoot the vynes of hem, and the fige trees of hem; and al to-brak the tree of the coostis of hem.
019	PSA	105	034	He seide, and a locuste cam; and a bruk of which was noon noumbre.
019	PSA	105	035	And it eet al the hey in the lond of hem; and it eet al the fruyt of the lond of hem.
019	PSA	105	036	And he killide ech the firste gendrid thing in the lond of hem; the firste fruitis of alle the trauel of hem.
019	PSA	105	037	And he ledde out hem with siluer and gold; and noon was sijk in the lynagis of hem.
019	PSA	105	038	Egipt was glad in the goyng forth of hem; for the drede of hem lai on Egipcians.
019	PSA	105	039	He spredde abrood a cloude, in to the hiling of hem; and fier, that it schynede to hem bi nyyt.
019	PSA	105	040	Thei axiden, and a curlew cam; and he fillide hem with the breed of heuene.
019	PSA	105	041	He brak a stoon, and watris flowiden; floodis yeden forth in the drye place.
019	PSA	105	042	For he was myndeful of his hooli word; which he hadde to Abraham, his child.
