019	PSA	106	001	Alleluya. Kouleche ye to the Lord, for he is good; for his mercy is with outen ende.
019	PSA	106	002	Who schal speke the powers of the Lord; schal make knowun alle hise preisyngis?
019	PSA	106	003	Blessid ben thei that kepen dom; and doon riytfulnesse in al tyme.
019	PSA	106	004	Lord, haue thou mynde on vs in the good plesaunce of thi puple; visite thou vs in thin heelthe.
019	PSA	106	005	To se in the goodnesse of thi chosun men, to be glad in the gladnes of thi folk; that thou be heried with thin eritage.
019	PSA	106	006	We han synned with oure fadris; we han do vniustli, we han do wickidnesse.
019	PSA	106	007	Oure fadris in Egipt vndirstoden not thi merueils; thei weren not myndeful of the multitude of thi merci. And thei stiynge in to the see, in to the reed see, terreden to wraththe;
019	PSA	106	008	and he sauede hem for his name, that `he schulde make knowun his power.
