019	PSA	107	026	Thei stien til to heuenes, and goen doun `til to the depthis; the soule of hem failide in yuelis.
019	PSA	107	027	Thei weren troblid, and thei weren moued as a drunkun man; and al the wisdom of hem was deuourid.
019	PSA	107	028	And thei crieden to the Lord, whanne thei weren set in tribulacioun; and he ledde hem out of her nedynessis.
019	PSA	107	029	And he ordeynede the tempest therof in to a soft wynde; and the wawis therof weren stille.
019	PSA	107	030	And thei weren glad, for tho weren stille; and he ladde hem forth in to the hauene of her wille.
019	PSA	107	031	The mercies of the Lord knouleche to hym; and hise merueilis to the sones of men.
019	PSA	107	032	And enhaunse thei him in the chirche of the puple; and preise thei him in the chaier of eldre men.
019	PSA	107	033	He hath set floodis in to deseert; and the out goingis of watris in to thirst.
019	PSA	107	034	He hath set fruytful lond in to saltnesse; for the malice of men dwellyng ther ynne.
019	PSA	107	035	He hath set deseert in to pondis of watris; and erthe with out watir in to outgoyngis of watris.
019	PSA	107	036	And he settide there hungri men; and thei maden a citee of dwelling.
019	PSA	107	037	And thei sowiden feeldis, and plauntiden vynes; and maden fruyt of birthe.
019	PSA	107	038	And he blesside hem, and thei weren multiplied greetli; and he made not lesse her werk beestis.
019	PSA	107	039	And thei weren maad fewe; and thei weren trauelid of tribulacioun of yuelis and of sorewis.
019	PSA	107	040	Strijf was sched out on princes; and he made hem for to erre without the weie, and not in the weie.
019	PSA	107	041	And he helpide the pore man fro pouert; and settide meynees as a scheep bringynge forth lambren.
019	PSA	107	042	Riytful men schulen se, and schulen be glad; and al wickidnesse schal stoppe his mouth.
019	PSA	107	043	Who is wijs, and schal kepe these thingis; and schal vndirstonde the mercies of the Lord?
019	PSA	108	001	The song of `the salm of Dauid. Min herte is redi, God, myn herte is redi; Y schal singe, and Y schal seie salm in my glorie.
019	PSA	108	002	My glorie, ryse thou vp, sautrie and harp, rise thou vp; Y schal rise vp eerli.
019	PSA	108	003	Lord, Y schal knouleche to thee among puplis; and Y schal seie salm to thee among naciouns.
019	PSA	108	004	For whi, God, thi merci is greet on heuenes; and thi treuthe is til to the cloudis.
019	PSA	108	005	God, be thou enhaunsid aboue heuenes; and thi glorie ouer al erthe.
019	PSA	108	006	That thi derlingis be delyuerid, make thou saaf with thi riythond, and here me; God spak in his hooli.
019	PSA	108	007	I schal make ful out ioye, and Y schal departe Siccimam; and Y schal mete the grete valei of tabernaclis.
019	PSA	108	008	Galaad is myn, and Manasses is myn; and Effraym is the vptaking of myn heed. Juda is my king; Moab is the caudron of myn hope.
019	PSA	108	009	In to Ydume Y schal stretche forth my scho; aliens ben maad frendis to me.
019	PSA	108	010	Who schal lede me forth in to a stronge citee; who schal lede me forth til in to Idume?
019	PSA	108	011	Whether not thou, God, that hast put vs awei; and, God, schalt thou not go out in oure vertues?
019	PSA	108	012	Yyue thou help to vs of tribulacioun; for the heelthe of man is veyn.
019	PSA	108	013	We schulen make vertu in God; and he schal bringe oure enemyes to nouyt.
019	PSA	109	001	To victorye, the salm of Dauid.
019	PSA	109	002	God, holde thou not stille my preisyng; for the mouth of the synner, and the mouth of the gileful man is openyd on me.
019	PSA	109	003	Thei spaken ayens me with a gileful tunge, and thei cumpassiden me with wordis of hatrede; and fouyten ayens me with out cause.
019	PSA	109	004	For that thing that thei schulden loue me, thei bacbitiden me; but Y preiede.
019	PSA	109	005	And thei settiden ayens me yuelis for goodis; and hatrede for my loue.
019	PSA	109	006	Ordeyne thou a synner on him; and the deuel stonde on his riyt half.
019	PSA	109	007	Whanne he is demed, go he out condempned; and his preier `be maad in to synne.
019	PSA	109	008	Hise daies be maad fewe; and another take his bischopriche.
019	PSA	109	009	Hise sones be maad faderles; and his wijf a widewe.
019	PSA	109	010	Hise sones tremblinge be born ouer, and begge; and be cast out of her habitaciouns.
019	PSA	109	011	An vsurere seke al his catel; and aliens rauysche hise trauelis.
019	PSA	109	012	Noon helpere be to him; nether ony be that haue mercy on hise modirles children.
019	PSA	109	013	Hise sones be maad in to perisching; the name of him be don awei in oon generacioun.
019	PSA	109	014	The wickidnesse of hise fadris come ayen in to mynde in the siyt of the Lord; and the synne of his modir be not don awei.
019	PSA	109	015	Be thei maad euere ayens the Lord; and the mynde of hem perische fro erthe.
019	PSA	109	016	For that thing that he thouyte not to do merci,
019	PSA	109	017	and he pursuede a pore man and beggere; and to slee a man compunct in herte.
019	PSA	109	018	And he louede cursing, and it schal come to hym; and he nolde blessing, and it schal be maad fer fro him. And he clothide cursing as a cloth, and it entride as water in to hise ynnere thingis; and as oile in hise boonus.
019	PSA	109	019	Be it maad to him as a cloth, with which he is hilyd; and as a girdil, with which he is euere gird.
019	PSA	109	020	This is the werk of hem that bacbiten me anentis the Lord; and that speke yuels ayens my lijf.
019	PSA	109	021	And thou, Lord, Lord, do with me for thi name; for thi merci is swete.
019	PSA	109	022	Delyuere thou me, for Y am nedi and pore; and myn herte is disturblid with ynne me.
019	PSA	109	023	I am takun awei as a schadowe, whanne it bowith awei; and Y am schakun awei as locustis.
019	PSA	109	024	Mi knees ben maad feble of fasting; and my fleische was chaungid for oile.
019	PSA	109	025	And Y am maad schenschipe to hem; thei sien me, and moueden her heedis.
019	PSA	109	026	Mi Lord God, helpe thou me; make thou me saaf bi thi merci.
019	PSA	109	027	And thei schulen wite, that this is thin hond; and thou, Lord, hast do it.
019	PSA	109	028	Thei schulen curse, and thou schalt blesse, thei that risen ayens me, be schent; but thi seruaunt schal be glad.
019	PSA	109	029	Thei that bacbiten me, be clothid with schame; and be thei hilid with her schenschipe as with a double cloth.
019	PSA	109	030	I schal knouleche to the Lord greetli with my mouth; and Y schal herie hym in the myddil of many men.
019	PSA	109	031	Which stood nyy on the riyt half of a pore man; to make saaf my soule fro pursueris.
019	PSA	110	001	`The salm of Dauith. The Lord seide to my Lord; Sitte thou on my riyt side. Til Y putte thin enemyes; a stool of thi feet.
019	PSA	110	002	The Lord schal sende out fro Syon the yerde of thi vertu; be thou lord in the myddis of thin enemyes.
019	PSA	110	003	The bigynnyng is with thee in the dai of thi vertu, in the briytnessis of seyntis; Y gendride thee of the wombe before the dai sterre.
019	PSA	110	004	The Lord swoor, and it schal not repente him; Thou art a preest with outen ende, bi the ordre of Melchisedech.
019	PSA	110	005	The Lord on thi riyt side; hath broke kyngis in the dai of his veniaunce.
019	PSA	110	006	He schal deme among naciouns, he schal fille fallyngis; he schal schake heedis in the lond of many men.
019	PSA	110	007	He dranke of the stronde in the weie; therfor he enhaunside the heed.
019	PSA	111	001	Alleluya. Lord, Y schal knouleche to thee in al myn herte; in the counsel and congregacioun of iust men.
019	PSA	111	002	The werkis of the Lord ben greete; souyt out in to alle hise willis.
019	PSA	111	003	His werk is knoulechyng and grete doyng; and his riytfulnesse dwellith in to the world of world.
019	PSA	111	004	The Lord merciful in wille, and a merciful doere, hath maad a mynde of hise merueilis;
019	PSA	111	005	he hath youe meete to men dredynge hym. He schal be myndeful of his testament in to the world;
019	PSA	111	006	he schal telle to his puple the vertu of hise werkis.
019	PSA	111	007	That he yyue to hem the eritage of folkis; the werkis of hise hondis ben treuthe and doom.
019	PSA	111	008	Alle hise comaundementis ben feithful, confermed in to the world of world; maad in treuthe and equite.
019	PSA	111	009	The Lord sente redempcioun to hys puple; he comaundide his testament with outen ende. His name is hooli and dreedful;
019	PSA	111	010	the bigynnyng of wisdom is the drede of the Lord. Good vndirstondyng is to alle that doen it; his preising dwellith in to the world of world.
019	PSA	112	001	Alleluya. Blissid is the man that dredith the Lord; he schal wilne ful myche in hise comaundementis.
019	PSA	112	002	His seed schal be myyti in erthe; the generacioun of riytful men schal be blessid.
019	PSA	112	003	Glorie and richessis ben in his hous; and his riytfulnesse dwellith in to the world of world.
019	PSA	112	004	Liyt is risun vp in derknessis to riytful men; the Lord is merciful in wille, and a merciful doere, and riytful.
019	PSA	112	005	The man is merye, that doith merci, and leeneth; he disposith hise wordis in dom;
019	PSA	112	006	for he schal not be moued with outen ende.
019	PSA	112	007	A iust man schal be in euerlastinge mynde; he schal not drede of an yuel heryng. His herte is redi for to hope in the Lord;
019	PSA	112	008	his herte is confermed, he schal not be moued, til he dispise hise enemyes.
019	PSA	112	009	He spredde abrood, he yaf to pore men; his riytwisnesse dwellith in to the world of world; his horn schal be reisid in glorie.
019	PSA	112	010	A synner schal se, and schal be wrooth; he schal gnaste with hise teeth, and schal faile; the desijr of synneris schal perische.
019	PSA	113	001	Alleluya. Children, preise ye the Lord; preise ye the name of the Lord.
019	PSA	113	002	The name of the Lord be blessid; fro this tyme now and til in to the world.
019	PSA	113	003	Fro the risyng of the sunne til to the goyng doun; the name of the Lord is worthi to be preisid.
019	PSA	113	004	The Lord is hiy aboue alle folkis; and his glorie is aboue heuenes.
019	PSA	113	005	Who is as oure Lord God, that dwellith in hiye thingis;
019	PSA	113	006	and biholdith meke thingis in heuene and in erthe?
019	PSA	113	007	Reisynge a nedi man fro the erthe; and enhaunsinge a pore man fro drit.
019	PSA	113	008	That he sette hym with princes; with the princes of his puple.
019	PSA	113	009	Which makith a bareyn womman dwelle in the hous; a glad modir of sones.
019	PSA	114	001	Alleluya. In the goyng out of Israel fro Egipt; of the hous of Jacob fro the hethene puple.
019	PSA	114	002	Judee was maad the halewyng of hym; Israel the power of hym.
019	PSA	114	003	The see siy, and fledde; Jordan was turned abac.
019	PSA	114	004	Munteyns ful out ioyeden as rammes; and litle hillis as the lambren of scheep.
019	PSA	114	005	Thou see, what was to thee, for thou fleddist; and thou, Jordan, for thou were turned abak?
019	PSA	114	006	Munteyns, ye maden ful out ioye as rammes; and litle hillis, as the lambren of scheep.
019	PSA	114	007	The erthe was moued fro the face of `the Lord; fro the face of God of Jacob.
019	PSA	114	008	Which turnede a stoon in to pondis of watris; and an hard rooch in to wellis of watris.
019	PSA	115	001	Lord, not to vs, not to vs; but yyue thou glorie to thi name.
019	PSA	115	002	On thi merci and thi treuthe; lest ony tyme hethene men seien, Where is the God of hem?
019	PSA	115	003	Forsothe oure God in heuene; dide alle thingis, whiche euere he wolde.
019	PSA	115	004	The symulacris of hethene men ben siluer and gold; the werkis of mennus hondis.
019	PSA	115	005	Tho han mouth, and schulen not speke; tho han iyen, and schulen not se.
019	PSA	115	006	Tho han eeris, and schulen not here; tho han nose thurls, and schulen not smelle.
019	PSA	115	007	Tho han hondis, and schulen not grope; tho han feet, and schulen not go; tho schulen not crye in her throte.
019	PSA	115	008	Thei that maken tho ben maad lijk tho; and alle that triste in tho.
019	PSA	115	009	The hous of Israel hopide in the Lord; he is the helpere `of hem, and the defendere of hem.
019	PSA	115	010	The hous of Aaron hopide in the Lord; he is the helpere of hem, and the defendere of hem.
019	PSA	115	011	Thei that dreden the Lord, hopiden in the Lord; he is the helpere of hem, and the defendere of hem.
019	PSA	115	012	The Lord was myndeful of vs; and blesside vs. He blesside the hous of Israel; he blesside the hous of Aaron.
019	PSA	115	013	He blesside alle men that dreden the Lord; `he blesside litle `men with the grettere.
019	PSA	115	014	The Lord encreesse on you; on you and on youre sones.
019	PSA	115	015	Blessid be ye of the Lord; that made heuene and erthe.
019	PSA	115	016	Heuene of `heuene is to the Lord; but he yaf erthe to the sones of men.
019	PSA	115	017	Lord, not deed men schulen herie thee; nether alle men that goen doun in to helle.
019	PSA	115	018	But we that lyuen, blessen the Lord; fro this tyme now and til in to the world.
019	PSA	116	001	Alleluia. I louede `the Lord; for the Lord schal here the vois of my preier.
019	PSA	116	002	For he bowide doun his eere to me; and Y schal inwardli clepe in my daies.
019	PSA	116	003	The sorewis of deth cumpassiden me; and the perelis of helle founden me. I foond tribulacioun and sorewe;
019	PSA	116	004	and Y clepide inwardli the name of the Lord. Thou, Lord, delyuere my soule;
019	PSA	116	005	the Lord is merciful, and iust; and oure God doith merci.
019	PSA	116	006	And the Lord kepith litle children; Y was mekid, and he delyuerede me.
019	PSA	116	007	Mi soule, turne thou in to thi reste; for the Lord hath do wel to thee.
019	PSA	116	008	For he hath delyuered my soule fro deth; myn iyen fro wepingis, my feet fro fallyng doun.
019	PSA	116	009	I schal plese the Lord; in the cuntrei of hem that lyuen.
019	PSA	116	010	I bileuede, for which thing Y spak; forsoth Y was maad low ful myche.
019	PSA	116	011	I seide in my passing; Ech man is a lier.
019	PSA	116	012	What schal Y yelde to the Lord; for alle thingis which he yeldide to me?
019	PSA	116	013	I schal take the cuppe of heelthe; and Y schal inwardli clepe the name of the Lord.
019	PSA	116	014	I schal yelde my vowis to the Lord bifor al his puple;
019	PSA	116	015	the deth of seyntis of the Lord is precious in his siyt.
019	PSA	116	016	O! Lord, for Y am thi seruant; Y am thi seruaunt, and the sone of thi handmaide. Thou hast broke my bondys,
019	PSA	116	017	to thee Y schal offre a sacrifice of heriyng; and Y schal inwardli clepe the name of the Lord.
019	PSA	116	018	I schal yelde my vowis to the Lord, in the siyt of al his puple;
019	PSA	116	019	in the porchis of the hous of the Lord, in the myddil of thee, Jerusalem.
019	PSA	117	001	Alleluya. Alle hethen men, herie ye the Lord; alle puplis, herie ye hym.
019	PSA	117	002	For his merci is confermyd on vs; and the treuthe of the Lord dwellith with outen ende.
019	PSA	118	001	Alleluia. Knouleche ye to the Lord, for he is good; for his merci is with outen ende.
019	PSA	118	002	Israel seie now, for he is good; for his merci is with outen ende.
019	PSA	118	003	The hous of Aaron seie now; for his merci is with outen ende.
019	PSA	118	004	Thei that dreden the Lord, seie now; for his merci is withouten ende.
019	PSA	118	005	Of tribulacioun Y inwardli clepide the Lord; and the Lord herde me in largenesse.
019	PSA	118	006	The Lord is an helpere to me; Y schal not drede what a man schal do to me.
019	PSA	118	007	The Lord is an helpere to me; and Y schal dispise myn enemyes.
019	PSA	118	008	It is betere for to trist in the Lord; than for to triste in man.
019	PSA	118	009	It is betere for to hope in the Lord; than for to hope in princes.
019	PSA	118	010	Alle folkis cumpassiden me; and in the name of the Lord it bifelde, for Y am auengide on hem.
019	PSA	118	011	Thei cumpassinge cumpassiden me; and in the name of the Lord, for Y am auengid on hem.
019	PSA	118	012	Thei cumpassiden me as been, and thei brenten out as fier doith among thornes; and in the name of the Lord, for Y am avengid on hem.
019	PSA	118	013	I was hurlid, and turnede vpsedoun, that Y schulde falle doun; and the Lord took me vp.
019	PSA	118	014	The Lord is my strengthe, and my heryyng; and he is maad to me in to heelthe.
019	PSA	118	015	The vois of ful out ioiyng and of heelthe; be in the tabernaclis of iust men.
019	PSA	118	016	The riyt hond of the Lord hath do vertu, the riyt hond of the Lord enhaunside me; the riyt hond of the Lord hath do vertu.
019	PSA	118	017	I schal not die, but Y schal lyue; and Y schal telle the werkis of the Lord.
019	PSA	118	018	The Lord chastisinge hath chastisid me; and he yaf not me to deth.
019	PSA	118	019	Opene ye to me the yatis of riytfulnesse, and Y schal entre bi tho, and Y schal knouleche to the Lord;
019	PSA	118	020	this yate is of the Lord, and iust men schulen entre bi it.
019	PSA	118	021	I schal knouleche to thee, for thou herdist me; and art maad to me in to heelthe.
019	PSA	118	022	The stoon which the bilderis repreueden; this is maad in to the heed of the corner.
019	PSA	118	023	This thing is maad of the Lord; and it is wonderful bifore oure iyen.
019	PSA	118	024	This is the dai which the Lord made; make we ful out ioye, and be we glad ther ynne.
019	PSA	118	025	O! Lord, make thou me saaf, O! Lord, make thou wel prosperite;
019	PSA	118	026	blessid is he that cometh in the name of the Lord. We blesseden you of the hous of the Lord;
019	PSA	118	027	God is Lord, and hath youe liyt to vs. Ordeyne ye a solempne dai in thicke puplis; til to the horn of the auter.
019	PSA	118	028	Thou art my God, and Y schal knouleche to thee; thou art my God, and Y schal enhaunse thee. I schal knouleche to thee, for thou herdist me; and thou art maad to me in to heelthe.
019	PSA	118	029	Knouleche ye to the Lord, for he is good; for his merci is with outen ende.
019	PSA	119	001	Alleluia. Blessid ben men with out wem in the weie; that gon in the lawe of the Lord.
019	PSA	119	002	Blessid ben thei, that seken hise witnessingis; seken him in al the herte.
019	PSA	119	003	For thei that worchen wickidnesse; yeden not in hise weies.
019	PSA	119	004	Thou hast comaundid; that thin heestis be kept greetly.
019	PSA	119	005	I wolde that my weies be dressid; to kepe thi iustifiyngis.
019	PSA	119	006	Thanne Y schal not be schent; whanne Y schal biholde perfitli in alle thin heestis.
019	PSA	119	007	I schal knouleche to thee in the dressing of herte; in that that Y lernyde the domes of thi riytfulnesse.
019	PSA	119	008	I schal kepe thi iustifiyngis; forsake thou not me on ech side.
019	PSA	119	009	In what thing amendith a yong waxinge man his weie? in keping thi wordis.
019	PSA	119	010	In al myn herte Y souyte thee; putte thou me not awei fro thin heestis.
019	PSA	119	011	In myn herte Y hidde thi spechis; that Y do not synne ayens thee.
019	PSA	119	012	Lord, thou art blessid; teche thou me thi iustifiyngis.
019	PSA	119	013	In my lippis Y haue pronounsid; alle the domes of thi mouth.
019	PSA	119	014	I delitide in the weie of thi witnessingis; as in alle richessis.
019	PSA	119	015	I schal be ocupied in thin heestis; and Y schal biholde thi weies.
019	PSA	119	016	I schal bithenke in thi iustifiyngis; Y schal not foryete thi wordis.
019	PSA	119	017	Yelde to thi seruaunt; quiken thou me, and Y schal kepe thi wordis.
019	PSA	119	018	Liytne thou myn iyen; and Y schal biholde the merueils of thi lawe.
019	PSA	119	019	I am a comeling in erthe; hide thou not thin heestis fro me.
019	PSA	119	020	Mi soule coueitide to desire thi iustifiyngis; in al tyme.
019	PSA	119	021	Thou blamedist the proude; thei ben cursid, that bowen awei fro thin heestis.
019	PSA	119	022	Do thou awei `fro me schenschipe and dispising; for Y souyte thi witnessingis.
019	PSA	119	023	For whi princis saten, and spaken ayens me; but thi seruaunt was exercisid in thi iustifiyngis.
019	PSA	119	024	For whi and thi witnessyngis is my thenkyng; and my counsel is thi iustifiyngis.
019	PSA	119	025	Mi soule cleuede to the pawment; quykine thou me bi thi word.
019	PSA	119	026	I telde out my weies, and thou herdist me; teche thou me thi iustifiyngis.
019	PSA	119	027	Lerne thou me the weie of thi iustifiyngis; and Y schal be exercisid in thi merueils.
019	PSA	119	028	Mi soule nappide for anoye; conferme thou me in thi wordis.
019	PSA	119	029	Remoue thou fro me the weie of wickidnesse; and in thi lawe haue thou merci on me.
019	PSA	119	030	I chees the weie of treuthe; Y foryat not thi domes.
019	PSA	119	031	Lord, Y cleuede to thi witnessyngis; nyle thou schende me.
019	PSA	119	032	I ran the weie of thi comaundementis; whanne thou alargidist myn herte.
019	PSA	119	033	Lord, sette thou to me a lawe, the weie of thi iustifiyngis; and Y schal seke it euere.
019	PSA	119	034	Yyue thou vndurstonding to me, and Y schal seke thi lawe; and Y schal kepe it in al myn herte.
019	PSA	119	035	Lede me forth in the path of thin heestis; for Y wolde it.
019	PSA	119	036	`Bowe thou myn herte in to thi witnessingus; and not in to aueryce.
019	PSA	119	037	Turne thou awei myn iyen, that `tho seen not vanyte; quykene thou me in thi weie.
019	PSA	119	038	Ordeyne thi speche to thi seruaunt; in thi drede.
019	PSA	119	039	Kitte awey my schenschip, which Y supposide; for thi domes ben myrie.
019	PSA	119	040	Lo! Y coueitide thi comaundementis; quikene thou me in thin equite.
019	PSA	119	041	And, Lord, thi merci come on me; thin heelthe come bi thi speche.
019	PSA	119	042	And Y schal answere a word to men seiynge schenschipe to me; for Y hopide in thi wordis.
019	PSA	119	043	And take thou not awei fro my mouth the word of treuthe outerli; for Y hopide aboue in thi domes.
019	PSA	119	044	And Y schal kepe thi lawe euere; in to the world, and in to the world of world.
019	PSA	119	045	And Y yede in largenesse; for Y souyte thi comaundementis.
019	PSA	119	046	And Y spak of thi witnessyngis in the siyt of kingis; and Y was not schent.
019	PSA	119	047	And Y bithouyte in thin heestis; whiche Y louede.
019	PSA	119	048	And Y reiside myn hondis to thi comaundementis, whiche Y louede; and Y schal be excercisid in thi iustifiyngis.
019	PSA	119	049	Lord, haue thou mynde on thi word to thi seruaunt; in which word thou hast youe hope to me.
019	PSA	119	050	This coumfortide me in my lownesse; for thi word quikenede me.
019	PSA	119	051	Proude men diden wickidli bi alle thingis; but Y bowide not awei fro thi lawe.
019	PSA	119	052	Lord, Y was myndeful on thi domes fro the world; and Y was coumfortid.
019	PSA	119	053	Failing helde me; for synneris forsakinge thi lawe.
019	PSA	119	054	Thi iustifiyngis weren delitable to me to be sungun; in the place of my pilgrimage.
019	PSA	119	055	Lord, Y hadde mynde of thi name bi niyt; and Y kepte thi lawe.
019	PSA	119	056	This thing was maad to me; for Y souyte thi iustifiyngis.
019	PSA	119	057	Lord, my part; Y seide to kepe thi lawe.
019	PSA	119	058	I bisouyte thi face in al myn herte; haue thou merci on me bi thi speche.
019	PSA	119	059	I bithouyte my weies; and Y turnede my feet in to thi witnessyngis.
019	PSA	119	060	I am redi, and Y am not disturblid; to kepe thi comaundementis.
019	PSA	119	061	The coordis of synneris han biclippid me; and Y haue not foryete thi lawe.
019	PSA	119	062	At mydnyyt Y roos to knouleche to thee; on the domes of thi iustifiyngis.
019	PSA	119	063	I am parcener of alle that dreden thee; and kepen thin heestis.
019	PSA	119	064	Lord, the erthe is ful of thi merci; teche thou me thi iustifiyngis.
019	PSA	119	065	Lord, thou hast do goodnesse with thi seruaunt; bi thi word.
019	PSA	119	066	Teche thou me goodnesse, and loore, and kunnyng; for Y bileuede to thin heestis.
019	PSA	119	067	Bifor that Y was maad meke, Y trespasside; therfor Y kepte thi speche.
019	PSA	119	068	Thou art good; and in thi goodnesse teche thou me thi iustifiyngis.
019	PSA	119	069	The wickidnesse of hem that ben proude, is multiplied on me; but in al myn herte Y schal seke thin heestis.
019	PSA	119	070	The herte of hem is cruddid as mylk; but Y bithouyte thi lawe.
019	PSA	119	071	It is good to me, that thou hast maad me meke; that Y lerne thi iustifiyngis.
019	PSA	119	072	The lawe of thi mouth is betere to me; than thousyndis of gold and of siluer.
019	PSA	119	073	Thin hondis maden me, and fourmeden me; yyue thou vndurstondyng to me, that Y lerne thin heestis.
019	PSA	119	074	Thei that dreden thee schulen se me, and schulen be glad; for Y hopide more on thi wordis.
019	PSA	119	075	Lord, Y knewe, that thi domes ben equite; and in thi treuth thou hast maad me meke.
019	PSA	119	076	Thi merci be maad, that it coumforte me; bi thi speche to thi seruaunt.
019	PSA	119	077	Thi merciful doyngis come to me, and Y schal lyue; for thi lawe is my thenkyng.
019	PSA	119	078	Thei that ben proude be schent, for vniustli thei diden wickidnesse ayens me; but Y schal be exercisid in thin heestis.
019	PSA	119	079	Thei that dreden thee be turned to me; and thei that knowen thi witnessyngis.
019	PSA	119	080	Myn herte be maad vnwemmed in thi iustifiyngis; that Y be not schent.
019	PSA	119	081	Mi soule failide in to thin helthe; and Y hopide more on thi word.
019	PSA	119	082	Myn iyen failiden in to thi speche; seiynge, Whanne schalt thou coumforte me?
019	PSA	119	083	For Y am maad as a bowge in frost; Y haue not foryete thi iustifiyngis.
019	PSA	119	084	Hou many ben the daies of thi seruaunt; whanne thou schalt make doom of hem that pursuen me?
019	PSA	119	085	Wickid men telden to me ianglyngis; but not as thi lawe.
019	PSA	119	086	Alle thi comaundementis ben treuthe; wickid men han pursued me, helpe thou me.
019	PSA	119	087	Almeest thei endiden me in erthe; but I forsook not thi comaundementis.
019	PSA	119	088	Bi thi mersi quikene thou me; and Y schal kepe the witnessingis of thi mouth.
019	PSA	119	089	Lord, thi word dwellith in heuene; with outen ende.
019	PSA	119	090	Thi treuthe dwellith in generacioun, and in to generacioun; thou hast foundid the erthe, and it dwellith.
019	PSA	119	091	The dai lastith contynueli bi thi ordynaunce; for alle thingis seruen to thee.
019	PSA	119	092	No but that thi lawe was my thenking; thanne perauenture Y hadde perischid in my lownesse.
019	PSA	119	093	With outen ende Y schal not foryete thi iustifiyngis; for in tho thou hast quikened me.
019	PSA	119	094	I am thin, make thou me saaf; for Y haue souyt thi iustifiyngis.
019	PSA	119	095	Synneris aboden me, for to leese me; Y vndurstood thi witnessingis.
019	PSA	119	096	I siy the ende of al ende; thi comaundement is ful large.
019	PSA	119	097	Lord, hou louede Y thi lawe; al dai it is my thenking.
019	PSA	119	098	Aboue myn enemyes thou madist me prudent bi thi comaundement; for it is to me with outen ende.
019	PSA	119	099	I vndurstood aboue alle men techinge me; for thi witnessingis is my thenking.
019	PSA	119	100	I vndirstood aboue eelde men; for Y souyte thi comaundementis.
019	PSA	119	101	I forbeed my feet fro al euel weie; that Y kepe thi wordis.
019	PSA	119	102	I bowide not fro thi domes; for thou hast set lawe to me.
019	PSA	119	103	Thi spechis ben ful swete to my cheekis; aboue hony to my mouth.
019	PSA	119	104	I vnderstood of thin heestis; therfor Y hatide al the weie of wickidnesse.
019	PSA	119	105	Thi word is a lanterne to my feet; and liyt to my pathis.
019	PSA	119	106	I swoor, and purposide stidefastli; to kepe the domes of thi riytfulnesse.
019	PSA	119	107	I am maad low bi alle thingis; Lord, quykene thou me bi thi word.
019	PSA	119	108	Lord, make thou wel plesinge the wilful thingis of my mouth; and teche thou me thi domes.
019	PSA	119	109	Mi soule is euere in myn hondis; and Y foryat not thi lawe.
019	PSA	119	110	Synneris settiden a snare to me; and Y erride not fro thi comaundementis.
019	PSA	119	111	I purchasside thi witnessyngis bi eritage with outen ende; for tho ben the ful ioiyng of myn herte.
019	PSA	119	112	I bowide myn herte to do thi iustifiyngis with outen ende; for reward.
019	PSA	119	113	I hatide wickid men; and Y louede thi lawe.
019	PSA	119	114	Thou art myn helpere, and my `taker vp; and Y hopide more on thi word.
019	PSA	119	115	Ye wickide men, bowe awei fro me; and Y schal seke the comaundementis of my God.
019	PSA	119	116	Vp take thou me bi thi word, and Y schal lyue; and schende thou not me fro myn abydyng.
019	PSA	119	117	Helpe thou me, and Y schal be saaf; and Y schal bithenke euere in thi iustifiyngis.
019	PSA	119	118	Thou hast forsake alle men goynge awey fro thi domes; for the thouyt of hem is vniust.
019	PSA	119	119	I arettide alle the synneris of erthe brekeris of the lawe; therfor Y louede thi witnessyngis.
019	PSA	119	120	Naile thou my fleischis with thi drede; for Y dredde of thi domes.
019	PSA	119	121	I dide doom and riytwisnesse; bitake thou not me to hem that falsli chalengen me.
019	PSA	119	122	Take vp thi seruaunt in to goodnesse; thei that ben proude chalenge not me.
019	PSA	119	123	Myn iyen failiden in to thin helthe; and in to the speche of thi riytfulnesse.
019	PSA	119	124	Do thou with thi seruaunt bi thi merci; and teche thou me thi iustifiyngis.
019	PSA	119	125	I am thi seruaunt, yyue thou vndurstondyng to me; that Y kunne thi witnessingis.
019	PSA	119	126	Lord, it is tyme to do; thei han distried thi lawe.
