019	PSA	119	134	Ayeyn bie thou me fro the false chalengis of men; that Y kepe thin heestis.
019	PSA	119	135	Liytne thi face on thi seruaunt; and teche thou me thi iustifiyngis.
019	PSA	119	136	Myn iyen ledden forth the outgoynges of watris; for thei kepten not thi lawe.
019	PSA	119	137	Lord, thou art iust; and thi dom is riytful.
019	PSA	119	138	Thou hast comaundid riytfulnesse, thi witnessingis; and thi treuthe greetli to be kept.
019	PSA	119	139	Mi feruent loue made me to be meltid; for myn enemys foryaten thi wordis.
019	PSA	119	140	Thi speche is greetli enflawmed; and thi seruaunt louede it.
019	PSA	119	141	I am yong, and dispisid; Y foryat not thi iustifiyngis.
019	PSA	119	142	Lord, thi riytfulnesse is riytfulnesse with outen ende; and thi lawe is treuthe.
019	PSA	119	143	Tribulacioun and angwische founden me; thin heestis is my thenking.
019	PSA	119	144	Thi witnessyngis is equite with outen ende; yyue thou vndirstondyng to me, and Y schal lyue.
019	PSA	119	145	I criede in al myn herte, Lord, here thou me; and Y schal seke thi iustifiyngis.
019	PSA	119	146	I criede to thee, make thou me saaf; that Y kepe thi comaundementis.
019	PSA	119	147	I bifor cam in ripenesse, and Y criede; Y hopide aboue on thi wordis.
