019	PSA	120	001	The song of greces. Whanne Y was set in tribulacioun, Y criede to the Lord; and he herde me.
019	PSA	120	002	Lord, delyuere thou my soule fro wickid lippis; and fro a gileful tunge.
019	PSA	120	003	What schal be youun to thee, ether what schal be leid to thee; to a gileful tunge?
019	PSA	120	004	Scharpe arowis of the myyti; with colis that maken desolat.
019	PSA	120	005	Allas to me! for my dwelling in an alien lond is maad long, Y dwellide with men dwellinge in Cedar; my soule was myche a comelyng.
019	PSA	120	006	I was pesible with hem that hatiden pees;
019	PSA	120	007	whanne Y spak to hem, thei ayenseiden me with outen cause.
019	PSA	121	001	The song of greces. I reiside myn iyen to the hillis; fro whannus help schal come to me.
019	PSA	121	002	Myn help is of the Lord; that made heuene and erthe.
019	PSA	121	003	The Lord yyue not thi foot in to mouyng; nether he nappe, that kepith thee.
019	PSA	121	004	Lo! he schal not nappe, nether slepe; that kepith Israel.
019	PSA	121	005	The Lord kepith thee; the Lord is thi proteccioun aboue thi riythond.
019	PSA	121	006	The sunne schal not brenne thee bi dai; nether the moone bi nyyt.
019	PSA	121	007	The Lord kepe thee fro al yuel; the Lord kepe thi soule.
019	PSA	121	008	The Lord kepe thi goyng in and thi goyng out; fro this tyme now and in to the world.
019	PSA	122	001	The song of the grecis of Dauid. I am glad in these thingis, that ben seid to me; We schulen go in to the hous of the Lord.
019	PSA	122	002	Oure feet weren stondynge; in thi hallis, thou Jerusalem.
019	PSA	122	003	Jerusalem, which is bildid as a citee; whos part taking therof is in to the same thing.
019	PSA	122	004	For the lynagis, the lynagis of the Lord stieden thidir, the witnessing of Israel; to knouleche to the name of the Lord.
019	PSA	122	005	For thei saten there on seetis in doom; seetis on the hous of Dauid.
019	PSA	122	006	Preie ye tho thingis, that ben to the pees of Jerusalem; and abundaunce be to hem that louen thee.
019	PSA	122	007	Pees be maad in thi vertu; and abundaunce in thi touris.
019	PSA	122	008	For my britheren and my neiyboris; Y spak pees of thee.
019	PSA	122	009	For the hous of oure Lord God; Y souyte goodis to thee.
019	PSA	123	001	`The song of grecis. To thee Y haue reisid myn iyen; that dwellist in heuenes.
019	PSA	123	002	Lo! as the iyen of seruauntis; ben in the hondis of her lordis. As the iyen of the handmaide ben in the hondis of her ladi; so oure iyen ben to oure Lord God, til he haue mercy on vs.
019	PSA	123	003	Lord, haue thou merci on vs, haue thou merci on vs; for we ben myche fillid with dispisyng.
019	PSA	123	004	For oure soule is myche fillid; we ben schenschipe to hem that ben abundaunte with richessis, and dispising to proude men.
019	PSA	124	001	The song of grecis `of Dauith. Israel seie now, No but for the Lord was in vs;
019	PSA	124	002	no but for `the Lord was in vs. Whanne men risiden vp ayens vs;
019	PSA	124	003	in hap thei hadden swalewid vs quike. Whanne the woodnesse of hem was wrooth ayens vs;
019	PSA	124	004	in hap watir hadde sope vs vp.
019	PSA	124	005	Oure soule passide thoruy a stronde; in hap oure soule hadde passide thoruy a watir vnsuffrable.
019	PSA	124	006	Blessid be the Lord; that `yaf not vs in taking to the teeth of hem.
019	PSA	124	007	Oure soule, as a sparowe, is delyuered; fro the snare of hunters. The snare is al to-brokun; and we ben delyuered.
019	PSA	124	008	Oure helpe is in the name of the Lord; that made heuene and erthe.
019	PSA	125	001	`The song of greces. Thei that tristen in the Lord ben as the hil of Syon; he schal not be moued with outen ende,
019	PSA	125	002	that dwellith in Jerusalem. Hillis ben in the cumpas of it, and the Lord is in the cumpas of his puple; fro this tyme now and in to the world.
019	PSA	125	003	For the Lord schal not leeue the yerde of synneris on the part of iust men; that iust men holde not forth her hondis to wickidnesse.
019	PSA	125	004	Lord, do thou wel; to good men, and of riytful herte.
019	PSA	125	005	But the Lord schal lede them that bowen in to obligaciouns, with hem that worchen wickidnesse; pees be on Israel.
019	PSA	126	001	The song of grecis. Whanne the Lord turnede the caitifte of Sion; we weren maad as coumfortid.
019	PSA	126	002	Thanne oure mouth was fillid with ioye; and oure tunge with ful out ioiyng. Thanne thei schulen seie among hethene men; The Lord magnefiede to do with hem.
019	PSA	126	003	The Lord magnefiede to do with vs; we ben maad glad.
019	PSA	126	004	Lord, turne thou oure caitifte; as a stronde in the south.
019	PSA	126	005	Thei that sowen in teeris; schulen repe in ful out ioiyng.
019	PSA	126	006	Thei goynge yeden, and wepten; sendynge her seedis. But thei comynge schulen come with ful out ioiyng; berynge her handfullis.
019	PSA	127	001	The song of greces of Salomon. `No but the Lord bilde the hous; thei that bilden it han trauelid in veyn. No but the Lord kepith the citee; he wakith in veyn that kepith it.
019	PSA	127	002	It is veyn to you to rise bifore the liyt; rise ye after that ye han sete, that eten the breed of sorewe. Whanne he schal yyue sleep to his loued; lo!
019	PSA	127	003	the eritage of the Lord `is sones, the mede is the fruyt of wombe.
019	PSA	127	004	As arowis ben in the hond of the miyti; so the sones of hem that ben schakun out.
019	PSA	127	005	Blessid is the man, that hath fillid his desier of tho; he schal not be schent, whanne he schal speke to hise enemyes in the yate.
019	PSA	128	001	The song of greces. Blessid ben alle men, that dreden the Lord; that gon in hise weies.
019	PSA	128	002	For thou schalt ete the trauels of thin hondis; thou art blessid, and it schal be wel to thee.
019	PSA	128	003	Thi wijf as a plenteous vyne; in the sidis of thin hous. Thi sones as the newe sprenges of olyue trees; in the cumpas of thi bord.
019	PSA	128	004	Lo! so a man schal be blessid; that dredith the Lord.
019	PSA	128	005	The Lord blesse thee fro Syon; and se thou the goodis of Jerusalem in alle the daies of thi lijf.
019	PSA	128	006	And se thou the sones of thi sones; se thou pees on Israel.
019	PSA	129	001	The song of greces. Israel seie now; Ofte thei fouyten ayens me fro my yongth.
019	PSA	129	002	Ofte thei fouyten ayens me fro my yongthe; and sotheli thei miyten not to me.
019	PSA	129	003	Synneris forgeden on my bak; thei maden long her wickidnesse.
019	PSA	129	004	The `iust Lord schal beete the nollis of synneris;
019	PSA	129	005	alle that haten Sion be schent, and turned abak.
019	PSA	129	006	Be thei maad as the hey of hous coppis; that driede vp, bifore that it be drawun vp.
