019	PSA	137	001	On the floodis of Babiloyne there we saten, and wepten; while we bithouyten on Syon.
019	PSA	137	002	In salewis in the myddil therof; we hangiden vp oure orguns.
019	PSA	137	003	For thei that ledden vs prisoners; axiden vs there the wordis of songis. And thei that ledden awei vs seiden; Synge ye to vs an ympne of the songis of Syon.
019	PSA	137	004	Hou schulen we singe a songe of the Lord; in an alien lond?
019	PSA	137	005	If Y foryete thee, Jerusalem; my riyt hond be youun to foryeting.
019	PSA	137	006	Mi tunge cleue to my chekis; if Y bithenke not on thee. If Y purposide not of thee, Jerusalem; in the bigynnyng of my gladnesse.
019	PSA	137	007	Lord, haue thou mynde on the sones of Edom; for the dai of Jerusalem. Whiche seien, Anyntische ye, anyntische ye; `til to the foundement ther ynne.
019	PSA	137	008	Thou wretchid douyter of Babiloyne; he is blessid, that `schal yelde to thee thi yelding, which thou yeldidist to vs.
019	PSA	137	009	He is blessid, that schal holde; and hurtle doun hise litle children at a stoon.
019	PSA	138	001	`To Dauith him silf. Lord, Y schal knouleche to thee in al myn herte; for thou herdist the wordis of my mouth. Mi God, Y schal singe to thee in the siyt of aungels;
019	PSA	138	002	Y schal worschipe to thin hooli temple, and Y schal knouleche to thi name. On thi merci and thi treuthe; for thou hast magnefied thin hooli name aboue al thing.
019	PSA	138	003	In what euere dai Y schal inwardli clepe thee, here thou me; thou schalt multipli vertu in my soule.
019	PSA	138	004	Lord, alle the kingis of erthe knouleche to thee; for thei herden alle the wordis of thi mouth.
019	PSA	138	005	And singe thei in the weies of the Lord; for the glorie of the Lord is greet.
019	PSA	138	006	For the Lord is hiy, and biholdith meke thingis; and knowith afer hiy thingis.
019	PSA	138	007	If Y schal go in the myddil of tribulacioun, thou schalt quikene me; and thou stretchidist forth thin hond on the ire of myn enemyes, and thi riyt hond made me saaf.
019	PSA	138	008	The Lord schal yelde for me, Lord, thi merci is with outen ende; dispise thou not the werkis of thin hondis.
019	PSA	139	001	`To victorie, the salm of Dauith. Lord, thou hast preued me, and hast knowe me;
019	PSA	139	002	thou hast knowe my sitting, and my rising ayen.
019	PSA	139	003	Thou hast vndirstonde my thouytis fro fer; thou hast enquerid my path and my corde.
019	PSA	139	004	And thou hast bifor seien alle my weies; for no word is in my tunge.
019	PSA	139	005	Lo! Lord, thou hast knowe alle thingis, the laste thingis and elde; thou hast formed me, and hast set thin hond on me.
019	PSA	139	006	Thi kunnyng is maad wondirful of me; it is coumfortid, and Y schal not mowe to it.
019	PSA	139	007	Whidir schal Y go fro thi spirit; and whider schal Y fle fro thi face?
019	PSA	139	008	If Y schal stie in to heuene, thou art there; if Y schal go doun to helle, thou art present.
019	PSA	139	009	If Y schal take my fetheris ful eerli; and schal dwelle in the last partis of the see.
019	PSA	139	010	And sotheli thider thin hond schal leede me forth; and thi riyt hond schal holde me.
019	PSA	139	011	And Y seide, In hap derknessis schulen defoule me; and the nyyt is my liytnyng in my delicis.
019	PSA	139	012	For whi derknessis schulen not be maad derk fro thee, aud the niyt schal be liytned as the dai; as the derknessis therof, so and the liyt therof.
019	PSA	139	013	For thou haddist in possessioun my reines; thou tokist me vp fro the wombe of my modir.
019	PSA	139	014	I schal knouleche to thee, for thou art magnefied dreedfuli; thi werkis ben wondirful, and my soule schal knouleche ful miche.
019	PSA	139	015	Mi boon, which thou madist in priuete, is not hyd fro thee; and my substaunce in the lower partis of erthe.
019	PSA	139	016	Thin iyen sien myn vnperfit thing, and alle men schulen be writun in thi book; daies schulen be formed, and no man is in tho.
019	PSA	139	017	Forsothe, God, thi frendis ben maad onourable ful myche to me; the princeheed of hem is coumfortid ful myche.
019	PSA	139	018	I schal noumbre hem, and thei schulen be multiplied aboue grauel; Y roos vp, and yit Y am with thee.
019	PSA	139	019	For thou, God, schalt slee synneris; ye menquelleris, bowe awei fro me.
019	PSA	139	020	For ye seien in thouyt; Take thei her citees in vanite.
019	PSA	139	021	Lord, whether Y hatide not hem that hatiden thee; and Y failide on thin enemyes?
019	PSA	139	022	Bi perfite haterede Y hatide hem; thei weren maad enemyes to me.
019	PSA	139	023	God, preue thou me, and knowe thou myn herte; axe thou me, and knowe thou my pathis.
019	PSA	139	024	And se thou, if weie of wickidnesse is in me; and lede thou me forth in euerlastinge wei.
019	PSA	140	001	To victorie, the salm of Dauith. Lord, delyuere thou me fro an yuel man; delyuere thou me fro a wickid man.
019	PSA	140	002	Whiche thouyten wickidnesses in the herte; al dai thei ordeyneden batels.
019	PSA	140	003	Thei scharpiden her tungis as serpentis; the venym of snakis vndir the lippis of hem.
019	PSA	140	004	Lord, kepe thou me fro the hond of the synnere; and delyuere thou me fro wickid men. Which thouyten to disseyue my goyngis;
019	PSA	140	005	proude men hidden a snare to me. And thei leiden forth cordis in to a snare; thei settiden sclaundir to me bisidis the weie.
019	PSA	140	006	I seide to the Lord, Thou art mi God; Lord, here thou the vois of my biseching.
019	PSA	140	007	Lord, Lord, the vertu of myn heelthe; thou madist schadowe on myn heed in the dai of batel.
019	PSA	140	008	Lord, bitake thou not me fro my desire to the synnere; thei thouyten ayens me, forsake thou not me, lest perauenture thei ben enhaunsid.
019	PSA	140	009	The heed of the cumpas of hem; the trauel of her lippis schal hile hem.
019	PSA	140	010	Colis schulen falle on hem, thou schalt caste hem doun in to fier; in wretchidnessis thei schulen not stonde.
019	PSA	140	011	A man a greet ianglere schal not be dressid in erthe; yuels schulen take an vniust man in perisching.
019	PSA	140	012	I haue knowe, that the Lord schal make dom of a nedi man; and the veniaunce of pore men.
019	PSA	140	013	Netheles iust men schulen knouleche to thi name; and riytful men schulen dwelle with thi cheer.
019	PSA	141	001	`The salm `of Dauith. Lord, Y criede to thee, here thou me; yyue thou tent to my vois, whanne Y schal crye to thee.
019	PSA	141	002	Mi preier be dressid as encense in thi siyt; the reisyng of myn hondis be as the euentid sacrifice.
019	PSA	141	003	Lord, sette thou a keping to my mouth; and a dore of stonding aboute to my lippis.
019	PSA	141	004	Bowe thou not myn herte in to wordis of malice; to excuse excusingis in synne. With men worchinge wickidnesse; and Y schal not comyne with the chosun men of hem.
019	PSA	141	005	A iust man schal repreue me in mersi, and schal blame me; but the oile of a synner make not fat myn heed. For whi and yit my preier is in the wel plesaunt thingis of hem;
019	PSA	141	006	for the domesmen of hem ioyned to the stoon weren sopun vp. Here thei my wordis,
019	PSA	141	007	for tho weren myyti. As fatnesse is brokun out on the erthe; oure bonys ben scatered niy helle. Lord, Lord,
019	PSA	141	008	for myn iyen ben to thee, Y hopide in thee; take thou not awei my soule.
019	PSA	141	009	Kepe thou me fro the snare which thei ordeyneden to me; and fro the sclaundris of hem that worchen wickidnesse. Synneris schulen falle in the nett therof;
019	PSA	141	010	Y am aloone til Y passe.
019	PSA	142	001	The lernyng of Dauid; `his preier, `whanne he was in the denne. With my vois Y criede to the Lord; with my vois Y preiede hertli to the Lord.
019	PSA	142	002	I schede out my preier in his siyt; and Y pronounce my tribulacioun bifor him.
019	PSA	142	003	While my spirit failith of me; and thou hast knowe my pathis. In this weie in which Y yede; proude men hidden a snare to me.
019	PSA	142	004	I bihelde to the riyt side, and Y siy; and noon was that knew me. Fliyt perischide fro me; and noon is that sekith my soule.
019	PSA	142	005	Lord, Y criede to thee, Y seide, Thou art myn hope; my part in the lond of lyueris.
019	PSA	142	006	Yyue thou tent to my biseching; for Y am maad low ful greetli. Delyuere thou me fro hem that pursuen me; for thei ben coumfortid on me.
019	PSA	142	007	Lede my soule out of keping to knouleche to thi name; iust men abiden me, til thou yelde to me.
019	PSA	143	001	The salm of Dauid. Lord, here thou my preier, with eeris perseyue thou my biseching; in thi treuthe here thou me, in thi riytwisnesse.
019	PSA	143	002	And entre thou not in to dom with thi seruaunt; for ech man lyuynge schal not be maad iust in thi siyt.
019	PSA	143	003	For the enemy pursuede my soule; he made lowe my lijf in erthe. He hath set me in derk placis, as the deed men of the world,
019	PSA	143	004	and my spirit was angwischid on me; myn herte was disturblid in me.
019	PSA	143	005	I was myndeful of elde daies, Y bithouyte in alle thi werkis; Y bithouyte in the dedis of thin hondis.
019	PSA	143	006	I helde forth myn hondis to thee; my soule as erthe with out water to thee.
019	PSA	143	007	Lord, here thou me swiftli; my spirit failide. Turne thou not a wei thi face fro me; and Y schal be lijk to hem that gon doun in to the lake.
019	PSA	143	008	Make thou erli thi merci herd to me; for Y hopide in thee. Make thou knowun to me the weie in which Y schal go; for Y reiside my soule to thee.
019	PSA	143	009	Delyuere thou me fro myn enemyes, Lord, Y fledde to thee;
019	PSA	143	010	teche thou me to do thi wille, for thou art my God. Thi good spirit schal lede me forth in to a riytful lond;
019	PSA	143	011	Lord, for thi name thou schalt quikene me in thin equite. Thou schalt lede my soule out of tribulacioun;
019	PSA	143	012	and in thi merci thou schalt scatere alle myn enemyes. And thou schalt leese alle them, that troublen my soule; for Y am thi seruaunt.
019	PSA	144	001	`A salm. Blessid be my Lord God, that techith myn hondis to werre; and my fyngris to batel.
019	PSA	144	002	Mi merci, and my refuyt; my takere vp, and my delyuerer. Mi defender, and Y hopide in him; and thou makist suget my puple vnder me.
019	PSA	144	003	Lord, what is a man, for thou hast maad knowun to him; ether the sone of man, for thou arettist him of sum valu?
019	PSA	144	004	A man is maad lijk vanyte; hise daies passen as schadow.
019	PSA	144	005	Lord, bowe doun thin heuenes, and come thou doun; touche thou hillis, and thei schulen make smoke.
019	PSA	144	006	Leite thou schynyng, and thou schalt scatere hem; sende thou out thin arowis, and thou schalt disturble hem.
019	PSA	144	007	Sende out thin hond fro an hiy, rauysche thou me out, and delyuere thou me fro many watris; and fro the hond of alien sones.
019	PSA	144	008	The mouth of which spak vanite; and the riythond of hem is the riyt hond of wickidnesse.
019	PSA	144	009	God, Y schal synge to thee a new song; I schal seie salm to thee in a sautre of ten stringis.
019	PSA	144	010	Which yyuest heelthe to kingis; which ayen bouytist Dauid, thi seruaunt, fro the wickid swerd rauische thou out me.
019	PSA	144	011	And delyuere thou me fro `the hond of alien sones; the mouth of whiche spak vanyte, and the riythond of hem is the riyt hond of wickidnesse.
019	PSA	144	012	Whose sones ben; as new plauntingis in her yongthe. The douytris of hem ben arayed; ourned about as the licnesse of the temple.
019	PSA	144	013	The selers of hem ben fulle; bringinge out fro this vessel in to that. The scheep of hem ben with lambre, plenteuouse in her goingis out;
019	PSA	144	014	her kien ben fatte. `No falling of wal is, nether passing ouere; nether cry is in the stretis of hem.
019	PSA	144	015	Thei seiden, `The puple is blessid, that hath these thingis; blessid is the puple, whos Lord is the God of it.
019	PSA	145	001	`The ympne of Dauith. Mi God king, Y schal enhaunse thee; and Y schal blesse thi name in to the world, and in to the world of world.
019	PSA	145	002	Bi alle daies Y schal blesse thee; and Y schal herie thi name in to the world, and in to the world of the world.
019	PSA	145	003	The Lord is greet, and worthi to be preisid ful myche; and noon ende is of his greetnesse.
019	PSA	145	004	Generacioun and generacioun schal preise thi werkis; and thei schulen pronounse thi power.
019	PSA	145	005	Thei schulen speke `the greet doyng of the glorie of thin holynesse; and thei schulen telle thi merueils.
019	PSA	145	006	And thei schulen seye the vertu of thi ferdful thingis; and thei schulen telle thi greetnesse.
019	PSA	145	007	Thei schulen bringe forth the mynde of the abundaunce of thi swetnesse; and thei schulen telle with ful out ioiyng thi riytfulnesse.
019	PSA	145	008	The Lord is a merciful doere, and merciful in wille; paciente, and myche merciful.
019	PSA	145	009	The Lord is swete in alle thingis; and hise merciful doyngis ben on alle hise werkis.
019	PSA	145	010	Lord, alle thi werkis knouleche to thee; and thi seyntis blesse thee.
019	PSA	145	011	Thei schulen seie the glorie of thi rewme; and thei schulen speke thi power.
019	PSA	145	012	That thei make thi power knowun to the sones of men; and the glorie of the greetnesse of thi rewme.
019	PSA	145	013	Thi rewme is the rewme of alle worldis; and thi lordschipe is in al generacioun and in to generacioun. The Lord is feithful in alle hise wordis; and hooli in alle hise werkis.
019	PSA	145	014	The Lord liftith vp alle that fallen doun; and reisith alle men hurtlid doun.
019	PSA	145	015	Lord, the iyen of alle beestis hopen in thee; and thou yyuest the mete of hem in couenable tyme.
019	PSA	145	016	Thou openest thin hond; and thou fillist ech beeste with blessing.
019	PSA	145	017	The Lord is iust in alle hise weies; and hooli in alle hise werkis.
019	PSA	145	018	The Lord is niy to alle that inwardli clepen him; to alle that inwardli clepen him in treuthe.
019	PSA	145	019	He schal do the wille of hem, that dreden him, and he schal here the biseching of hem; and he schal make hem saaf.
019	PSA	145	020	The Lord kepith alle men louynge him; and he schal leese alle synners.
019	PSA	145	021	Mi mouth schal speke the heriyng of the Lord; and ech man blesse his hooli name in to the world, and in to the world of world.
019	PSA	146	001	Alleluya.
019	PSA	146	002	Mi soule, herie thou the Lord; Y schal herie the Lord in my lijf, Y schal synge to my God as longe as Y schal be. Nile ye triste in princis;
019	PSA	146	003	nether in the sones of men, in whiche is noon helthe.
019	PSA	146	004	The spirit of hym schal go out, and he schal turne ayen in to his erthe; in that dai alle the thouytis of hem schulen perische.
019	PSA	146	005	He is blessid, of whom the God of Jacob is his helpere, his hope is in his Lord God, that made heuene and erthe;
019	PSA	146	006	the see, and alle thingis that ben in tho.
019	PSA	146	007	Which kepith treuthe in to the world, makith dom to hem that suffren wrong; yyueth mete to hem that ben hungri. The Lord vnbyndith feterid men;
