019	PSA	146	010	The Lord schal regne in to the worldis; Syon, thi God schal regne in generacioun and in to generacioun.
019	PSA	147	001	Alleluya. Herie ye the Lord, for the salm is good; heriyng be myrie, and fair to oure God.
019	PSA	147	002	The Lord schal bilde Jerusalem; and schal gadere togidere the scateryngis of Israel.
019	PSA	147	003	Which Lord makith hool men contrit in herte; and byndith togidere the sorewes of hem.
019	PSA	147	004	Which noumbrith the multitude of sterris; and clepith names to alle tho.
019	PSA	147	005	Oure Lord is greet, and his vertu is greet; and of his wisdom is no noumbre.
019	PSA	147	006	The Lord takith vp mylde men; forsothe he makith low synneris `til to the erthe.
019	PSA	147	007	Bifore synge ye to the Lord in knoulechyng; seye ye salm to oure God in an harpe.
019	PSA	147	008	Which hilith heuene with cloudis; and makith redi reyn to the erthe. Which bryngith forth hei in hillis; and eerbe to the seruice of men.
019	PSA	147	009	Which yyueth mete to her werk beestis; and to the briddys of crowis clepinge hym.
019	PSA	147	010	He schal not haue wille in the strengthe of an hors; nether it schal be wel plesaunt to hym in the leggis of a man.
019	PSA	147	011	It is wel plesaunt to the Lord on men that dreden hym; and in hem that hopen on his mercy.
019	PSA	147	012	Jerusalem, herie thou the Lord; Syon, herie thou thi God.
019	PSA	147	013	For he hath coumfortid the lockis of thi yatis; he hath blessid thi sones in thee.
019	PSA	147	014	Which hath set thi coostis pees; and fillith thee with the fatnesse of wheete.
019	PSA	147	015	Which sendith out his speche to the erthe; his word renneth swiftli.
019	PSA	147	016	Which yyueth snow as wolle; spredith abrood a cloude as aische.
019	PSA	147	017	He sendith his cristal as mussels; who schal suffre bifore the face of his cooldnesse?
019	PSA	147	018	He schal sende out his word, and schal melte tho; his spirit schal blowe, and watris schulen flowe.
019	PSA	147	019	Which tellith his word to Jacob; and hise riytfulnessis and domes to Israel.
019	PSA	147	020	He dide not so to ech nacioun; and he schewide not hise domes to hem.
019	PSA	148	001	Alleluya. Ye of heuenes, herie the Lord; herie ye hym in hiye thingis.
019	PSA	148	002	Alle hise aungels, herie ye hym; alle hise vertues, herye ye hym.
019	PSA	148	003	Sunne and moone, herie ye hym; alle sterris and liyt, herie ye hym.
019	PSA	148	004	Heuenes of heuenes, herie ye hym; and the watris that ben aboue heuenes,
019	PSA	148	005	herie ye the name of the Lord.
019	PSA	148	006	For he seide, and thingis weren maad; he comaundide, and thingis weren maad of nouyt. He ordeynede tho thingis in to the world, and in to the world of world; he settide a comaundement, and it schal not passe.
019	PSA	148	007	Ye of erthe, herie ye the Lord; dragouns, and alle depthis of watris.
019	PSA	148	008	Fier, hail, snow, iys, spiritis of tempestis; that don his word.
019	PSA	148	009	Mounteyns, and alle litle hillis; trees berynge fruyt, and alle cedris.
019	PSA	148	010	Wielde beestis, and alle tame beestis; serpentis, and fetherid briddis.
019	PSA	148	011	The kingis of erthe, and alle puplis; the princis, and alle iugis of erthe.
019	PSA	148	012	Yonge men, and virgyns, elde men with yongere, herie ye the name of the Lord;
019	PSA	148	013	for the name of hym aloone is enhaunsid.
019	PSA	148	014	His knouleching be on heuene and erthe; and he hath enhaunsid the horn of his puple. An ympne be to alle hise seyntis; to the children of Israel, to a puple neiyynge to hym.
019	PSA	149	001	Alleluya. Synge ye to the Lord a newe song; hise heriyng be in the chirche of seyntis.
019	PSA	149	002	Israel be glad in hym that made hym; and the douytris of Syon make ful out ioye in her king.
019	PSA	149	003	Herie thei his name in a queer; seie thei salm to hym in a tympan, and sautre.
019	PSA	149	004	For the Lord is wel plesid in his puple; and he hath reisid mylde men in to heelthe.
019	PSA	149	005	Seyntis schulen make ful out ioye in glorie; thei schulen be glad in her beddis.
019	PSA	149	006	The ful out ioiyngis of God in the throte of hem; and swerdis scharp on `ech side in the hondis of hem.
019	PSA	149	007	To do veniaunce in naciouns; blamyngis in puplis.
019	PSA	149	008	To bynde the kyngis of hem in stockis; and the noble men of hem in yrun manaclis.
019	PSA	149	009	That thei make in hem doom writun; this is glorye to alle hise seyntis.
019	PSA	150	001	Alleluya. Herie ye the Lord in hise seyntis; herie ye hym in the firmament of his vertu.
019	PSA	150	002	Herie ye hym in hise vertues; herie ye hym bi the multitude of his greetnesse.
019	PSA	150	003	Herie ye hym in the soun of trumpe; herie ye hym in a sautre and harpe.
019	PSA	150	004	Herie ye hym in a tympane and queer; herie ye hym in strengis and orgun.
019	PSA	150	005	Herie ye hym in cymbalis sownynge wel, herye ye hym in cymbalis of iubilacioun;
019	PSA	150	006	ech spirit, herye the Lord.
#
# BOOK	020	PRO	Proverbs	Proverbs
020	PRO	001	001	The parablis of Salomon, the sone of Dauid, king of Israel;
020	PRO	001	002	to kunne wisdom and kunnyng;
020	PRO	001	003	to vndurstonde the wordis of prudence; and to take the lernyng of teching; to take riytfulnesse, and dom, and equyte;
020	PRO	001	004	that felnesse be youun to litle children, and kunnyng, and vndurstonding to a yong wexynge man.
020	PRO	001	005	A wise man heringe schal be wisere; and a man vndurstondinge schal holde gouernails.
020	PRO	001	006	He schal perseyue a parable, and expownyng; the wordis of wise men, and the derk figuratif spechis of hem.
020	PRO	001	007	The drede of the Lord is the bigynning of wisdom; foolis dispisen wisdom and teching.
020	PRO	001	008	My sone, here thou the teching of thi fadir, and forsake thou not the lawe of thi modir;
020	PRO	001	009	that grace be addid, ethir encreessid, to thin heed, and a bie to thi necke.
020	PRO	001	010	Mi sone, if synneris flateren thee, assente thou not to hem.
020	PRO	001	011	If thei seien, Come thou with vs, sette we aspies to blood, hide we snaris of disseitis ayens an innocent without cause;
020	PRO	001	012	swolowe we him, as helle swolowith a man lyuynge; and al hool, as goynge doun in to a lake; we schulen fynde al preciouse catel,
020	PRO	001	013	we schulen fille oure housis with spuylis; sende thou lot with vs,
020	PRO	001	014	o purs be of vs alle;
020	PRO	001	015	my sone, go thou not with hem; forbede thi foot fro the pathis of hem.
020	PRO	001	016	For the feet of hem rennen to yuel; and thei hasten to schede out blood.
020	PRO	001	017	But a net is leid in veyn bifore the iyen of briddis, that han wengis.
020	PRO	001	018	Also `thilke wickid disseyueris setten aspies ayens her owne blood; and maken redi fraudis ayens her soulis.
020	PRO	001	019	So the pathis of ech auerouse man rauyschen the soulis of hem that welden.
020	PRO	001	020	Wisdom prechith with outforth; in stretis it yyueth his vois.
020	PRO	001	021	It crieth ofte in the heed of cumpenyes; in the leeues of yatis of the citee it bringith forth hise wordis,
020	PRO	001	022	and seith, Hou long, ye litle men in wit, louen yong childhod, and foolis schulen coueyte tho thingis, that ben harmful to hem silf, and vnprudent men schulen hate kunnyng?
020	PRO	001	023	Be ye conuertid at my repreuyng; lo, Y schal profre forth to you my spirit, and Y schal schewe my wordis.
020	PRO	001	024	For Y clepide, and ye forsoken; Y helde forth myn hond, and noon was that bihelde.
020	PRO	001	025	Ye dispisiden al my councel; and chargiden not my blamyngis.
020	PRO	001	026	And Y schal leiye in youre perisching; and Y schal scorne you, whanne that, that ye dreden, cometh to you.
020	PRO	001	027	Whanne sodeyne wretchidnesse fallith in, and perisching bifallith as tempest; whanne tribulacioun and angwisch cometh on you.
020	PRO	001	028	Thanne thei schulen clepe me, and Y schal not here; thei schulen rise eerli, and thei schulen not fynde me.
020	PRO	001	029	For thei hatiden teching, and thei token not the drede of the Lord,
020	PRO	001	030	nether assentiden to my councel, and depraueden al myn amendyng.
020	PRO	001	031	Therfor thei schulen ete the fruytis of her weie; and thei schulen be fillid with her counseils.
020	PRO	001	032	The turnyng awei of litle men in wit schal sle hem; and the prosperite of foolis schal leese hem.
020	PRO	001	033	But he that herith me, schal reste with outen drede; and he schal vse abundaunce, whanne the drede of yuels is takun awei.
020	PRO	002	001	Mi sone, if thou resseyuest my wordis, `and hidist myn heestis anentis thee;
020	PRO	002	002	that thin eere here wisdom, bowe thin herte to knowe prudence.
020	PRO	002	003	For if thou inwardli clepist wisdom, and bowist thin herte to prudence;
020	PRO	002	004	if thou sekist it as money, and diggist it out as tresours;
020	PRO	002	005	thanne thou schalt vndirstonde the drede of the Lord, and schalt fynde the kunnyng of God.
020	PRO	002	006	For the Lord yyueth wisdom; and prudence and kunnyng is of his mouth.
020	PRO	002	007	He schal kepe the heelthe of riytful men, and he schal defende hem that goen sympli.
020	PRO	002	008	And he schal kepe the pathis of riytfulnesse, and he schal kepe the weies of hooli men.
020	PRO	002	009	Thanne thou schalt vndirstonde riytfulnesse, and dom, and equytee, and ech good path.
020	PRO	002	010	If wysdom entrith in to thin herte, and kunnyng plesith thi soule,
020	PRO	002	011	good councel schal kepe thee, and prudence schal kepe thee; that thou be delyuered fro an yuel weie,
020	PRO	002	012	and fro a man that spekith weiward thingis.
020	PRO	002	013	Whiche forsaken a riytful weie, and goen bi derk weies;
020	PRO	002	014	whiche ben glad, whanne thei han do yuel, and maken ful out ioye in worste thingis;
020	PRO	002	015	whose weies ben weywerd, and her goyingis ben of yuel fame.
020	PRO	002	016	That thou be delyuered fro an alien womman, and fro a straunge womman, that makith soft hir wordis;
020	PRO	002	017	and forsakith the duyk of hir tyme of mariage,
020	PRO	002	018	and hath foryete the couenaunt of hir God. For the hous of hir is bowid to deeth, and hir pathis to helle.
020	PRO	002	019	Alle that entren to hir, schulen not turne ayen, nether schulen catche the pathis of lijf.
020	PRO	002	020	That thou go in a good weie, and kepe the pathis of iust men.
020	PRO	002	021	Forsothe thei that ben riytful, schulen dwelle in the lond; and symple men schulen perfitli dwelle ther ynne.
020	PRO	002	022	But vnfeithful men schulen be lost fro the loond; and thei that doen wickidli, schulen be takun awey fro it.
020	PRO	003	001	Mi sone, foryete thou not my lawe; and thyn herte kepe my comaundementis.
020	PRO	003	002	For tho schulen sette to thee the lengthe of daies, and the yeeris of lijf, and pees.
020	PRO	003	003	Merci and treuthe forsake thee not; bynde thou tho to thi throte, and write in the tablis of thin herte.
020	PRO	003	004	And thou schalt fynde grace, and good teching bifore God and men.
020	PRO	003	005	Haue thou trist in the Lord, of al thin herte; and triste thou not to thi prudence.
020	PRO	003	006	In alle thi weies thenke thou on hym, and he schal dresse thi goyngis.
020	PRO	003	007	Be thou not wijs anentis thi silf; drede thou God, and go awei fro yuel.
020	PRO	003	008	For whi helthe schal be in thi nawle, and moisting of thi boonys.
020	PRO	003	009	Onoure thou the Lord of thi catel, and of the beste of alle thi fruytis yyue thou to pore men;
020	PRO	003	010	and thi bernes schulen be fillid with abundaunce, and pressours schulen flowe with wiyn.
020	PRO	003	011	My sone, caste thou not awei the teching of the Lord; and faile thou not, whanne thou art chastisid of him.
020	PRO	003	012	For the Lord chastisith hym, whom he loueth; and as a fadir in the sone he plesith hym.
020	PRO	003	013	Blessid is the man that fyndith wisdom, and which flowith with prudence.
020	PRO	003	014	The geting therof is betere than the marchaundie of gold and of siluer; the fruytis therof ben the firste and clenneste.
020	PRO	003	015	It is preciousere than alle richessis; and alle thingis that ben desirid, moun not be comparisound to this.
020	PRO	003	016	Lengthe of daies is in the riythalf therof, and richessis and glorie ben in the lifthalf therof.
020	PRO	003	017	The weies therof ben feire weies, and alle the pathis therof ben pesible.
020	PRO	003	018	It is a tre of lijf to hem that taken it; and he that holdith it, is blessid.
020	PRO	003	019	The Lord foundide the erthe bi wisdom; he stablischide heuenes bi prudence.
020	PRO	003	020	The depthis of watris braken out bi his wisdom; and cloudis wexen togidere bi dewe.
020	PRO	003	021	My sone, these thingis flete not awey fro thin iyen; kepe thou my lawe, and my counsel;
020	PRO	003	022	and lijf schal be to thi soule, and grace `schal be to thi chekis.
020	PRO	003	023	Thanne thou schalt go tristili in thi weie; and thi foot schal not snapere.
020	PRO	003	024	If thou schalt slepe, thou schalt not drede; thou schalt reste, and thi sleep schal be soft.
020	PRO	003	025	Drede thou not bi sudeyne feer, and the powers of wickid men fallynge in on thee.
020	PRO	003	026	For the Lord schal be at thi side; and he schal kepe thi foot, that thou be not takun.
020	PRO	003	027	Nil thou forbede to do wel him that mai; if thou maist, and do thou wel.
020	PRO	003	028	Seie thou not to thi frend, Go, and turne thou ayen, and to morewe Y schal yyue to thee; whanne thou maist yyue anoon.
020	PRO	003	029	Ymagyne thou not yuel to thi freend, whanne he hath trist in thee.
020	PRO	003	030	Stryue thou not ayens a man with out cause, whanne he doith noon yuel to thee.
020	PRO	003	031	Sue thou not an vniust man, sue thou not hise weies.
020	PRO	003	032	For ech disseyuer is abhomynacioun of the Lord; and his speking is with simple men.
020	PRO	003	033	Nedinesse is sent of the Lord in the hous of a wickid man; but the dwelling places of iust men schulen be blessid.
020	PRO	003	034	He schal scorne scorneris; and he schal yyue grace to mylde men.
020	PRO	003	035	Wise men schulen haue glorie; enhaunsing of foolis is schenschipe.
020	PRO	004	001	Sones, here ye the teching of the fadir; and perseiue ye, that ye kunne prudence.
020	PRO	004	002	Y schal yyue to you a good yifte; forsake ye not my lawe.
020	PRO	004	003	For whi and Y was the sone of my fadir, a tendir sone, and oon `gendride bifore my modir.
020	PRO	004	004	And my fadir tauyte me, and seide, Thin herte resseyue my wordis; kepe thou myn heestis, and thou schalt lyue.
020	PRO	004	005	Welde thou wisdom, welde thou prudence; foryete thou not, nethir bowe thou awey fro the wordis of my mouth.
020	PRO	004	006	Forsake thou not it, and it schal kepe thee; loue thou it, and it schal kepe thee.
020	PRO	004	007	The bigynnyng of wisdom, welde thou wisdom; and in al thi possessioun gete thou prudence.
020	PRO	004	008	Take thou it, and it schal enhaunse thee; thou schalt be glorified of it, whanne thou hast biclippid it.
020	PRO	004	009	It schal yyue encresyngis of graces to thin heed; and a noble coroun schal defende thee.
020	PRO	004	010	Mi sone, here thou, and take my wordis; that the yeris of lijf be multiplied to thee.
020	PRO	004	011	Y schal schewe to thee the weie of wisdom; and Y schal lede thee bi the pathis of equyte.
020	PRO	004	012	In to whiche whanne thou hast entrid, thi goyngis schulen not be maad streit; and thou schalt rennen, and schalt not haue hirtyng.
020	PRO	004	013	Holde thou teching, and forsake it not; kepe thou it, for it is thi lijf.
020	PRO	004	014	Delite thou not in the pathis of wyckid men; and the weie of yuele men plese not thee.
020	PRO	004	015	Fle thou fro it, and passe thou not therbi; bowe thou awei, and forsake it.
020	PRO	004	016	For thei slepen not, `no but thei han do yuele; and sleep is rauyschid fro hem, no but thei han disseyued.
020	PRO	004	017	Thei eten the breed of vnpite, and drinken the wyn of wickidnesse.
020	PRO	004	018	But the path of iust men goith forth as liyt schynynge, and encreessith til to perfit dai.
020	PRO	004	019	The weie of wickid men is derk; thei witen not where thei schulen falle.
020	PRO	004	020	Mi sone, herkene thou my wordis; and bowe doun thin eeris to my spechis.
020	PRO	004	021	Go not tho awei fro thyn iyen; kepe thou hem in the myddil of thin herte.
020	PRO	004	022	For tho ben lijf to men fyndynge thoo, and heelthe `of al fleisch.
020	PRO	004	023	With al keping kepe thin herte, for lijf cometh forth of it.
020	PRO	004	024	Remoue thou a schrewid mouth fro thee; and backbitynge lippis be fer fro thee.
020	PRO	004	025	Thin iyen se riytful thingis; and thin iyeliddis go bifore thi steppis.
020	PRO	004	026	Dresse thou pathis to thi feet, and alle thi weies schulen be stablischid.
020	PRO	004	027	Bowe thou not to the riytside, nether to the leftside; turne awei thi foot fro yuel. For the Lord knowith the weies that ben at the riytside; but the weies ben weiward, that ben at the leftside. Forsothe he schal make thi goyngis riytful; and thi weies schulen be brouyt forth in pees.
020	PRO	005	001	Mi sone, perseyue thou my wisdom, and bowe doun thin eere to my prudence; that thou kepe thi thouytis,
020	PRO	005	002	and thi lippis kepe teching. Yyue thou not tent to the falsnesse of a womman;
020	PRO	005	003	for the lippis of an hoore ben an hony coomb droppinge, and hir throte is clerere than oile;
020	PRO	005	004	but the last thingis ben bittir as wormod, and hir tunge is scharp as a swerd keruynge on ech side.
020	PRO	005	005	Hir feet gon doun in to deeth; and hir steppis persen to hellis.
020	PRO	005	006	Tho goon not bi the path of lijf; hir steppis ben vncerteyn, and moun not be souyt out.
020	PRO	005	007	Now therfor, my sone, here thou me, and go not awei fro the wordis of my mouth.
020	PRO	005	008	Make fer thi weie fro hir, and neiye thou not to the doris of hir hous.
020	PRO	005	009	Yyue thou not thin onour to aliens, and thi yeeris to the cruel;
020	PRO	005	010	lest perauenture straungeris be fillid with thi strengthis, and lest thi trauels be in an alien hous;
020	PRO	005	011	and thou biweile in the laste daies, whanne thou hast wastid thi fleschis, and thi bodi; and thou seie,
020	PRO	005	012	Whi wlatide Y teching, and myn herte assentide not to blamyngis;
020	PRO	005	013	nether Y herde the voys of men techinge me, and Y bowide not doun myn eere to maistris?
020	PRO	005	014	Almest Y was in al yuel, in the myddis of the chirche, and of the synagoge.
020	PRO	005	015	Drinke thou watir of thi cisterne, and the floodis of thi pit.
020	PRO	005	016	Thi wellis be stremed forth; and departe thi watris in stretis.
020	PRO	005	017	Haue thou aloone `tho watris; and aliens be not thi parceneris.
020	PRO	005	018	Thi veyne be blessid; and be thou glad with the womman of thi yong wexynge age.
020	PRO	005	019	An hynde moost dereworthe; and an hert calf moost acceptable. Hir teetis fille thee in al tyme; and delite thou contynueli in the loue of hir.
020	PRO	005	020	Mi sone, whi art thou disseyued of an alien womman; and art fostrid in the bosum of an othere?
020	PRO	005	021	The Lord seeth the weie of a man; and biholdith alle hise steppis.
020	PRO	005	022	The wickidnessis of a wyckid man taken hym; and he is boundun with the roopis of hise synnes.
020	PRO	005	023	He schal die, for he hadde not lernyng; and he schal be disseyued in the mychilnesse of his fooli.
020	PRO	006	001	Mi sone, if thou hast bihiyt for thi freend; thou hast fastned thin hoond at a straunger.
020	PRO	006	002	Thou art boundun bi the wordis of thi mouth; and thou art takun with thin owne wordis.
020	PRO	006	003	Therfor, my sone, do thou that that Y seie, and delyuere thi silf; for thou hast fallun in to the hond of thi neiybore. Renne thou aboute, haste thou, reise thi freend;
020	PRO	006	004	yyue thou not sleep to thin iyen, nether thin iyeliddis nappe.
020	PRO	006	005	Be thou rauyschid as a doo fro the hond; and as a bridde fro aspiyngis of the foulere.
020	PRO	006	006	O! thou slowe man, go to the `amte, ether pissemyre; and biholde thou hise weies, and lerne thou wisdom.
020	PRO	006	007	Which whanne he hath no duyk, nethir comaundour, nether prince;
020	PRO	006	008	makith redi in somer mete to hym silf, and gaderith togidere in heruest that, that he schal ete.
020	PRO	006	009	Hou long schalt thou, slow man, slepe? whanne schalt thou rise fro thi sleep?
020	PRO	006	010	A litil thou schalt slepe, a litil thou schalt nappe; a litil thou schalt ioyne togidere thin hondis, that thou slepe.
020	PRO	006	011	And nedynesse, as a weigoere, schal come to thee; and pouert, as an armed man. Forsothe if thou art not slow, thi ripe corn schal come as a welle; and nedynesse schal fle fer fro thee.
020	PRO	006	012	A man apostata, a man vnprofitable, he goith with a weiward mouth;
020	PRO	006	013	he bekeneth with iyen, he trampith with the foot, he spekith with the fyngur,
020	PRO	006	014	bi schrewid herte he ymagyneth yuel, and in al tyme he sowith dissenciouns.
020	PRO	006	015	His perdicioun schal come to hym anoon, and he schal be brokun sodeynli; and he schal no more haue medecyn.
020	PRO	006	016	Sixe thingis ben, whyche the Lord hatith; and hise soule cursith the seuenthe thing.
020	PRO	006	017	Hiye iyen, a tunge liere, hondis schedinge out innocent blood,
020	PRO	006	018	an herte ymagynynge worste thouytis, feet swifte to renne in to yuel,
020	PRO	006	019	a man bringynge forth lesingis, a fals witnesse; and him that sowith discordis among britheren.
020	PRO	006	020	Mi sone, kepe the comaundementis of thi fadir; and forsake not the lawe of thi modir.
020	PRO	006	021	Bynde thou tho continueli in thin herte; and cumpasse `to thi throte.
020	PRO	006	022	Whanne thou goist, go tho with thee; whanne thou slepist, kepe tho thee; and thou wakynge speke with tho.
020	PRO	006	023	For the comaundement of God is a lanterne, and the lawe is liyt, and the blamyng of techyng is the weie of lijf;
020	PRO	006	024	`that the comaundementis kepe thee fro an yuel womman, and fro a flaterynge tunge of a straunge womman.
020	PRO	006	025	Thin herte coueite not the fairnesse of hir; nether be thou takun bi the signes of hir.
020	PRO	006	026	For the prijs of an hoore is vnnethe of o loof; but a womman takith the preciouse soule of a man.
020	PRO	006	027	Whether a man mai hide fier in his bosum, that hise clothis brenne not;
020	PRO	006	028	ethir go on colis, and hise feet be not brent?
020	PRO	006	029	So he that entrith to the wijf of his neiybore; schal not be cleene, whanne he hath touchid hir.
020	PRO	006	030	It is not greet synne, whanne a man stelith; for he stelith to fille an hungri soule.
020	PRO	006	031	And he takun schal yelde the seuenthe fold; and he schal yyue al the catel of his hous, and schal delyuere hym silf.
020	PRO	006	032	But he that is avouter; schal leese his soule, for the pouert of herte.
020	PRO	006	033	He gaderith filthe, and sclaundrith to hym silf; and his schenschip schal not be don awei.
020	PRO	006	034	For the feruent loue and strong veniaunce of the man schal not spare in the dai of veniaunce,
020	PRO	006	035	nether schal assente to the preieris of ony; nether schal take ful many yiftis for raunsum.
020	PRO	007	001	Mi sone, kepe thou my wordis; and kepe myn heestis to thee. Sone, onoure thou the Lord, and thou schalt be `myyti; but outakun hym drede thou not an alien.
020	PRO	007	002	Kepe thou myn heestis, and thou schalt lyue; and my lawe as the appil of thin iyen.
020	PRO	007	003	Bynde thou it in thi fyngris; write thou it in the tablis of thin herte.
020	PRO	007	004	Seie thou to wisdom, Thou art my sistir; and clepe thou prudence thi frendesse.
020	PRO	007	005	That it kepe thee fro a straunge womman; and fro an alien womman, that makith hir wordis swete.
020	PRO	007	006	For whi fro the wyndow of myn hous bi the latijs Y bihelde; and Y se litle children.
020	PRO	007	007	I biholde a yong man coward,
020	PRO	007	008	that passith bi the stretis, bisidis the corner; and he
020	PRO	007	009	goith niy the weie of hir hous in derk tyme, whanne the dai drawith to niyt, in the derknessis and myst of the nyyt.
020	PRO	007	010	And lo! a womman, maad redi with ournement of an hoore to disseyue soulis, meetith hym, and sche is a ianglere, and goynge about,
020	PRO	007	011	and vnpacient of reste, and mai not stonde in the hous with hir feet;
020	PRO	007	012	and now without forth, now in stretis, now bisidis corneris sche `aspieth.
020	PRO	007	013	And sche takith, and kissith the yong man; and flaterith with wowynge cheer, and seith, Y ouyte sacrifices for heelthe;
020	PRO	007	014	to dai Y haue yolde my vowis.
020	PRO	007	015	Therfor Y yede out in to thi meetyng, and Y desiride to se thee; and Y haue founde thee.
020	PRO	007	016	Y haue maad my bed with coordis, Y haue arayed with tapetis peyntid of Egipt;
020	PRO	007	017	Y haue bispreynt my bed with myrre, and aloes, and canel.
020	PRO	007	018	Come thou, be we fillid with tetis, and vse we collyngis that ben coueitid; til the dai bigynne to be cleer.
020	PRO	007	019	For myn hosebonde is not in his hows; he is goon a ful long weie.
020	PRO	007	020	He took with hym a bagge of money; he schal turne ayen in to his hous in the dai of ful moone.
020	PRO	007	021	Sche boonde hym with many wordis; and sche drow forth hym with flateryngis of lippis.
020	PRO	007	022	Anoon he as an oxe led to slayn sacrifice sueth hir, and as a ioli lomb and vnkunnynge; and the fool woot not, that he is drawun to bondys,
020	PRO	007	023	til an arowe perse his mawe. As if a brid hastith to the snare; and woot not, that it is don of the perel of his lijf.
020	PRO	007	024	Now therfor, my sone, here thou me; and perseyue the wordis of my mouth.
020	PRO	007	025	Lest thi soule be drawun awei in the weies of hir; nether be thou disseyued in the pathis of hir.
020	PRO	007	026	For sche castide doun many woundid men; and alle strongeste men weren slayn of hir.
020	PRO	007	027	The weies of helle is hir hous; and persen in to ynnere thingis of deeth.
020	PRO	008	001	Whether wisdom crieth not ofte; and prudence yyueth his vois?
020	PRO	008	002	In souereyneste and hiy coppis, aboue the weie, in the myddis of pathis,
020	PRO	008	003	and it stondith bisidis the yate of the citee, in thilke closyngis, and spekith, and seith, A!
020	PRO	008	004	ye men, Y crie ofte to you; and my vois is to the sones of men.
020	PRO	008	005	Litle children, vndirstonde ye wisdom; and ye vnwise men, `perseyue wisdom.
020	PRO	008	006	Here ye, for Y schal speke of grete thingis; and my lippis schulen be openyd, to preche riytful thingis.
020	PRO	008	007	My throte schal bithenke treuthe; and my lippis schulen curse a wickid man.
020	PRO	008	008	My wordis ben iust; no schrewid thing, nether weiward is in tho.
020	PRO	008	009	`My wordis ben riytful to hem that vndurstonden; and ben euene to hem that fynden kunnyng.
020	PRO	008	010	Take ye my chastisyng, and not money; chese ye teching more than tresour.
020	PRO	008	011	For wisdom is betere than alle richessis moost preciouse; and al desirable thing mai not be comparisound therto.
020	PRO	008	012	Y, wisdom, dwelle in counsel; and Y am among lernyd thouytis.
020	PRO	008	013	The drede of the Lord hatith yuel; Y curse boost, and pride, and a schrewid weie, and a double tungid mouth.
020	PRO	008	014	Counseil is myn, and equyte `is myn; prudence is myn, and strengthe `is myn.
020	PRO	008	015	Kyngis regnen bi me; and the makeris of lawis demen iust thingis bi me.
020	PRO	008	016	Princis comaunden bi me; and myyti men demen riytfulnesse bi me.
020	PRO	008	017	I loue hem that louen me; and thei that waken eerli to me, schulen fynde me.
020	PRO	008	018	With me ben rychessis, and glorie; souereyn richessis, and riytfulnesse.
020	PRO	008	019	My fruyt is betere than gold, and precyouse stoon; and my seedis ben betere than chosun siluer.
020	PRO	008	020	Y go in the weies of riytfulnesse, in the myddis of pathis of doom;
020	PRO	008	021	that Y make riche hem that louen me, and that Y fille her tresouris.
020	PRO	008	022	The Lord weldide me in the bigynnyng of hise weies; bifore that he made ony thing, at the bigynnyng.
020	PRO	008	023	Fro with out bigynnyng Y was ordeined; and fro elde tymes, bifor that the erthe was maad.
020	PRO	008	024	Depthis of watris weren not yit; and Y was conseyued thanne. The wellis of watris hadden not brokun out yit,
020	PRO	008	025	and hillis stoden not togidere yit bi sad heuynesse; bifor litil hillis Y was born.
020	PRO	008	026	Yit he hadde not maad erthe; and floodis, and the herris of the world.
020	PRO	008	027	Whanne he made redi heuenes, Y was present; whanne he cumpasside the depthis of watris bi certeyn lawe and cumpas.
020	PRO	008	028	Whanne he made stidfast the eir aboue; and weiede the wellis of watris.
020	PRO	008	029	Whanne he cumpasside to the see his marke; and settide lawe to watris, that tho schulden not passe her coostis. Whanne he peiside the foundementis of erthe;
020	PRO	008	030	Y was making alle thingis with him. And Y delitide bi alle daies, and pleiede bifore hym in al tyme,
020	PRO	008	031	and Y pleiede in the world; and my delices ben to be with the sones of men.
020	PRO	008	032	Now therfor, sones, here ye me; blessid ben thei that kepen my weies.
020	PRO	008	033	Here ye teching, and be ye wise men; and nile ye caste it awei.
020	PRO	008	034	Blessid is the man that herith me, and that wakith at my yatis al dai; and kepith at the postis of my dore.
020	PRO	008	035	He that fyndith me, schal fynde lijf; and schal drawe helthe of the Lord.
020	PRO	008	036	But he that synneth ayens me, schal hurte his soule; alle that haten me, louen deeth.
020	PRO	009	001	Wisdom bildide an hous to him silf; he hewide out seuene pileris,
020	PRO	009	002	he offride his slayn sacrifices, he medlide wijn, and settide forth his table.
020	PRO	009	003	He sente hise handmaides, that thei schulden clepe to the tour; and to the wallis of the citee.
020	PRO	009	004	If ony man is litil; come he to me. And wisdom spak to vnwise men,
020	PRO	009	005	Come ye, ete ye my breed; and drynke ye the wiyn, which Y haue medlid to you.
020	PRO	009	006	Forsake ye yong childhed, and lyue ye; and go ye bi the weyes of prudence.
020	PRO	009	007	He that techith a scornere, doith wrong to him silf; and he that vndirnymmeth a wickid man, gendrith a wem to him silf.
020	PRO	009	008	Nile thou vndirnyme a scornere; lest he hate thee. Vndirnyme thou a wise man; and he schal loue thee.
020	PRO	009	009	Yyue thou occasioun to a wise man; and wisdom schal be encreessid to hym. Teche thou a iust man; and he schal haste to take.
020	PRO	009	010	The bigynnyng of wisdom is the dreed of the Lord; and prudence is the kunnyng of seyntis.
020	PRO	009	011	For thi daies schulen be multiplied bi me; and yeeris of lijf schulen be encreessid to thee.
020	PRO	009	012	If thou art wijs; thou schalt be to thi silf, and to thi neiyboris. Forsothe if thou art a scornere; thou aloone schalt bere yuel.
020	PRO	009	013	A fonned womman, and ful of cry, and ful of vnleueful lustis, and that kan no thing outirli,
020	PRO	009	014	sittith in the doris of hir hous, on a seete, in an hiy place of the cite;
020	PRO	009	015	to clepe men passinge bi the weie, and men goynge in her iournei.
020	PRO	009	016	Who is a litil man `of wit; bowe he to me. And sche spak to a coward,
020	PRO	009	017	Watris of thefte ben swettere, and breed hid is swettere.
020	PRO	009	018	And wiste not that giauntis ben there; and the gestis `of hir ben in the depthis of helle. Sotheli he that schal be applied, ether fastned, to hir; schal go doun to hellis. For whi he that goith awei fro hir; schal be saued.
020	PRO	010	001	The parablis of Salomon. A wijs sone makith glad the fadir; but a fonned sone is the sorewe of his modir.
020	PRO	010	002	Tresouris of wickidnesse schulen not profite; but riytfulnesse schal delyuere fro deth.
020	PRO	010	003	The Lord schal not turmente the soule of a iust man with hungur; and he schal distrie the tresouns of vnpitouse men.
020	PRO	010	004	A slow hond hath wrouyt nedynesse; but the hond of stronge men makith redi richessis. Forsothe he that enforsith to gete `ony thing bi leesyngis, fedith the wyndis; sotheli the same man sueth briddis fleynge.
020	PRO	010	005	He that gaderith togidere in heruest, is a wijs sone; but he that slepith in sommer, is a sone of confusioun.
020	PRO	010	006	The blessing of God is ouer the heed of a iust man; but wickidnesse hilith the mouth of wickid men.
020	PRO	010	007	The mynde of a iust man schal be with preisingis; and the name of wickid men schal wexe rotun.
020	PRO	010	008	A wijs man schal resseyue comaundementis with herte; a fool is betun with lippis.
020	PRO	010	009	He that goith simpli, goith tristili; but he that makith schrewid hise weies, schal be opyn.
020	PRO	010	010	He that bekeneth with the iye, schal yyue sorewe; a fool schal be betun with lippis.
020	PRO	010	011	The veyne of lijf is the mouth of a iust man; but the mouth of wickid men hilith wickidnesse.
020	PRO	010	012	Hatrede reisith chidingis; and charite hilith alle synnes.
020	PRO	010	013	Wisdom is foundun in the lippis of a wise man; and a yerd in the bak of him that is nedi of herte.
020	PRO	010	014	Wise men hiden kunnyng; but the mouth of a fool is nexte to confusioun.
020	PRO	010	015	The catel of a riche man is the citee of his strengthe; the drede of pore men is the nedynesse of hem.
020	PRO	010	016	The werk of a iust man is to lijf; but the fruyt of a wickid man is to synne.
020	PRO	010	017	The weie of lijf is to him that kepith chastising; but he that forsakith blamyngis, errith.
020	PRO	010	018	False lippis hiden hatrede; he that bringith forth dispisinge is vnwijs.
020	PRO	010	019	Synne schal not faile in myche spekyng; but he that mesurith hise lippis, is moost prudent.
020	PRO	010	020	Chosun siluer is the tunge of a iust man; the herte of wickid men is for nouyt.
020	PRO	010	021	The lippis of a iust man techen ful manye men; but thei that ben vnlerned, schulen die in nedinesse of herte.
020	PRO	010	022	The blessing of the Lord makith riche men; and turment schal not be felowschipid to hem.
020	PRO	010	023	A fool worchith wickidnesse as bi leiyyng; but `wisdom is prudence to a man.
020	PRO	010	024	That that a wickid man dredith, schal come on hym; the desire of iust men schalbe youun to hem.
020	PRO	010	025	As a tempeste passynge, a wickid man schal not be; but a iust man schal be as an euerlastynge foundement.
020	PRO	010	026	As vynegre noieth the teeth, and smoke noieth the iyen; so a slow man noieth hem that senten hym in the weie.
020	PRO	010	027	The drede of the Lord encreesith daies; and the yeeris of wickid men schulen be maad schort.
020	PRO	010	028	Abiding of iust men is gladnesse; but the hope of wickid men schal perische.
020	PRO	010	029	The strengthe of a symple man is the weie of the Lord; and drede to hem that worchen yuel.
020	PRO	010	030	A iust man schal not be moued with outen ende; but wickid men schulen not dwelle on the erthe.
020	PRO	010	031	The mouth of a iust man schal bringe forth wisdom; the tunge of schrewis schal perische.
020	PRO	010	032	The lippis of a iust man biholden pleasaunt thingis; and the mouth of wickid men byholdith weiward thingis.
020	PRO	011	001	A gileful balaunce is abhominacioun anentis God; and an euene weiyte is his wille.
020	PRO	011	002	Where pride is, there also dispising schal be; but where meeknesse is, there also is wisdom.
020	PRO	011	003	The simplenesse of iust men schal dresse hem; and the disseyuyng of weiward men schal destrie hem.
020	PRO	011	004	Richessis schulen not profite in the dai of veniaunce; but riytfulnesse schal delyuere fro deth.
020	PRO	011	005	The riytfulnesse of a simple man schal dresse his weie; and a wickid man schal falle in his wickidnesse.
020	PRO	011	006	The riytfulnesse of riytful men schal delyuere hem; and wickid men schulen be takun in her aspiyngis.
020	PRO	011	007	Whanne a wickid man is deed, noon hope schal be ferther; and abidyng of bisy men schal perische.
020	PRO	011	008	A iust man is delyuered from angwisch; and a wickid man schal be youun for hym.
020	PRO	011	009	A feynere bi mouth disseyueth his freend; but iust men schulen be deliuered bi kunnyng.
020	PRO	011	010	A citee schal be enhaunsid in the goodis of iust men; and preysyng schal be in the perdicioun of wickid men.
020	PRO	011	011	A citee schal be enhaunsid bi blessing of iust men; and it schal be distried bi the mouth of wickid men.
020	PRO	011	012	He that dispisith his freend, is nedi in herte; but a prudent man schal be stille.
020	PRO	011	013	He that goith gilefuli, schewith priuetees; but he that is feithful, helith the priuetee of a freend.
020	PRO	011	014	Where a gouernour is not, the puple schal falle; but helthe `of the puple is, where ben many counsels.
020	PRO	011	015	He that makith feith for a straunger, schal be turmentid with yuel; but he that eschewith snaris, schal be sikur.
020	PRO	011	016	A graciouse womman schal fynde glorie; and stronge men schulen haue richessis.
020	PRO	011	017	A merciful man doith wel to his soule; but he that is cruel, castith awei, yhe, kynnesmen.
020	PRO	011	018	A wickid man makith vnstable werk; but feithful mede is to hym, that sowith riytfulnesse.
020	PRO	011	019	Merci schal make redi lijf; and the suyng of yuels `schal make redi deth.
020	PRO	011	020	A schrewid herte is abhomynable to the Lord; and his wille is in hem, that goen symply.
020	PRO	011	021	Thouy hond be in the hond, an yuel man schal not be innocent; but the seed of iust men schal be sauyd.
020	PRO	011	022	A goldun `sercle, ether ryng, in the `nose thrillis of a sowe, a womman fair and fool.
020	PRO	011	023	The desir of iust men is al good; abiding of wickid men is woodnesse.
020	PRO	011	024	Sum men departen her owne thingis, and ben maad richere; other men rauyschen thingis, that ben not hern, and ben euere in nedynesse.
020	PRO	011	025	A soule that blessith, schal be maad fat; and he that fillith, schal be fillid also.
020	PRO	011	026	He that hidith wheete `in tyme, schal be cursid among the puplis; but blessyng schal come on the heed of silleris.
020	PRO	011	027	Wel he risith eerli, that sekith good thingis; but he that is a serchere of yuels, schal be oppressid of tho.
020	PRO	011	028	He that tristith in hise richessis, schal falle; but iust men schulen buriowne as a greene leef.
020	PRO	011	029	He that disturblith his hows, schal haue wyndis in possessioun; and he that is a fool, schal serue a wijs man.
020	PRO	011	030	The fruyt of a riytful man is the tre of lijf; and he that takith soulis, is a wijs man.
020	PRO	011	031	If a iust man receyueth in erthe, how miche more an vnfeithful man, and synnere.
020	PRO	012	001	He that loueth chastisyng, loueth kunnyng; but he that hatith blamyngis, is vnwijs.
020	PRO	012	002	He that is good, schal drawe to hym silf grace of the Lord; but he that tristith in hise thouytis, doith wickidli.
020	PRO	012	003	A man schal not be maad strong by wyckidnesse; and the root of iust men schal not be moued.
020	PRO	012	004	A diligent womman is a coroun to hir hosebond; and rot is in the boonys of that womman, that doith thingis worthi of confusioun.
020	PRO	012	005	The thouytis of iust men ben domes; and the counselis of wickid men ben gileful.
020	PRO	012	006	The wordis of wickid men setten tresoun to blood; the mouth of iust men schal delyuere hem.
020	PRO	012	007	Turne thou wickid men, and thei schulen not be; but the housis of iust men schulen dwelle perfitli.
020	PRO	012	008	A man schal be knowun bi his teching; but he that is veyn and hertles, schal be open to dispising.
020	PRO	012	009	Betere is a pore man, and sufficient to him silf, than a gloriouse man, and nedi of breed.
020	PRO	012	010	A iust man knowith the soulis of hise werk beestis; but the entrailis of wickid men ben cruel.
020	PRO	012	011	He that worchith his lond, schal be fillid with looues; but he that sueth idilnesse, is moost fool. He that is swete, lyueth in temperaunces; and in hise monestyngis he forsakith dispisyngis.
020	PRO	012	012	The desir of a wickid man is the memorial of worste thingis; but the roote of iust men schal encreesse.
020	PRO	012	013	For the synnes of lippis `falling doun neiyeth to an yuel man; but a iust man schal scape fro angwisch.
020	PRO	012	014	Of the fruyt of his mouth ech man schal be fillid with goodis; and bi the werkis of hise hondis it schal be yoldun to him.
020	PRO	012	015	The weie of a fool is riytful in hise iyen; but he that is wijs, herith counsels.
020	PRO	012	016	A fool schewith anoon his ire; but he that dissymelith wrongis, is wijs.
020	PRO	012	017	He that spekith that, that he knowith, is a iuge of riytfulnesse; but he that lieth, is a gileful witnesse.
020	PRO	012	018	A man is that bihetith, and he is prickid as with the swerd of conscience; but the tunge of wise men is helthe.
020	PRO	012	019	The lippe of treuthe schal be stidfast with outen ende; but he that is a sudeyn witnesse, makith redi the tunge of leesyng.
020	PRO	012	020	Gile is in the herte of hem that thenken yuels; but ioye sueth hem, that maken counsels of pees.
020	PRO	012	021	What euere bifallith to a iust man, it schal not make hym sori; but wickid men schulen be fillid with yuel.
020	PRO	012	022	False lippis is abhominacioun to the Lord; but thei that don feithfuli, plesen him.
020	PRO	012	023	A fel man hilith kunnyng; and the herte of vnwise men stirith foli.
020	PRO	012	024	The hond of stronge men schal haue lordschip; but the hond that is slow, schal serue to tributis.
020	PRO	012	025	Morenynge in the herte of a iust man schal make hym meke; and he schal be maad glad bi a good word.
020	PRO	012	026	He that dispisith harm for a frend, is a iust man; but the weie of wickid men schal disseyue hem.
020	PRO	012	027	A gileful man schal not fynde wynnyng; and the substaunce of man schal be the prijs of gold.
020	PRO	012	028	Lijf is in the path of riytfulnesse; but the wrong weie leedith to deeth.
020	PRO	013	001	A wijs sone is the teching of the fadir; but he that is a scornere, herith not, whanne he is repreuyd.
020	PRO	013	002	A man schal be fillid with goodis of the fruit of his mouth; but the soule of vnpitouse men is wickid.
020	PRO	013	003	He that kepith his mouth, kepith his soule; but he that is vnwar to speke, schal feel yuels.
020	PRO	013	004	A slow man wole, and wole not; but the soule of hem that worchen schal be maad fat.
020	PRO	013	005	A iust man schal wlate a fals word; but a wickid man schendith, and schal be schent.
020	PRO	013	006	Riytfulnesse kepith the weie of an innocent man; but wickidnesse disseyueth a synnere.
020	PRO	013	007	A man is as riche, whanne he hath no thing; and a man is as pore, whanne he is in many richessis.
020	PRO	013	008	Redempcioun of the soule of man is hise richessis; but he that is pore, suffrith not blamyng.
020	PRO	013	009	The liyt of iust men makith glad; but the lanterne of wickid men schal be quenchid.
020	PRO	013	010	Stryues ben euere a mong proude men; but thei that don alle thingis with counsel, ben gouerned bi wisdom.
020	PRO	013	011	Hastid catel schal be maad lesse; but that that is gaderid litil and litil with hond, schal be multiplied.
020	PRO	013	012	Hope which is dilaied, turmentith the soule; a tre of lijf is desir comyng.
020	PRO	013	013	He that bacbitith ony thing, byndith hym silf in to tyme to comynge; but he that dredith the comaundement, schal lyue in pees.
020	PRO	013	014	The lawe of a wise man is a welle of lijf; that he bowe awei fro the falling of deth.
020	PRO	013	015	Good teching schal yyue grace; a swolowe is in the weie of dispiseris.
020	PRO	013	016	A fel man doith alle thingis with counsel; but he that is a fool, schal opene foli.
020	PRO	013	017	The messanger of a wickid man schal falle in to yuel; a feithful messanger is helthe.
020	PRO	013	018	Nedynesse and schenschip is to him that forsakith techyng; but he that assentith to a blamere, schal be glorified.
020	PRO	013	019	Desir, if it is fillid, delitith the soule; foolis wlaten hem that fleen yuels.
020	PRO	013	020	He that goith with wijs men, schal be wijs; the freend of foolis schal be maad lijk hem.
020	PRO	013	021	Yuel pursueth synneris; and goodis schulen be yoldun to iust men.
020	PRO	013	022	A good man schal leeue aftir him eiris, sones, and the sones of sones; and the catel of a synnere is kept to a iust man.
020	PRO	013	023	Many meetis ben in the new tilid feeldis of fadris; and ben gaderid to othere men with out doom.
020	PRO	013	024	He that sparith the yerde, hatith his sone; but he that loueth him, techith bisili.
020	PRO	013	025	A iust man etith, and fillith his soule; but the wombe of wickid men is vnable to be fillid.
020	PRO	014	001	A wijs womman bildith hir hous; and an unwijs womman schal distrie with hondis an hous bildid.
020	PRO	014	002	A man goynge in riytful weie, and dredinge God, is dispisid of hym, that goith in a weie of yuel fame.
020	PRO	014	003	The yerde of pride is in the mouth of a fool; the lippis of wijs men kepen hem.
020	PRO	014	004	Where oxis ben not, the cratche is void; but where ful many cornes apperen, there the strengthe of oxe is opyn.
020	PRO	014	005	A feithful witnesse schal not lie; a gileful witnesse bringith forth a leesing.
020	PRO	014	006	A scornere sekith wisdom, and he fyndith not; the teching of prudent men is esy.
020	PRO	014	007	Go thou ayens a man a fool; and he schal not knowe the lippis of prudence.
020	PRO	014	008	The wisdom of a fel man is to vndirstonde his weie; and the vnwarnesse of foolis errith.
020	PRO	014	009	A fool scorneth synne; grace schal dwelle among iust men.
020	PRO	014	010	The herte that knowith the bittirnesse of his soule; a straunger schal not be meddlid in the ioie therof.
020	PRO	014	011	The hous of wickid men schal be don awei; the tabernaclis of iust men schulen buriowne.
020	PRO	014	012	Sotheli a weie is, that semeth iust to a man; but the laste thingis therof leden forth to deth.
020	PRO	014	013	Leiyyng schal be medlid with sorewe; and morenyng ocupieth the laste thingis of ioye.
020	PRO	014	014	A fool schal be fillid with hise weies; and a good man schal be aboue hym.
020	PRO	014	015	An innocent man bileueth to eche word; a felle man biholdith hise goyngis.
020	PRO	014	016	A wijs man dredith, and bowith awei fro yuel; a fool skippith ouer, and tristith.
020	PRO	014	017	A man vnpacient schal worche foli; and a gileful man is odiouse.
020	PRO	014	018	Litle men of wit schulen holde foli; and felle men schulen abide kunnyng.
020	PRO	014	019	Yuel men schulen ligge bifor goode men; and vnpitouse men bifor the yatis of iust men.
020	PRO	014	020	A pore man schal be hateful, yhe, to his neiybore; but many men ben frendis of riche men.
020	PRO	014	021	He that dispisith his neiybore, doith synne; but he that doith merci to a pore man, schal be blessid. He that bileueth in the Lord, loueth merci;
020	PRO	014	022	thei erren that worchen yuel. Merci and treuthe maken redi goodis;
020	PRO	014	023	abundaunce `schal be in ech good werk. Sotheli where ful many wordis ben, there nedynesse is ofte.
020	PRO	014	024	The coroun of wise men is the richessis of hem; the fooli of foolis is vnwarnesse.
020	PRO	014	025	A feithful witnesse delyuereth soulis; and a fals man bringith forth leesyngis.
020	PRO	014	026	In the drede of the Lord is triste of strengthe; and hope schal be to the sones of it.
020	PRO	014	027	The drede of the Lord is a welle of lijf; that it bowe awei fro the fallyng of deth.
020	PRO	014	028	The dignite of the king is in the multitude of puple; and the schenschipe of a prince is in the fewnesse of puple.
020	PRO	014	029	He that is pacient, is gouerned bi myche wisdom; but he that is vnpacient, enhaunsith his foli.
020	PRO	014	030	Helthe of herte is the lijf of fleischis; enuye is rot of boonys.
020	PRO	014	031	He that falsli chalengith a nedi man, dispisith his maker; but he that hath merci on a pore man, onourith that makere.
020	PRO	014	032	A wickid man is put out for his malice; but a iust man hopith in his deth.
020	PRO	014	033	Wisdom restith in the herte of a wijs man; and he schal teche alle vnlerned men.
020	PRO	014	034	Riytfulnesse reisith a folc; synne makith puplis wretchis.
020	PRO	014	035	A mynystre vndurstondynge is acceptable to a kyng; a mynystre vnprofitable schal suffre the wrathfulnesse of him.
020	PRO	015	001	A soft answere brekith ire; an hard word reisith woodnesse.
020	PRO	015	002	The tunge of wise men ourneth kunnyng; the mouth of foolis buylith out foli.
020	PRO	015	003	In ech place the iyen of the Lord biholden good men, and yuel men.
020	PRO	015	004	A plesaunt tunge is the tre of lijf; but the tunge which is vnmesurable, schal defoule the spirit.
020	PRO	015	005	A fool scorneth the techyng of his fadir; but he that kepith blamyngis, schal be maad wisere. Moost vertu schal be in plenteuouse riytfulnesse; but the thouytis of wickid men schulen be drawun vp bi the roote.
020	PRO	015	006	The hous of a iust man is moost strengthe; and disturbling is in the fruitis of a wickid man.
020	PRO	015	007	The lippis of wise men schulen sowe abrood kunnyng; the herte of foolis schal be vnlijc.
020	PRO	015	008	The sacrifices of wickyd men ben abhomynable to the Lord; avowis of iust men ben plesaunt.
020	PRO	015	009	The lijf of the vnpitouse man is abhomynacioun to the Lord; he that sueth riytfulnesse, schal be loued of the Lord.
020	PRO	015	010	Yuel teching is of men forsakinge the weie of lijf; he that hatith blamyngis, schal die.
020	PRO	015	011	Helle and perdicioun ben open bifor the Lord; hou myche more the hertis of sones of men.
020	PRO	015	012	A man ful of pestilence loueth not hym that repreueth him; and he goith not to wyse men.
020	PRO	015	013	A ioiful herte makith glad the face; the spirit is cast doun in the morenyng of soule.
020	PRO	015	014	The herte of a wijs man sekith techyng; and the mouth of foolis is fed with vnkunnyng.
020	PRO	015	015	Alle the daies of a pore man ben yuele; a sikir soule is a contynuel feeste.
020	PRO	015	016	Betere is a litil with the drede of the Lord, than many tresouris and vnfillable.
020	PRO	015	017	It is betere to be clepid to wortis with charite, than with hatrede to a calf maad fat.
020	PRO	015	018	A wrathful man reisith chidyngis; he that is pacient, swagith chidyngis reisid.
020	PRO	015	019	The weie of slow men is an hegge of thornes; the weie of iust men is with out hirtyng.
020	PRO	015	020	A wise sone makith glad the fadir; and a fonned man dispisith his modir.
020	PRO	015	021	Foli is ioye to a fool; and a prudent man schal dresse hise steppis.
020	PRO	015	022	Thouytis ben distried, where no counsel is; but where many counseleris ben, tho ben confermyd.
020	PRO	015	023	A man is glad in the sentence of his mouth; and a couenable word is best.
020	PRO	015	024	The path of lijf is on a lernyd man; that he bowe awei fro the laste helle.
020	PRO	015	025	The Lord schal distrie the hows of proude men; and he schal make stidefast the coostis of a widewe.
020	PRO	015	026	Iuele thouytis is abhomynacioun of the Lord; and a cleene word moost fair schal be maad stidfast of hym.
020	PRO	015	027	He that sueth aueryce, disturblith his hous; but he that hatith yiftis schal lyue. Synnes ben purgid bi merci and feith; ech man bowith awei fro yuel bi the drede of the Lord.
020	PRO	015	028	The soule of a iust man bithenkith obedience; the mouth of wickid men is ful of yuelis.
020	PRO	015	029	The Lord is fer fro wickid men; and he schal here the preyers of iust men.
020	PRO	015	030	The liyt of iyen makith glad the soule; good fame makith fat the boonys.
020	PRO	015	031	The eere that herith the blamyngis of lijf, schal dwelle in the myddis of wise men.
020	PRO	015	032	He that castith awei chastisyng, dispisith his soule; but he that assentith to blamyngis, is pesible holdere of the herte.
020	PRO	015	033	The drede of the Lord is teching of wisdom; and mekenesse goith bifore glorie.
020	PRO	016	001	It perteyneth to man to make redi the soule; and it perteyneth to the Lord to gouerne the tunge.
020	PRO	016	002	Alle the weies of men ben opyn to the iyen of God; the Lord is a weiere of spiritis.
020	PRO	016	003	Schewe thi werkys to the Lord; and thi thouytis schulen be dressid.
020	PRO	016	004	The Lord wrouyte alle thingis for hym silf; and he made redi a wickid man to the yuel dai.
020	PRO	016	005	Abhomynacioun of the Lord is ech proude man; yhe, thouy the hond is to the hond, he schal not be innocent. The bigynnyng of good weie is to do riytwisnesse; forsothe it is more acceptable at God, than to offre sacrifices.
020	PRO	016	006	Wickidnesse is ayen bouyt bi merci and treuthe; and me bowith awei fro yuel bi the drede of the Lord.
020	PRO	016	007	Whanne the weyes of man plesen the Lord, he schal conuerte, yhe, hise enemyes to pees.
020	PRO	016	008	Betere is a litil with riytfulnesse, than many fruytis with wickidnesse.
020	PRO	016	009	The herte of a man schal dispose his weie; but it perteyneth to the Lord to dresse hise steppis.
020	PRO	016	010	Dyuynyng is in the lippis of a king; his mouth schal not erre in doom.
020	PRO	016	011	The domes of the Lord ben weiyte and a balaunce; and hise werkis ben alle the stoonys of the world.
020	PRO	016	012	Thei that don wickidli ben abhomynable to the king; for the trone of the rewme is maad stidfast bi riytfulnesse.
020	PRO	016	013	The wille of kyngis is iust lippis; he that spekith riytful thingis, schal be dressid.
020	PRO	016	014	Indignacioun of the kyng is messangeris of deth; and a wijs man schal plese him.
020	PRO	016	015	Lijf is in the gladnesse of the `cheer of the king; and his merci is as a reyn comynge late.
020	PRO	016	016	Welde thou wisdom, for it is betere than gold; and gete thou prudence, for it is precyousere than siluer.
020	PRO	016	017	The path of iust men bowith awei yuelis; the kepere of his soule kepith his weie.
020	PRO	016	018	Pride goith bifore sorewe; and the spirit schal be enhaunsid byfor fallyng.
020	PRO	016	019	It is betere to be maad meke with mylde men, than to departe spuylis with proude men.
020	PRO	016	020	A lerned man in word schal fynde goodis; and he that hopith in the Lord is blessid.
020	PRO	016	021	He that is wijs in herte, schal be clepid prudent; and he that is swete in speche, schal fynde grettere thingis.
020	PRO	016	022	The welle of lijf is the lernyng of him that weldith; the techyng of foolis is foli.
020	PRO	016	023	The herte of a wijs man schal teche his mouth; and schal encreesse grace to hise lippis.
020	PRO	016	024	Wordis wel set togidere is a coomb of hony; helthe of boonys is the swetnesse of soule.
020	PRO	016	025	A weye is that semeth riytful to a man; and the laste thingis therof leden to deth.
020	PRO	016	026	The soule of a man trauelinge trauelith to hym silf; for his mouth compellide hym.
020	PRO	016	027	An vnwijs man diggith yuel; and fier brenneth in hise lippis.
020	PRO	016	028	A weiward man reisith stryues; and a man ful of wordis departith princis.
020	PRO	016	029	A wickid man flaterith his frend; and ledith hym bi a weie not good.
020	PRO	016	030	He that thenkith schrewid thingis with iyen astonyed, bitith hise lippis, and parformeth yuel.
020	PRO	016	031	A coroun of dignyte is eelde, that schal be foundun in the weies of riytfulnesse.
020	PRO	016	032	A pacient man is betere than a stronge man; and he that `is lord of his soule, is betere than an ouercomere of citees.
020	PRO	016	033	Lottis ben sent into the bosum; but tho ben temperid of the Lord.
020	PRO	017	001	Betere is a drie mussel with ioye, than an hous ful of sacrifices with chidyng.
020	PRO	017	002	A wijs seruaunt schal be lord of fonned sones; and he schal departe eritage among britheren.
020	PRO	017	003	As siluer is preued bi fier, and gold is preued bi a chymnei, so the Lord preueth hertis.
020	PRO	017	004	An yuel man obeieth to a wickid tunge; and a fals man obeieth to false lippis.
020	PRO	017	005	He that dispisith a pore man, repreueth his maker; and he that is glad in the fallyng of another man, schal not be vnpunyschid.
020	PRO	017	006	The coroun of elde men is the sones of sones; and the glorie of sones is the fadris of hem.
020	PRO	017	007	Wordis wel set togidere bisemen not a fool; and a liynge lippe bicometh not a prince.
020	PRO	017	008	A preciouse stoon moost acceptable is the abiding of hym that sekith; whidur euere he turneth hym silf, he vndurstondith prudentli.
020	PRO	017	009	He that helith trespas, sekith frenschipis; he that rehersith bi an hiy word, departith hem, that ben knyt togidere in pees.
020	PRO	017	010	A blamyng profitith more at a prudent man, than an hundryd woundis at a fool.
020	PRO	017	011	Euere an yuel man sekith stryues; forsothe a cruel aungel schal be sent ayens hym.
020	PRO	017	012	It spedith more to meete a femal bere, whanne the whelpis ben rauyschid, than a fool tristynge to hym silf in his foli.
020	PRO	017	013	Yuel schal not go a wei fro the hous of hym, that yeldith yuels for goodis.
020	PRO	017	014	He that leeueth watir, is heed of stryues; and bifor that he suffrith wrong, he forsakith dom.
020	PRO	017	015	Bothe he that iustifieth a wickid man, and he that condempneth a iust man, euer ethir is abhomynable at God.
020	PRO	017	016	What profitith it to a fool to haue richessis, sithen he mai not bie wisdom? He that makith his hous hiy, sekith falling; and he that eschewith to lerne, schal falle in to yuels.
020	PRO	017	017	He that is a frend, loueth in al tyme; and a brother is preuyd in angwischis.
020	PRO	017	018	A fonned man schal make ioie with hondis, whanne he hath bihiyt for his frend.
020	PRO	017	019	He that bithenkith discordis, loueth chidingis; and he that enhaunsith his mouth, sekith fallyng.
020	PRO	017	020	He that is of weiward herte, schal not fynde good; and he that turneth the tunge, schal falle in to yuel.
020	PRO	017	021	A fool is borun in his schenschipe; but nether the fadir schal be glad in a fool.
020	PRO	017	022	A ioiful soule makith likinge age; a sorewful spirit makith drie boonys.
020	PRO	017	023	A wickid man takith yiftis fro the bosum, to mys turne the pathis of doom.
020	PRO	017	024	Wisdom schyneth in the face of a prudent man; the iyen of foolis ben in the endis of erthe.
020	PRO	017	025	A fonned sone is the ire of the fadir, and the sorewe of the modir that gendride hym.
020	PRO	017	026	It is not good to brynge in harm to a iust man; nether to smyte the prince that demeth riytfuli.
020	PRO	017	027	He that mesurith his wordis, is wijs and prudent; and a lerud man is of preciouse spirit.
020	PRO	017	028	Also a foole, if he is stille, schal be gessid a wijs man; and, if he pressith togidre hise lippis, he `schal be gessid an vndurstondynge man.
020	PRO	018	001	He that wole go a wei fro a frend, sekith occasiouns; in al tyme he schal be dispisable.
020	PRO	018	002	A fool resseyueth not the wordis of prudence; `no but thou seie tho thingis, that ben turned in his herte.
020	PRO	018	003	A wickid man, whanne he cometh in to depthe of synnes, dispisith; but sclaundre and schenschipe sueth hym.
020	PRO	018	004	Deep watir is the wordis of the mouth of a man; and a stronde fletinge ouer is the welle of wisdom.
020	PRO	018	005	It is not good to take the persoone of a wickid man in doom, that thou bowe awei fro the treuthe of dom.
020	PRO	018	006	The lippis of a fool medlen hem silf with chidyngis; and his mouth excitith stryues.
020	PRO	018	007	The mouth of a fool is defoulyng of hym; and hise lippis ben the fallynge of his soule.
020	PRO	018	008	The wordis of a double tungid man ben as symple; and tho comen `til to the ynnere thingis of the wombe. Drede castith doun a slowe man; forsothe the soulis of men turned in to wymmens condicioun schulen haue hungur.
020	PRO	018	009	He that is neisch, and vnstidfast in his werk, is the brother of a man distriynge hise werkis.
020	PRO	018	010	A strongeste tour is the name of the Lord; a iust man renneth to hym, and schal be enhaunsid.
020	PRO	018	011	The catel of a riche man is the citee of his strengthe; and as a stronge wal cumpassinge hym.
020	PRO	018	012	The herte of man is enhaunsid, bifor that it be brokun; and it is maad meke, bifore that it be glorified.
020	PRO	018	013	He that answerith bifore that he herith, shewith hym silf to be a fool; and worthi of schenschipe.
020	PRO	018	014	The spirit of a man susteyneth his feblenesse; but who may susteyne a spirit liyt to be wrooth?
020	PRO	018	015	The herte of a prudent man schal holde stidfastli kunnyng; and the eere of wise men sekith techyng.
020	PRO	018	016	The yift of a man alargith his weie; and makith space to hym bifore princes.
020	PRO	018	017	A iust man is the first accusere of hym silf; his frend cometh, and schal serche hym.
020	PRO	018	018	Lot ceessith ayenseiyngis; and demeth also among miyti men.
020	PRO	018	019	A brother that is helpid of a brothir, is as a stidfast citee; and domes ben as the barris of citees.
020	PRO	018	020	A mannus wombe schal be fillid of the fruit of his mouth; and the seedis of hise lippis schulen fille hym.
020	PRO	018	021	Deth and lijf ben in the werkis of tunge; thei that louen it, schulen ete the fruytis therof.
020	PRO	018	022	He that fyndith a good womman, fyndith a good thing; and of the Lord he schal drawe vp myrthe. He that puttith a wey a good womman, puttith awei a good thing; but he that holdith auowtresse, is a fool and vnwijs.
020	PRO	018	023	A pore man schal speke with bisechingis; and a riche man schal speke sterneli.
020	PRO	018	024	A man freendli to felouschipe schal more be a frend, than a brothir.
020	PRO	019	001	Betere is a pore man, that goith in his simplenesse, than a riche man bitynge hise lippis, and vnwijs.
020	PRO	019	002	Where is not kunnyng of the soule, is not good; and he that is hasti, in feet hirtith.
020	PRO	019	003	The foli of a man disseyueth hise steppis; and he brenneth in his soule ayens God.
020	PRO	019	004	Richessis encreessen ful many freendis; forsothe also thei ben departid fro a pore man, whiche he hadde.
020	PRO	019	005	A fals witnesse schal not be vnpunyschid; and he that spekith leesingis, schal not ascape.
020	PRO	019	006	Many men onouren the persoone of a myyti man; and ben frendis of hym that deelith yiftis.
020	PRO	019	007	The britheren of a pore man haten hym; ferthermore and the freendis yeden awei fer fro hym. He that sueth wordis oonli, schal haue no thing;
020	PRO	019	008	but he that holdith stabli the mynde, loueth his soule, and the kepere of prudence schal fynde goodis.
020	PRO	019	009	A fals witnesse schal not be vnpunyschid; and he that spekith leesyngis, schal perische.
020	PRO	019	010	Delices bicomen not a fool; nether `it bicometh a seruaunt to be lord of princes.
020	PRO	019	011	The teching of a man is knowun bi pacience; and his glorie is to passe ouere wickid thingis.
020	PRO	019	012	As the gnasting of a lioun, so and the ire of the king; and as deewe on eerbe, so and the gladnesse of the kyng.
020	PRO	019	013	The sorewe of the fadir is a fonned sone; and roofes droppynge contynueli is a womman ful of chiding.
020	PRO	019	014	Housis and richessis ben youun of fadir and modir; but a prudent wijf is youun propirli of the Lord.
020	PRO	019	015	Slouth bringith in sleep; and a negligent soule schal haue hungur.
020	PRO	019	016	He that kepith the comaundement of God, kepith his soule; but he that chargith not his weie, schal be slayn.
020	PRO	019	017	He that hath mercy on a pore man, leeneth to the Lord; and he schal yelde his while to hym.
020	PRO	019	018	Teche thi sone, and dispeire thou not; but sette thou not thi soule to the sleyng of hym.
020	PRO	019	019	Forsothe he that is vnpacient, schal suffre harm; and whanne he hath rauyschid, he schal leie to anothir thing.
020	PRO	019	020	Here thou counsel, and take thou doctryn; that thou be wijs in thi laste thingis.
020	PRO	019	021	Many thouytis ben in the herte of a man; but the wille of the Lord schal dwelle.
020	PRO	019	022	A nedi man is merciful; and betere is a pore iust man, than a man liere.
020	PRO	019	023	The drede of the Lord ledith to lijf `of blis; and he `that dredith God schal dwelle in plentee, with outen visityng `of the worste.
020	PRO	019	024	A slow man hidith his hond vndur the armpit; and putteth it not to his mouth.
020	PRO	019	025	Whanne a man ful of pestilence is betun, a fool schal be wisere. If thou blamist a wijs man, he schal vndurstonde techyng.
020	PRO	019	026	He that turmentith the fadir, and fleeth fro the modir, schal be ful of yuel fame, and schal be cursid.
020	PRO	019	027	Sone, ceesse thou not to here techyng; and knowe thou the wordis of kunnyng.
020	PRO	019	028	A wickid witnesse scorneth doom; and the mouth of vnpitouse men deuourith wickidnesse.
020	PRO	019	029	Domes ben maad redi to scorneris; and hameris smytynge ben maad redi to the bodies of foolis.
020	PRO	020	001	Wiyn is a letcherouse thing and drunkenesse is ful of noise; who euere delitith in these, schal not be wijs.
020	PRO	020	002	As the roryng of a lioun, so and the drede of the kyng; he that territh hym to ire, synneth ayens his owne lijf.
020	PRO	020	003	It is onour to a man that departith hym silf fro stryuyngis; but fonned men ben medlid with dispisyngis.
