020	PRO	026	011	As a dogge that turneth ayen to his spuyng; so is an vnprudent man, that rehersith his fooli.
020	PRO	026	012	Thou hast seyn a man seme wijs to hym silf; an vnkunnyng man schal haue hope more than he.
020	PRO	026	013	A slow man seith, A lioun is in the weie, a liounnesse is in the foot pathis.
020	PRO	026	014	As a dore is turned in his hengis; so a slow man in his bed.
020	PRO	026	015	A slow man hidith hise hondis vndur his armpit; and he trauelith, if he turneth tho to his mouth.
020	PRO	026	016	A slow man semeth wysere to hym silf, than seuene men spekynge sentensis.
020	PRO	026	017	As he that takith a dogge bi the eeris; so he that passith, and is vnpacient, and is meddlid with the chiding of anothir man.
020	PRO	026	018	As he is gilti, that sendith speris and arowis in to deth;
020	PRO	026	019	so a man that anoieth gilefuli his frend, and whanne he is takun, he schal seie, Y dide pleiynge.
020	PRO	026	020	Whanne trees failen, the fier schal be quenchid; and whanne a priuy bacbitere is withdrawun, stryues resten.
020	PRO	026	021	As deed coolis at quic coolis, and trees at the fier; so a wrathful man reisith chidyngis.
020	PRO	026	022	The wordis of a pryuei bacbitere ben as symple; and tho comen til to the ynneste thingis of the herte.
020	PRO	026	023	As if thou wolt ourne a vessel of erthe with foul siluer; so ben bolnynge lippis felouschipid with `the werste herte.
020	PRO	026	024	An enemy is vndirstondun bi hise lippis, whanne he tretith giles in the herte.
020	PRO	026	025	Whanne he `makith low his vois, bileue thou not to hym; for seuene wickidnessis ben in his herte.
020	PRO	026	026	The malice of hym that hilith hatrede gilefuli, schal be schewid in a counsel.
020	PRO	026	027	He that delueth a diche, schal falle in to it; and if a man walewith a stoon, it schal turne ayen to hym.
020	PRO	026	028	A fals tunge loueth not treuth; and a slidir mouth worchith fallyngis.
020	PRO	027	001	Haue thou not glorie on the morewe, `not knowynge what thing the dai to comynge schal bringe forth.
020	PRO	027	002	Another man, and not thi mouth preise thee; a straunger, and not thi lippis `preise thee.
020	PRO	027	003	A stoon is heuy, and grauel is chariouse; but the ire of a fool is heuyere than euer eithir.
020	PRO	027	004	Ire hath no merci, and woodnesse brekynge out `hath no merci; and who mai suffre the fersnesse of a spirit stirid?
020	PRO	027	005	Betere is opyn repreuyng, than loue hid.
020	PRO	027	006	Betere ben the woundis of hym that loueth, than the gileful cossis of hym that hatith.
020	PRO	027	007	A man fillid schal dispise an hony coomb; but an hungri man schal take, yhe, bittir thing for swete.
020	PRO	027	008	As a brid passinge ouer fro his nest, so is a man that forsakith his place.
020	PRO	027	009	The herte delitith in oynement, and dyuerse odours; and a soule is maad swete bi the good counsels of a frend.
020	PRO	027	010	Forsake thou not thi frend, and the frend of thi fadir; and entre thou not in to the hous of thi brothir, in the dai of thi turment. Betere is a neiybore nyy, than a brothir afer.
020	PRO	027	011	Mi sone, studie thou a boute wisdom, and make thou glad myn herte; that thou maist answere a word to a dispisere.
020	PRO	027	012	A fel man seynge yuel was hid; litle men of wit passinge forth suffriden harmes.
020	PRO	027	013	Take thou awei his clooth, that bihiyte for a straunger; and take thou awei a wed fro hym for an alien man.
020	PRO	027	014	He that blessith his neiybore with greet vois; and risith bi niyt, schal be lijk hym that cursith.
020	PRO	027	015	Roouys droppynge in the dai of coold, and a womman ful of chidyng ben comparisond.
020	PRO	027	016	He that withholdith hir, as if he holdith wynd; and auoidith the oile of his riyt hond.
020	PRO	027	017	Yrun is whettid bi irun; and a man whettith the face of his frend.
020	PRO	027	018	He that kepith a fige tre, schal ete the fruytis therof; and he that is a kepere of his lord, schal be glorified.
020	PRO	027	019	As the cheris of men biholdinge schynen in watris; so the hertis of men ben opyn to prudent men.
020	PRO	027	020	Helle and perdicioun schulen not be fillid; so and the iyen of men moun not be fillid.
020	PRO	027	021	As siluer is preuyd in a wellyng place, and gold `is preued in a furneys; so a man is preued bi the mouth of preyseris. The herte of a wickid man sekith out yuels; but a riytful herte sekith out kunnyng.
020	PRO	027	022	Thouy thou beetist a fool in a morter, as with a pestel smytynge aboue dried barli; his foli schal not be don awei fro him.
020	PRO	027	023	Knowe thou diligentli the cheere of thi beeste; and biholde thou thi flockis.
020	PRO	027	024	For thou schalt not haue power contynueli; but a coroun schal be youun to thee in generacioun and in to generacioun.
020	PRO	027	025	Medewis ben openyd, and greene eerbis apperiden; and hey is gaderid fro hillis.
020	PRO	027	026	Lambren be to thi clothing; and kidis be to the prijs of feeld.
020	PRO	027	027	The mylke of geete suffice to thee for thi meetis; in to the necessarie thingis of thin hous, and to lijflode to thin handmaidis.
020	PRO	028	001	A wickid man fleeth, whanne no man pursueth; but a iust man as a lioun tristynge schal be with out ferdfulnesse.
020	PRO	028	002	For the synnes of the lond ben many princis therof; and for the wisdom of a man, and for the kunnyng of these thingis that ben seid, the lijf of the duyk schal be lengere.
020	PRO	028	003	A pore man falsli calengynge pore men, is lijk a grete reyn, wherynne hungur is maad redi.
020	PRO	028	004	Thei that forsaken the lawe, preisen a wickid man; thei that kepen `the lawe, ben kyndlid ayens hym.
020	PRO	028	005	Wickid men thenken not doom; but thei that seken the Lord, perseyuen alle thingis.
020	PRO	028	006	Betere is a pore man goynge in his sympilnesse, than a riche man in schrewid weies.
020	PRO	028	007	He that kepith the lawe, is a wijs sone; but he that fedith glotouns, schendith his fadir.
020	PRO	028	008	He that gaderith togidere richessis bi vsuris, and fre encrees, gaderith tho togidere ayens pore men.
020	PRO	028	009	His preyer schal be maad cursid, that bowith awei his eere; that he here not the lawe.
020	PRO	028	010	He that disseyueth iust men in an yuel weye, schal falle in his perisching; and iuste men schulen welde hise goodis.
020	PRO	028	011	A ryche man semeth wijs to him silf; but a pore man prudent schal serche him.
020	PRO	028	012	In enhaunsing of iust men is miche glorie; whanne wickid men regnen, fallyngis of men ben.
020	PRO	028	013	He that hidith hise grete trespassis, schal not be maad riytful; but he that knoulechith and forsakith tho, schal gete merci.
020	PRO	028	014	Blessid is the man, which is euere dredeful; but he that is `harde of soule, schal falle in to yuel.
020	PRO	028	015	A rorynge lioun, and an hungry bere, is a wickid prince on a pore puple.
020	PRO	028	016	A duyk nedi of prudence schal oppresse many men bi fals chalenge; but the daies of hym that hatith aueryce, schulen be maad longe.
020	PRO	028	017	No man susteyneth a man that falsly chalengith the blood of a man, if he fleeth `til to the lake.
020	PRO	028	018	He that goith simpli, schal be saaf; he that goith bi weiward weies, schal falle doun onys.
020	PRO	028	019	He that worchith his lond, schal be fillid with looues; he that sueth ydelnesse, schal be fillid with nedynesse.
020	PRO	028	020	A feithful man schal be preisid myche; but he that hastith to be maad riche, schal not be innocent.
020	PRO	028	021	He that knowith a face in doom, doith not wel; this man forsakith treuthe, yhe, for a mussel of breed.
020	PRO	028	022	A man that hastith to be maad riche, and hath enuye to othere men; woot not that nedinesse schal come on hym.
020	PRO	028	023	He that repreueth a man, schal fynde grace aftirward at hym; more than he that disseyueth bi flateryngis of tunge.
020	PRO	028	024	He that withdrawith ony thing fro his fadir and fro his modir, and seith that this is no synne, is parcener of a manquellere.
020	PRO	028	025	He that auauntith hym silf, and alargith, reisith stryues; but he that hopith in the Lord, schal be sauyd.
020	PRO	028	026	He that tristith in his herte, is a fool; but he that goith wiseli,
020	PRO	028	027	schal be preysid. He that yyueth to a pore man, schal not be nedi; he that dispisith `a pore man bisechynge, schal suffre nedynesse.
020	PRO	028	028	Whanne vnpitouse men risen, men schulen be hid; whanne tho `vnpitouse men han perischid, iust men schulen be multiplied.
020	PRO	029	001	Sodeyn perischyng schal come on that man, that with hard nol dispisith a blamere; and helth schal not sue hym.
020	PRO	029	002	The comynalte schal be glad in the multipliyng of iust men; whanne wickid men han take prinshod, the puple schal weyle.
020	PRO	029	003	A man that loueth wisdom, makith glad his fadir; but he that nurschith `an hoore, schal leese catel.
020	PRO	029	004	A iust king reisith the lond; an auerouse man schal distrie it.
020	PRO	029	005	A man that spekith bi flaterynge and feyned wordis to his frend; spredith abrood a net to hise steppis.
020	PRO	029	006	A snare schal wlappe a wickid man doynge synne; and a iust man schal preise, and schal make ioye.
020	PRO	029	007	A iust man knowith the cause of pore men; an vnpitouse man knowith not kunnyng.
020	PRO	029	008	Men ful of pestilence distryen a citee; but wise men turnen awei woodnesse.
020	PRO	029	009	If a wijs man stryueth with a fool; whether he be wrooth, `ether he leiyith, he schal not fynde reste.
020	PRO	029	010	Menquelleris haten a simple man; but iust men seken his soule.
020	PRO	029	011	A fool bringith forth al his spirit; a wise man dilaieth, and reserueth in to tyme comynge afterward.
020	PRO	029	012	A prince that herith wilfuli the wordis of a leesyng; schal haue alle mynystris vnfeithful.
020	PRO	029	013	A pore man and a leenere metten hem silf; the Lord is liytnere of euer ethir.
020	PRO	029	014	If a kyng demeth pore men in treuthe; his trone schal be maad stidfast with outen ende.
020	PRO	029	015	A yerde and chastisyng schal yyue wisdom; but a child, which is left to his wille, schendith his modir.
020	PRO	029	016	Grete trespassis schulen be multiplied in the multipliyng of wickid men; and iust men schulen se the fallyngis of hem.
020	PRO	029	017	Teche thi sone, and he schal coumforte thee; and he schal yyue delicis to thi soule.
020	PRO	029	018	Whanne prophesie faylith, the puple schal be distried; but he that kepith the lawe, is blessid.
020	PRO	029	019	A seruaunt mai not be tauyt bi wordis; for he vndirstondith that that thou seist, and dispisith for to answere.
020	PRO	029	020	Thou hast seyn a man swift to speke; foli schal be hopid more than his amendyng.
020	PRO	029	021	He that nurschith his seruaunt delicatli fro childhod; schal fynde hym rebel aftirward.
020	PRO	029	022	A wrathful man territh chidingis; and he that is liyt to haue indignacioun, schal be more enclynaunt to synnes.
020	PRO	029	023	Lownesse sueth a proude man; and glorie schal vp take a meke man of spirit.
020	PRO	029	024	He that takith part with a theef, hatith his soule; he herith a man chargynge greetli, and schewith not.
020	PRO	029	025	He that dredith a man, schal falle soon; he that hopith in the Lord, shal be reisid.
020	PRO	029	026	Many men seken the face of the prince; and the doom of alle men schal go forth of the Lord.
020	PRO	029	027	Iust men han abhomynacioun of a wickid man; and wickid men han abhomynacioun of hem, that ben in a riytful weye. A sone kepynge a word, schal be out of perdicioun.
020	PRO	030	001	The wordis of hym that gaderith, of the sone spuynge. The prophesie which a man spak, with whom God was, and which man was coumfortid bi God dwellyng with hym,
020	PRO	030	002	and seide, Y am the moost fool of men; and the wisdom of men is not with me.
020	PRO	030	003	Y lernede not wisdom; and Y knew not the kunnyng of hooli men.
020	PRO	030	004	Who stiede in to heuene, and cam doun? Who helde togidere the spirit in hise hondis? who bonde togidere watris as in a cloth? Who reiside alle the endis of erthe? What is name of hym? and what is the name of his sone, if thou knowist?
020	PRO	030	005	Ech word of God is a scheld set a fiere, to alle that hopen in hym.
020	PRO	030	006	Adde thou not ony thing to the wordis of hym, and thou be repreued, and be foundun a liere.
020	PRO	030	007	I preiede thee twei thingis; denye not thou to me, bifor that Y die.
020	PRO	030	008	Make thou fer fro me vanyte and wordis of leesyng; yyue thou not to me beggery and richessis; yyue thou oneli necessaries to my lijflode;
020	PRO	030	009	lest perauenture Y be fillid, and be drawun to denye, and seie, Who is the Lord? and lest Y compellid bi nedynesse, stele, and forswere the name of my God.
020	PRO	030	010	Accuse thou not a seruaunt to his lord, lest perauenture he curse thee, and thou falle doun.
020	PRO	030	011	A generacioun that cursith his fadir, and that blessith not his modir.
020	PRO	030	012	A generacioun that semeth cleene to it silf, and netheles is not waischun fro hise filthis.
020	PRO	030	013	A generacioun whose iyen ben hiy, and the iye liddis therof ben reisid in to hiy thingis.
020	PRO	030	014	A generacioun that hath swerdis for teeth, and etith with hise wank teeth; that it ete nedi men of erthe, and the porails of men.
020	PRO	030	015	The watir leche hath twei douytris, seiynge, Brynge, bringe. Thre thingis ben vnable to be fillid, and the fourthe, that seith neuere, It suffisith;
020	PRO	030	016	helle, and the mouth of the wombe, and the erthe which is neuere fillid with water; but fier seith neuere, It suffisith.
020	PRO	030	017	Crowis of the stronde picke out thilke iye, that scorneth the fadir, and that dispisith the child beryng of his modir; and the briddis of an egle ete that iye.
020	PRO	030	018	Thre thingis ben hard to me, and outirli Y knowe not the fourthe thing;
020	PRO	030	019	the weye of an egle in heuene, the weie of a serpent on a stoon, the weie of a schip in the myddil of the see, and the weie of a man in yong wexynge age.
020	PRO	030	020	Siche is the weie of a womman auowtresse, which etith, and wipith hir mouth, and seith, Y wrouyte not yuel.
020	PRO	030	021	The erthe is moued bi thre thingis, and the fourthe thing, which it may not susteyne;
020	PRO	030	022	bi a seruaunt, whanne he regneth; bi a fool, whanne he is fillid with mete;
020	PRO	030	023	bi an hateful womman, whanne sche is takun in matrymonye; and bi an handmaide, whanne sche is eir of hir ladi.
020	PRO	030	024	Foure ben the leeste thingis of erthe, and tho ben wisere than wise men;
020	PRO	030	025	amtis, a feble puple, that maken redi mete in heruest to hem silf;
020	PRO	030	026	a hare, a puple vnmyyti, that settith his bed in a stoon;
020	PRO	030	027	a locust hath no kyng, and al goith out bi cumpanyes; an euete enforsith with hondis,
020	PRO	030	028	and dwellith in the housis of kingis.
020	PRO	030	029	Thre thingis ben, that goon wel, and the fourthe thing, that goith richeli.
020	PRO	030	030	A lioun, strongeste of beestis, schal not drede at the meetyng of ony man;
020	PRO	030	031	a cok gird the leendis, and a ram, and noon is that schal ayenstonde him.
020	PRO	030	032	He that apperith a fool, aftir that he is reisid an hiy; for if he hadde vndurstonde, he hadde sett hond on his mouth.
020	PRO	030	033	Forsothe he that thristith strongli teetis, to drawe out mylk, thristith out botere; and he that smytith greetli, drawith out blood; and he that stirith iris, bringith forth discordis.
020	PRO	031	001	The wordis of Lamuel, the king; the visioun bi which his modir tauyte hym.
020	PRO	031	002	What my derlyng? what the derlyng of my wombe? what the derlyng of my desiris?
020	PRO	031	003	Yyue thou not thi catel to wymmen, and thi richessis to do awei kyngis.
020	PRO	031	004	A! Lamuel, nyle thou yiue wyn to kingis; for no pryuete is, where drunkenesse regneth.
020	PRO	031	005	Lest perauenture thei drynke, and foryete domes, and chaunge the cause of the sones of a pore man.
020	PRO	031	006	Yyue ye sidur to hem that morenen, and wyn to hem that ben of bitter soule.
020	PRO	031	007	Drinke thei, and foryete thei her nedinesse; and thenke thei no more on her sorewe.
020	PRO	031	008	Opene thi mouth for a doumb man,
020	PRO	031	009	and opene thi mouth for the causes of alle sones that passen forth. Deme thou that that is iust, and deme thou a nedi man and a pore man.
020	PRO	031	010	Who schal fynde a stronge womman? the prijs of her is fer, and fro the laste endis.
020	PRO	031	011	The herte of hir hosebond tristith in hir; and sche schal not haue nede to spuylis.
020	PRO	031	012	Sche schal yelde to hym good, and not yuel, in alle the daies of hir lijf.
020	PRO	031	013	Sche souyte wolle and flex; and wrouyte bi the counsel of hir hondis.
020	PRO	031	014	Sche is maad as the schip of a marchaunt, that berith his breed fro fer.
020	PRO	031	015	And sche roos bi nyyt, and yaf prey to hir meyneals, and metis to hir handmaidis.
020	PRO	031	016	Sche bihelde a feeld, and bouyte it; of the fruyt of hir hondis sche plauntide a vyner.
020	PRO	031	017	Sche girde hir leendis with strengthe, and made strong hir arm.
020	PRO	031	018	Sche taastide, and siy, that hir marchaundie was good; hir lanterne schal not be quenchid in the niyt.
020	PRO	031	019	Sche putte hir hondis to stronge thingis, and hir fyngris token the spyndil.
020	PRO	031	020	Sche openyde hir hond to a nedi man, and stretchide forth hir hondis to a pore man.
020	PRO	031	021	Sche schal not drede for hir hous of the cooldis of snow; for alle hir meyneals ben clothid with double clothis.
020	PRO	031	022	Sche made to hir a ray cloth; bijs and purpur is the cloth of hir.
020	PRO	031	023	Hir hosebonde is noble in the yatis, whanne he sittith with the senatours of erthe.
020	PRO	031	024	Sche made lynnun cloth, and selde; and yaf a girdil to a Chananei.
020	PRO	031	025	Strengthe and fairnesse is the clothing of hir; and sche schal leiye in the laste dai.
020	PRO	031	026	Sche openyde hir mouth to wisdom; and the lawe of merci is in hir tunge.
020	PRO	031	027	Sche bihelde the pathis of hir hous; and sche eet not breed idili.
020	PRO	031	028	Hir sones risiden, and prechiden hir moost blessid; hir hosebonde roos, and preiside hir.
020	PRO	031	029	Many douytris gaderiden richessis; thou passidist alle.
020	PRO	031	030	Fairnesse is disseiuable grace, and veyn; thilke womman, that dredith the Lord, schal be preisid.
020	PRO	031	031	Yyue ye to hir of the fruyt of hir hondis; and hir werkis preise hir in the yatis.
