# BOOK	040	MAT	Matthew	Matthew
040	MAT	001	001	The book of the generacioun of Jhesu Crist, the sone of Dauid, the sone of Abraham.
040	MAT	001	002	Abraham bigat Isaac. Isaac bigat Jacob. Jacob bigat Judas and hise britheren.
040	MAT	001	003	Judas bigat Fares and Zaram, of Tamar. Fares bigat Esrom.
040	MAT	001	004	Esrom bigat Aram. Aram bigat Amynadab. Amynadab bigat Naason. Naason bigat Salmon.
040	MAT	001	005	Salmon bigat Booz, of Raab. Booz bigat Obeth, of Ruth. Obeth bigat Jesse. Jesse bigat Dauid the king.
040	MAT	001	006	Dauid the king bigat Salamon, of hir that was Vries wijf.
040	MAT	001	007	Salomon bigat Roboam. Roboam bigat Abias.
040	MAT	001	008	Abias bigat Asa. Asa bigat Josaphath. Josaphath bigat Joram. Joram bigat
040	MAT	001	009	Osias. Osias bigat Joathan. Joathan bigat Achaz. Achaz bigat Ezechie.
040	MAT	001	010	Ezechie bigat Manasses. Manasses bigat Amon.
040	MAT	001	011	Amon bigat Josias. Josias bigat Jeconyas and his britheren, in to the transmygracioun of Babiloyne.
040	MAT	001	012	And aftir the transmygracioun of Babiloyne, Jeconyas bigat Salatiel. Salatiel bigat Zorobabel.
040	MAT	001	013	Zorobabel bigat Abyut. Abyut bigat Eliachym. Eliachym bigat Asor.
040	MAT	001	014	Asor bigat Sadoc. Sadoc bigat Achym.
040	MAT	001	015	Achym bigat Elyut. Elyut bigat Eleasar. Eleasar bigat Mathan.
040	MAT	001	016	Mathan bigat Jacob. Jacob bigat Joseph, the hosebonde of Marye, of whom Jhesus was borun, that is clepid Christ.
040	MAT	001	017	And so alle generaciouns fro Abraham to Dauid ben fourtene generacions, and fro Dauid to the transmygracioun of Babiloyne ben fourtene generaciouns, and fro the transmygracioun of Babiloyne to Crist ben fourtene generaciouns.
040	MAT	001	018	But the generacioun of Crist was thus. Whanne Marie, the modir of Jhesu, was spousid to Joseph, bifore thei camen togidere, she was foundun hauynge of the Hooli Goost in the wombe.
040	MAT	001	019	And Joseph, hir hosebonde, for he was riytful, and wolde not puplische hir, he wolde priueli haue left hir.
040	MAT	001	020	But while he thouyte thes thingis, lo! the aungel of the Lord apperide `in sleep to hym, and seide, Joseph, the sone of Dauid, nyle thou drede to take Marie, thi wijf; for that thing that is borun in hir is of the Hooli Goost.
040	MAT	001	021	And she shal bere a sone, and thou shalt clepe his name Jhesus; for he schal make his puple saaf fro her synnes.
040	MAT	001	022	For al this thing was don, that it schulde be fulfillid, that was seid of the Lord bi a prophete, seiynge, Lo!
040	MAT	001	023	a virgyn shal haue in wombe, and she schal bere a sone, and thei schulen clepe his name Emanuel, that is to seie, God with vs.
040	MAT	001	024	And Joseph roos fro sleepe, and dide as the aungel of the Lord comaundide hym, and took Marie, his wijf;
040	MAT	001	025	and he knew her not, til she hadde borun her firste bigete sone, and clepide his name Jhesus.
040	MAT	002	001	Therfor whanne Jhesus was borun in Bethleem of Juda, in the daies of king Eroude, lo! astromyenes camen fro the eest to Jerusalem,
040	MAT	002	002	and seiden, Where is he, that is borun king of Jewis? for we han seyn his sterre in the eest, and we comen to worschipe him.
040	MAT	002	003	But king Eroude herde, and was trublid, and al Jerusalem with hym.
040	MAT	002	004	And he gaderide to gidre alle the prynces of prestis, and scribis of the puple, and enqueride of hem, where Crist shulde be borun.
040	MAT	002	005	And thei seiden to hym, In Bethleem of Juda; for so it is writun bi a profete,
040	MAT	002	006	And thou, Bethleem, the lond of Juda, art not the leest among the prynces of Juda; for of thee a duyk schal go out, that schal gouerne my puple of Israel.
040	MAT	002	007	Thanne Eroude clepide pryueli the astromyens, and lernyde bisili of hem the tyme of the sterre that apperide to hem.
040	MAT	002	008	And he sente hem in to Bethleem, and seide, Go ye, and axe ye bisili of the child, and whanne yee han foundun, telle ye it to me, that Y also come, and worschipe hym.
040	MAT	002	009	And whanne thei hadden herd the kyng, thei wenten forth. And lo! the sterre, that thei siyen in the eest, wente bifore hem, til it cam, and stood aboue, where the child was.
040	MAT	002	010	And thei siyen the sterre, and ioyeden with a ful greet ioye.
040	MAT	002	011	And thei entriden in to the hous, and founden the child with Marie, his modir; and thei felden doun, and worschipiden him. And whanne thei hadden openyd her tresouris, thei offryden to hym yiftis, gold, encense, and myrre.
040	MAT	002	012	And whanne thei hadden take an aunswere in sleep, that thei schulden not turne ayen to Eroude, thei turneden ayen bi anothir weie in to her cuntrey.
040	MAT	002	013	And whanne thei weren goon, lo! the aungel of the Lord apperide to Joseph in sleep, and seide, Rise vp, and take the child and his modir, and fle in to Egipt, and be thou there, til that I seie to thee; for it is to come, that Eroude seke the child, to destrie hym.
040	MAT	002	014	And Joseph roos, and took the child and his modir bi nyyt, and wente in to Egipt,
040	MAT	002	015	and he was there to the deeth of Eroude; that it schulde be fulfillid, that was seid of the Lord bi the profete, seiynge, Fro Egipt Y haue clepid my sone.
040	MAT	002	016	Thanne Eroude seynge that he was disseyued of the astromyens, was ful wrooth; and he sente, and slowe alle the children, that weren in Bethleem, and in alle the coostis therof, fro two yeer age and with inne, aftir the tyme that he had enquerid of the astromyens.
040	MAT	002	017	Thanne `it was fulfillid, that was seid bi Jeremye, the profete,
040	MAT	002	018	seiynge, A vois was herd an hiy, wepynge and moche weilyng, Rachel biwepynge hir sones, and she wolde not be coumfortid, for thei ben noyt.
040	MAT	002	019	But whanne Eroude was deed, loo! the aungel of the Lord apperide to Joseph in sleep in Egipt,
040	MAT	002	020	and seide, Ryse vp, and take the child and his modir, and go in to the lond of Israel; for thei that souyten the lijf of the chijld ben deed.
040	MAT	002	021	Joseph roos, and took the child and his modir, and cam in to the loond of Israel.
040	MAT	002	022	And he herde that Archilaus regnede in Judee for Eroude, his fadir, and dredde to go thidir. And he was warned in sleep, and wente in to the parties of Galilee;
040	MAT	002	023	and cam, and dwelte in a citee, that ys clepid Nazareth, that it shulde be fulfillid, that was seid bi profetis, For he shal be clepid a Nazarey.
040	MAT	003	001	In tho daies Joon Baptist cam, and prechide in the desert of Judee,
040	MAT	003	002	and seide, Do ye penaunce, for the kyngdom of heuenes shal neiye.
040	MAT	003	003	For this is he, of whom it is seid bi Ysaie, the prophete, seyinge, A vois of a crier in desert, Make ye redi the weies of the Lord; make ye riyt the pathis of hym.
040	MAT	003	004	And this Joon hadde clothing of camels heeris, and a girdil of skynne aboute hise leendis; and his mete was honysoukis, and hony of the wode.
040	MAT	003	005	Thanne Jerusalem wente out to hym, and al Judee, and al the cuntre aboute Jordan;
040	MAT	003	006	and thei weren waischun of hym in Jordan, `and knowlechiden her synnes.
040	MAT	003	007	But he siy manye of the Farysees and of Saduceis comynge to his baptym, and seide to hem, Generaciouns of eddris, who shewide to you to fle fro the wraththe that is to come?
040	MAT	003	008	Therfor do ye worthi fruyte of penaunce,
040	MAT	003	009	and nyle ye seie with ynne you, We han Abraham to fadir; for Y seie to you, that God is myyti to reise vp of these stoones the sones of Abraham.
040	MAT	003	010	And now the ax is put to the roote of the tree; therfore euery tree that makith not good fruyt, shal be kit doun, and shal be cast in to the fier.
040	MAT	003	011	Y waische you in water, in to penaunce; but he that shal come after me is strongere than Y, whos schoon Y am not worthi to bere; he shal baptise you in the Hooli Goost and fier.
040	MAT	003	012	Whos wynewing cloth is in his hoond, and he shal fulli clense his corn flore, and shal gadere his whete in to his berne; but the chaffe he shal brenne with fier that mai not be quenchid.
