# BOOK	042	LUK	Luke	Luke
042	LUK	001	001	Forsothe for manye men enforceden to ordeyne the tellyng of thingis, whiche ben fillid in vs,
042	LUK	001	002	as thei that seyn atte the bigynnyng, and weren ministris of the word,
042	LUK	001	003	bitaken, it is seen also to me, hauynge alle thingis diligentli bi ordre, to write to thee,
042	LUK	001	004	thou best Theofile, that thou knowe the treuthe of tho wordis, of whiche thou art lerned.
042	LUK	001	005	In the daies of Eroude, kyng of Judee, ther was a prest, Sakarie bi name, of the sorte of Abia, and his wijf was of the douytris of Aaron, and hir name was Elizabeth.
042	LUK	001	006	And bothe weren iust bifor God, goynge in alle the maundementis and iustifiyngis of the Lord, withouten pleynt.
042	LUK	001	007	And thei hadden no child, for Elizabeth was bareyn, and bothe weren of grete age in her daies.
042	LUK	001	008	And it bifel, that whanne Zacarie schulde do the office of preesthod, in the ordre of his cours tofor God,
042	LUK	001	009	aftir the custome of the preesthod, he wente forth bi lot, and entride in to the temple, to encense.
042	LUK	001	010	And al the multitude of the puple was with outforth, and preiede in the our of encensyng.
042	LUK	001	011	And an aungel of the Lord apperide to hym, and stood on the riythalf of the auter of encense.
042	LUK	001	012	And Zacarie seynge was afraied, and drede fel vpon hym.
042	LUK	001	013	And the aungel seide to hym, Zacarie, drede thou not; for thi preyer is herd, and Elizabeth, thi wijf, schal bere to thee a sone, and his name schal be clepid Joon.
042	LUK	001	014	And ioye and gladyng schal be to thee; and many schulen `haue ioye in his natyuyte.
042	LUK	001	015	For he schal be greet bifor the Lord, and he schal not drynke wyn and sidir, and he schal be fulfillid with the Hooli Goost yit of his modir wombe.
042	LUK	001	016	And he schal conuerte many of the children of Israel to her Lord God;
042	LUK	001	017	and he schal go bifor hym in the spirit and the vertu of Helie; and he schal turne the hertis of the fadris in to the sones, and men out of bileue to the prudence of iust men, to make redi a perfit puple to the Lord.
042	LUK	001	018	And Zacarie seide to the aungel, Wherof schal Y wite this? for Y am eld, and my wijf hath gon fer in to hir daies.
042	LUK	001	019	And the aungel answeride, and seide to hym, For Y am Gabriel, that stonde niy bifor God; and Y am sent to thee to speke, and to euangelize to thee these thingis.
042	LUK	001	020	And lo! thou schalt be doumbe, and thou schalt not mow speke til in to the dai, in which these thingis schulen be don; for thou hast not bileued to my wordis, whiche schulen be fulfillid in her tyme.
042	LUK	001	021	And the puple was abidynge Zacarie, and thei wondriden, that he tariede in the temple.
042	LUK	001	022	And he yede out, and myyte not speke to hem, and thei knewen that he hadde seyn a visioun in the temple. And he bikenyde to hem, and he dwellide stille doumbe.
042	LUK	001	023	And it was don, whanne the daies of his office weren fulfillid, he wente in to his hous.
042	LUK	001	024	And aftir these daies Elizabeth, his wijf, conseyuede, and hidde hir fyue monethis, and seide,
042	LUK	001	025	For so the Lord dide to me in the daies, in whiche he bihelde, to take awei my repreef among men.
042	LUK	001	026	But in the sixte moneth the aungel Gabriel was sent fro God in to a citee of Galilee, whos name was Nazareth,
042	LUK	001	027	to a maidyn, weddid to a man, whos name was Joseph, of the hous of Dauid; and the name of the maidun was Marie.
