# BOOK	043	JOH	John	John
043	JOH	001	001	In the bigynnyng was the word, and the word was at God, and God was the word.
043	JOH	001	002	This was in the bigynnyng at God.
043	JOH	001	003	Alle thingis weren maad bi hym, and withouten hym was maad no thing, that thing that was maad.
043	JOH	001	004	In hym was lijf, and the lijf was the liyt of men; and the liyt schyneth in derknessis,
043	JOH	001	005	and derknessis comprehendiden not it.
043	JOH	001	006	A man was sent fro God, to whom the name was Joon.
043	JOH	001	007	This man cam in to witnessyng, that he schulde bere witnessing of the liyt, that alle men schulden bileue bi hym.
043	JOH	001	008	He was not the liyt, but that he schulde bere witnessing of the liyt.
043	JOH	001	009	There was a very liyt, which liytneth ech man that cometh in to this world.
043	JOH	001	010	He was in the world, and the world was maad bi hym, and the world knew hym not.
043	JOH	001	011	He cam in to his owne thingis, and hise resseyueden hym not.
043	JOH	001	012	But hou many euer resseyueden hym, he yaf to hem power to be maad the sones of God, to hem that bileueden in his name; the whiche not of bloodis,
043	JOH	001	013	nether of the wille of fleische, nether of the wille of man, but ben borun of God.
043	JOH	001	014	And the word was maad man, and dwellyde among vs, and we han seyn the glorie of hym, as the glorie of the `oon bigetun sone of the fadir, ful of grace and of treuthe.
043	JOH	001	015	Joon berith witnessyng of hym, and crieth, and seith, This is, whom Y seide, He that schal come aftir me, is maad bifore me, for he was tofor me;
043	JOH	001	016	and of the plente of hym we alle han takun, and grace for grace.
043	JOH	001	017	For the lawe was youun bi Moises; but grace and treuthe `is maad bi Jhesu Crist.
043	JOH	001	018	No man sai euer God, no but the `oon bigetun sone, that is in the bosum of the fadir, he hath teld out.
043	JOH	001	019	And this is the witnessyng of Joon, whanne Jewis senten fro Jerusalem prestis and dekenes to hym, that thei schulden axe hym, Who art thou?
043	JOH	001	020	He knoulechide, and denyede not, and he knoulechide, For Y am not Crist.
043	JOH	001	021	And thei axiden hym, What thanne? Art thou Elie? And he seide, Y am not. Art thou a profete? And he answeride, Nay.
043	JOH	001	022	Therfor thei seiden to hym, Who art thou? that we yyue an answere to these that senten vs. What seist thou of thi silf?
043	JOH	001	023	He seide, Y am a vois of a crier in deseert, Dresse ye the weie of the Lord, as Ysaie, the prophete, seide.
043	JOH	001	024	And thei that weren sent, weren of the Fariseis.
043	JOH	001	025	And thei axiden hym, and seiden to hym, What thanne baptisist thou, if thou art not Crist, nether Elie, nether a profete?
043	JOH	001	026	Joon answeride to hem, and seide, Y baptise in watir, but in the myddil of you hath stonde oon, that ye knowen not;
043	JOH	001	027	he it is, that schal come aftir me, that was maad bifor me, of whom Y am not worthi to louse the thwong of his schoo.
043	JOH	001	028	These thingis weren don in Bethanye biyende Jordan, where Joon was baptisyng.
043	JOH	001	029	Anothir day Joon say Jhesu comynge to hym, and he seide, Lo! the lomb of God; lo! he that doith awei the synnes of the world.
043	JOH	001	030	This is he, that Y seide of, Aftir me is comun a man, which was maad bifor me; for he was rather than Y.
043	JOH	001	031	And Y knew hym not, but that he be schewid in Israel, therfor Y cam baptisynge in watir.
043	JOH	001	032	And Joon bar witnessyng, and seide, That Y saiy the spirit comynge doun as a culuer fro heuene, and dwellide on hym.
043	JOH	001	033	And Y knew hym not; but he that sente me to baptise in watir, seide to me, On whom thou seest the Spirit comynge doun, and dwellynge on hym, this is he, that baptisith in the Hooli Goost.
043	JOH	001	034	And Y say, and bar witnessyng, that this is the sone of God.
043	JOH	001	035	Anothir dai Joon stood, and tweyne of hise disciplis;
043	JOH	001	036	and he biheeld Jhesu walkinge, and seith, Lo! the lomb of God.
043	JOH	001	037	And twei disciplis herden hym spekynge,
043	JOH	001	038	and folewiden Jhesu. And Jhesu turnede, and say hem suynge hym, and seith to hem, What seken ye? And thei seiden to hym, Rabi, that is to seie, Maistir, where dwellist thou?
043	JOH	001	039	And he seith to hem, Come ye, and se. And thei camen, and sayn where he dwellide; and dwelten with hym that dai. And it was as the tenthe our.
043	JOH	001	040	And Andrewe, the brother of Symount Petir, was oon of the tweyne, that herden of Joon, and hadden sued hym.
043	JOH	001	041	This foond first his brother Symount, and he seide to him, We han foundun Messias, that is to seie, Crist; and he ledde him to Jhesu.
043	JOH	001	042	And Jhesus bihelde hym, and seide, Thou art Symount, the sone of Johanna; thou schalt be clepid Cefas, that is to seie, Petre.
043	JOH	001	043	And on the morewe he wolde go out in to Galilee, and he foond Filip; and he seith to hym, Sue thou me.
043	JOH	001	044	Filip was of Bethsaida, the citee of Andrew and of Petre.
043	JOH	001	045	Filip foond Nathanael, and seide to hym, We han foundun Jhesu, the sone of Joseph, of Nazareth, whom Moyses wroot in the lawe and profetis.
043	JOH	001	046	And Nathanael seide to hym, Of Nazareth may sum good thing be?
043	JOH	001	047	Filip seide to hym, Come, and se. Jhesus siy Nathanael comynge to hym, and seide to hym, Lo! verili a man of Israel, in whom is no gile.
043	JOH	001	048	Nathanael seide to hym, Wherof hast thou knowun me? Jhesus `answerde, and seide to hym, Bifor that Filip clepide thee, whanne thou were vndur the fige tree, Y saiy thee. Nathanael answerde to hym,
043	JOH	001	049	`and seide, Rabi, thou art the sone of God, thou art kyng of Israel.
043	JOH	001	050	Jhesus answerde, and seide to hym, For Y seide to thee, Y sawy thee vndur the fige tre, thou bileuest; thou schalt se more than these thingis.
043	JOH	001	051	And he seide to hem, Treuli, treuli, Y seie to you, ye schulen se heuene opened, and the aungels of God stiynge vp and comynge doun on mannys sone.
043	JOH	002	001	And the thridde dai weddyngis weren maad in the Cane of Galilee; and the modir of Jhesu was there.
043	JOH	002	002	And Jhesus was clepid, and hise disciplis, to the weddyngis.
043	JOH	002	003	And whanne wijn failide, the modir of Jhesu seide to hym, Thei han not wijn.
043	JOH	002	004	And Jhesus seith to hir, What to me and to thee, womman? myn our cam not yit.
043	JOH	002	005	His modir seith to the mynystris, What euere thing he seie to you, do ye.
043	JOH	002	006	And there weren set `sixe stonun cannes, aftir the clensyng of the Jewis, holdynge ech tweyne ether thre metretis.
043	JOH	002	007	And Jhesus seith to hem, Fille ye the pottis with watir. And thei filliden hem, vp to the mouth.
043	JOH	002	008	And Jhesus seide to hem, Drawe ye now, and bere ye to the architriclyn. And thei baren.
043	JOH	002	009	And whanne the architriclyn hadde tastid the watir maad wiyn, and wiste not wherof it was, but the mynystris wisten that drowen the watir, the architriclyn clepith the spouse,
043	JOH	002	010	and seith to hym, Ech man settith first good wiyn, and whanne men ben fulfillid, thanne that that is worse; but thou hast kept the good wiyn `in to this tyme.
043	JOH	002	011	Jhesus dide this the bigynnyng of signes in the Cane of Galilee, and schewide his glorie; and hise disciplis bileueden in hym.
043	JOH	002	012	Aftir these thingis he cam doun to Cafarnaum, and his modir, and hise britheren, and hise disciplis; and thei dwelliden `there not many daies.
043	JOH	002	013	And the pask of Jewis was nyy, and Jhesus wente vp to Jerusalem.
043	JOH	002	014	And he foond in the temple men sillynge oxun, and scheep, and culueris, and chaungeris sittynge.
043	JOH	002	015	And whanne he hadde maad as it were a scourge of smale cordis, he droof out alle of the temple, and oxun, and scheep; and he schedde the money of chaungeris, and turnede vpsedoun the boordis.
043	JOH	002	016	And he seide to hem that selden culueris, Take awei fro hennus these thingis, and nyle ye make the hous of my fadir an hous of marchaundise.
043	JOH	002	017	And hise disciplis hadden mynde, for it was writun, The feruent loue of thin hous hath etun me.
043	JOH	002	018	Therfor the Jewis answeriden, and seiden to hym, What token schewist thou to vs, that thou doist these thingis?
043	JOH	002	019	Jhesus answerde, and seide to hem, Vndo ye this temple, and in thre daies Y schal reise it.
043	JOH	002	020	Therfor the Jewis seiden to hym, In fourti and sixe yeer this temple was bildid, and schalt thou in thre daies reise it?
043	JOH	002	021	But he seide of the temple of his bodi.
043	JOH	002	022	Therfor whanne he was risun fro deeth, hise disciplis hadden mynde, that he seide these thingis of his bodi; and thei bileueden to the scripture, and to the word that Jhesus seide.
043	JOH	002	023	And whanne Jhesus was at Jerusalem in pask, in the feeste dai, many bileueden in his name, seynge his signes that he dide.
043	JOH	002	024	But Jhesus trowide not hym silf to hem, for he knewe alle men;
043	JOH	002	025	and for it was not nede to hym, that ony man schulde bere witnessyng, for he wiste, what was in man.
043	JOH	003	001	And there was a man of the Farisees, Nychodeme bi name, a prince of the Jewis.
043	JOH	003	002	And he cam to Jhesu bi niyt, and seide to hym, Rabi, we witen, that thou art comun fro God maister; for no man may do these signes, that thou doist, but God be with hym.
043	JOH	003	003	Jhesus answerde, and seide to hym, Treuli, treuli, Y seie to thee, but a man be borun ayen, he may not se the kyngdom of God.
043	JOH	003	004	Nychodeme seide to hym, Hou may a man be borun, whanne he is eeld? whether he may entre ayen in to his modris wombe, and be borun ayen?
043	JOH	003	005	Jhesus answeride, Treuli, treuli, Y seie to thee, but a man be borun ayen of watir, and of the Hooli Goost, he may not entre in to the kyngdom of God.
043	JOH	003	006	`That that is borun of the fleisch, is fleisch; and `that that is borun of spirit, is spirit.
043	JOH	003	007	Wondre thou not, for Y seide to thee, It bihoueth you to be borun ayen.
043	JOH	003	008	The spirit brethith where he wole, and thou herist his vois, but thou wost not, fro whennus he cometh, ne whidir he goith; so is ech man that is borun of the spirit.
043	JOH	003	009	Nychodeme answeride, and seide to hym, Hou moun these thingis be don?
043	JOH	003	010	Jhesus answeride, and seide to hym, Thou art a maister in Israel, and knowist not these thingis?
043	JOH	003	011	Treuli, treuli, Y seie to thee, for we speken that that we witen, and we witnessen that that we han seyn, and ye taken not oure witnessyng.
043	JOH	003	012	If Y haue seid to you ertheli thingis, and ye bileuen not, hou if Y seie to you heueneli thingis, schulen ye bileue?
043	JOH	003	013	And no man stieth in to heuene, but he that cam doun fro heuene, mannys sone that is in heuene.
043	JOH	003	014	And as Moises areride a serpent in desert, so it bihoueth mannys sone to be reisid,
043	JOH	003	015	that ech man that bileueth in hym, perische not, but haue euerlastynge lijf.
043	JOH	003	016	For God louede so the world, that he yaf his `oon bigetun sone, that ech man that bileueth in him perische not, but haue euerlastynge lijf.
043	JOH	003	017	For God sente not his sone in to the world, that he iuge the world, but that the world be saued bi him.
043	JOH	003	018	He that bileueth in hym, is not demed; but he that bileueth not, is now demed, for he bileueth not in the name of the `oon bigetun sone of God.
043	JOH	003	019	And this is the dom, for liyt cam in to the world, and men loueden more derknessis than liyt; for her werkes weren yuele.
043	JOH	003	020	For ech man that doith yuele, hatith the liyt; and he cometh not to the liyt, that hise werkis be not repreued.
043	JOH	003	021	But he that doith treuthe, cometh to the liyt, that hise werkis be schewid, that thei ben don in God.
043	JOH	003	022	Aftir these thingis Jhesus cam, and hise disciplis, in to the loond of Judee, and there he dwellide with hem, and baptiside.
043	JOH	003	023	And Joon was baptisinge in Ennon, bisidis Salym, for many watris weren there; and thei camen, and weren baptisid.
043	JOH	003	024	And Joon was not yit sent in to prisoun.
043	JOH	003	025	Therfor a questioun was maad of Jonys disciplis with the Jewis, of the purificacioun.
043	JOH	003	026	And thei camen to Joon, and seiden `to hym, Maister, he that was with thee biyonde Jordan, to whom thou hast borun witnessyng, lo! he baptisith, and alle men comen to hym.
043	JOH	003	027	Joon answerde, and seide, A man may not take ony thing, but it be youun to hym fro heuene.
043	JOH	003	028	Ye you silf beren witnessyng to me, that Y seide, Y am not Crist, but that Y am sent bifore hym.
043	JOH	003	029	He that hath a wijf, is the hosebonde; but the freend of the spouse that stondith, and herith hym, ioieth with ioye, for the vois of the spouse. Therfor in this thing my ioye is fulfillid.
043	JOH	003	030	It bihoueth hym to wexe, but me to be maad lesse.
043	JOH	003	031	He that cam from aboue, is aboue alle; he that is of the erthe, spekith of the erthe; he that cometh from heuene, is aboue alle.
043	JOH	003	032	And he witnessith that thing that he hath seie, and herde, and no man takith his witnessing.
043	JOH	003	033	But he that takith his witnessyng, hath confermyd that God is sothefast.
043	JOH	003	034	But he whom God hath sent, spekith the wordis of God; for not to mesure God yyueth the spirit.
043	JOH	003	035	The fadir loueth the sone, and he hath youun alle thingis in his hoond.
043	JOH	003	036	He that bileueth in the sone, hath euerlastynge lijf; but he that is vnbileueful to the sone, schal not se euerlastynge lijf, but the wraththe of God dwellith on hym.
043	JOH	004	001	Therfor as Jhesu knew, that the Farisees herden, that Jhesu makith and baptisith mo disciplis than Joon,
043	JOH	004	002	thouy Jhesus baptiside not, but hise disciplis, he lefte Judee,
043	JOH	004	003	and wente ayen in to Galilee.
043	JOH	004	004	And it bihofte hym to passe bi Samarie.
043	JOH	004	005	Therfor Jhesus cam in to a citee of Samarie, that is seid Sicar, bisidis the place, that Jacob yaf to Joseph, his sone.
043	JOH	004	006	And the welle of Jacob was there; and Jhesus was weri of the iourney, and sat thus vpon the welle. And the our was, as it were the sixte.
043	JOH	004	007	And a womman cam fro Samarie, to drawe watir. And Jhesus seith to hir, Yyue me drynk.
043	JOH	004	008	And hise disciplis weren gon in to the citee, to bie mete.
043	JOH	004	009	Therfor thilke womman of Samarie seith to him, Hou thou, `whanne thou art a Jewe, axist of me drynk, that am a womman of Samarie? for Jewis vsiden not to dele with Samaritans.
043	JOH	004	010	Jhesus answerde, and seide to hir, If thou wistist the yifte of God, and who `he is, that seith to thee, Yyue me drynk, thou perauenture woldist haue axid of hym, and he schulde haue youun to thee quyk watir.
043	JOH	004	011	The womman seith to him, Sire, thou hast not where ynne to drawe, and the pit is deep; wherof thanne hast thou quik watir?
043	JOH	004	012	Whethir thou art grettere than oure fadir Jacob, that yaf to vs the pit? and he drank therof, and hise sones, and hise beestis.
043	JOH	004	013	Jhesus answerde, and seide to hir, Eche man that drynkith of this watir, schal thirste efte soone;
043	JOH	004	014	but he that drynkith of the watir that Y schal yyue hym, schal not thirste with outen ende; but the watir that Y schal yyue hym, schal be maad in hym a welle `of watir, spryngynge vp in to euerlastynge lijf.
043	JOH	004	015	The womman seith to hym, Sire, yyue me this watir, that Y thirste not, nether come hidur to drawe.
043	JOH	004	016	Jhesus seith to hir, Go, clepe thin hosebonde, and come hidir.
043	JOH	004	017	The womman answerde, and seide, Y haue noon hosebonde. Jhesus seith to hir, Thou seidist wel, That Y haue noon hosebonde;
043	JOH	004	018	for thou hast hadde fyue hosebondis, and he that thou hast, is not thin hosebonde. This thing thou seidist sotheli.
043	JOH	004	019	The womman seith to hym, Lord, Y se, that thou art a prophete.
043	JOH	004	020	Oure fadris worschipiden in this hil, and ye seien, that at Jerusalem is a place, where it bihoueth to worschipe.
043	JOH	004	021	Jhesus seith to hir, Womman, bileue thou to me, for the our schal come, whanne nether in this hil, nethir in Jerusalem, ye schulen worschipe the fadir.
043	JOH	004	022	Ye worschipen that ye knowen not; we worschipen that that we knowen; for helthe is of the Jewis.
043	JOH	004	023	But the tyme is comun, and now it is, whanne trewe worschiperis schulen worschipe the fadir in spirit and treuthe; for also the fadir sekith suche, that worschipen hym.
043	JOH	004	024	God is a spirit, and it bihoueth hem that worschipen hym, to worschipe in spirit and treuthe.
043	JOH	004	025	The womman seith to hym, Y woot that Messias is comun, that is seid Crist; therfor whanne he cometh, he schal telle vs alle thingis.
043	JOH	004	026	Jhesus seith to hir, Y am he, that spekith with thee.
043	JOH	004	027	And anoon hise disciplis camen, and wondriden, that he spak with the womman; netheles no man seide to hym, What sekist thou, or, What spekist thou with hir?
043	JOH	004	028	Therfor the womman lefte hir watir pot, and wente in to the citee, and seide to tho men,
043	JOH	004	029	Come ye, and se ye a man, that seide to me alle thingis that Y haue don; whether he be Crist?
043	JOH	004	030	And thei wenten out of the citee, and camen to hym.
043	JOH	004	031	In the mene while hise disciplis preieden hym, and seiden, Maistir, ete.
043	JOH	004	032	But he seide to hem, Y haue mete to ete, that ye knowen not.
043	JOH	004	033	Therfor disciplis seiden togidir, Whether ony man hath brouyt him mete to ete?
043	JOH	004	034	Jhesus seith to hem, My mete is, that Y do the wille of hym that sente me, that Y perfourme the werk of hym.
043	JOH	004	035	Whether ye seien not, that yit foure monethis ben, and rype corn cometh? Lo! Y seie to you, lifte vp youre iyen, and se ye the feeldis, for now thei ben white to repe.
043	JOH	004	036	And he that repith takith hire, and gaderith fruyt in to euerlastynge lijf; that bothe he that sowith, and he that repith, haue ioye togidere.
043	JOH	004	037	In this thing is the word trewe, for anothir is that sowith, and anothir that repith.
043	JOH	004	038	Y sente you to repe, that that ye `haue not trauelid; `othere men han trauelid, and ye han entrid `in to her trauels.
043	JOH	004	039	And of that citee many Samaritans bileueden in hym, for the word of the womman, that bare witnessyng, That he seide to me alle thingis that Y haue don.
043	JOH	004	040	Therfor whanne Samaritans camen to hym, thei preieden hym to dwelle there; and he dwelte there twey daies.
043	JOH	004	041	And many mo bileueden for his word,
043	JOH	004	042	and seiden to the womman, That now not for thi speche we bileuen; for we han herd, and we witen, that this is verili the sauyour of the world.
043	JOH	004	043	And aftir twei daies he wente out fro thennus, and wente in to Galilee.
043	JOH	004	044	And he bar witnessyng, that a profete in his owne cuntre hath noon onour.
043	JOH	004	045	Therfor whanne he cam in to Galilee, men of Galilee resseyueden hym, whanne thei hadden seyn alle thingis that he hadde don in Jerusalem in the feeste dai; for also thei hadden comun to the feeste dai.
043	JOH	004	046	Therfor he cam eftsoone in to the Cane of Galile, where he made the watir wiyn. And `a litil kyng was, whos sone was sijk at Cafarnaum.
043	JOH	004	047	Whanne this hadde herd, that Jhesu schulde come fro Judee in to Galilee, he wente to hym, and preiede hym, that he schulde come doun, and heele his sone; for he bigan to die.
043	JOH	004	048	Therfor Jhesus seide to him, But ye se tokenes and grete wondris, ye bileuen not.
043	JOH	004	049	The litil kyng seith to hym, Lord, come doun, bifor that my sone die.
043	JOH	004	050	Jhesus seith to hym, Go, thi sone lyueth. The man bileuede to the word, that Jhesus seide to hym, and he wente.
043	JOH	004	051	And now whanne he cam doun, the seruauntis camen ayens hym, and telden to hym, and seiden, That his sone lyuede.
