043	JOH	004	053	Therfor the fadir knewe, that thilke our it was, in which Jhesus seide to hym, Thi sone lyueth; and he bileuede, and al his hous.
043	JOH	004	054	Jhesus dide eft this secounde tokene, whanne he cam fro Judee in to Galilee.
043	JOH	005	001	Aftir these thingis ther was a feeste dai of Jewis, and Jhesus wente vp to Jerusalem.
043	JOH	005	002	And in Jerusalem is a waissynge place, that in Ebrew is named Bethsaida, and hath fyue porchis.
043	JOH	005	003	In these lay a greet multitude of sike men, blynde, crokid, and drie, abidynge the mouyng of the watir.
043	JOH	005	004	For the aungel `of the Lord cam doun certeyne tymes in to the watir, and the watir was moued; and he that first cam doun in to the sisterne, aftir the mouynge of the watir, was maad hool of what euer sijknesse he was holdun.
043	JOH	005	005	And a man was there, hauynge eiyte and thritti yeer in his sikenesse.
043	JOH	005	006	And whanne Jhesus hadde seyn hym liggynge, and hadde knowun, that he hadde myche tyme, he seith to hym, Wolt thou be maad hool?
043	JOH	005	007	The sijk man answerde to hym, Lord, Y haue no man, that whanne the watir is moued, to putte me `in to the cisterne; for the while Y come, anothir goith doun bifor me.
043	JOH	005	008	Jhesus seith to hym, Rise vp, take thi bed, and go.
043	JOH	005	009	And anoon the man was maad hool, and took vp his bed, and wente forth. And it was sabat in that dai.
043	JOH	005	010	Therfor the Jewis seiden to him that was maad hool, It is sabat, it is not leueful to thee, to take awei thi bed.
043	JOH	005	011	He answeride to hem, He that made me hool, seide to me, Take thi bed, and go.
043	JOH	005	012	Therfor thei axiden him, What man `is that, that seide to thee, Take vp thi bed, and go?
043	JOH	005	013	But he that was maad hool, wiste not who it was. And Jhesus bowide awei fro the puple, that was set in the place.
