043	JOH	005	015	Thilke man wente, and telde to the Jewis, that it was Jhesu that made hym hool.
043	JOH	005	016	Therfor the Jewis pursueden Jhesu, for he dide this thing in the sabat.
043	JOH	005	017	And Jhesus answeride to hem, My fadir worchith til now, and Y worche.
043	JOH	005	018	Therfor the Jewis souyten more to sle hym, for not oneli he brak the sabat, but he seide that God was his fadir, and made hym euene to God.
043	JOH	005	019	Therfor Jhesus answerde, and seide to hem, Treuli, treuli, Y seye to you, the sone may not of hym silf do ony thing, but that thing that he seeth the fadir doynge; for what euere thingis he doith, the sone doith in lijk maner tho thingis.
043	JOH	005	020	For the fadir loueth the sone, and schewith to hym alle thingis that he doith; and he schal schewe to hym grettere werkis than these, that ye wondren.
043	JOH	005	021	For as the fadir reisith deed men, and quykeneth, so the sone quykeneth whom he wole.
