043	JOH	006	006	But he seide this thing, temptynge hym; for he wiste what he was to do.
043	JOH	006	007	Filip answerde to hym, The looues of tweyn hundrid pans sufficen not to hem, that ech man take a litil what.
043	JOH	006	008	Oon of hise disciplis, Andrew, the brothir of Symount Petre,
043	JOH	006	009	seith to him, A child is here, that hath fyue barli looues and twei fischis; but what ben these among so manye?
043	JOH	006	010	Therfor Jhesus seith, Make ye hem sitte to the mete. And there was myche hey in the place. And so men saten to the mete, as `fyue thousynde in noumbre.
043	JOH	006	011	And Jhesus took fyue looues, and whanne he hadde do thankyngis, he departide to men that saten to the mete, and also of the fischis, as myche as thei wolden.
