# BOOK	045	ROM	Romans	Romans
045	ROM	001	001	Poul, the seruaunt of Jhesu Crist, clepid an apostle, departid in to the gospel of God;
045	ROM	001	002	which he hadde bihote tofore bi his profetis in holi scripturis of his sone,
045	ROM	001	003	which is maad to hym of the seed of Dauid bi the flesch,
045	ROM	001	004	and he was bifor ordeyned the sone of God in vertu, bi the spirit of halewyng of the ayenrisyng of deed men, of Jhesu Crist oure Lord,
045	ROM	001	005	bi whom we han resseyued grace and the office of apostle, to obeie to the feith in alle folkis for his name,
045	ROM	001	006	among whiche ye ben also clepid of Jhesu Crist,
045	ROM	001	007	to alle that ben at Rome, derlyngis of God, and clepid hooli, grace to you, and pees of God oure fadir, and of the Lord Jhesu Crist.
045	ROM	001	008	First Y do thankyngis to my God, bi Jhesu Crist, for alle you, for youre feith is schewid in al the world.
045	ROM	001	009	For God is a witnesse to me, to whom Y serue in my spirit, in the gospel of his sone,
045	ROM	001	010	that with outen ceessyng Y make mynde of you euere in my preieris, and biseche, if in ony maner sum tyme Y haue a spedi weie in the wille of God to come to you.
045	ROM	001	011	For Y desire to se you, to parten sumwhat of spiritual grace,
045	ROM	001	012	that ye be confermyd, that is, to be coumfortid togidere in you, bi feith that is bothe youre and myn togidere.
045	ROM	001	013	And, britheren, Y nyle, that ye vnknowun, that ofte Y purposide to come to you, and Y am lett to this tyme, that Y haue sum fruyt in you, as in othere folkis.
045	ROM	001	014	To Grekis and to barberyns, to wise men and to vnwise men,
045	ROM	001	015	Y am dettour, so that that is in me is redi to preche the gospel also to you that ben at Rome.
045	ROM	001	016	For Y schame not the gospel, for it is the vertu of God in to heelthe to ech man that bileueth, to the Jew first, and to the Greke.
045	ROM	001	017	For the riytwisnesse of God is schewid in it, of feith in to feith,
045	ROM	001	018	as it is writun, For a iust man lyueth of feith. For the wraththe of God is schewid fro heuene on al vnpite and wickidnesse of tho men, that withholden the treuthe of God in vnriytwisnes.
045	ROM	001	019	For that thing of God that is knowun, is schewid to hem, for God hath schewid to hem.
