045	ROM	016	013	Grete wel Rufus, chosun in the Lord, and his modir, and myn.
045	ROM	016	014	Grete wel Ansicrete, Flegoncia, Hermen, Patroban, Herman, and britheren that ben with hem.
045	ROM	016	015	Grete wel Filologus, and Julian, and Nereum, and his sistir, and Olympiades, and alle the seyntis that ben with hem.
045	ROM	016	016	Grete ye wel togidere in hooli coss. Alle the chirches of Crist greten you wel.
045	ROM	016	017	But, britheren, Y preye you, that ye aspie hem that maken discenciouns and hirtyngis, bisidis the doctryne that ye han lerned, and bowe ye awei fro hem.
045	ROM	016	018	For suche men seruen not to the Lord Crist, but to her wombe, and bi swete wordis and blessyngis disseyuen the hertis of innocent men.
045	ROM	016	019	But youre obedience is pupplischid in to euery place, therfor Y haue ioye in you. But Y wole that ye be wise in good thing, and symple in yuel.
045	ROM	016	020	And God of pees tredde Sathanas vndur youre feet swiftli. The grace of oure Lord Jhesu Crist be with you.
045	ROM	016	021	Tymothe, myn helpere, gretith you wel, and also Lucius, and Jason, and Sosipater, my cosyns.
045	ROM	016	022	Y Tercius grete you wel, that wroot this epistle, in the Lord.
045	ROM	016	023	Gayus, myn oost, gretith you wel, and al the chirche. Erastus, tresorere of the city, gretith you wel, and Quartus brother.
045	ROM	016	024	The grace of oure Lord Jhesu Crist be with you alle. Amen.
045	ROM	016	025	And onour and glorie be to hym, that is myyti to conferme you bi my gospel, and prechyng of Jhesu Crist, bi the reuelacioun of mysterie holdun stylle in tymes euerlastinge;
045	ROM	016	026	which mysterie is now maad opyn bi scripturis of prophetis, bi the comaundement of God with outen bigynnyng and endyng, to the obedience of feith in alle hethene men, the mysterie
045	ROM	016	027	knowun bi Jhesu Crist to God aloone wiss, to whom be onour and glorie in to worldis of worldis. Amen.
