# BOOK	046	1CO	1 Corinthians	1 Corinthians
046	1CO	001	001	Poul, clepid apostle of Jhesu Crist, bi the wille of God, and Sostenes, brothir, to the chirche of God that is at Corynthe,
046	1CO	001	002	to hem that ben halewid in Crist Jhesu, and clepid seyntis, with alle that inwardli clepen the name of oure Lord Jhesu Crist, in ech place of hem and of oure,
046	1CO	001	003	grace to you and pees of God, oure fadir, and of the Lord Jhesu Crist.
046	1CO	001	004	Y do thankyngis to my God eueremore for you, in the grace of God that is youun to you in Crist Jhesu.
046	1CO	001	005	For in alle thingis ye ben maad riche in hym, in ech word, and in ech kunnyng,
046	1CO	001	006	as the witnessyng of Crist is confermyd in you;
046	1CO	001	007	so that no thing faile to you in ony grace, that abiden the schewyng of oure Lord Jhesu Crist;
046	1CO	001	008	which also schal conferme you in to the ende with outen cryme, in the dai of the comyng of oure Lord Jhesu Crist.
046	1CO	001	009	`A trewe God, bi whom ye ben clepid in to the felouschipe of his sone Jhesu Crist oure Lord.
046	1CO	001	010	But, britheren, Y biseche you, bi the name of oure Lord Jhesu Crist, that ye alle seie the same thing, and that dissenciouns be not among you; but be ye perfit in the same wit, and in the same kunnyng.
046	1CO	001	011	For, my britheren, it is teld to me of hem that ben at Cloes, that stryues ben among you.
046	1CO	001	012	And Y seie that, that ech of you seith, For Y am of Poul, and Y am of Apollo, and Y am of Cefas, but Y am of Crist.
046	1CO	001	013	Whether Crist is departid? whether Poul was crucified for you, ether ye ben baptisid in the name of Poul?
046	1CO	001	014	Y do thankyngis to my God, that Y baptiside noon of you, but Crispus and Gayus;
046	1CO	001	015	lest ony man seie, that ye ben baptisid in my name.
046	1CO	001	016	And Y baptiside also the hous of Stephan, but Y woot not, that Y baptiside ony other.
046	1CO	001	017	For Crist sente me not to baptise, but to preche the gospel; not in wisdom of word, that the cros of Crist be not voidid awei.
046	1CO	001	018	For the word of the cros is foli to hem that perischen; but to hem that ben maad saaf, that is to seie, to vs, it is the vertu of God.
046	1CO	001	019	For it is writun, Y schal distruye the wisdom of wise men, and Y schal reproue the prudence of prudent men.
046	1CO	001	020	Where is the wise man? where is the wise lawiere? where is the purchasour of this world? Whether God hath not maad the wisdom of this world fonned?
046	1CO	001	021	For the world in wisdom of God knewe not God bi wisdom, it pleside to God, bi foli of prechyng, `to maken hem saaf that bileueden.
046	1CO	001	022	For Jewis seken signes, and Grekis seken wisdom;
046	1CO	001	023	but we prechen Crist crucified, to Jewis sclaundre, and to hethene men foli;
046	1CO	001	024	but to tho Jewis and Grekis that ben clepid, we prechen Crist the vertu of God and the wisdom of God.
046	1CO	001	025	For that that is foli thing of God, is wiser than men; and that that is the feble thing of God, is strengere than men.
046	1CO	001	026	But, britheren, se ye youre clepyng; for not many wise men aftir the fleisch, not many myyti, not many noble.
046	1CO	001	027	But God chees tho thingis that ben fonned of the world, to confounde wise men;
046	1CO	001	028	and God chees the feble thingis of the world, to confounde the stronge thingis; and God chees the vnnoble thingis `and dispisable thingis of the world, and tho thingis that ben not, to distruye tho thingis that ben;
046	1CO	001	029	that ech man haue not glorie in his siyt.
046	1CO	001	030	But of hym ye ben in Crist Jhesu, which is maad of God to vs wisdom, and riytwisnesse, and holynesse, and ayenbiyng; that,
046	1CO	001	031	as it is wrytun, He that glorieth, haue glorie in the Lord.
046	1CO	002	001	And Y, britheren, whanne Y cam to you, cam not in the heiynesse of word, ethir of wisdom, tellynge to you the witnessyng of Crist.
046	1CO	002	002	For Y demede not me to kunne ony thing among you, but Crist Jhesu, and hym crucified.
046	1CO	002	003	And Y in sikenesse, and drede, and myche trembling, was among you;
046	1CO	002	004	and my word and my preching was not in suteli sturyng wordis of mannus wisdom, but in schewyng of spirit and of vertu;
046	1CO	002	005	that youre feith be not in the wisdom of men, but in the vertu of God.
046	1CO	002	006	For we speken wisdom among perfit men, but not wisdom of this world, nether of princes of this world, that ben distried;
046	1CO	002	007	but we speken the wisdom of God in mysterie, `which wisdom is hid; which wisdom God bifor ordeynede bifor worldis in to oure glorie,
046	1CO	002	008	which noon of the princes of this world knew; for if thei hadden knowe, thei schulden neuere haue crucified the Lord of glorie.
046	1CO	002	009	But as it is writun, That iye say not, ne eere herde, nether it stiede in to herte of man, what thingis God arayede to hem that louen hym;
046	1CO	002	010	but God schewide to vs bi his spirit. For whi the spirit serchith alle thingis, yhe, the depe thingis of God.
046	1CO	002	011	And who of men woot, what thingis ben of man, but the spirit of man that is in hym? So what thingis ben of God, no man knowith, but the spirit of God.
046	1CO	002	012	And we han not resseiued the spirit of this world, but the spirit that is of God, that we wite what thingis ben youun to vs of God.
046	1CO	002	013	Whiche thingis we speken also, not in wise wordis of mannus wisdom, but in the doctryn of the spirit, and maken a liknesse of spiritual thingis to goostli men.
046	1CO	002	014	For a beestli man perseyueth not tho thingis that ben of the spirit of God; for it is foli to hym, and he may not vndurstonde, for it is examyned goostli.
046	1CO	002	015	But a spiritual man demeth alle thingis, and he is demed of no man.
046	1CO	002	016	As it is writun, And who knew the wit of the Lord, or who tauyte hym? And we han the wit of Crist.
046	1CO	003	001	And Y, britheren, myyte not speke to you as to spiritual men, but as to fleischli men;
046	1CO	003	002	as to litle children in Crist, Y yaf to you mylk drynke, not mete; for ye myyten not yit, nether ye moun now, for yit ye ben fleischli.
046	1CO	003	003	For while strijf is among you, whether ye ben not fleischli, and ye gon aftir man?
046	1CO	003	004	For whanne summe seith, Y am of Poul, another, But Y am of Apollo, whethir ye ben not men? What therfor is Apollo, and what Poul?
046	1CO	003	005	Thei ben mynystris of hym, to whom ye han bileuyd; and to ech man as God hath youun.
046	1CO	003	006	Y plauntide, Apollo moystide, but God yaf encreessyng.
046	1CO	003	007	Therfor nether he that plauntith is ony thing, nethir he that moistith, but God that yiueth encreessyng.
046	1CO	003	008	And he that plauntith, and he that moistith, ben oon; and ech schal take his owne mede, aftir his trauel.
046	1CO	003	009	For we ben the helperis of God; ye ben the erthetiliyng of God, ye ben the bildyng of God.
046	1CO	003	010	Aftir the grace `of God that is youun to me, as a wise maistir carpenter Y settide the foundement; and another bildith aboue. But ech man se, hou he bildith aboue.
046	1CO	003	011	For no man may sette another foundement, outtakun that that is sett, which is Crist Jhesus.
046	1CO	003	012	For if ony bildith ouer this foundement, gold, siluer, preciouse stoonys, stickis, hey, or stobil, euery mannus werk schal be open;
046	1CO	003	013	for the dai of the Lord schal declare, for it schal be schewid in fier; the fier schal preue the werk of ech man, what maner werk it is.
046	1CO	003	014	If the werk of ony man dwelle stille, which he bildide aboue, he schal resseyue mede.
046	1CO	003	015	If ony mannus werk brenne, he schal suffre harm; but he schal be saaf, so netheles as bi fier.
046	1CO	003	016	Witen ye not, that ye ben the temple of God, and the spirit of God dwellith in you?
046	1CO	003	017	And if ony defoulith the temple of God, God schal leese hym; for the temple of God is hooli, which ye ben.
046	1CO	003	018	No man disseyue hym silf. If ony man among you is seyn to be wiys in this world, be he maad a fool, that he be wijs.
046	1CO	003	019	For the wisdom of this world is foli anentis God; for it is writun, Y schal catche wise men in her fel wisdom;
046	1CO	003	020	and eft, The Lord knowith the thouytis of wise men, for tho ben veyn.
046	1CO	003	021	Therfor no man haue glorie in men.
046	1CO	003	022	For alle thingis ben youre, ethir Poul, ether Apollo, ether Cefas, ether the world, ether lijf, ether deth, ether thingis present, ethir thingis to comynge; for alle thingis ben youre,
046	1CO	003	023	and ye ben of Crist, and Crist is of God.
046	1CO	004	001	So a man gesse vs, as mynystris of Crist, and dispenderis of the mynysteries of God.
046	1CO	004	002	Now it is souyt here among the dispenderis, that a man be foundun trewe.
046	1CO	004	003	And to me it is for the leest thing, that Y be demyd of you, or of mannus dai; but nether Y deme my silf.
046	1CO	004	004	For Y am no thing ouer trowynge to my silf, but not in this thing Y am iustified; for he that demeth me, is the Lord.
046	1CO	004	005	Therfor nyle ye deme bifore the tyme, til that the Lord come, which schal liytne the hyd thingis of derknessis, and schal schewe the counseils of hertis; and thanne preisyng schal be to ech man of God.
046	1CO	004	006	And, britheren, Y haue transfigurid these thingis in to me and in to Apollo, for you; that in vs ye lerne, lest ouer that it is writun, oon ayens another be blowun with pride for another.
046	1CO	004	007	Who demeth thee? And what hast thou, that thou hast not resseyued? And if thou hast resseyued, what gloriest thou, as thou haddist not resseyued?
046	1CO	004	008	Nowe ye ben fyllid, now ye ben maad riche; ye regnen with outen vs; and Y wolde that ye regnen, that also we regnen with you.
046	1CO	004	009	And Y gesse, that God schewide vs the laste apostlis, as thilke that ben sent to the deth; for we ben maad a spectacle to the world, and to aungels, and to men.
046	1CO	004	010	We foolis for Crist, but ye prudent in Crist; we sike, but ye stronge; ye noble, but we vnnoble.
046	1CO	004	011	Til in to this our we hungren, and thirsten, and ben nakid, and ben smytun with buffatis,
046	1CO	004	012	and we ben vnstable, and we trauelen worchynge with oure hondis; we ben cursid, and we blessen; we suffren persecucioun, and we abiden longe; we ben blasfemyd, and we bisechen;
046	1CO	004	013	as clensyngis of this world we ben maad the `out castyng of alle thingis `til yit.
046	1CO	004	014	Y write not these thingis, that Y confounde you, but Y warne as my moste dereworthe sones.
046	1CO	004	015	For whi if ye han ten thousynde of vndur maistris in Crist, but not many fadris; for in Crist Jhesu Y haue gendrid you bi the gospel.
046	1CO	004	016	Therfor, britheren, Y preye you, be ye foleweris of me, as Y of Crist.
046	1CO	004	017	Therfor Y sente to you Tymothe, which is my most dereworthe sone, and feithful in the Lord, which schal teche you my weies, that ben in Crist Jhesu; as Y teche euery where in ech chirche.
046	1CO	004	018	As thouy Y schulde not come to you, so summe ben blowun with pride;
046	1CO	004	019	but Y schal come to you soone, if God wole; and Y schal knowe not the word of hem that ben blowun with pride, but the vertu.
046	1CO	004	020	For the rewme of God is not in word, but in vertu.
046	1CO	004	021	What wole ye? Schal Y come to you in a yerde, or in charite, and in spirit of myldenesse?
046	1CO	005	001	In al maner fornycacioun is herd among you, and siche fornycacioun, which is not among hethene men, so that summan haue the wijf of his fadir.
046	1CO	005	002	And ye ben bolnyd with pride, and not more hadden weilyng, that he that dide this werk, be takun awei fro the myddil of you.
046	1CO	005	003	And Y absent in bodi, but present in spirit, now haue demyd as present hym that hath thus wrouyt, whanne
046	1CO	005	004	ye ben gaderid togidere in the name of oure Lord Jhesu Crist, and my spirit, with the vertu of the Lord Jhesu,
046	1CO	005	005	to take siche a man to Sathanas, in to the perischyng of fleisch, that the spirit be saaf in the dai of oure Lord Jhesu Crist.
046	1CO	005	006	Youre gloriyng is not good. Witen ye not, that a litil sourdow apeyrith al the gobet?
046	1CO	005	007	Clense ye out the old sourdow, that ye be new sprengyng togidere, as ye ben therf. For Crist offrid is oure pask.
046	1CO	005	008	Therfor ete we, not in eld sourdowy, nether in sourdowy of malice and weywardnesse, but in therf thingis of clernesse and of treuthe.
046	1CO	005	009	I wroot to you in a pistle, that ye be not medlid with letchours,
046	1CO	005	010	not with letchours of this world, ne coueitous men, ne raueynours, ne with men seruynge to mawmetis, ellis ye schulden haue go out of this world.
046	1CO	005	011	But now Y wroot to you, that ye be not meynd. But if he that is named a brother among you, and is a letchour, or coueitouse, or seruynge to ydols, or cursere, or ful of drunkenesse, or raueynour, to take no mete with siche.
046	1CO	005	012	For what is it to me to deme of hem that ben with oute forth? Whether ye demen not of thingis that ben with ynne forth?
046	1CO	005	013	For God schal deme hem that ben withouten forth. Do ye awei yuel fro you silf.
046	1CO	006	001	Dar any of you that hath a cause ayens another, be demed at wickid men, and not at hooli men?
046	1CO	006	002	Whether ye witen not, that seyntis schulen deme of this world? And if the world schal be demed bi you, be ye vnworthi to deme of the leste thingis?
046	1CO	006	003	Witen ye not, that we schulen deme aungels? hou myche more worldli thingis?
046	1CO	006	004	Therfor if ye han worldli domes, ordeyne ye tho contemptible men, that ben in the chirche, to deme.
046	1CO	006	005	Y seie to make you aschamed. So ther is not ony wise man, that may deme bitwixe a brothir and his brothir;
046	1CO	006	006	but a brothir with brothir stryueth in dom, and that among vnfeithful men.
046	1CO	006	007	And now trespas is algatis in you, for ye han domes among you. Whi rather take ye no wrong? whi rather suffre ye not disseit?
046	1CO	006	008	But and ye doen wrong, and doen fraude, and that to britheren.
046	1CO	006	009	Whether ye witen not, that wickid men schulen not welde the kyngdom of God? Nyle ye erre; nethir letchours, nether men that seruen mawmetis, nether auouteris,
046	1CO	006	010	nether letchouris ayen kynde, nether thei that doon letcheri with men, nether theues, nether auerouse men, nethir `ful of drunkenesse, nether curseris, nether rauenours, schulen welde the kyngdom of God.
046	1CO	006	011	And ye weren sum tyme these thingis; but ye ben waischun, but ye ben halewid, but ye ben iustefied in the name of oure Lord Jhesu Crist, and in the spirit of oure God.
046	1CO	006	012	Alle thingis ben leeueful to me, but not alle thingis ben spedeful. Alle thingis ben leeueful to me, but Y schal not be brouyt doun vndur ony mannus power.
046	1CO	006	013	Mete to the wombe, and the wombe to metis; and God schal distruye bothe this and that. And the bodi not to fornycacioun, but to the Lord, and the Lord to the bodi.
046	1CO	006	014	For God reiside the Lord, and schal reise vs bi his vertu.
046	1CO	006	015	Witen ye not, that youre bodies ben membris of Crist? Schal Y thanne take the membris of Crist, and schal Y make the membris of an hoore? God forbede.
046	1CO	006	016	Whether ye witen not, that he that cleueth to an hoore, is maad o bodi? For he seith, Ther schulen be tweyne in o fleisch.
046	1CO	006	017	And he that cleueth to the Lord, is o spirit.
046	1CO	006	018	Fle ye fornycacioun; al synne what euere synne a man doith, is with out the bodi; but he that doith fornycacioun, synneth ayens his bodi.
046	1CO	006	019	Whether ye witen not, that youre membris ben the temple of the Hooli Goost, that is in you, whom ye han of God, and ye ben not youre owne?
046	1CO	006	020	For ye ben bouyt with greet prijs. Glorifie ye, and bere ye God in youre bodi.
046	1CO	007	001	But of thilke thingis that ye han write to me, it is good to a man to touche not a womman.
046	1CO	007	002	But for fornycacioun eche man haue his owne wijf, and ech womman haue hir owne hosebonde.
046	1CO	007	003	The hosebonde yelde dette to the wijf, and also the wijf to the hosebonde.
046	1CO	007	004	The womman hath not power of hir bodi, but the hosebonde; and the hosebonde hath not power of his bodi, but the womman.
046	1CO	007	005	Nyle ye defraude eche to othere, but perauenture of consent to a tyme, that ye yyue tent to preier; and eft turne ye ayen to the same thing, lest Sathanas tempte you for youre vncontynence.
046	1CO	007	006	But Y seie this thing as yyuyng leeue, not bi comaundement.
046	1CO	007	007	For Y wole, that alle men be as my silf. But eche man hath his propre yifte of God; oon thus, and another thus.
046	1CO	007	008	But Y seie to hem, that ben not weddid, and to widewis, it is good to hem, if thei dwellen so as Y.
046	1CO	007	009	That if thei conteynen not hem silf, be thei weddid; for it is betere to be weddid, than to be brent.
046	1CO	007	010	But to hem that ben ioyned in matrymonye, Y comaunde, not Y, but the Lord, that the wijf departe not fro the hosebonde;
046	1CO	007	011	and that if sche departith, that sche dwelle vnweddid, or be recounselid to hir hosebonde; and the hosebonde forsake not the wijf.
046	1CO	007	012	But to othere Y seie, not the Lord. If ony brother hath an vnfeithful wijf, and sche consenteth to dwelle with hym, leeue he hir not.
046	1CO	007	013	And if ony womman hath an vnfeithful hosebonde, and this consentith to dwelle with hir, leeue sche not the hosebonde.
046	1CO	007	014	For the vnfeithful hosebonde is halewid bi the feithful womman, and the vnfeithful womman is halewid bi the feithful hosebonde. Ellis youre children weren vncleene, but now thei ben hooli.
046	1CO	007	015	That if the vnfeithful departith, departe he. For whi the brother or sistir is not suget to seruage in siche; for God hath clepid vs in pees.
046	1CO	007	016	And wherof wost thou, womman, if thou schalt make the man saaf; or wherof wost thou, man, if thou schalt make the womman saaf?
046	1CO	007	017	But as the Lord hath departid to ech, and as God hath clepid ech man, so go he, as Y teche in alle chirchis.
046	1CO	007	018	A man circumcidid is clepid, brynge he not to the prepucie. A man is clepid in prepucie, be he not circumcidid.
046	1CO	007	019	Circumcisioun is nouyt, and prepucie is nouyt, but the kepyng of the maundementis of God.
046	1CO	007	020	Ech man in what clepyng he is clepid, in that dwelle he.
046	1CO	007	021	Thou seruaunt art clepid, be it no charge to thee; but if thou maist be fre, `the rather vse thou.
046	1CO	007	022	He that is a seruaunt, and is clepid in the Lord, is a freman of the Lord. Also he that is a freman, and is clepid, is the seruaunt of Crist.
046	1CO	007	023	With prijs ye ben bouyt; nyle ye be maad seruauntis of men.
046	1CO	007	024	Therfor ech man in what thing he is clepid a brothir, dwelle he in this anentis God.
046	1CO	007	025	But of virgyns Y haue no comaundement of God; but Y yyue counseil, as he that hath mercy of the Lord, that Y be trewe.
046	1CO	007	026	Therfor Y gesse, that this thing is good for the present nede; for it is good to a man to be so.
046	1CO	007	027	Thou art boundun to a wijf, nyle thou seke vnbyndyng; thou art vnboundun fro a wijf, nyle thou seke a wijf.
046	1CO	007	028	But if thou hast takun a wijf, thou hast not synned; and if a maidun is weddid, sche synnede not; nethelesse siche schulen haue tribulacioun of fleisch.
