# BOOK	048	GAL	Galatians	Galatians
048	GAL	001	001	Poul the apostle, not of men, ne bi man, but bi Jhesu Crist, and God the fadir,
048	GAL	001	002	that reiside hym fro deth, and alle the britheren that ben with me, to the chirchis of Galathie,
048	GAL	001	003	grace to you and pees of God the fadir, and of the Lord Jhesu Crist,
048	GAL	001	004	that yaf hym silf for oure synnes, to delyuere vs fro the present wickid world, bi the wille of God and of oure fadir,
048	GAL	001	005	to whom is worschip and glorie in to worldis of worldis. Amen.
048	GAL	001	006	I wondur, that so soone ye be thus moued fro hym that clepid you in to the grace of Crist, in to another euangelie; which is not anothir,
048	GAL	001	007	but that ther ben summe that troublen you, and wolen mysturne the euangelie of Crist.
048	GAL	001	008	But thouy we, or an aungel of heuene, prechide to you, bisidis that that we han prechid to you, be he acursid.
048	GAL	001	009	As Y haue seid bifore, and now eftsoones Y seie, if ony preche to you bisidis that that ye han vndurfongun, be he cursid.
048	GAL	001	010	For now whether counsele Y men, or God? or whether Y seche to plese men? If Y pleside yit men, Y were not Cristis seruaunt.
048	GAL	001	011	For, britheren, Y make knowun to you the euangelie, that was prechid of me, for it is not bi man;
048	GAL	001	012	ne Y took it of man, ne lernyde, but bi reuelacioun of Jhesu Crist.
048	GAL	001	013	For ye han herd my conuersacioun sumtyme in the Jurie, and that Y pursuede passyngli the chirche of God, and fauyt ayen it.
048	GAL	001	014	And Y profitide in the Jurie aboue many of myn eueneldis in my kynrede, and was more aboundauntli a folewere of my fadris tradiciouns.
048	GAL	001	015	But whanne it pleside hym, that departide me fro my modir wombe,
048	GAL	001	016	and clepide bi his grace, to schewe his sone in me, that Y schulde preche hym among the hethene, anoon Y drowy me not to fleisch and blood; ne Y cam to Jerusalem to the apostlis,
048	GAL	001	017	that weren tofor me, but Y wente in to Arabie, and eftsoones Y turnede ayen in to Damask.
048	GAL	001	018	And sith thre yeer aftir Y cam to Jerusalem, to se Petre, and Y dwellide with hym fiftene daies;
048	GAL	001	019	but Y sawy noon othere of the apostlis, but James, oure Lordis brother.
048	GAL	001	020	And these thingis which Y write to you, lo! tofor God Y lie not.
048	GAL	001	021	Afterward Y cam in to the coostis of Syrie and Cilicie.
048	GAL	001	022	But Y was vnknowun bi face to the chirchis of Judee, that weren in Crist; and thei hadden oonli an heryng,
048	GAL	001	023	that he that pursuede vs sum tyme, prechide now the feith, ayens which he fauyte sum tyme;
048	GAL	001	024	and in me thei glorifieden God.
048	GAL	002	001	And sith fourtene yeer aftir, eftsones Y wente vp to Jerusalem with Barnabas, and took with me Tite.
048	GAL	002	002	Y wente vp bi reuelacioun, and spak with hem the euangelie, which Y preche among the hethene; and bi hem silf to these that semeden to be sumwhat, lest Y runne, or hadde runne in veyne.
048	GAL	002	003	And nother Tite, that hadde be with me, while he was hethene, was compellid to be circumsidid;
048	GAL	002	004	but for false britheren that weren brouyt ynne, whiche hadden entrid to aspie oure fredom, which we han in Jhesu Crist, to bring vs in to seruage.
048	GAL	002	005	But we yyue no place to subieccioun, that the treuthe of the gospel schulde dwelle with you.
048	GAL	002	006	But of these that semeden to be sumwhat; whiche thei weren sum tyme, it perteyneth not to me, for God takith not the persoone of man; for thei that semeden to be sumwhat, yauen me no thing.
048	GAL	002	007	But ayenward, whanne thei hadden seyn, that the euangelie of prepucie was youun to me, as the euangelie of circumcisioun was youun to Petre;
048	GAL	002	008	for he that wrouyte to Petre in apostlehed of circumcisioun, wrouyte also to me among the hethene;
048	GAL	002	009	and whanne thei hadden knowe the grace of God, that was youun to me, James, and Petre, and Joon, whiche weren seyn to be the pileris, thei yauen riythond of felowschip to me and to Barnabas, that we among the hethene, and thei in to circumcisioun;
048	GAL	002	010	oneli that we hadde mynde of pore men `of Crist, the which thing Y was ful bisi to doon.
048	GAL	002	011	But whanne Petre was comun to Antioche, Y ayenstood hym in the face, for he was worthi to be vndirnommen.
048	GAL	002	012	For bifor that ther camen summen fro James, he eete with the hethene men; but whanne thei weren comun, he withdrowy, and departide hym, dredinge hem that weren of circumcisioun.
048	GAL	002	013	And the othere Jewis assentiden to his feynyng, so that Barnabas was drawun of hem in to that feynyng.
048	GAL	002	014	But whanne Y sawy, that thei walkiden not riytli to the treuthe of the gospel, Y seide to Petre bifor alle men, If thou, that art a Jew, lyuest hethenlich, and not Jewelich, hou constreynest thou hethene men to bicome Jewis?
048	GAL	002	015	We Jewis of kynde, and not synful men of the hethene,
048	GAL	002	016	knowen that a man is not iustified of the werkis of lawe, but bi the feith of Jhesu Crist; and we bileuen in Jhesu Crist, that we ben iustified of the feith of Crist, and not of the werkis of lawe. Wherfor of the werkis of lawe ech fleisch schal not be iustified.
048	GAL	002	017	And if we sechen to be iustified in Crist, we oure silf ben foundun synful men, whether Crist be mynystre of synne?
048	GAL	002	018	God forbede. And if Y bylde ayen thingis that Y haue distruyed, Y make my silf a trespassour.
048	GAL	002	019	For bi the lawe Y am deed to the lawe, and Y am fitchid to the crosse, that Y lyue to God with Crist.
048	GAL	002	020	And now lyue not Y, but Crist lyueth in me. But that Y lyue now in fleisch, Y lyue in the feith of Goddis sone, that louede me, and yaf hym silf for me.
048	GAL	002	021	Y caste not awey the grace of God; for if riytwisnesse be thoruy lawe, thanne Crist diede with out cause.
048	GAL	003	001	Vnwitti Galathies, tofor whos iyen Jhesu Crist is exilid, and is crucified in you, who hath disseyued you, that ye obeyen not to treuthe?
048	GAL	003	002	This oneli Y wilne to lerne of you, whether ye han vndurfonge the spirit of werkis of the lawe, or of heryng of bileue?
048	GAL	003	003	So ye ben foolis, that whanne ye han bigunne in spirit, ye ben endid in fleisch.
048	GAL	003	004	So grete thingis ye han suffrid without cause, if it be withoute cause.
048	GAL	003	005	He that yyueth to you spirit, and worchith vertues in you, whether of werkis of the lawe, or of hering of bileue?
048	GAL	003	006	As it is writun, Abraham bileuede to God, and it was rettid to hym to riytfulnesse.
048	GAL	003	007	And therfor knowe ye, that these that ben of bileue, ben the sones of Abraham.
048	GAL	003	008	And the scripture seynge afer, that God iustifieth the hethene, of bileue told tofor to Abraham, That in thee alle the hethene schulen be blessid.
048	GAL	003	009	And therfor these that ben of bileue, schulen be blessid with feithful Abraham.
048	GAL	003	010	For alle that ben of the werkis of the lawe, ben vndur curse; for it is writun, Ech man is cursid, that abidith not in alle thingis that ben writun in the book of the lawe, to do tho thingis.
048	GAL	003	011	And that no man is iustified in the lawe bifor God, it is opyn, for a riytful man lyueth of bileue.
048	GAL	003	012	But the lawe is not of bileue, but he that doith tho thingis of the lawe, schal lyue in hem.
048	GAL	003	013	But Crist ayenbouyte us fro the curse of the lawe, and was maad acursid for vs; for it is writun, Ech man is cursid that hangith in the tre;
048	GAL	003	014	that among the hethene the blessyng of Abraham were maad in `Crist Jhesu, that we vndurfonge the biheeste of spirit thoruy bileue.
048	GAL	003	015	Britheren, Y seie aftir man, no man dispisith the testament of a man that is confermed, or ordeyneth aboue.
048	GAL	003	016	The biheestis weren seid to Abraham and to his seed; he seith not, In seedis, as in many, but as in oon, And to thi seed, that is, Crist.
048	GAL	003	017	But Y seie, this testament is confermed of God; the lawe that was maad after foure hundrid and thritti yeer, makith not the testament veyn to auoide awei the biheest.
048	GAL	003	018	For if eritage were of the lawe, it were not now of biheeste. But God grauntide to Abraham thoruy biheest.
048	GAL	003	019	What thanne the lawe? It was sett for trespassing, to the seed come, to whom he hadde maad his biheest. Whiche lawe was ordeyned bi aungels, in the hoond of a mediatour.
048	GAL	003	020	But a mediatour is not of oon. But God is oon.
048	GAL	003	021	Is thanne the lawe ayens the biheestis of God? God forbede. For if the lawe were youun, that myyte quikene, verili were riytfulnesse of lawe.
048	GAL	003	022	But scripture hath concludid alle thingis vndir synne, that the biheeste of the feith of Jhesu Crist were yyuen to hem that bileuen.
048	GAL	003	023	And tofor that bileue cam, thei weren kept vndur the lawe, enclosid in to that bileue that was to be schewid.
048	GAL	003	024	And so the lawe was oure vndirsmaister in Crist, that we ben iustified of bileue.
048	GAL	003	025	But aftir that bileue cam, we ben not now vndur the vndurmaistir.
048	GAL	003	026	For alle ye ben the children of God thoruy the bileue of Jhesu Crist.
048	GAL	003	027	For alle ye that ben baptisid, ben clothid with Crist.
048	GAL	003	028	Ther is no Jewe, ne Greke, ne bond man, ne fre man, ne male, ne female; for alle ye ben oon in `Jhesu Crist.
048	GAL	003	029	And if ye ben oon in `Jhesu Crist, thanne ye ben the seed of Abraham, and eiris bi biheest.
048	GAL	004	001	But Y seie, as long tyme as the eir is a litil child, he dyuersith no thing fro a seruaunt, whanne he is lord of alle thingis;
048	GAL	004	002	but he is vndur keperis and tutoris, in to the tyme determyned of the fadir.
048	GAL	004	003	So we, whanne we weren litle children, we serueden vndur the elementis of the world.
048	GAL	004	004	But aftir that the fulfilling of tyme cam, God sente his sone,
048	GAL	004	005	maad of a womman, maad vndur the lawe, that he schulde ayenbie hem that weren vndur the lawe, that we schulden vnderfonge the adopcioun of sones.
048	GAL	004	006	And for ye ben Goddis sones, God sente his spirit in to youre hertis, criynge, Abba, fadir.
048	GAL	004	007	And so ther is not now a seruaunt, but a sone; and if he is a sone, he is an eir bi God.
048	GAL	004	008	But thanne ye vnknowynge God, serueden to hem that in kynde weren not goddis.
048	GAL	004	009	But now whanne ye han knowe God, and ben knowun of God, hou ben ye turned eftsoone to the febil and nedi elementis, to the whiche ye wolen eft serue?
048	GAL	004	010	Ye taken kepe to daies, and monethis, and tymes, and yeris.
048	GAL	004	011	But Y drede you, lest without cause Y haue trauelid among you.
048	GAL	004	012	Be ye as Y, for Y am as ye. Britheren, Y biseche you, ye han hurt me no thing.
048	GAL	004	013	But ye knowen, that bi infirmyte of fleisch Y haue prechid to you now bifore;
048	GAL	004	014	and ye dispiseden not, nether forsoken youre temptacioun in my fleisch, but ye resseyueden me as an aungel of God, as `Crist Jhesu.
048	GAL	004	015	Where thanne is youre blessyng? For Y bere you witnesse, that if it myyte haue be don. ye wolden haue put out youre iyen, and haue yyuen hem to me.
048	GAL	004	016	Am Y thanne maad an enemye to you, seiynge to you the sothe?
048	GAL	004	017	Thei louen not you wel, but thei wolen exclude you, that ye suen hem.
048	GAL	004	018	But sue ye the good euermore in good, and not oneli whanne Y am present with you.
048	GAL	004	019	My smale children, whiche Y bere eftsoones, til that Crist be fourmed in you,
048	GAL	004	020	and Y wolde now be at you, and chaunge my vois, for Y am confoundid among you.
048	GAL	004	021	Seie to me, ye that wolen be vndir the lawe, `han ye not red the lawe?
048	GAL	004	022	For it is writun, that Abraham hadde two sones, oon of a seruaunt, and oon of a fre womman.
048	GAL	004	023	But he that was of the seruaunt, was borun after the flesh; but he that was of the fre womman, by a biheeste.
048	GAL	004	024	The whiche thingis ben seid bi an othir vndirstonding. For these ben two testamentis; oon in the hille of Synai, gendringe in to seruage, which is Agar.
048	GAL	004	025	For Syna is an hille that is in Arabie, which hille is ioyned to it that is now Jerusalem, and seruith with hir children.
048	GAL	004	026	But that Jerusalem that is aboue, is fre, whiche is oure modir.
048	GAL	004	027	For it is writun, Be glad, thou bareyn, that berist not; breke out and crye, that bringist forth no children; for many sones ben of hir that is left of hir hosebonde, more than of hir that hath an hosebonde.
048	GAL	004	028	For, britheren, we ben sones of biheeste aftir Isaac;
048	GAL	004	029	but now as this that was borun after the fleisch pursuede him that was aftir the spirit, so now.
048	GAL	004	030	But what seith the scripture? Caste out the seruaunt and hir sone, for the sone of the seruaunt schal not be eir with the sone of the fre wijf.
048	GAL	004	031	And so, britheren, we ben not sones of the seruaunt, but of the fre wijf, bi which fredom Crist hath maad vs fre.
048	GAL	005	001	Stonde ye therfor, and nyl ye eftsoones be holdun in the yok of seruage.
048	GAL	005	002	Lo! Y Poul seie to you, that if ye ben circumcidid, Crist schal no thing profite to you.
048	GAL	005	003	And Y witnesse eftsoones to ech man that circumcidith hym silf, that he is dettour of al the lawe to be don.
048	GAL	005	004	And ye ben voidid awei fro Crist, and ye that be iustified in the lawe, ye han fallen awei fro grace.
048	GAL	005	005	For we thoruy the spirit of bileue abiden the hope of riytfulnesse.
048	GAL	005	006	For in Jhesu Crist nether circumcisioun is ony thing worth, nether prepucie, but the bileue that worchith bi charite.
048	GAL	005	007	Ye runnen wel; who lettide you that ye obeyede not to treuthe?
048	GAL	005	008	Consente ye to no man; for this counsel ys not of hym that hath clepid you.
048	GAL	005	009	A litil souredowy apeirith al the gobet.
048	GAL	005	010	I trust on you in oure Lord, that ye schulden vndurstonde noon other thing. And who that disturblith you, schal bere dom, who euere he be.
048	GAL	005	011	And, britheren, if Y preche yit circumcisioun, what suffre Y yit persecucioun? thanne the sclaundre of the crosse is auoidid.
048	GAL	005	012	Y wolde that thei weren cut awei, that disturblen you.
048	GAL	005	013	For, britheren, ye ben clepid in to fredom; oneli yyue ye not fredom in to occasioun of fleisch, but bi charite of spirit serue ye togidere.
048	GAL	005	014	For euery lawe is fulfillid in o word, Thou schalt loue thi neiybore as thi silf.
048	GAL	005	015	And if ye bite, and ete ech othere, se ye, lest ye be wastid ech fro othere.
048	GAL	005	016	And Y seie you in Crist, walke ye in spirit, and ye schulen not performe the desiris of the fleisch.
048	GAL	005	017	For the fleisch coueitith ayens the spirit, and the spirit ayen the fleisch; for these ben aduersaries togidere, that ye don not alle thingis that ye wolen.
048	GAL	005	018	That if ye be led bi spirit, ye ben not vnder the lawe.
048	GAL	005	019	And werkis of the fleisch ben opyn, whiche ben fornicacioun, vnclennes, vnchastite, letcherie, seruice of false goddis,
048	GAL	005	020	witchecraftis, enmytees, striuyngis, indignaciouns, wraththis, chidingis, discenciouns, sectis, enuyes,
048	GAL	005	021	manslauytris, dronkennessis, vnmesurable etyngis, and thingis lijk to these, whiche Y seie to you, as Y haue told to you `to fore, for thei that doon suche thingis, schulen not haue the kyngdom of God.
048	GAL	005	022	But the fruyt of the spirit is charite, ioye, pees, pacience, long abidyng,
048	GAL	005	023	benygnyte, goodnesse, myldenesse, feith, temperaunce, contynence, chastite; ayen suche thingis is no lawe.
048	GAL	005	024	And they that ben of Crist, han crucified her fleisch with vices and coueytyngis.
048	GAL	005	025	If we lyuen bi spirit, walke we bi spirit;
048	GAL	005	026	be we not made coueytouse of veyn glorie, stirynge ech othere to wraththe, or hauynge enuye ech to othere.
048	GAL	006	001	Britheren, if a man be occupied in ony gilt, ye that ben spiritual, enforme ye such oon in spirit of softnesse, biholdinge thi silf, lest that thou be temptid.
048	GAL	006	002	Ech bere othere chargis, and so ye schulen fulfille the lawe of Crist.
048	GAL	006	003	For who that trowith that he be ouyt, whanne he is nouyt, he bigilith him silf.
048	GAL	006	004	But ech man preue his owne werk, and so he schal haue glorie in him silf, and not in an othere.
048	GAL	006	005	For ech man schal bere his owne charge.
048	GAL	006	006	He that is tauyt bi word, comune he with him that techith hym, in `alle goodis.
048	GAL	006	007	Nyle ye erre, God is not scorned; for tho thingis that a man sowith, tho thingis he schal repe.
048	GAL	006	008	For he that sowith in his fleisch, of the fleisch he schal repe corrupcioun; but he that sowith in the spirit, of the spirit he schal repe euerelastynge lijf.
048	GAL	006	009	And doynge good faile we not; for in his tyme we schal repe, not failinge.
048	GAL	006	010	Therfor while we han tyme, worche we good to alle men; but most to hem that ben homliche of the feith.
048	GAL	006	011	Se ye, what maner lettris Y haue write to you with myn owne hoond.
048	GAL	006	012	For who euere wole plese in the fleisch, `this constreyneth you to be circumcidid, oonli that thei suffren not the persecucioun of Cristis crosse.
048	GAL	006	013	For nether thei that ben circumcidid kepen the lawe; but thei wolen that ye be circumcidid, that thei haue glorie in youre fleisch.
048	GAL	006	014	But fer be it fro me to haue glorie, no but in the crosse of oure Lord Jhesu Crist, bi whom the world is crucified to me, and Y to the world.
048	GAL	006	015	For in Jhesu Crist nether circumcisioun is ony thing worth, ne prepucie, but a newe creature.
048	GAL	006	016	And who euere suwen this reule, pees on hem, and merci, and on Israel of God.
048	GAL	006	017	And heraftir no man be heuy to me; for Y bere in my bodi the tokenes of oure Lord Jhesu Crist.
048	GAL	006	018	The grace of oure Lord Jhesu Crist be with youre spirit, britheren. Amen.
