# BOOK	049	EPH	Ephesians	Ephesians
049	EPH	001	001	Poul, the apostle of Jhesu Crist, bi the wille of God, to alle seyntis that ben at Effesie, and to the feithful men in Jhesu Crist,
049	EPH	001	002	grace be to you and pees of God, oure fader, and oure Lord Jhesu Crist.
049	EPH	001	003	Blessid be God and the fadir of oure Lord Jhesu Crist, that hath blessid vs in al spiritual blessing in heuenli thingis in Crist,
049	EPH	001	004	as he hath chosun vs in hym silf bifor the makyng of the world, that we weren hooli, and with out wem in his siyt, in charite.
049	EPH	001	005	Which hath bifor ordeyned vs in to adopcioun of sones bi Jhesu Crist in to hym, bi the purpos of his wille,
049	EPH	001	006	in to the heriyng of the glorie of his grace;
049	EPH	001	007	in which he hath glorified vs in his dereworthe sone. In whom we han redempcioun bi his blood, foryyuenesse of synnes, aftir the ritchessis of his grace,
049	EPH	001	008	that aboundide greetli in vs in al wisdom and prudence,
049	EPH	001	009	to make knowun to vs the sacrament of his wille, bi the good plesaunce of hym; the which sacrament he purposide in
049	EPH	001	010	hym in the dispensacioun of plente of tymes to enstore alle thingis in Crist, whiche ben in heuenes, and whiche ben in erthe, in hym.
049	EPH	001	011	In whom we ben clepid bi sort, bifor ordeyned bi the purpos of hym that worchith alle thingis bi the counsel of his wille;
049	EPH	001	012	that we be in to the heriyng of his glorie, we that han hopid bifor in Crist.
049	EPH	001	013	In whom also ye weren clepid, whanne ye herden the word of treuthe, the gospel of youre heelthe, in whom ye bileuynge ben merkid with the Hooli Goost of biheest, which is the ernes of oure eritage,
049	EPH	001	014	in to the redempcioun of purchasyng, in to heriyng of his glorie.
049	EPH	001	015	Therfor and Y herynge youre feith, that is in Crist Jhesu, and the loue in to alle seyntis,
049	EPH	001	016	ceesse not to do thankyngis for you, makynge mynde of you in my preieris;
049	EPH	001	017	that God of oure Lord Jhesu Crist, the fadir of glorie, yyue to you the spirit of wisdom and of reuelacioun, in to the knowyng of hym;
049	EPH	001	018	and the iyen of youre herte liytned, that ye wite, which is the hope of his clepyng, and whiche ben the richessis of the glorie of his eritage in seyntis;
049	EPH	001	019	and whych is the excellent greetnesse of his vertu in to vs that han bileuyd, bi the worchyng of the myyt of his vertu,
049	EPH	001	020	which he wrouyte in Crist, reisynge hym fro deth, and settynge him on his riyt half in heuenli thingis,
049	EPH	001	021	aboue ech principat, and potestat, and vertu, and domynacioun, and aboue ech name that is named, not oneli in this world, but also in the world to comynge;
049	EPH	001	022	and made alle thingis suget vndur hise feet, and yaf hym to be heed ouer al the chirche,
049	EPH	001	023	that is the bodi of hym, and the plente of hym, which is alle thingis in alle thingis fulfillid.
049	EPH	002	001	And whanne ye weren deed in youre giltis and synnes,
049	EPH	002	002	in which ye wandriden sum tyme aftir the cours of this world, aftir the prince of the power of this eir, of the spirit that worchith now in to the sones of vnbileue;
049	EPH	002	003	in which also we `alle lyueden sum tyme in the desiris of oure fleisch, doynge the willis of the fleisch and of thouytis, and we weren bi kynde the sones of wraththe, as othere men;
049	EPH	002	004	but God, that is riche in merci, for his ful myche charite in which he louyde vs,
049	EPH	002	005	yhe, whanne we weren deed in synnes, quikenede vs togidere in Crist, bi whos grace ye ben sauyd, and ayen reiside togidere,
049	EPH	002	006	and made togidere to sitte in heuenli thingis in Crist Jhesu;
049	EPH	002	007	that he schulde schewe in the worldis aboue comynge the plenteuouse ritchessis of his grace in goodnesse on vs in Crist Jhesu.
049	EPH	002	008	For bi grace ye ben sauyd bi feith, and this not of you; for it is the yifte of God,
049	EPH	002	009	not of werkis, that no man haue glorie.
049	EPH	002	010	For we ben the makyng of hym, maad of nouyt in Crist Jhesu, in good werkis, whiche God hath ordeyned, that we go in tho werkis.
049	EPH	002	011	For which thing be ye myndeful, that sumtyme ye weren hethene in fleisch, which weren seid prepucie, fro that that is seid circumcisioun maad bi hond in fleisch;
049	EPH	002	012	and ye weren in that time with out Crist, alienyd fro the lyuyng of Israel, and gestis of testamentis, not hauynge hope of biheest, and with outen God in this world.
049	EPH	002	013	But now in Crist Jhesu ye that weren sum tyme fer, ben maad nyy in the blood of Crist.
049	EPH	002	014	For he is oure pees, that made bothe oon, and vnbyndynge the myddil wal of a wal with out morter, enmytees in his fleisch;
049	EPH	002	015	and auoidide the lawe of maundementis bi domes, that he make twei in hym silf in to a newe man,
049	EPH	002	016	makynge pees, to recounsele bothe in o bodi to God bi the cros, sleynge the enemytees in hym silf.
049	EPH	002	017	And he comynge prechide pees to you that weren fer, and pees to hem that weren niy;
049	EPH	002	018	for bi hym we bothe han niy comyng in o spirit to the fadir.
049	EPH	002	019	Therfor now ye ben not gestis and straungeris, but ye ben citeseyns of seyntis, and houshold meine of God;
049	EPH	002	020	aboue bildid on the foundement of apostlis and of profetis, vpon that hiyeste corner stoon, Crist Jhesu;
049	EPH	002	021	in whom ech bildyng maad waxith in to an hooli temple in the Lord.
049	EPH	002	022	In whom also `be ye bildid togidere in to the habitacle of God, in the Hooli Goost.
049	EPH	003	001	For the grace of this thing I Poul, the boundun of Crist Jhesu, for you hethene men,
049	EPH	003	002	if netheles ye han herd the dispensacioun of Goddis grace, that is youun to me in you.
049	EPH	003	003	For bi reuelacioun the sacrament is maad knowun to me, as Y aboue wroot in schort thing,
049	EPH	003	004	as ye moun rede, and vndurstonde my prudence in the mysterie of Crist.
049	EPH	003	005	Which was not knowun to othere generaciouns to the sones of men, as it is now schewid to his hooli apostlis and prophetis in the spirit,
049	EPH	003	006	that hethene men ben euen eiris, and of oo bodi, and parteneris togidere of his biheest in Crist Jhesu bi the euangelie;
049	EPH	003	007	whos mynystre Y am maad, bi the yifte of Goddis grace, which is youun to me bi the worchyng of his vertu.
049	EPH	003	008	To me, leeste of alle seyntis, this grace is youun to preche among hethene men the vnserchable richessis of Crist,
049	EPH	003	009	and to liytne alle men, which is the dispensacioun of sacrament hid fro worldis in God, that made alle thingis of nouyt;
049	EPH	003	010	that the myche fold wisdom of God be knowun to princis and potestatis in heuenli thingis bi the chirche,
049	EPH	003	011	bi the bifore ordinaunce of worldis, which he made in Crist Jhesu oure Lord.
049	EPH	003	012	In whom we han trist and nyy comyng, in tristenyng bi the feith of hym.
049	EPH	003	013	For which thing Y axe, that ye faile not in my tribulaciouns for you, which is youre glorie.
049	EPH	003	014	For grace of this thing Y bowe my knees to the fadir of oure Lord Jhesu Crist,
049	EPH	003	015	of whom ech fadirhod in heuenes and in erthe is named,
049	EPH	003	016	that he yyue to you, aftir the richessis of his glorie, vertu to be strengthid bi his spirit in the ynnere man,
049	EPH	003	017	that Crist dwelle bi feith in youre hertis; that ye rootid and groundid in charite,
049	EPH	003	018	moun comprehende with alle seyntis, which is the breede, and the lengthe, and the hiynesse, and the depnesse;
049	EPH	003	019	also to wite the charite of Crist more excellent than science, that ye be fillid in al the plentee of God.
049	EPH	003	020	And to hym that is myyti to do alle thingis more plenteuousli than we axen or vndurstondun, bi the vertu that worchith in vs,
049	EPH	003	021	to hym be glorie in the chirche, and in Crist Jhesu, in to alle the generaciouns of the world of worldis. Amen.
049	EPH	004	001	Therfor Y boundun for the Lord biseche you, that ye walke worthili in the clepyng,
049	EPH	004	002	in which ye ben clepid, with al mekenesse and myldenesse, with pacience supportinge ech other in charite,
049	EPH	004	003	bisi to kepe vnyte of spirit in the boond of pees.
049	EPH	004	004	O bodi and o spirit, as ye ben clepid in oon hope of youre cleping;
049	EPH	004	005	o Lord,
049	EPH	004	006	o feith, o baptym, o God and fadir of alle, which is aboue alle men, and bi alle thingis, and in vs alle.
049	EPH	004	007	But to ech of vs grace is youun bi the mesure of the yyuyng of Crist;
049	EPH	004	008	for which thing he seith, He stiynge an hiy, ledde caitifte caitif, he yaf yiftis to men.
049	EPH	004	009	But what is it, that he stiede vp, no but that also he cam doun first in to the lowere partis of the erthe?
049	EPH	004	010	He it is that cam doun, and that stiede on alle heuenes, that he schulde fille alle thingis.
049	EPH	004	011	And he yaf summe apostlis, summe prophetis, othere euangelistis, othere scheepherdis and techeris,
049	EPH	004	012	to the ful endyng of seyntis, in to the werk of mynystrie, in to edificacioun of Cristis bodi,
049	EPH	004	013	til we rennen alle, in to vnyte of feith and of knowyng of Goddis sone, in to a parfit man, aftir the mesure of age of the plente of Crist;
049	EPH	004	014	that we be not now litle children, mouynge as wawis, and be not borun aboute with ech wynd of teching, in the weiwardnesse of men, in sutil wit, to the disseyuyng of errour.
049	EPH	004	015	But do we treuthe in charite, and wexe in him by alle thingis, that is Crist oure heed;
049	EPH	004	016	of whom alle the bodi set togidere, and boundun togidere bi ech ioynture of vnder seruyng, bi worching in to the mesure of ech membre, makith encreesyng of the bodi, in to edificacioun of it silf in charite.
049	EPH	004	017	Therfor Y seie and witnesse this thing in the Lord, that ye walke not now, as hethene men walken, in the vanyte of her wit;
049	EPH	004	018	that han vndurstondyng derkned with derknessis, and ben alienyd fro the lijf of God, bi ignoraunce that is in hem, for the blyndenesse of her herte.
049	EPH	004	019	Which dispeirynge bitoken hem silf to vnchastite, in to the worchyng of al vnclennesse in coueitise.
049	EPH	004	020	But ye han not so lerud Crist, if netheles ye herden hym,
049	EPH	004	021	and ben tauyt in hym, as is treuthe in Jhesu.
049	EPH	004	022	Do ye awey bi the elde lyuyng the elde man, that is corrupt bi the desiris of errour;
049	EPH	004	023	and be ye renewlid in the spirit of youre soule;
049	EPH	004	024	and clothe ye the newe man, which is maad aftir God in riytwisnesse and hoolynesse of treuthe.
049	EPH	004	025	For which thing `ye putte awei leesyng, and speke ye treuthe ech man with his neiybore, for we ben membris ech to othere.
049	EPH	004	026	Be ye wrooth, and nyle ye do synne; the sunne falle not doun on youre wraththe.
049	EPH	004	027	Nyle ye yyue stide to the deuel.
049	EPH	004	028	He that stal, now stele he not; but more trauele he in worchinge with hise hondis that that is good, that he haue whereof he schal yyue to nedi.
049	EPH	004	029	Ech yuel word go not of youre mouth; but if ony is good to the edificacioun of feith, that it yyue grace to men that heren.
049	EPH	004	030	And nyle ye make the Hooli Goost of God sori, in which ye ben markid in the dai of redempcioun.
049	EPH	004	031	Al bitternesse, and wraththe, and indignacioun, and cry, and blasfemye be takun awey fro you, with al malice;
049	EPH	004	032	and be ye togidere benygne, merciful, foryyuynge togidere, as also God foryaf to you in Crist.
049	EPH	005	001	Therfor be ye foloweris of God, as moost dereworthe sones;
049	EPH	005	002	and walke ye in loue, as Crist louyde vs, and yaf hym silf for vs an offryng and a sacrifice to God, in to the odour of swetnesse.
049	EPH	005	003	And fornycacioun, and al vnclennesse, or aueryce, be not named among you, as it bicometh holi men;
049	EPH	005	004	ethir filthe, or foli speche, or harlatrye, that perteyneth not to profit, but more doyng of thankyngis.
049	EPH	005	005	For wite ye this, and vndurstonde, that ech letchour, or vnclene man, or coueytouse, that serueth to mawmetis, hath not eritage in the kingdom of Crist and of God.
049	EPH	005	006	No man disseyue you bi veyn wordis; for whi for these thingis the wraththe of God cam on the sones of vnbileue.
049	EPH	005	007	Therfor nyle ye be maad parteneris of hem.
049	EPH	005	008	For ye weren sum tyme derknessis, but now `ye ben liyt in the Lord. Walke ye as the sones of liyt.
049	EPH	005	009	For the fruyt of liyt is in al goodnesse, and riytwisnesse, and treuthe.
049	EPH	005	010	And preue ye what `thing is wel plesynge to God.
049	EPH	005	011	And nyle ye comyne to vnfruytouse werkis of derknessis; but more repreue ye.
049	EPH	005	012	For what thingis ben don of hem in priuy, it is foule, yhe, to speke.
049	EPH	005	013	And alle thingis that ben repreuyd of the liyt, ben opynli schewid; for al thing that is schewid, is liyt.
049	EPH	005	014	For which thing he seith, Rise thou that slepist, and rise vp fro deth, and Crist schal liytne thee.
049	EPH	005	015	Therfor, britheren, se ye, hou warli ye schulen go;
049	EPH	005	016	not as vnwise men, but as wise men, ayenbiynge tyme, for the daies ben yuele.
049	EPH	005	017	Therfor nyle ye be maad vnwise, but vndurstondynge which is the wille of God.
049	EPH	005	018	And nyle ye be drunkun of wyn, in which is letcherie, but be ye fillid with the Hooli Goost; and speke ye to you silf in salmes,
049	EPH	005	019	and ymnes, and spiritual songis, syngynge and seiynge salm in youre hertis to the Lord;
049	EPH	005	020	euermore doynge thankingis for alle thingis in the name of oure Lord Jhesu Crist to God and to the fadir.
049	EPH	005	021	Be ye suget togidere in the drede of Crist.
049	EPH	005	022	Wymmen, be thei suget to her hosebondis,
049	EPH	005	023	as to the Lord, for the man is heed of the wymman, as Crist is heed of the chirche; he is sauyour of his bodi.
049	EPH	005	024	But as the chirche is suget to Crist, so wymmen to her hosebondis in alle thingis.
049	EPH	005	025	Men, loue ye youre wyues, as Crist louyde the chirche, and yaf hym silf for it, to make it holi;
049	EPH	005	026	and clenside it with the waisching of watir, in the word of lijf,
049	EPH	005	027	to yyue the chirche gloriouse to hym silf, that it hadde no wem, ne ryueling, or ony siche thing, but that it be hooli and vndefoulid.
049	EPH	005	028	So and men `schulen loue her wyues, as her owne bodies. He that loueth his wijf, loueth hym silf;
049	EPH	005	029	for no man hatide euere his owne fleisch, but nurischith and fostrith it, as Crist doith the chirche.
049	EPH	005	030	And we ben membris of his bodi, of his fleisch, and of his boonys.
049	EPH	005	031	For this thing a man schal forsake his fadir and modir, and he schal drawe to his wijf; and thei schulen be tweyne in o fleisch.
049	EPH	005	032	This sacrament is greet; yhe, Y seie in Crist, and in the chirche.
049	EPH	005	033	Netheles ye alle, ech man loue his wijf as hym silf; and the wijf drede hir hosebonde.
049	EPH	006	001	Sones, obeische ye to youre fadir and modir, in the Lord; for this thing is riytful.
049	EPH	006	002	Onoure thou thi fadir and thi modir, that is the firste maundement in biheest;
049	EPH	006	003	that it be wel to thee, and that thou be long lyuynge on the erthe.
049	EPH	006	004	And, fadris, nyle ye terre youre sones to wraththe; but nurische ye hem in the teching and chastising of the Lord.
049	EPH	006	005	Seruauntis, obeische ye to fleischli lordis with drede and trembling, in simplenesse of youre herte, as to Crist;
049	EPH	006	006	not seruynge at the iye, as plesinge to men, but as seruauntis of Crist; doynge the wille of God bi discrecioun,
049	EPH	006	007	with good wille seruynge as to the Lord, and not as to men;
049	EPH	006	008	witinge that ech man, what euere good thing he schal do, he schal resseyue this of the Lord, whether seruaunt, whether fre man.
049	EPH	006	009	And, ye lordis, do the same thingis to hem, foryyuynge manaasis; witinge that bothe her Lord and youre is in heuenes, and the taking of persones is not anentis God.
049	EPH	006	010	Her aftirward, britheren, be ye coumfortid in the Lord, and in the miyt of his vertu.
049	EPH	006	011	Clothe you with the armere of God, that ye moun stonde ayens aspiynges of the deuel.
049	EPH	006	012	For whi stryuyng is not to vs ayens fleisch and blood, but ayens princis and potestatis, ayens gouernours of the world of these derknessis, ayens spiritual thingis of wickidnesse, in heuenli thingis.
049	EPH	006	013	Therfor take ye the armere of God, that ye moun ayenstonde in the yuel dai; and in alle thingis stonde perfit.
049	EPH	006	014	Therfor stonde ye, and be gird aboute youre leendis in sothefastnesse, and clothid with the haburioun of riytwisnesse,
049	EPH	006	015	and youre feet schood in making redi of the gospel of pees.
049	EPH	006	016	In alle thingis take ye the scheld of feith, in which ye moun quenche alle the firy dartis of `the worste.
049	EPH	006	017	And take ye the helm of helthe, and the swerd of the Goost, that is, the word of God.
049	EPH	006	018	Bi al preier and bisechyng preie ye al tyme in spirit, and in hym wakinge in al bisynesse, and bisechyng for alle hooli men, and for me;
049	EPH	006	019	that word be youun to me in openyng of my mouth, with trist to make knowun the mysterie of the gospel,
049	EPH	006	020	for which Y am set in message in a chayne; so that in it Y be hardi to speke, as it bihoueth me.
049	EPH	006	021	And ye wite, what thingis ben aboute me, what Y do, Titicus, my moost dere brother, and trewe mynystre in the Lord, schal make alle thingis knowun to you;
049	EPH	006	022	whom Y sente to you for this same thing, that ye knowe what thingis ben aboute vs, and that he coumforte youre hertis.
049	EPH	006	023	Pees to britheren, and charite, with feith of God oure fadir, and of the Lord Jhesu Crist.
049	EPH	006	024	Grace with alle men that louen oure Lord Jhesu Crist in vncorrupcioun. Amen, `that is, So be it.
#
# BOOK	050	PHI	Philippians	Philippians
050	PHI	001	001	Poul and Tymothe, seruauntis of Jhesu Crist, to alle the hooli men in Crist Jhesu, that ben at Filippis, with bischopis and dekenes,
050	PHI	001	002	grace and pees to you of God oure fadir, and of the Lord Jhesu Crist.
050	PHI	001	003	I do thankyngis to my God
050	PHI	001	004	in al mynde of you euere more in alle my preyeris for alle you with ioye, and
050	PHI	001	005	make a bisechyng on youre comynyng in the gospel of Crist, fro the firste day til nowe;
050	PHI	001	006	tristenynge this ilke thing, that he that bigan in you a good werk, schal perfourme it til in to the dai of Jhesu Crist.
050	PHI	001	007	As it is iust to me to feele this thing for alle you, for that Y haue you in herte, and in my boondis, and in defending and confermyng of the gospel, that alle ye be felowis of my ioye.
050	PHI	001	008	For God is a witnesse to me, hou Y coueyte alle you in the bowelis of Jhesu Crist.
050	PHI	001	009	And this thing Y preie, that youre charite be plenteuouse more and more in kunnyng, and in al wit;
050	PHI	001	010	that ye preue the betere thingis, that ye be clene and without offence in the dai of Crist;
050	PHI	001	011	fillid with the fruyt of riytwysnesse bi Jhesu Crist, in to the glory and the heriyng of God.
050	PHI	001	012	For, britheren, Y wole that ye wite, that the thingis that ben aboute me han comun more to the profit of the gospel,
050	PHI	001	013	so that my boondis weren maad knowun in Crist, in ech moot halle, and in alle other placis;
050	PHI	001	014	that mo of britheren tristinge in the Lord more plenteuously for my boondis, dursten without drede speke the word of God.
050	PHI	001	015	But summe for enuye and strijf, summe for good wille, prechen Crist;
050	PHI	001	016	and summe of charite, witinge that Y am put in the defense of the gospel.
050	PHI	001	017	But summe of strijf schewen Crist not cleneli, gessynge hem to reise tribulacioun to my boondis.
050	PHI	001	018	But what? the while on al maner, ethir bi occasioun, ethir bi treuthe, Crist is schewid; and in this thing Y haue ioye, but also Y schal haue ioye.
050	PHI	001	019	And Y woot, that this thing schal come to me in to heelthe bi youre preyer, and the vndurmynystring of the spirit of `Jhesu Crist, bi myn abidyng and hope.
050	PHI	001	020	For in no thing Y schal be schamed, but in al trist as euere more and now, Crist schal be magnefied in my bodi, ether bi lijf, ether bi deth.
050	PHI	001	021	For me to lyue is Crist, and to die is wynnyng.
050	PHI	001	022	That if to lyue in fleisch, is fruyt of werk to me, lo! what Y schal chese, Y knowe not.
050	PHI	001	023	But Y am constreyned of twei thingis, Y haue desire to be dissolued, and to be with Crist, it is myche more betere; but to dwelle in fleisch,
050	PHI	001	024	is nedeful for you.
050	PHI	001	025	And Y tristinge this thing, woot that Y schal dwelle, and perfitli dwelle to alle you, to youre profit and ioye of feith,
050	PHI	001	026	that youre thanking abounde in Crist Jhesu in me, bi my comyng eftsoone to you.
050	PHI	001	027	Oneli lyue ye worthili to the gospel of Crist, that whether whanne Y come and se you, ethir absent Y here of you, that ye stonden in o spirit of o wille, trauelinge togidere to the feith of the gospel.
050	PHI	001	028	And in no thing be ye aferd of aduersaries, which is to hem cause of perdicioun,
050	PHI	001	029	but to you cause of heelthe. And this thing is of God. For it is youun to you for Crist, that not oneli ye bileuen in hym, but also that ye suffren for hym;
050	PHI	001	030	hauynge the same strijf, which ye saien in me, and now ye han herd of me.
050	PHI	002	001	Therfor if ony coumfort is in Crist, if ony solace of charite, if ony felouschipe of spirit, if ony inwardnesse of merci doyng,
050	PHI	002	002	fille ye my ioye, that ye vndurstonde the same thing, and haue the same charite, of o wille, and feelen the same thing;
050	PHI	002	003	no thing bi strijf, nether by veyn glorie, but in mekenesse, demynge eche othere to be heiyer than hym silf;
050	PHI	002	004	not biholdinge ech bi hym silf what thingis ben his owne, but tho thingis that ben of othere men.
050	PHI	002	005	And fele ye this thing in you, which also in Crist Jhesu;
050	PHI	002	006	that whanne he was in the forme of God, demyde not raueyn, that hym silf were euene to God;
050	PHI	002	007	but he lowide hym silf, takinge the forme of a seruaunt, and was maad in to the licknesse of men, and in abite was foundun as a man.
050	PHI	002	008	He mekide hym silf, and was maad obedient to the deth, yhe, to the deth of the cross.
050	PHI	002	009	For which thing God enhaunside hym, and yaf to hym a name that is aboue al name;
050	PHI	002	010	that in the name of Jhesu ech kne be bowid, of heuenli thingis, of ertheli thingis, and of hellis;
050	PHI	002	011	and ech tunge knouleche, that the Lord Jhesu Crist is in the glorie of God the fadir.
050	PHI	002	012	Therfor, my most dereworthe britheren, as euere more ye han obeischid, not in my presence onely, but myche more now in myn absence, worche ye with drede and trembling youre heelthe.
050	PHI	002	013	For it is God that worchith in you, bothe to wilne, and to performe, for good wille.
050	PHI	002	014	And do ye alle thingis with out grutchingis and doutyngis;
050	PHI	002	015	that ye be with out playnt, and symple as the sones of God, with out repreef, in the myddil of a schrewid nacioun and a weiward; among whiche ye schynen as yyueris of liyt in the world.
050	PHI	002	016	And holde ye togidere the word of lijf to my glorie in the day of Crist; for Y haue not runnen in veyn, nether Y haue trauelid in veyn.
050	PHI	002	017	But thouy Y be offrid or slayn on the sacrifice and seruyce of youre feith, Y haue ioye, and Y thanke you alle.
050	PHI	002	018	And the same thing haue ye ioye, and thanke ye me.
050	PHI	002	019	And Y hope in the Lord Jhesu, that Y schal sende Tymothe soone to you, that Y be of good coumfort, whanne tho thingis ben knowun that ben aboute you.
050	PHI	002	020	For Y haue no man so of o wille, that is bisi for you with clene affeccioun.
050	PHI	002	021	For alle men seken tho thingis that ben her owne, not tho that ben of Crist Jhesu.
050	PHI	002	022	But knowe ye the asaie of hym, for as a sone to the fadir he hath seruyd with me in the gospel.
050	PHI	002	023	Therfor Y hope that Y schal sende hym to you, anoon as Y se what thingis ben aboute me.
050	PHI	002	024	And Y triste in the Lord, that also my silf schal come to you soone.
050	PHI	002	025	And Y gesside it nedeful to sende to you Epafrodite, my brother and euene worchere, and myn euene knyyt, but youre apostle, and the mynystre of my nede.
050	PHI	002	026	For he desiride you alle, and he was sorewful, therfor that ye herden that he was sijk.
050	PHI	002	027	For he was sijk to the deth, but God hadde merci on him; and not oneli on hym, but also on me, lest Y hadde heuynesse on heuynesse.
050	PHI	002	028	Therfor more hastili Y sente hym, that whanne ye han seyn hym, ye haue ioye eft, and Y be withouten heuynesse.
050	PHI	002	029	Therfor resseyue ye hym with al ioye in the Lord, and haue ye suche with al onour.
050	PHI	002	030	For the werk of Crist he wente to deth, yyuynge his lijf, that he schulde fulfille that that failide of you anentis my seruyce.
050	PHI	003	001	Hennus forward, my britheren, haue ye ioye in the Lord. To write to you the same thingis, to me it is not slow, and to you it is necessarie.
050	PHI	003	002	Se ye houndis, se ye yuele werk men, se ye dyuysioun.
050	PHI	003	003	For we ben circumcisioun, which bi spirit seruen to God, and glorien in Crist Jhesu, and han not trist in the fleisch,
050	PHI	003	004	thouy Y haue trust, yhe, in the fleisch. If ony othere man is seyn to triste in the fleisch,
050	PHI	003	005	Y more, that was circumcidid in the eiytthe dai, of the kyn of Israel, of the lynage of Beniamyn, an Ebrew of Ebrewis, bi the lawe a Farisee,
050	PHI	003	006	bi loue pursuynge the chirche of God, bi riytwisnesse that is in the lawe lyuynge with out playnt.
050	PHI	003	007	But whiche thingis weren to me wynnyngis, Y haue demed these apeyryngis for Crist.
050	PHI	003	008	Netheles Y gesse alle thingis to be peirement for the cleer science of Jhesu Crist my Lord. For whom Y made alle thingis peyrement, and Y deme as drit,
050	PHI	003	009	that Y wynne Crist, and that Y be foundun in hym, not hauynge my riytwisnesse that is of the lawe, but that that is of the feith of Crist Jhesu, that is of God the riytwisnesse in feith,
050	PHI	003	010	to knowe hym, and the vertu of his risyng ayen, and the felouschipe of his passioun, and be maad lijk to his deeth,
050	PHI	003	011	if on ony maner Y come to the resurreccioun that is fro deth.
050	PHI	003	012	Not that now Y haue takun, or now am parfit; but Y sue, if in ony maner Y comprehende, in which thing also Y am comprehendid of Crist Jhesu.
050	PHI	003	013	Bretheren, Y deme me not that Y haue comprehendid; but o thing, Y foryete tho thingis that ben bihyndis, and stretche forth my silf to tho thingis that ben bifore,
050	PHI	003	014	and pursue to the ordeyned mede of the hiy clepyng of God in Crist Jhesu.
050	PHI	003	015	Therfor who euere we ben perfit, feele we this thing. And if ye vndurstonden in othere manere ony thing, this thing God schal schewe to you.
050	PHI	003	016	Netheles to what thing we han comun, that we vndurstonden the same thing, and that we perfitli dwelle in the same reule.
050	PHI	003	017	Britheren, be ye my foleweris, and weyte ye hem that walken so, as ye han oure fourme.
050	PHI	003	018	For many walken, whiche Y haue seid ofte to you, but now Y wepinge seie, the enemyes of Cristis cros,
050	PHI	003	019	who ende is deth, whos god is the wombe, and the glorie in confusioun of hem, that saueren ertheli thingis.
050	PHI	003	020	But oure lyuyng is in heuenes; fro whennus also we abiden the sauyour oure Lord Jhesu Crist,
050	PHI	003	021	which schal reforme the bodi of oure mekenesse, that is maad lijk to the bodi of his clerenesse, bi the worching bi which he mai `also make alle thingis suget to hym.
050	PHI	004	001	Therfor, my britheren most dereworthe and most desirid, my ioye and my coroun, so stonde ye in the Lord, most dere britheren.
050	PHI	004	002	Y preye Eucodiam, and biseche Synticem, to vndurstonde the same thing in the Lord.
050	PHI	004	003	Also Y preye and thee, german felow, helpe thou the ilke wymmen that traueliden with me in the gospel, with Clement and othere myn helperis, whos names ben in the book of lijf.
050	PHI	004	004	Ioye ye in the Lord euere more; eft Y seie, ioye ye.
050	PHI	004	005	Be youre pacyence knowun to alle men; the Lord is niy.
050	PHI	004	006	Be ye nothing bisi, but in al preyer and biseching, with doyng of thankyngis, be youre axyngis knowun at God.
050	PHI	004	007	And the pees of God, that passith al wit, kepe youre hertis and vndurstondingis in Crist Jhesu.
050	PHI	004	008	Fro hennus forth, britheren, what euere thingis ben sothe, what euere thingis chast, what euere thingis iust, what euere thingis hooli, what euere thingis able to be louyd, what euere thingis of good fame, if ony vertu, if ony preising of discipline, thenke ye these thingis,
050	PHI	004	009	that also ye han lerud, and take, and heed, and seyn in me. Do ye these thingis, and God of pees schal be with you.
050	PHI	004	010	But Y ioyede greetli in the Lord, that sum tyme aftirward ye floureden ayen to feele for me, as also ye feeliden. But ye weren ocupied, Y seie not as for nede,
050	PHI	004	011	for Y haue lerud to be sufficient in whiche thingis Y am.
050	PHI	004	012	And Y can also be lowid, Y can also haue plentee. Euery where and in alle thingis Y am tauyt to be fillid, and to hungur, and to abounde, and to suffre myseiste.
050	PHI	004	013	Y may alle thingis in hym that coumfortith me.
050	PHI	004	014	Netheles ye han doon wel, comynynge to my tribulacioun.
050	PHI	004	015	For and ye, Filipensis, witen, that in the bigynnyng of the gospel, whanne Y wente forth fro Macedonye, no chirche comynede with me in resoun of thing youun and takun, but ye aloone.
050	PHI	004	016	Whiche senten to Tessalonyk onys and twies also in to vss to me.
050	PHI	004	017	Not for Y seke yifte, but Y requyre fruyt aboundinge in youre resoun.
050	PHI	004	018	For Y haue alle thingis, and abounde; Y am fillid with tho thingis takun of Epafrodite, whiche ye senten in to the odour of swetnesse, a couenable sacrifice, plesynge to God.
050	PHI	004	019	And my God fil alle youre desire, by hise richessis in glorie in Crist Jhesu.
050	PHI	004	020	But to God and oure fadir be glorie in to worldis of worldis.
050	PHI	004	021	Amen. Grete ye wel euery hooli man in Crist Jhesu.
050	PHI	004	022	Tho britheren that ben with me, greten you wel. Alle hooli men greten you wel, moost sotheli thei that ben of the emperouris hous.
050	PHI	004	023	The grace of oure Lord Jhesu Crist be with youre spirit. Amen.
