# BOOK	053	2TH	2 Thessalonians	2 Thessalonians
053	2TH	001	001	Poul, and Siluan, and Tymothe, to the chirche of Tessalonicensis, in God oure fadir,
053	2TH	001	002	and in the Lord Jhesu Crist, grace to you and pees of God, oure fadir, and of the Lord Jhesu Crist.
053	2TH	001	003	We owen to do thankyngis eueremore to God for you, britheren, so as it is worthi, for youre feith ouer wexith, and the charite of ech of you to othere aboundith.
053	2TH	001	004	So that we silf glorien in you in the chirchis of God, for youre pacience and feith in alle youre persecuciouns and tribulaciouns.
053	2TH	001	005	Whiche ye susteynen in to the ensaumple of the iust dom of God, that ye be had worthi in the kingdom of God, for which ye suffren.
053	2TH	001	006	If netheles it is iust tofor God to quite tribulacioun to hem that troblen you,
053	2TH	001	007	and to you that ben troblid, rest with vs in the schewing of the Lord Jhesu fro heuene, with aungelis of his vertu,
053	2TH	001	008	in the flawme of fier, that schal yyue veniaunce to hem that knowen not God, and that obeien not to the euangelie of oure Lord Jhesu Crist.
053	2TH	001	009	Whiche schulen suffre euere lastinge peynes, in perischinge fro the face of the Lord, and fro the glorie of his vertu,
053	2TH	001	010	whanne he schal come to be glorified in hise seyntis, and to be maad wondurful in alle men that bileueden, for oure witnessing is bileuyd on you, in that dai.
053	2TH	001	011	In which thing also we preien euere more for you, that oure God make you worthi to his cleping, and fille al the wille of his goodnesse, and the werk of feith in vertu;
053	2TH	001	012	that the name of oure Lord Jhesu Crist be clarified in you, and ye in hym, bi the grace of oure Lord Jhesu Crist.
053	2TH	002	001	But, britheren, we preien you bi the comyng of oure Lord Jhesu Crist, and of oure congregacioun in to the same comyng,
053	2TH	002	002	that ye be not mouyd soone fro youre witt, nether be aferd, nether bi spirit, nether bi word, nether bi epistle as sent bi vs, as if the dai of the Lord be nyy.
053	2TH	002	003	No man disseyue you in ony manere. For but dissencioun come first, and the man of synne be schewid, the sonne of perdicioun,
053	2TH	002	004	that is aduersarie, and is enhaunsid ouer `al thing that is seid God, or that is worschipid, so that he sitte in the temple of God, and schewe hym silf as if he were God.
053	2TH	002	005	Whether ye holden not, that yit whanne Y was at you, Y seide these thingis to you?
053	2TH	002	006	And now what withholdith, ye witen, that he be schewid in his tyme.
053	2TH	002	007	For the priuete of wickidnesse worchith now; oneli that he that holdith now, holde, til he be do awei.
053	2TH	002	008	And thanne thilke wickid man schal be schewid, whom the Lord Jhesu schal sle with the spirit of his mouth, and schal distrie with liytnyng of his comyng;
053	2TH	002	009	hym, whos comyng is bi the worching of Sathanas, in al vertu, and signes,
053	2TH	002	010	and grete wondris, false, and in al disseit of wickidnesse, to hem that perischen. For that thei resseyueden not the charite of treuthe, that thei schulden be maad saaf.
053	2TH	002	011	And therfor God schal sende to hem a worching of errour, that thei bileue to leesing,
053	2TH	002	012	that alle be demed, whiche bileueden not to treuthe, but consentiden to wickidnesse.
053	2TH	002	013	But, britheren louyd of God, we owen to do thankyngis euermore to God for you, that God chees vs the firste fruytis in to heelthe, in halewing of spirit and in feith of treuthe;
053	2TH	002	014	in which also he clepide you bi oure gospel, in to geting of the glorie of oure Lord Jhesu Crist.
053	2TH	002	015	Therfor, britheren, stonde ye, and holde ye the tradiciouns, that ye han lerud, ethir bi word, ethir bi oure pistle.
053	2TH	002	016	And oure Lord Jhesu Crist him silf, and God oure fadir, which louyde vs, and yaf euerlastinge coumfort and good hope in grace,
053	2TH	002	017	stire youre hertis, and conferme in al good werk and word.
053	2TH	003	001	Britheren, fro hennus forward preye ye for vs, that the word of God renne, and be clarified, as it is anentis you;
053	2TH	003	002	and that we be delyuered fro noyous and yuele men; for feith is not of alle men.
053	2TH	003	003	But the Lord is trewe, that schal conferme you, and schal kepe fro yuel.
053	2TH	003	004	And, britheren, we trusten of you in the Lord, for what euere thingis we comaunden to you, bothe ye don and schulen do.
053	2TH	003	005	And the Lord dresse youre hertis, in the charite of God, and in the pacience of Crist.
053	2TH	003	006	But, britheren, we denouncen to you in the name of oure Lord Jhesu Crist, that ye withdrawe you from ech brother that wandrith out of ordre, and not aftir the techyng, that thei resseyueden of vs.
053	2TH	003	007	For `ye silf witen, hou it bihoueth to sue vs. For we weren not vnpesible among you,
053	2TH	003	008	nethir with outen oure owne trauel we eeten breed of ony man, but in trauel and werynesse worchiden niyt and dai, that we greuyden noon of you.
053	2TH	003	009	Not as we hadden not power, but that we schulden yyue vs silf ensaumple to you to sue vs.
053	2TH	003	010	For also whanne we weren among you, we denounsiden this thing to you, that if ony man wole not worche, nethir ete he.
053	2TH	003	011	For we han herd that summe among you goon in reste, and no thing worchen, but don curiousli.
053	2TH	003	012	But we denouncen to hem that ben suche men, and bisechen in the Lord Jhesu Crist, that thei worchen with silence, and ete her owne breed.
053	2TH	003	013	But nyle ye, britheren, faile wel doynge.
053	2TH	003	014	That if ony man obeie not to oure word bi epistle, marke ye him, and comyne ye not with hym, that he be schamed;
053	2TH	003	015	and nyle ye gesse hym as an enemye, but repreue ye hym as a brother. And God hym silf of pees yyue to you euerlastinge pees in al place.
053	2TH	003	016	The Lord be with `you alle.
053	2TH	003	017	My salutacioun bi the hoond of Poul; which signe in ech epistle Y write thus.
053	2TH	003	018	The grace of oure Lord Jhesu Crist be with `alle you. Amen.
