# BOOK	055	2TI	2 Timothy	2 Timothy
055	2TI	001	001	Poul, apostle of Jhesu Crist, bi the wille of God, bi the biheest of lijf that is in Crist Jhesu,
055	2TI	001	002	to Tymothe, his moost dereworthe sone, grace, merci, and pees of God the fadir, and of Jhesu Crist, oure Lord.
055	2TI	001	003	I do thankyngis to my God, to whom Y serue fro my progenytouris in clene conscience, that with outen ceessyng Y haue mynde of thee in my preyeris,
055	2TI	001	004	niyt and dai, desirynge to se thee; hauynge mynde of thi teeris, that Y be fillid with ioye.
055	2TI	001	005	And Y bithenke of that feith, that is in thee not feyned, which also dwellide firste in thin aunte Loide, and in thi modir Eunyce. And Y am certeyn, that also in thee.
055	2TI	001	006	For which cause Y moneste thee, that thou reise ayen the grace of God, that is in thee bi the settyng on of myn hondis.
055	2TI	001	007	For whi God yaf not to vs the spirit of drede, but of vertu, and of loue, and of sobrenesse.
055	2TI	001	008	Therfor nyl thou schame the witnessyng of oure Lord Jhesu Crist, nether me, his prisoner; but trauele thou togidere in the gospel bi the vertu of God;
055	2TI	001	009	that delyueride vs, and clepide with his hooli clepyng, not after oure werkis, but bi his purpos and grace, that is youun in Crist Jhesu bifore worldli tymes;
055	2TI	001	010	but now it is opyn bi the liytnyng of oure sauyour Jhesu Crist, which destriede deth, and liytnede lijf and vncorrupcioun bi the gospel.
055	2TI	001	011	In which Y am set a prechour and apostle, and maistir of hethene men.
055	2TI	001	012	For which cause also Y suffre these thingis; but Y am not confoundid. For Y woot to whom Y haue bileuyd, and Y am certeyne that he is miyti for to kepe that is take to my keping in to that dai.
055	2TI	001	013	Haue thou the fourme of hoolsum wordis, whiche thou herdist of me in feith and loue in Crist Jhesu.
055	2TI	001	014	Kepe thou the good takun to thi kepyng bi the Hooli Goost, that dwellith in vs.
055	2TI	001	015	Thou wost this, that alle that ben in Asie ben turnyd awey fro me, of whiche is Figelus and Ermogenes.
055	2TI	001	016	The Lord yyue merci to the hous of Onesyforus, for ofte he refreischide me, and schamyde not my chayne.
055	2TI	001	017	But whanne he cam to Rome, he souyte me bisili, and foond.
055	2TI	001	018	The Lord yyue to hym to fynde merci of God in that dai. And hou grete thingis he mynystride to me at Effesi, thou knowist betere.
055	2TI	002	001	Therfor thou, my sone, be coumfortid in grace that is in Crist Jhesu.
055	2TI	002	002	And what thingis thou hast herd of me bi many witnessis, bitake thou these to feithful men, whiche schulen `be also able to teche othere men.
055	2TI	002	003	Trauele thou as a good knyyt of Crist Jhesu.
055	2TI	002	004	No man holdinge knyythod to God, wlappith hym silf with worldli nedis, that he plese to hym, to whom he hath preuyd hym silf.
055	2TI	002	005	For he that fiytith in a batel, schal not be corowned, but he fiyte lawfuli.
055	2TI	002	006	It bihoueth an erthetiliere to resseyue first of the fruytis.
055	2TI	002	007	Vndurstonde thou what thingis Y seie. For the Lord schal yyue to thee vndurstonding in alle thingis.
055	2TI	002	008	Be thou myndeful that the Lord Jhesu Crist of the seed of Dauid hath rise ayen fro deth,
055	2TI	002	009	aftir my gospel, in which Y trauele `til to boondis, as worching yuele, but the word of God is not boundun.
055	2TI	002	010	Therfor Y suffre alle thingis for the chosun, that also thei gete the heelthe, that is in Crist Jhesu, with heuenli glorie.
055	2TI	002	011	A trewe word, that if we ben deed togidere, also we schulen liue togidere;
055	2TI	002	012	if we suffren, we schulen regne togidere; if we denyen, he schal denye vs;
055	2TI	002	013	if we bileuen not, he dwellith feithful, he mai not denye hym silf.
055	2TI	002	014	Teche thou these thingis, witnessinge bifore God. Nyle thou stryue in wordis; for to no thing it is profitable, but to the subuerting of men that heren.
055	2TI	002	015	Bisili kepe to yyue thi silf a preued preisable werkman to God, with oute schame, riytli tretinge the word of treuthe.
055	2TI	002	016	But eschewe thou vnhooli and veyn spechis, for whi tho profiten myche to vnfeithfulnesse,
055	2TI	002	017	and the word of hem crepith as a canker. Of whiche Filete is, and Ymeneus,
055	2TI	002	018	whiche felden doun fro the treuthe, seiynge that the rising ayen is now doon, and thei subuertiden the feith of summen.
055	2TI	002	019	But the sad foundement of God stondith, hauynge this marke, The Lord knowith whiche ben hise, and, Ech man that nameth the name of the Lord, departith fro wickidnesse.
055	2TI	002	020	But in a greet hous ben not oneli vessels of gold and of siluer, but also of tree and of erthe; and so summen ben in to onour, and summe in to dispit.
055	2TI	002	021	Therfor if ony man clensith hym silf fro these, he schal be a vessel halewid in to onour, and profitable to the Lord, redi to al good werk.
055	2TI	002	022	And fle thou desiris of yongthe, but sue thou riytwisnesse, feith, charite, pees, with hem that inwardli clepen the Lord of a clene herte.
055	2TI	002	023	And eschewe thou foltische questiouns, and without kunnyng, wytynge that tho gendren chidyngis.
055	2TI	002	024	But it bihoueth the seruaunt of the Lord to chide not; but to be mylde to alle men, able to teche,
055	2TI	002	025	paciente, with temperaunce repreuynge hem that ayenstonden the treuthe, that sum tyme God yyue to hem forthenkyng, that thei knowen the treuthe,
055	2TI	002	026	and that thei rise ayen fro the snares of the deuel, of whom thei ben holdun prisoneris at his wille.
055	2TI	003	001	But wite thou this thing, that in the laste daies perelouse tymes schulen neiye, and men schulen be louynge hem silf,
055	2TI	003	002	coueitouse, hiy of bering, proude, blasfemeris, not obedient to fadir and modir, vnkynde,
055	2TI	003	003	cursid, with outen affeccioun, with out pees, false blameris, vncontynent, vnmylde,
055	2TI	003	004	with out benygnyte, traitouris, ouerthwert, bollun with proude thouytis, blynde, loueris of lustis more than of God,
055	2TI	003	005	hauynge the licknesse of pitee, but denyynge the vertu of it. And eschewe thou these men.
055	2TI	003	006	Of these thei ben that persen housis, and leden wymmen caitifs chargid with synnes, whiche ben led with dyuerse desiris, euere more lernynge,
055	2TI	003	007	and neuere perfitli comynge to the science of treuthe.
055	2TI	003	008	And as Jannes and Mambres ayenstoden Moises, so these ayenstonden treuthe, men corrupt in vndirstonding, repreuyd aboute the feith.
055	2TI	003	009	But ferthere thei schulen not profite, for the vnwisdom of hem schal be knowun to alle men, as hern was.
055	2TI	003	010	But thou hast getun my teching, ordinaunce, purposing, feith, long abiding, loue,
055	2TI	003	011	pacience, persecuciouns, passiouns, whiche weren maad to me at Antioche, at Ycony, at Listris, what maner persecucyouns Y suffride, and the Lord hath delyuered me of alle.
055	2TI	003	012	And alle men that wolen lyue feithfuli in Crist Jhesu, schulen suffre persecucioun.
055	2TI	003	013	But yuele men and disseyueris schulen encreese in to worse, errynge, and sendinge in to errour.
055	2TI	003	014	But dwelle thou in these thingis that thou hast lerud, and that ben bitakun to thee, witinge of whom thou hast lerud;
055	2TI	003	015	for thou hast knowun hooli lettris fro thi youthe, whiche moun lerne thee to heelthe, bi feith that is in Crist Jhesu.
055	2TI	003	016	For al scripture inspirid of God is profitable to teche, to repreue, to chastice, to lerne in riytwisnes,
055	2TI	003	017	that the man of God be parfit, lerud to al good werk.
055	2TI	004	001	I witnesse bifore God and Crist Jhesu, that schal deme the quike and the deed, and bi the comyng of hym, and the kyngdom of hym,
055	2TI	004	002	preche the word, be thou bisi couenabli with outen rest, repreue thou, biseche thou, blame thou in al pacience and doctryn.
055	2TI	004	003	For tyme schal be, whanne men schulen not suffre hoolsum teching, but at her desiris thei schulen gadere `togidere to hem silf maistris yitchinge to the eeris.
055	2TI	004	004	And treuli thei schulen turne awei the heryng fro treuthe, but to fablis thei schulen turne.
055	2TI	004	005	But wake thou, in alle thingis traueile thou, do the werk of an euangelist, fulfille thi seruyce, be thou sobre.
055	2TI	004	006	For Y am sacrifisid now, and the tyme of my departyng is nyy.
055	2TI	004	007	Y haue stryuun a good strijf, Y haue endid the cours, Y haue kept the feith.
055	2TI	004	008	In `the tothir tyme a coroun of riytwisnesse is kept to me, which the Lord, a iust domesman, schal yelde to me in that dai; and not oneli to me, but also to these that louen his comyng.
055	2TI	004	009	Hyye thou to come to me soone.
055	2TI	004	010	For Demas, louynge this world, hath forsakun me, and wente to Tessalonyk, Crescens in to Galathi, Tite in to Dalmacie;
055	2TI	004	011	Luk aloone is with me. Take thou Mark, and brynge with thee; for he is profitable to me in to seruyce.
055	2TI	004	012	Forsothe Y sente Titicus to Effesi.
055	2TI	004	013	The cloth which Y lefte at Troade at Carpe, whanne thou comest, bringe with thee, and the bookis, but moost parchemyne.
055	2TI	004	014	Alisaundre, the tresorer, schewide to me myche yuele; `the Lord schal yelde to hym aftir his werkis.
055	2TI	004	015	Whom also thou eschewe; for he ayenstood ful greetli oure wordis.
055	2TI	004	016	In my firste defence no man helpide me, but alle forsoken me; be it not arettid to hem.
055	2TI	004	017	But the Lord helpide me, and coumfortide me, that the preching be fillid bi me, and that alle folkis here, that Y am delyueride fro the mouth of the lioun.
055	2TI	004	018	And the Lord delyueride me fro al yuel werk, and schal make me saaf in to his heuenly kingdom, to whom be glorie in to worldis of worldis.
055	2TI	004	019	Amen. Grete wel Prisca, and Aquila, and the hous of Oneseforus.
055	2TI	004	020	Erastus lefte at Corynthi, and Y lefte Trofymus sijk at Mylete.
055	2TI	004	021	Hiye thou to come bifore wyntir. Eubolus, and Prudent, and Lynus, and Claudia, and alle britheren, greten thee wel.
055	2TI	004	022	Oure Lord Jhesu Crist be with thi spirit. The grace of God be with you. Amen.
