# BOOK	056	TIT	Titus	Titus
056	TIT	001	001	Poul, the seruaunt of God, and apostle of Jhesu Crist, bi the feith of the chosun of God, and bi the knowing of the treuthe, whiche is aftir pitee,
056	TIT	001	002	in to the hope of euerlastinge lijf, which lijf God that lieth not, bihiyte bifore tymes of the world;
056	TIT	001	003	but he hath schewid in hise tymes his word in preching, that is bitakun to me bi the comaundement of `God oure sauyour,
056	TIT	001	004	to Tite, most dereworthe sone bi the comyn feith, grace and pees of God the fadir, and of Crist Jhesu, oure sauyour.
056	TIT	001	005	For cause of this thing Y lefte thee at Crete, that thou amende tho thingis that failen, and ordeyne preestis bi citees, as also Y disposide to thee.
056	TIT	001	006	If ony man is withoute cryme, an hosebonde of o wijf, and hath feithful sones, not in accusacioun of letcherie, or not suget.
056	TIT	001	007	For it bihoueth a bischop to be without cryme, a dispendour of God, not proud, not wrathful, not drunkelew, not smytere, not coueytouse of foul wynnyng;
056	TIT	001	008	but holdinge hospitalite, benygne, prudent, sobre, iust,
056	TIT	001	009	hooli, contynent, takinge that trewe word, that is aftir doctryn; that he be miyti to amoneste in hoolsum techyng, and to repreue hem that ayenseien.
056	TIT	001	010	For ther ben many vnobedient, and veyn spekeris, and disseyueris, moost thei that ben of circumcisyoun,
056	TIT	001	011	whiche it bihoueth to be repreued; whiche subuerten alle housis, techinge whiche thingis it bihoueth not, for the loue of foul wynnyng.
056	TIT	001	012	And oon of hem, her propre profete, seide, Men of Crete ben euere more lyeris, yuele beestis, of slowe wombe.
056	TIT	001	013	This witnessyng is trewe. For what cause blame hem sore, that thei be hool in feith,
056	TIT	001	014	not yyuynge tent to fablis of Jewis, and to maundementis of men, that turnen awei hem fro treuthe.
056	TIT	001	015	And alle thingis ben clene to clene men; but to vnclene men and to vnfeithful no thing is clene, for the soule and conscience of hem ben maad vnclene.
056	TIT	001	016	Thei knoulechen that thei knowen God, but bi dedis thei denyen; whanne thei ben abhominable, and vnbileueful, and repreuable to al good werk.
056	TIT	002	001	But speke thou tho thingis that bisemen hoolsum teching;
056	TIT	002	002	that elde men be sobre, chast, prudent, hool in feith, in loue, and pacience;
056	TIT	002	003	also olde wymmen in hooli abite, not sclaundereris, not seruynge myche to wyn, wel techynge, that thei teche prudence.
056	TIT	002	004	Moneste thou yonge wymmen, that thei loue here hosebondis, that thei loue her children;
056	TIT	002	005	and that thei be prudent, chast, sobre, hauynge cure of the hous, benygne, suget to her hosebondis, that the word of God be not blasfemyd.
056	TIT	002	006	Also moneste thou yonge men, that thei be sobre.
056	TIT	002	007	In alle thingis yyue thi silf ensaumple of good werkis, in teching, in hoolnesse, in sadnesse.
056	TIT	002	008	An hoolsum word, and vnrepreuable; that he that is of the contrarie side, be aschamed, hauynge noon yuel thing to seie of you.
056	TIT	002	009	Moneste thou seruauntis to be suget to her lordis; in alle thingis plesinge, not ayenseiynge, not defraudynge,
056	TIT	002	010	but in alle thingis schewinge good feith, that thei onoure in alle thingis the doctryn of `God, oure sauyour.
056	TIT	002	011	For the grace of `God, oure sauyour, hath apperid to alle men,
056	TIT	002	012	and tauyte vs, that we forsake wickidnesse, and worldli desyris, lyue sobreli, and iustli, `and piteuousli in this world,
056	TIT	002	013	abidinge the blessid hope and the comyng of the glorie of the greet God, and of oure sauyour Jhesu Crist;
056	TIT	002	014	that yaf hym silf for vs, to ayenbie vs fro al wickidnesse, and make clene to hym silf a puple acceptable, and suere of good werkis.
056	TIT	002	015	Speke thou these thingis, and moneste thou, and repreue thou with al comaundement; no man dispise thee.
056	TIT	003	001	Amoneste hem to be sugetis to prynces, and to poweris; to obeische to that that is seid, and to be redi to al good werk;
056	TIT	003	002	to blasfeme no man, to be not ful of chiding, but temperat, schewynge al myldenesse to alle men.
056	TIT	003	003	For we weren sum tyme vnwise, vnbileueful, errynge, and seruynge to desiris, and to dyuerse lustis, doynge in malice and enuye, worthi to be hatid, hatinge ech othere.
056	TIT	003	004	But whanne the benygnyte and the manhed of oure sauyour God aperide,
056	TIT	003	005	not of werkis of riytwisnesse that we diden, but bi his merci he made vs saaf, bi waischyng of ayen bigetyng, and ayen newyng of the Hooli Goost,
056	TIT	003	006	whom he schedde into vs plenteuousli bi Jhesu Crist, oure saueour,
056	TIT	003	007	that we iustified bi his grace, ben eiris by hope of euerlastinge lijf.
056	TIT	003	008	A trewe word is, and of these thingis Y wole that thou conferme othere, that thei that bileuen to God, be bisy to be aboue othere in good werkis. These thingis ben good, and profitable to men.
056	TIT	003	009	And eschewe thou foltische questiouns, and genologies, and stryues, and fiytyngis of the lawe; for tho ben vnprofitable and veyn.
056	TIT	003	010	Eschewe thou a man eretik, aftir oon and the secound correccioun;
056	TIT	003	011	witinge that he that is siche a maner man is subuertid, and trespassith, and is dampned bi his owne dom.
056	TIT	003	012	Whanne Y sende to thee Arteman, or Titicus, hiy thou to `come to me to Nycopolis; for Y haue purposid to dwelle in wyntir there.
056	TIT	003	013	Bisili byfor sende Zenam, a wise man of lawe, and Apollo, that no thing faile to hem.
056	TIT	003	014	Thei that ben of ouris, lerne to be gouernouris in good werkis, to necessarie vsis, that thei be not with out fruyt.
056	TIT	003	015	Alle men that ben with me greeten thee wel. Grete thou wel hem, that louen vs in feith. The grace of God be with you alle. Amen.
