# BOOK	057	PHM	Philemon	Philemon
057	PHM	001	001	Poul, the boundun of Crist Jhesu, and Timothe, brother, to Filemon, bilouyd, and oure helpere, and to Appia,
057	PHM	001	002	most dere sister, and to Archip, oure euene kniyt, and to the chirche that is in thin hous,
057	PHM	001	003	grace be to you, and pees of God oure fader, and of the Lord Jhesu Crist.
057	PHM	001	004	I do thankingis to my God, euere more makinge mynde of thee in my preieris,
057	PHM	001	005	heringe thi charite and feith, that thou hast in the Lord Jhesu, and to alle hooli men,
057	PHM	001	006	that the comynyng of thi feith be maad opyn, in knowing of al good thing in Crist Jhesu.
057	PHM	001	007	And Y hadde greet ioye and coumfort in thi charite, for the entrailis of hooli men restiden bi thee, brother.
057	PHM	001	008	For which thing Y hauynge myche trist in Crist Jhesu, to comaunde to thee that that perteyneth to profit;
057	PHM	001	009	but Y biseche more for charite, sithen thou art siche as the elde Poul, and now the boundun of Jhesu Crist.
057	PHM	001	010	Y biseche thee for my sone Onesyme, whom Y in boondis bigat,
057	PHM	001	011	which sumtyme was vnprofitable to thee, but now profitable bothe to thee and to me; whom Y sente ayen to thee.
057	PHM	001	012	And resseyue thou hym as myn entrailis;
057	PHM	001	013	whom Y wolde withholde with me, that he schulde serue for thee to me in boondis of the gospel;
057	PHM	001	014	but with out thi counseil Y wolde not do ony thing, that thi good schulde not be as of nede, but wilful.
057	PHM	001	015	For perauenture therfor he departide fro thee for a tyme, that thou schuldist resseyue hym with outen ende;
057	PHM	001	016	now not as a seruaunt, but for a seruaunt a most dere brother, most to me; and how myche more to thee, bothe in fleisch and in the Lord?
057	PHM	001	017	Therfor if thou hast me a felowe, resseyue hym as me; for if he hath ony thing anoied thee,
057	PHM	001	018	ethir owith, arette thou this thing to me.
057	PHM	001	019	Y Poul wroot with myn hoond, Y schal yelde; that Y seie not to thee, that also thou owist to me thi silf.
057	PHM	001	020	So, brothir, Y schal vse thee in the Lord; fille thou myn entrails in Crist.
057	PHM	001	021	Y tristnynge of thin obedience wroot to thee, witynge that thou schalt do ouer that that Y seie.
057	PHM	001	022	Also make thou redi to me an hous to dwelle in; for Y hope that bi youre preyeris Y schal be youun to you.
057	PHM	001	023	Epafras, prisoner with me in Crist Jhesu,
057	PHM	001	024	greetith thee wel, and Mark, Aristark, Demas, Lucas, myn helperis.
057	PHM	001	025	The grace of oure Lord Jhesu Crist be with youre spirit. Amen.
