# BOOK	058	HEB	Hebrews	Hebrews
058	HEB	001	001	God, that spak sum tyme bi prophetis in many maneres to oure fadris, at the
058	HEB	001	002	laste in these daies he hath spoke to vs bi the sone; whom he hath ordeyned eir of alle thingis, and bi whom he made the worldis.
058	HEB	001	003	Which whanne also he is the briytnesse of glorie, and figure of his substaunce, and berith alle thingis bi word of his vertu, he makith purgacioun of synnes, and syttith on the riythalf of the maieste in heuenes;
058	HEB	001	004	and so myche is maad betere than aungels, bi hou myche he hath eneritid a more dyuerse name bifor hem.
058	HEB	001	005	For to whiche of the aungels seide God ony tyme, Thou art my sone, Y haue gendrid thee to dai? And eftsoone, Y schal be to hym in to a fadir, and he schal be to me in to a sone?
058	HEB	001	006	And whanne eftsoone he bryngith in the firste bigetun sone in to the world, he seith, And alle the aungels of God worschipe hym.
058	HEB	001	007	But he seith to aungels, He that makith hise aungels spiritis, and hise mynystris flawme of fier.
058	HEB	001	008	But to the sone he seith, God, thi trone is in to the world of world; a yerde of equite is the yerde of thi rewme;
058	HEB	001	009	thou hast louyd riytwisnesse, and hatidist wickidnesse; therfor the God, thi God, anoyntide thee with oile of ioye, more than thi felowis.
058	HEB	001	010	And, Thou, Lord, in the bigynnyng foundidist the erthe, and heuenes ben werkis of thin hondis; thei schulen perische,
058	HEB	001	011	but thou schalt perfitli dwelle; and alle schulen wexe elde as a cloth, and thou schalt chaunge hem as a cloth,
058	HEB	001	012	and thei schulen be chaungid. But thou art the same thi silf, and thi yeeris schulen not faile.
058	HEB	001	013	But to whiche of the aungels seide God at ony tyme, Sitte thou on my riythalf, till Y putte thin enemyes a stool of thi feet?
058	HEB	001	014	Whether thei alle ben not seruynge spiritis, sente to seruen for hem that taken the eritage of heelthe?
058	HEB	002	001	Therfor more plenteuousli it bihoueth vs to kepe tho thingis, that we han herd, lest perauenture we fleten awei.
058	HEB	002	002	For if the ilke word that was seid bi aungels, was maad sad, and ech brekyng of the lawe and vnobedience took iust retribucioun of meede,
058	HEB	002	003	hou schulen we ascape, if we despisen so greet an heelthe? Which, whanne it hadde takun bigynnyng to be teld out by the Lord, of hem that herden is confermyd in to vs.
058	HEB	002	004	For God witnesside to gidere bi myraclis, and wondris, and grete merueilis, and dyuerse vertues, and departyngis of the Hooli Goost, bi his wille.
058	HEB	002	005	But not to aungels God sugetide the world that is to comynge, of which we speken.
058	HEB	002	006	But sum man witnesside in a place, and seide, What thing is man, that thou art myndeful of hym, or mannus sone, for thou visitist hym?
058	HEB	002	007	Thou hast maad hym a litil lesse than aungels; thou hast corowned hym with glorie and onour; and thou hast ordeyned him on the werkis of thin hondis.
058	HEB	002	008	Thou hast maad alle thingis suget vndur hise feet. And in that that he sugetide alle thingis to hym, he lefte no thing vnsuget to him. But now we seen not yit alle thingis suget to hym;
058	HEB	002	009	but we seen hym that was maad a litil lesse than aungels, Jhesu, for the passioun of deth crowned with glorie and onour, that he thorouy grace of God schulde taste deth for alle men.
058	HEB	002	010	For it bisemede hym, for whom alle thingis, and bi whom `alle thingis weren maad, which hadde brouyt many sones into glorie, and was auctour of the heelthe of hem, that he hadde an ende bi passioun.
058	HEB	002	011	For he that halewith, and thei that ben halewid, ben alle of oon; for which cause he is not schamed to clepe hem britheren,
058	HEB	002	012	seiynge, Y schal telle thi name to my britheren; in the myddil of the chirche Y schal herie thee.
058	HEB	002	013	And eftsoone, Y schal be tristnynge in to hym; and eftsoone, Lo! Y and my children, whiche God yaf to me.
058	HEB	002	014	Therfor for children comyneden to fleisch and blood, and he also took part of the same, that bi deth he schulde destrie hym that hadde lordschipe of deth, that is to seie, the deuel,
058	HEB	002	015	and that he schulde delyuere hem that bi drede of deth, `bi al lijf weren boundun to seruage.
058	HEB	002	016	And he took neuere aungelis, but he took the seed of Abraham.
058	HEB	002	017	Wherfor he ouyte to be likned to britheren bi alle thingis, that he schulde be maad merciful and a feithful bischop to God, that he schulde be merciful to the trespassis of the puple.
058	HEB	002	018	For in that thing in which he suffride, and was temptid, he is miyti to helpe also hem that ben temptid.
058	HEB	003	001	Therfor, hooli britheren, and parceneris of heuenli cleping, biholde ye the apostle and the bischop of oure confessioun, Jhesu,
058	HEB	003	002	which is trewe to hym that made hym, as also Moises in al the hous of hym.
058	HEB	003	003	But this byschop is had worthi of more glorie than Moises, bi as myche as he hath more honour of the hous, that made the hous.
058	HEB	003	004	For ech hous is maad of sum man; he that made alle thingis of nouyt is God.
058	HEB	003	005	And Moises was trewe in al his hous, as a seruaunt, in to witnessyng of tho thingis that weren to be seid;
058	HEB	003	006	but Crist as a sone in his hous. Which hous we ben, if we holden sad trist and glorie of hope in to the ende.
058	HEB	003	007	Wherfor as the Hooli Goost seith, To dai, if ye han herd his vois, nyle ye hardne youre hertis,
058	HEB	003	008	as in wraththing, lijk the dai of temptacioun in desert;
058	HEB	003	009	where youre fadris temptiden me, and preueden, and siyen my werkis fourti yeeris.
058	HEB	003	010	Wherfor Y was wrooth to this generacioun, and Y seide, Euere more thei erren in herte, for thei knewen not my weies;
058	HEB	003	011	to whiche Y swore in my wraththe, thei schulen not entre in to my reste.
058	HEB	003	012	Britheren, se ye, lest perauenture in ony of you be an yuel herte of vnbileue, to departe fro the lyuynge God.
058	HEB	003	013	But moneste you silf bi alle daies, the while to dai is named, that noon of you be hardned bi fallas of synne.
058	HEB	003	014	For we ben maad parceneris of Crist, if netheles we holden the bigynnyng of his substaunce sad in to the ende.
