058	HEB	013	003	Thenke ye on boundun men, as ye weren togidere boundun, and of trauelinge men, as ye silf dwellinge in the body.
058	HEB	013	004	`Wedding is in alle thingis onourable, and bed vnwemmed; for God schal deme fornicatouris and auouteris.
058	HEB	013	005	Be youre maneres withoute coueitise, apaied with present thingis; for he seide, Y schal not leeue thee,
058	HEB	013	006	nether forsake, so that we seie tristily, The Lord is an helpere to me; Y schal not drede, what a man schal do to me.
058	HEB	013	007	Haue ye mynde of youre souereyns, that han spokun to you the word of God; of whiche `biholde ye the goyng out of lyuynge, and sue ye the feith of hem,
058	HEB	013	008	Jhesu Crist, yistirdai, and to dai, he is also into worldis.
058	HEB	013	009	Nyle ye be led awei with dyuerse `techingis, and straunge. For it is best to stable the herte with grace, not with metis, whiche profitiden not to men wandringe in hem.
058	HEB	013	010	We han an auter, of which thei that seruen to the tabernacle, han not power to ete.
058	HEB	013	011	For of whiche beestis the blood is borun in for synne in to hooli thingis bi the bischop, the bodies of hem ben brent with out the castels.
058	HEB	013	012	For which thing Jhesu, that he schulde halewe the puple bi his blood, suffride with out the gate.
058	HEB	013	013	Therfor go we out to hym with out the castels, berynge his repreef.
058	HEB	013	014	For we han not here a citee dwellynge, but we seken a citee to comynge.
058	HEB	013	015	Therfor bi hym offre we a sacrifice of heriyng euere more to God, that is to seye, the fruyt of lippis knoulechinge to his name.
058	HEB	013	016	And nyle ye foryete wel doynge, and comynyng; for bi siche sacrifices God is disserued.
058	HEB	013	017	Obeie ye to youre souereyns, and be ye suget to hem; for thei perfitli waken, as to yeldinge resoun for youre soulis, that thei do this thing with ioie, and not sorewinge; for this thing spedith not to you.
058	HEB	013	018	Preie ye for vs, and we tristen that we han good conscience in alle thingis, willynge to lyue wel.
058	HEB	013	019	More ouer Y biseche you to do, that Y be restorid the sunnere to you.
058	HEB	013	020	And God of pees, that ladde out fro deth the greet scheepherd of scheep, in the blood of euerlastinge testament, oure Lord Jhesu Crist,
058	HEB	013	021	schape you in al good thing, that ye do the wille of hym; and he do in you that thing that schal plese bifor hym, bi Jhesu Crist, to whom be glorie in to worldis of worldis. Amen.
058	HEB	013	022	And, britheren, Y preie you, that ye suffre a word of solace; for bi ful fewe thingis Y haue writun to you.
058	HEB	013	023	Knowe ye oure brother Tymothe, that is sent forth, with whom if he schal come more hastili, Y schal se you.
058	HEB	013	024	Grete ye wel alle youre souereyns, and alle hooli men. The britheren of Italie greten you wel.
058	HEB	013	025	The grace of God be with you alle. Amen.
