# BOOK	060	1PE	1 Peter	1 Peter
060	1PE	001	001	Petre, apostle of Jhesu Crist, to the chosun men, to the comelingis of scateryng abrood, of Ponte, of Galathie, of Capadosie,
060	1PE	001	002	of Asye, and of Bitynye, bi the `bifor knowyng of God, the fadir, in halewyng of spirit, bi obedience, and springyng of the blood of Jhesu Crist, grace and pees be multiplied to you.
060	1PE	001	003	Blessid be God, and the fadir of oure Lord Jhesu Crist, which bi his greet merci bigat vs ayen in to lyuynge hope, bi the ayen risyng of Jhesu Crist fro deth,
060	1PE	001	004	in to eritage vncorruptible, and vndefoulid, and that schal not fade, that is kept in heuenes for you,
060	1PE	001	005	that in the vertu of God ben kept bi the feith in to heelthe, and is redi to be schewid in the last tyme.
060	1PE	001	006	In which ye schulen make ioye, thouy it bihoueth now a litil to be sori in dyuerse temptaciouns;
060	1PE	001	007	that the preuyng of youre feith be myche more preciouse than gold, that is preuyd bi fier; and be foundun in to heriyng, and glorie, and onour, in the reuelacioun of Jhesu Crist.
060	1PE	001	008	Whom whanne ye han not seyn, ye louen; in to whom also now ye not seynge, bileuen; but ye that bileuen schulen haue ioye, and gladnesse that may not be teld out,
060	1PE	001	009	and ye schulen be glorified, and haue the ende of youre feith, the helthe of youre soulis.
060	1PE	001	010	Of which helthe profetis souyten, and enserchiden, that profecieden of the grace to comyng in you,
060	1PE	001	011	and souyten which euer what maner tyme the spirit of Crist signyfiede in hem, and bifor telde tho passiouns, that ben in Crist, and the latere glories.
060	1PE	001	012	To which it was schewid, for not to hem silf, but to you thei mynystriden tho thingis, that now ben teld to you bi hem that prechiden to you bi the Hooli Goost sent fro heuene, in to whom aungelis desiren to biholde.
060	1PE	001	013	For which thing be ye gird the leendis of youre soule, sobre, perfit, and hope ye in to the ilke grace that is profrid to you bi the schewyng of Jhesu Crist,
060	1PE	001	014	as sones of obedience, not made lijk to the formere desiris of youre vnkunnyngnesse,
060	1PE	001	015	but lijk him that hath `clepid you hooli; that also `ye silf be hooli in `al lyuyng;
060	1PE	001	016	for it is writun, Ye schulen be hooli, for Y am hooli.
060	1PE	001	017	And if ye inwardli clepe him fadir, which demeth withouten accepcioun of persoones bi the werk of ech man, lyue ye in drede in the time of youre pilgrimage; witynge that not bi corruptible gold,
060	1PE	001	018	ethir siluer, ye ben bouyt ayen of youre veyn liuynge of fadris tradicioun,
060	1PE	001	019	but bi the precious blood as of the lomb vndefoulid and vnspottid,
060	1PE	001	020	Crist Jhesu, that was knowun bifor the makyng of the world, but he is schewid in the laste tymes,
060	1PE	001	021	for you that bi hym ben feithful in God; that reiside hym fro deth, and yaf to hym euerlastynge glorie, that youre feith and hope were in God.
060	1PE	001	022	And make ye chast youre soulis in obedience of charite, in loue of britherhod; of simple herte loue ye togidre more bisili.
060	1PE	001	023	And be ye borun ayen, not of corruptible seed, `but vncorruptible, bi the word of lyuynge God, and dwellynge in to with outen ende.
060	1PE	001	024	For ech fleisch is hey, and al the glorie of it is as flour of hey; the hei driede vp, and his flour felde doun;
060	1PE	001	025	but the word of the Lord dwellith with outen ende. And this is the word, that is prechid to you.
060	1PE	002	001	Therfor putte ye awei al malice, and al gile, and feynyngis, and enuyes, and alle bacbityngis;
060	1PE	002	002	as now borun yonge children, resonable, with out gile, coueite ye mylk, that in it ye wexe in to helthe; if netheles ye han tastid,
060	1PE	002	003	that the Lord is swete.
060	1PE	002	004	And neiye ye to hym, that is a lyuyng stoon, and repreuyd of men, but chosun of God, and onourid;
060	1PE	002	005	and ye silf as quyk stoonys be ye aboue bildid in to spiritual housis, and an hooli preesthod, to offre spiritual sacrifices, acceptable to God bi Jhesu Crist.
060	1PE	002	006	For which thing the scripture seith, Lo! Y schal sette in Syon the hiyeste corner stoon, chosun and preciouse; and he that schal belieue in hym, schal not be confoundid.
060	1PE	002	007	Therfor onour to you that bileuen; but to men that bileuen not, the stoon whom the bilderis repreuyden, this is maad in to the heed of the corner; and the stoon of hirtyng,
060	1PE	002	008	and stoon of sclaundre, to hem that offenden to the word, nethir bileuen it, in which thei ben set.
060	1PE	002	009	But ye ben a chosun kyn, a kyngli preesthod, hooli folc, a puple of purchasing, that ye telle the vertues of hym, that clepide you fro derknessis in to his wondirful liyt.
060	1PE	002	010	Which sum tyme were not a puple of God, but now ye ben the puple of God; which hadden not merci, but now ye han merci.
060	1PE	002	011	Moost dere, Y biseche you, as comelyngis and pilgrymys, to absteine you fro fleischli desiris, that fiyten ayens the soule;
060	1PE	002	012	and haue ye youre conuersacioun good among hethene men, that in that thing that thei bacbite of you, as of mysdoeris, thei biholden you of good werkis, and glorifie God in the dai of visitacioun.
060	1PE	002	013	Be ye suget to ech creature, for God; ethir to the kyng, as to hym that is hiyer in state,
060	1PE	002	014	ethir to duykis, as to thilke that ben sent of hym to the veniaunce of mysdoers, and to the preisyng of good men.
060	1PE	002	015	For so is the wille of God, that ye do wel, and make the vnkunnyngnesse of vnprudent men to be doumb.
060	1PE	002	016	As fre men, and not as hauynge fredom the keuering of malice, but as the seruauntis of God.
060	1PE	002	017	Onoure ye alle men, loue ye brithirhod, drede ye God, onoure ye the king.
060	1PE	002	018	Seruauntis, be ye sugetis in al drede to lordis, not oneli to good and to mylde, but also to tyrauntis.
060	1PE	002	019	For this is grace, if for conscience of God ony man suffrith heuynessis, and suffrith vniustli.
060	1PE	002	020	For what grace is it, if ye synnen, and ben buffatid, and suffren? But if ye don wel, and suffren pacientli, this is grace anentis God.
060	1PE	002	021	For to this thing ye ben clepid. For also Crist suffride for vs, and lefte ensaumple to you, that ye folewe the steppis of hym.
060	1PE	002	022	Which dide not synne, nethir gile was foundun in his mouth.
060	1PE	002	023	And whanne he was cursid, he curside not; whanne he suffride, he manasside not; but he bitook hym silf to hym, that demyde hym vniustli.
060	1PE	002	024	And he hym silf bar oure synnes in his bodi on a tre, that we be deed to synnes, and lyue to riytwisnesse, bi whos wan wounde ye ben heelid.
060	1PE	002	025	For ye weren as scheep errynge, but ye ben now turned to the schipherde, and bischop of youre soulis.
