# BOOK	064	3JO	3 John	3 John
064	3JO	001	001	The eldere man to Gayus, most dere brother, whom Y loue in treuthe.
064	3JO	001	002	Most dere brothir, of alle thingis Y make preyer, that thou entre, and fare welefuly, as thi soule doith welefuli.
064	3JO	001	003	Y ioyede greetli, for britheren camen, and baren witnessing to thi treuthe, `as thou walkist in treuthe.
064	3JO	001	004	Y haue not more grace of these thingis, than that Y here that my sones walke in treuthe.
064	3JO	001	005	Most dere brother, thou doist feithfuli, what euer thou worchist in britheren, and that in to pilgrymys,
064	3JO	001	006	which yeldiden witnessing to thi charite, in the siyt of the chirche; which thou leddist forth, and doist wel worthili to God.
064	3JO	001	007	For thei wenten forth for his name, and token no thing of hethene men.
064	3JO	001	008	Therfor we owen to resseyue siche, that we be euen worcheris of treuthe.
064	3JO	001	009	I hadde write perauenture to the chirche, but this Diotrepes, that loueth to bere primacie in hem, resseyueth not vs.
064	3JO	001	010	For this thing, if Y schal come, Y schal moneste hise werkis, whiche he doith, chidinge ayens vs with yuel wordis. And as if these thingis suffisen not to hym, nether he resseyueth britheren, and forbedith hem that resseyuen, and puttith out of the chirche.
064	3JO	001	011	Moost dere brothir, nyle thou sue yuel thing, but that that is good thing. He that doith wel, is of God; he that doith yuel, seeth not God.
064	3JO	001	012	Witnessing is yoldun to Demetrie of alle men, and of treuthe it silf; but also we beren witnessing, and thou knowist, that oure witnessing is trewe.
064	3JO	001	013	Y hadde many thingis to wryte to thee, but Y wolde not write to thee bi enke and penne.
064	3JO	001	014	For Y hope soone to se thee, and we schulen speke mouth to mouth. Pees be to thee. Frendis greten thee wel. Greete thou wel frendis bi name.
